const TRAINING = [{"topic": "", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Asset management Certification Questions – training material", "ONE Support", "Internal- SAP Only", "Version control", "If you find any content in this document is out of date, feel free to contact the Authors for feedback!", "Thanks for your cooperation in advance!", "1. OSS role in mistakenly started Hardware return process in My IT Equipment"], "content": "Asset management Certification Questions – training material ONE Support Internal- SAP Only Version control If you find any content in this document is out of date, feel free to contact the Authors for feedback! Thanks for your cooperation in advance! 1. OSS role in mistakenly started Hardware return process in My IT Equipment", "source": "Asset management", "id": 1}, {"topic": "", "section": "1.1 Overview", "paragraphs": ["OSS Team's Role: The OSS team must promptly cancel accidental tickets to prevent further action and ensure accurate records."], "content": "OSS Team's Role: The OSS team must promptly cancel accidental tickets to prevent further action and ensure accurate records.", "source": "Asset management", "id": 2}, {"topic": "", "section": "1.2 Introduction", "paragraphs": ["Efficient equipment return management is crucial, but errors, such as accidental initiation of returns in the My IT Equipment app, can occur.", "Effective communication between clients and the OSS team, along with coordination between My IT Equipment and the IT support portal, is key to managing these situations.", "This article discusses how the OSS team can efficiently cancel mistaken tickets.", "For more details about Hardware Return and asset management in general regarding My IT Equipment and", "CLEA please find the following KB: KB0837836 Cancellation Process", "1. Receive communication from the End User about the error.", "2. Cancel the ticket using the IT Support Portal.", "This will remove the “Equipment return process started remotely” flag from both CLEA:", "And the “Return for this Device is in Progress” flag from My IT Equipment:", "The flag should disappear the next day.", "For more information, please refer to KB0846415 OSS role in mistakenly started Hardware return process in My IT Equipment"], "content": "Efficient equipment return management is crucial, but errors, such as accidental initiation of returns in the My IT Equipment app, can occur. Effective communication between clients and the OSS team, along with coordination between My IT Equipment and the IT support portal, is key to managing these situations. This article discusses how the OSS team can efficiently cancel mistaken tickets. For more details about Hardware Return and asset management in general regarding My IT Equipment and CLEA please find the following KB: KB0837836 Cancellation Process 1. Receive communication from the End User about the error. 2. Cancel the ticket using the IT Support Portal. This will remove the “Equipment return process started remotely” flag from both CLEA: And the “Return for this Device is in Progress” flag from My IT Equipment: The flag should disappear the next day. For more information, please refer to KB0846415 OSS role in mistakenly started Hardware return process in My IT Equipment", "source": "Asset management", "id": 3}, {"topic": "2. New CLEA IT Storage Room Scan Inventory App", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["During Inventory Week, all technicians are required to scan equipment in all SAP locations globally using the New Inventory Scanner Application. This tool is accessible via iPhone, iPad, or Laptop using the CLEA App.", "Key Benefits of the New Scanner App", "Increased Speed & Efficiency – Scan and process data faster than ever before.", "Real-Time Inventory Updates – Technicians can begin work immediately on the official inventory date, eliminating the need for manual snapshots.", "Seamless CLEA Integration – Directly sync with the CLEA system for streamlined operations", "Improve ISP Data Quality", "Supported Equipment Categories", "The following equipment must be scanned:", "LAPTOP (Windows Laptop)", "PC (Windows Desktop)", "MACBOOK (Apple Laptop)", "IMAC (Apple Desktop)", "PH_IPHONE (iPhone)", "PH_ANDROID (Android Phone)", "T_IOS (iOS Tablet)", "T_ANDROID (Android Tablet)", "TFT-DISP (Display Monitor)", "The following ABC Indicators are in scope for the IT Storage Room scanning process:", "N – New: Equipment that is not assigned to a client for up to 6 months old.", "U – User/Productive: All User-Productive Client Hardware related to daily work", "R – Re-Use: Not based on depreciation/age but on warranty and equipment status", "S – Stock: All Equipment returned to IT must first be set to S (Stock)", "You will get more ABC Indicators information with ABC Indicator for EMR", "For more information, please refer to KB0977538 New CLEA IT Storage Room Scan Inventory App – OSS Documentation", "3. CLEA Offboarding and General Hardware Return Process"], "content": "During Inventory Week, all technicians are required to scan equipment in all SAP locations globally using the New Inventory Scanner Application. This tool is accessible via iPhone, iPad, or Laptop using the CLEA App. Key Benefits of the New Scanner App Increased Speed & Efficiency – Scan and process data faster than ever before. Real-Time Inventory Updates – Technicians can begin work immediately on the official inventory date, eliminating the need for manual snapshots. Seamless CLEA Integration – Directly sync with the CLEA system for streamlined operations Improve ISP Data Quality Supported Equipment Categories The following equipment must be scanned: LAPTOP (Windows Laptop) PC (Windows Desktop) MACBOOK (Apple Laptop) IMAC (Apple Desktop) PH_IPHONE (iPhone) PH_ANDROID (Android Phone) T_IOS (iOS Tablet) T_ANDROID (Android Tablet) TFT-DISP (Display Monitor) The following ABC Indicators are in scope for the IT Storage Room scanning process: N – New: Equipment that is not assigned to a client for up to 6 months old. U – User/Productive: All User-Productive Client Hardware related to daily work R – Re-Use: Not based on depreciation/age but on warranty and equipment status S – Stock: All Equipment returned to IT must first be set to S (Stock) You will get more ABC Indicators information with ABC Indicator for EMR For more information, please refer to KB0977538 New CLEA IT Storage Room Scan Inventory App – OSS Documentation 3. CLEA Offboarding and General Hardware Return Process", "source": "Asset management", "id": 4}, {"topic": "2. New CLEA IT Storage Room Scan Inventory App", "section": "3.1 Overview", "paragraphs": ["You will find below the steps to be taken to return a device to IT via CLEA. This guide describes the process difference between offboarding and hardware return in general.", "Important notice: A device can be returned to IT on behalf of someone else. The most convenient way to process such a request is to have the client who wishes to return an asset to IT initiate the hardware return process from My IT Equipment as a self-service.", "Please ensure all CLEA-generated tickets are collected and maintained, as clients may use them for ongoing communication."], "content": "You will find below the steps to be taken to return a device to IT via CLEA. This guide describes the process difference between offboarding and hardware return in general. Important notice: A device can be returned to IT on behalf of someone else. The most convenient way to process such a request is to have the client who wishes to return an asset to IT initiate the hardware return process from My IT Equipment as a self-service. Please ensure all CLEA-generated tickets are collected and maintained, as clients may use them for ongoing communication.", "source": "Asset management", "id": 5}, {"topic": "2. New CLEA IT Storage Room Scan Inventory App", "section": "3.2 A device is being returned to SAP IT", "paragraphs": ["Note: If a device has been selected for return mistakenly, you can cancel the process. More info: KB0846415", "A device can be returned to IT either in person or remotely. Clients can initiate the hardware return process through My IT Equipment and choose between returning the device remotely or bringing it to the IT Link Center.", "If the client starts a remote return, CLEA will show: “Equipment return process started remotely.” My IT Equipment will also display: “Return for this Device is in Progress.”", "Please note that devices must be returned to the location where they were originally assigned, unless local or country-specific policies specify otherwise. In countries such as Germany and the USA, where multiple SAP offices operate, equipment may be returned to any office within national borders.", "After identifying the device, please navigate to Manage IT Equipment to complete the return process.", "Use the asset’s Equipment number or Serial number, or locate it in the client's inventory using the user ID, then select the Returned to IT button. If applicable, choose Returned by Manager instead.", "Note: CLEA can only process assets with the ABC indicator U - User/Productive.", "3.3 Hardware Return PIN code", "When a device is being returned to the IT Link Center by the client, a PIN code must be provided by the client to OSS to be able to proceed.", "Hardware Return PIN codes are valid for 180 minutes.", "A PIN code is not required if the client has been identified by CLEA as a leaver, or if the client has initiated the hardware return process in My IT Equipment."], "content": "Note: If a device has been selected for return mistakenly, you can cancel the process. More info: KB0846415 A device can be returned to IT either in person or remotely. Clients can initiate the hardware return process through My IT Equipment and choose between returning the device remotely or bringing it to the IT Link Center. If the client starts a remote return, CLEA will show: “Equipment return process started remotely.” My IT Equipment will also display: “Return for this Device is in Progress.” Please note that devices must be returned to the location where they were originally assigned, unless local or country-specific policies specify otherwise. In countries such as Germany and the USA, where multiple SAP offices operate, equipment may be returned to any office within national borders. After identifying the device, please navigate to Manage IT Equipment to complete the return process. Use the asset’s Equipment number or Serial number, or locate it in the client's inventory using the user ID, then select the Returned to IT button. If applicable, choose Returned by Manager instead. Note: CLEA can only process assets with the ABC indicator U - User/Productive. 3.3 Hardware Return PIN code When a device is being returned to the IT Link Center by the client, a PIN code must be provided by the client to OSS to be able to proceed. Hardware Return PIN codes are valid for 180 minutes. A PIN code is not required if the client has been identified by CLEA as a leaver, or if the client has initiated the hardware return process in My IT Equipment.", "source": "Asset management", "id": 6}, {"topic": "2. New CLEA IT Storage Room Scan Inventory App", "section": "3.4 Check the device for damage and personal accounts", "paragraphs": ["Please ensure the returned device is checked for any damage and follow the applicable local process if needed. Collect all accessories issued to the client along with the device, such as the charger or peripherals.", "Also confirm that the client has signed out of all accounts, including Apple ID, Google, and Samsung, before proceeding with the hardware return.", "If the log out hasn't been done before/while return process, you can proceed with these steps, BUT, only when the device changed to Green HRC status How to disable \"Find My\" Activation from returned Apple Devices without User Interaction"], "content": "Please ensure the returned device is checked for any damage and follow the applicable local process if needed. Collect all accessories issued to the client along with the device, such as the charger or peripherals. Also confirm that the client has signed out of all accounts, including Apple ID, Google, and Samsung, before proceeding with the hardware return. If the log out hasn't been done before/while return process, you can proceed with these steps, BUT, only when the device changed to Green HRC status How to disable \"Find My\" Activation from returned Apple Devices without User Interaction", "source": "Asset management", "id": 7}, {"topic": "2. New CLEA IT Storage Room Scan Inventory App", "section": "3.5 Asset Management and background processes", "paragraphs": ["CLEA will manage and process any existing and relevant IT tickets from start to finish. If no suitable ticket exists, CLEA will create a new one. My IT Equipment tickets are also processed and resolved automatically as part of this workflow.", "Offboarding related hardware return tickets are being raised 2 weeks in advance before the termination dates. The leavers have the option to convert these tickets into remote hardware return tickets in My IT Equipment.", "PLEASE NOTE: Due to restrictions within the External Workforce system, SAP Contractor leavers will not appear in the CLEA Off-Boarding Leaving Users button like D or I number leavers. The OSS team can process Contractor Leavers returning their equipment using the CLEA Manage IT Equipment button, but the PIN will be required unless the My IT Equipment tool is used by the contractor.", "ISP is being updated automatically.", "Storage Room information must be updated.", "HRC is being checked as well. If the device is not Green, an alert will be displayed by CLEA that describes how to proceed. CLEA will automatically create new entries in HRC for Amber/Red devices. Make sure to mark an Amber/Red device as such and store it safely.", "3.6 Apple Device Management Cleanup", "If an Apple device is returned to the IT Link Center with a Green HRC status, and Apple ID's, Google or Samsung accounts, etc logged out, please proceed with the cleanup and deletion in the Jamf system.", "iPhone/iPad: https://applebucket.jamfcloud.com/mobileDevices.html", "Macbook: This can only be handled by the Mac 3rd-level team and will be processed separately at a later time.", "3.7 Unreturned Hardware Action Timeline", "All devices must be returned to SAP IT by the last working day. If any hardware is not returned by the termination date, appropriate actions will be taken.", "Day 1: A first reminder email is sent to the manager.", "Day 7: A second reminder email is sent to the manager, and an IT incident is raised to disable the device.", "Day 14: A final reminder email is sent to the manager.", "Day 21: A Resolver incident is raised for GPS, and the pending hardware return ticket is closed.", "For more information, please refer to KB0837836 CLEA Offboarding and General Hardware Return Process", "4. CLEA Lost/Stolen process"], "content": "CLEA will manage and process any existing and relevant IT tickets from start to finish. If no suitable ticket exists, CLEA will create a new one. My IT Equipment tickets are also processed and resolved automatically as part of this workflow. Offboarding related hardware return tickets are being raised 2 weeks in advance before the termination dates. The leavers have the option to convert these tickets into remote hardware return tickets in My IT Equipment. PLEASE NOTE: Due to restrictions within the External Workforce system, SAP Contractor leavers will not appear in the CLEA Off-Boarding Leaving Users button like D or I number leavers. The OSS team can process Contractor Leavers returning their equipment using the CLEA Manage IT Equipment button, but the PIN will be required unless the My IT Equipment tool is used by the contractor. ISP is being updated automatically. Storage Room information must be updated. HRC is being checked as well. If the device is not Green, an alert will be displayed by CLEA that describes how to proceed. CLEA will automatically create new entries in HRC for Amber/Red devices. Make sure to mark an Amber/Red device as such and store it safely. 3.6 Apple Device Management Cleanup If an Apple device is returned to the IT Link Center with a Green HRC status, and Apple ID's, Google or Samsung accounts, etc logged out, please proceed with the cleanup and deletion in the Jamf system. iPhone/iPad: https://applebucket.jamfcloud.com/mobileDevices.html Macbook: This can only be handled by the Mac 3rd-level team and will be processed separately at a later time. 3.7 Unreturned Hardware Action Timeline All devices must be returned to SAP IT by the last working day. If any hardware is not returned by the termination date, appropriate actions will be taken. Day 1: A first reminder email is sent to the manager. Day 7: A second reminder email is sent to the manager, and an IT incident is raised to disable the device. Day 14: A final reminder email is sent to the manager. Day 21: A Resolver incident is raised for GPS, and the pending hardware return ticket is closed. For more information, please refer to KB0837836 CLEA Offboarding and General Hardware Return Process 4. CLEA Lost/Stolen process", "source": "Asset management", "id": 8}, {"topic": "2. New CLEA IT Storage Room Scan Inventory App", "section": "4.1 Overview", "paragraphs": ["This article is for OSS IT Technicians who process lost or stolen device reports using CLEA. It covers the full process from the initial report through automatic incident creation, device locking, and ISP update.", "Note: KB0703453 describes the background process of the ITOC team about blocking devices from corporate access.", "4.2 When to Use This Process", "Use the CLEA Lost/Stolen process when:", "An employee contacts IT to report their SAP device as lost or stolen.", "An employee reported the device as lost/stolen in My IT Equipment and equipment record in ISP needs to be updated accordingly.", "An IT technician at an IT Link Center is initiating the report on behalf of the employee.", "A device is confirmed lost or stolen and needs to be locked and removed from active use.", "NOTE: This process applies to SAP-managed devices (enrolled in JAMF Pro for Mac/Apple or Intune for Android or MS Entra for Windows). BYOD devices follow a different process.", "4.3 Process Steps", "IT Technician Actions in CLEA", "Log in to CLEA and navigate to Asset Management Operations → Manage IT Equipment.", "Search for the device by Equipment Number, Serial Number, or User ID.", "Open the device record.", "Click the 'Reported as lost/stolen' button.", "When Reported as Lost/Stolen button is clicked, you are first ask whether the end user has already reported the item as lost or stolen. If confirmed, the ISP equipment record is updated accordingly:", "ABC indicator => G (Stolen)", "Inventory Number => timestamp", "No additional security incidents are generated.", "Confirm the action in the pop-up dialog. - You need to fill the lost/stolen form with the end user clarifying whether the item is lost or stolen, how the end user lost it, where, and so on.", "NOTE: After clicking 'Reported as lost/stolen' in CLEA, no further manual action is needed from the IT technician for the locking and incident creation steps — these are fully automated.", "4.4 Employee Actions (if reporting directly)", "The default method for the employees to report lost/stolen IT equipment should be the \"Lost or Stolen\" button in My IT Equipment app.", "NOTE: Device locking is performed by the CSD ITOC Team within 24 hours of the locking request being raised.", "For more information, please refer to KB0837842 CLEA Lost/Stolen process", "5. Asset Management - SAP IT Equipment Policy and Lifecycle – instructions for clients (end-users)"], "content": "This article is for OSS IT Technicians who process lost or stolen device reports using CLEA. It covers the full process from the initial report through automatic incident creation, device locking, and ISP update. Note: KB0703453 describes the background process of the ITOC team about blocking devices from corporate access. 4.2 When to Use This Process Use the CLEA Lost/Stolen process when: An employee contacts IT to report their SAP device as lost or stolen. An employee reported the device as lost/stolen in My IT Equipment and equipment record in ISP needs to be updated accordingly. An IT technician at an IT Link Center is initiating the report on behalf of the employee. A device is confirmed lost or stolen and needs to be locked and removed from active use. NOTE: This process applies to SAP-managed devices (enrolled in JAMF Pro for Mac/Apple or Intune for Android or MS Entra for Windows). BYOD devices follow a different process. 4.3 Process Steps IT Technician Actions in CLEA Log in to CLEA and navigate to Asset Management Operations → Manage IT Equipment. Search for the device by Equipment Number, Serial Number, or User ID. Open the device record. Click the 'Reported as lost/stolen' button. When Reported as Lost/Stolen button is clicked, you are first ask whether the end user has already reported the item as lost or stolen. If confirmed, the ISP equipment record is updated accordingly: ABC indicator => G (Stolen) Inventory Number => timestamp No additional security incidents are generated. Confirm the action in the pop-up dialog. - You need to fill the lost/stolen form with the end user clarifying whether the item is lost or stolen, how the end user lost it, where, and so on. NOTE: After clicking 'Reported as lost/stolen' in CLEA, no further manual action is needed from the IT technician for the locking and incident creation steps — these are fully automated. 4.4 Employee Actions (if reporting directly) The default method for the employees to report lost/stolen IT equipment should be the \"Lost or Stolen\" button in My IT Equipment app. NOTE: Device locking is performed by the CSD ITOC Team within 24 hours of the locking request being raised. For more information, please refer to KB0837842 CLEA Lost/Stolen process 5. Asset Management - SAP IT Equipment Policy and Lifecycle – instructions for clients (end-users)", "source": "Asset management", "id": 9}, {"topic": "2. New CLEA IT Storage Room Scan Inventory App", "section": "5.1 Overview", "paragraphs": ["SAP IT Equipment Policy. This document provides information on standard employee device assignment policy, where to order equipment when you should replace your hardware, and costs associated with procurement."], "content": "SAP IT Equipment Policy. This document provides information on standard employee device assignment policy, where to order equipment when you should replace your hardware, and costs associated with procurement.", "source": "Asset management", "id": 10}, {"topic": "2. New CLEA IT Storage Room Scan Inventory App", "section": "5.2 Workplace @ SAP", "paragraphs": ["SAP provides each employee with one standard workplace device; this can be a PC or a notebook and an additional display (if needed). The recommended usage of hardware is at least 3 years because of the warranty.", "Unused (not connected to SAP system) devices will be deactivated within 6 months."], "content": "SAP provides each employee with one standard workplace device; this can be a PC or a notebook and an additional display (if needed). The recommended usage of hardware is at least 3 years because of the warranty. Unused (not connected to SAP system) devices will be deactivated within 6 months.", "source": "Asset management", "id": 11}, {"topic": "2. New CLEA IT Storage Room Scan Inventory App", "section": "5.3 What is SAP's Policy regarding employee IT Equipment?", "paragraphs": ["Employees are assigned to one computer. An additional computer requires approval from your cost center manager. Before ordering your equipment, confirm first with your cost center manager to ensure a smooth approval and delivery process. SAP", "standard hardware is supported by SAP IT.", "Learn more about:", "It's all about your IT devices", "Review the equipment inventory assigned to you"], "content": "Employees are assigned to one computer. An additional computer requires approval from your cost center manager. Before ordering your equipment, confirm first with your cost center manager to ensure a smooth approval and delivery process. SAP standard hardware is supported by SAP IT. Learn more about: It's all about your IT devices Review the equipment inventory assigned to you", "source": "Asset management", "id": 12}, {"topic": "2. New CLEA IT Storage Room Scan Inventory App", "section": "5.4 How Do I Order a New Device?", "paragraphs": ["Go to SAP Ariba Buying and choose the End User Hardware and Software catalog to find sub-catalogs for all of your Hardware and Software needs.", "You may also refer to our It's all about your device site on IT for You to view information on IT devices for your workplace at SAP.", "SAP Concur employees should reference the Concur Procurement Help Desk for country-specific ordering instructions.", "For more information, you can read KB How to Order a New Device", "Can I order a Mac?", "Yes, please have a look on Mac@SAP."], "content": "Go to SAP Ariba Buying and choose the End User Hardware and Software catalog to find sub-catalogs for all of your Hardware and Software needs. You may also refer to our It's all about your device site on IT for You to view information on IT devices for your workplace at SAP. SAP Concur employees should reference the Concur Procurement Help Desk for country-specific ordering instructions. For more information, you can read KB How to Order a New Device Can I order a Mac? Yes, please have a look on Mac@SAP.", "source": "Asset management", "id": 13}, {"topic": "2. New CLEA IT Storage Room Scan Inventory App", "section": "5.5 When can I replace my hardware?", "paragraphs": ["Please find additional information on the My IT Equipment App and When to replacement your computer How to order a New Device.", "Only Primary devices can be replaced when eligible for replacement. You can find more information in these articles:", "IT Asset Management - Guidelines for Multiple Device Usage and Individual Responsibilities", "Redundant Devices - Hardware Multiplicity in My IT Equipment", "We recommend a minimum of hardware usage of at least 3 years.", "If your device is lost or stolen, please report this through the My IT Equipment app. You are permitted to purchase replacement equipment if your device is lost or stolen.", "Please be aware of the following criteria for ordering new IT Equipment in case of replacement:", "Visit the My IT Equipment App to get the technical details (e.g. acquisition date) of your currently used equipment.", "Additional information regarding iPad/Tablet: As part of our ongoing efforts to optimize our resources and align with the market demands, it has been decided to discontinue the offering of iPads and tablets in the Ariba Catalog. This decision was made by the board of directors as a safeguarding measure to ensure that we are operating efficiently and effectively in the current market conditions.", "Additional information regarding external monitor: Monitors must only be shipped to an office location. This is a strict global Policy requirement with no exception. Upon receipt, be mindful that the monitors are designated for office use (fixed desk in an SAP location) and may not be taken to home offices. For more information, see External Monitor - SAP Global Asset Management Policy and Standard.", "You will get more SAP IT Equipment policy from KB0013173 Asset Management - SAP IT Equipment Policy and Lifecycle"], "content": "Please find additional information on the My IT Equipment App and When to replacement your computer How to order a New Device. Only Primary devices can be replaced when eligible for replacement. You can find more information in these articles: IT Asset Management - Guidelines for Multiple Device Usage and Individual Responsibilities Redundant Devices - Hardware Multiplicity in My IT Equipment We recommend a minimum of hardware usage of at least 3 years. If your device is lost or stolen, please report this through the My IT Equipment app. You are permitted to purchase replacement equipment if your device is lost or stolen. Please be aware of the following criteria for ordering new IT Equipment in case of replacement: Visit the My IT Equipment App to get the technical details (e.g. acquisition date) of your currently used equipment. Additional information regarding iPad/Tablet: As part of our ongoing efforts to optimize our resources and align with the market demands, it has been decided to discontinue the offering of iPads and tablets in the Ariba Catalog. This decision was made by the board of directors as a safeguarding measure to ensure that we are operating efficiently and effectively in the current market conditions. Additional information regarding external monitor: Monitors must only be shipped to an office location. This is a strict global Policy requirement with no exception. Upon receipt, be mindful that the monitors are designated for office use (fixed desk in an SAP location) and may not be taken to home offices. For more information, see External Monitor - SAP Global Asset Management Policy and Standard. You will get more SAP IT Equipment policy from KB0013173 Asset Management - SAP IT Equipment Policy and Lifecycle", "source": "Asset management", "id": 14}, {"topic": "2. New CLEA IT Storage Room Scan Inventory App", "section": "5.6 Multiple Devices - Hardware Multiplicity in My IT Equipment", "paragraphs": ["Overview", "This policy outlines the appropriate usage of multiple devices within the company. The aim is to ensure the responsible use of company devices by aligning the right device for the right job, promoting sustainability, and minimizing unnecessary duplication of devices.", "Please read KB0976050 Guidelines for Multiple Device Usage and Individual Responsibilities", "The Multiple Devices Tool is an extension of the My IT Equipment app. Its purpose is to track multiple devices based on device type in users' inventories and offer various actions and solutions to reduce the use of unnecessary additional devices.", "If you are a Line Manager, you have the ability to directly maintain the assets of your direct reports.", "Should you encounter issues beyond the control of OSS regarding asset management, please raise an IT ticket with the following details:", "Service Offering: IES-CS-ITAM Tool", "Assignment group: IES CS Advanced - ITAM Tools", "Managing Multiple Devices – Notification Process", "Multiple Devices", "Every employee is entitled to one standard work device. Multiple devices can only be kept if there is a valid business reason and the exception is formally approved. This ensures fairness, strengthens security, supports sustainability, and helps maintain compliance with company policy while controlling costs.", "The My IT Equipment application helps employees stay up to date with their devices and complete all necessary actions — report, return, or request an exception — directly within the tool. When needed, notification emails are also sent to both the user and their manager to ensure timely follow-up.", "Initial email: After a grace period, the first email provides information about your assigned devices and the actions available.", "Reminder email: Sent if no action is taken. Your manager will be also notified about the assigned multiple devices.", "Escalation emails: If multiple devices remain after the reminder period, both you and your manager will continue to receive follow-up emails until the situation is resolved.", "You will get more Multiple Devices from KB1280813 Managing Multiple Devices – Notification Process", "Available Actions", "The Multiplicity section displays all additional devices categorized by type, including their current statuses. You can designate a device as your Primary, request and extend an exception, or initiate a hardware return to SAP IT.", "Note: A device must be selected as Primary before initiating hardware returns on other assets.", "How to designate a device as Primary?", "Click the Select Action button under Actions to make a device Primary by clicking Set Primary. Confirm in the dialog box.", "The selected device will now be designated as Primary, and all other relevant assets will be marked as Multiple.", "How to request an exception?", "To request an exception for using a secondary device, click the Select Action button and provide a business reason for retaining the asset. Submit the request for your manager's approval.", "Your manager will have the option to approve or reject your exception request.", "You may also Extend an Exception if more time is needed for your work with a given device.", "You may also decide to return the asset to SAP IT instead.", "You will get more Multiple Devices from KB0945001 Multiple Devices - Hardware Multiplicity in My IT Equipment"], "content": "Overview This policy outlines the appropriate usage of multiple devices within the company. The aim is to ensure the responsible use of company devices by aligning the right device for the right job, promoting sustainability, and minimizing unnecessary duplication of devices. Please read KB0976050 Guidelines for Multiple Device Usage and Individual Responsibilities The Multiple Devices Tool is an extension of the My IT Equipment app. Its purpose is to track multiple devices based on device type in users' inventories and offer various actions and solutions to reduce the use of unnecessary additional devices. If you are a Line Manager, you have the ability to directly maintain the assets of your direct reports. Should you encounter issues beyond the control of OSS regarding asset management, please raise an IT ticket with the following details: Service Offering: IES-CS-ITAM Tool Assignment group: IES CS Advanced - ITAM Tools Managing Multiple Devices – Notification Process Multiple Devices Every employee is entitled to one standard work device. Multiple devices can only be kept if there is a valid business reason and the exception is formally approved. This ensures fairness, strengthens security, supports sustainability, and helps maintain compliance with company policy while controlling costs. The My IT Equipment application helps employees stay up to date with their devices and complete all necessary actions — report, return, or request an exception — directly within the tool. When needed, notification emails are also sent to both the user and their manager to ensure timely follow-up. Initial email: After a grace period, the first email provides information about your assigned devices and the actions available. Reminder email: Sent if no action is taken. Your manager will be also notified about the assigned multiple devices. Escalation emails: If multiple devices remain after the reminder period, both you and your manager will continue to receive follow-up emails until the situation is resolved. You will get more Multiple Devices from KB1280813 Managing Multiple Devices – Notification Process Available Actions The Multiplicity section displays all additional devices categorized by type, including their current statuses. You can designate a device as your Primary, request and extend an exception, or initiate a hardware return to SAP IT. Note: A device must be selected as Primary before initiating hardware returns on other assets. How to designate a device as Primary? Click the Select Action button under Actions to make a device Primary by clicking Set Primary. Confirm in the dialog box. The selected device will now be designated as Primary, and all other relevant assets will be marked as Multiple. How to request an exception? To request an exception for using a secondary device, click the Select Action button and provide a business reason for retaining the asset. Submit the request for your manager's approval. Your manager will have the option to approve or reject your exception request. You may also Extend an Exception if more time is needed for your work with a given device. You may also decide to return the asset to SAP IT instead. You will get more Multiple Devices from KB0945001 Multiple Devices - Hardware Multiplicity in My IT Equipment", "source": "Asset management", "id": 15}, {"topic": "2. New CLEA IT Storage Room Scan Inventory App", "section": "5.7 Hardware Return", "paragraphs": ["Initiate the return process by going to the My IT Equipment app, select the device you would like to return and select on \"Return Equipment\". You will be prompted with the available return options for your location:", "Return personally - Bring your device with all the provided accessories to", "an IT Link Center in the country where it was issued initially and return it to the IT personnel.", "Return remote - Follow the onscreen instruction to request for a remote", "return.", "If you decide to return the device personally without going through the above step, you will be asked by the IT personnel to provide an auto-generated PIN code which will be sent to your SAP email (not applicable for Internal leaving SAP employees). Be sure to have access to a secondary SAP-issued mobile/laptop during the return process to obtain the code. If you cannot provide the auto-generated PIN code.", "During the time of return, you will have to give the PIN code to the IT personnel remotely once you have access to your email.", "You will get more How to return Equipment from KB Hardware - How to return Equipment and Return Equipment FAQ"], "content": "Initiate the return process by going to the My IT Equipment app, select the device you would like to return and select on \"Return Equipment\". You will be prompted with the available return options for your location: Return personally - Bring your device with all the provided accessories to an IT Link Center in the country where it was issued initially and return it to the IT personnel. Return remote - Follow the onscreen instruction to request for a remote return. If you decide to return the device personally without going through the above step, you will be asked by the IT personnel to provide an auto-generated PIN code which will be sent to your SAP email (not applicable for Internal leaving SAP employees). Be sure to have access to a secondary SAP-issued mobile/laptop during the return process to obtain the code. If you cannot provide the auto-generated PIN code. During the time of return, you will have to give the PIN code to the IT personnel remotely once you have access to your email. You will get more How to return Equipment from KB Hardware - How to return Equipment and Return Equipment FAQ", "source": "Asset management", "id": 16}, {"topic": "6. Hardware Return Checker FAQ", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Overview", "The Hardware Return Checker (HRC) is a platform that helps a field service technician quickly determine whether to reuse, dispose, or securely store (hold) an asset based on the “traffic-light” system (Green, Amber, Red).", "The process of retrieving, securely storing, and adding equipment to the HRC based on the \"traffic light system\" results is very important to the overall end-to-end process. All users' devices marked as RED, or AMBER must be securely stored with data retained until its status has changed to GREEN.", "The HRC platform includes support for Global Physical Security (GPS) and Secure Storage Rooms (SSR), as they become available, which allows GPS to take over the responsibility for storing and managing RED assets.", "Regional RSE’s:", "AMER – Wenerd, Richard, richard.wenerd@sap.com EMEA – Hoffman, Darryl, darryl.hoffman@sap.com Germany – Mann, Peter, peter.mann@sap.com APJ – Leng, Fui Loong, fui.loong.leng@sap.com", "Link to Hardware Return Checker App", "You will get more Hardware Return Checker from KB Hardware Return Checker FAQ"], "content": "Overview The Hardware Return Checker (HRC) is a platform that helps a field service technician quickly determine whether to reuse, dispose, or securely store (hold) an asset based on the “traffic-light” system (Green, Amber, Red). The process of retrieving, securely storing, and adding equipment to the HRC based on the \"traffic light system\" results is very important to the overall end-to-end process. All users' devices marked as RED, or AMBER must be securely stored with data retained until its status has changed to GREEN. The HRC platform includes support for Global Physical Security (GPS) and Secure Storage Rooms (SSR), as they become available, which allows GPS to take over the responsibility for storing and managing RED assets. Regional RSE’s: AMER – Wenerd, Richard, richard.wenerd@sap.com EMEA – Hoffman, Darryl, darryl.hoffman@sap.com Germany – Mann, Peter, peter.mann@sap.com APJ – Leng, Fui Loong, fui.loong.leng@sap.com Link to Hardware Return Checker App You will get more Hardware Return Checker from KB Hardware Return Checker FAQ", "source": "Asset management", "id": 17}, {"topic": "7. Secure Workstation (PAW)", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Overview", "This document outlines the required steps for Local IT when handling a PAW (Privileged Access Workstation) device — whether a user reports an issue or the device is returned.", "Instructions", "Step 1: Identify the Device Type", "Flip the device over and look for the SWS asset tag (PAW label).", "You can also validate by checking the ABC indicator in ISP (W = PAW).", "Step 2: Determine the Situation", "User-Reported Issue If the device is confirmed to be a PAW and the user reports a problem:", "Do not troubleshoot or attempt repairs.", "Go to Secure Workstation - Landing Page and submit a support ticket to the Secure Workstation Services (SWS) Team. Include a brief description, user contact information, and device details (serial number or hostname).", "Inform the user:", "Their device is a PAW, and the SWS team will handle further support.", "No further action required by Local IT.", "Returned Device If the device has been returned (user separation, upgrade, or no longer needed):", "Do not reprovision, modify, or reassign the device.", "Send the PAW to SIMS for secure disposal.", "No further action required by Local IT.", "Important Notes", "Local IT is not authorized to troubleshoot, modify, re-provision, or de-provision PAW devices.", "All PAW issues must be escalated to the SWS Team or disposed of through SIMS, depending on the situation.", "Additional Information Secure Workstation - Landing Page"], "content": "Overview This document outlines the required steps for Local IT when handling a PAW (Privileged Access Workstation) device — whether a user reports an issue or the device is returned. Instructions Step 1: Identify the Device Type Flip the device over and look for the SWS asset tag (PAW label). You can also validate by checking the ABC indicator in ISP (W = PAW). Step 2: Determine the Situation User-Reported Issue If the device is confirmed to be a PAW and the user reports a problem: Do not troubleshoot or attempt repairs. Go to Secure Workstation - Landing Page and submit a support ticket to the Secure Workstation Services (SWS) Team. Include a brief description, user contact information, and device details (serial number or hostname). Inform the user: Their device is a PAW, and the SWS team will handle further support. No further action required by Local IT. Returned Device If the device has been returned (user separation, upgrade, or no longer needed): Do not reprovision, modify, or reassign the device. Send the PAW to SIMS for secure disposal. No further action required by Local IT. Important Notes Local IT is not authorized to troubleshoot, modify, re-provision, or de-provision PAW devices. All PAW issues must be escalated to the SWS Team or disposed of through SIMS, depending on the situation. Additional Information Secure Workstation - Landing Page", "source": "Asset management", "id": 18}, {"topic": "8. Apple AirPods Warranty Information", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Apple AirPods are not included in SAP’s Apple Care for Enterprise (ACE) program, which does cover MacBooks, iPhones, iPads in participating countries. Additionally, these devices do not have Apple Care Plus (AC+) coverage.", "If your Apple AirPods or accessories have defects and the issue isn't due to mishandling or accidents, the Apple One (1) Year Apple Limited Warranty may cover repair or replacement.", "For country-specific legal warranty details and Apple Support contact information, please refer to the Apple One (1) Year Limited Warranty Accessory document Legal - Accessory Warranty English - Apple .", "Accidental Physical or Liquid Damage", "The Apple Limited Warranty does not cover AirPods that have physical or liquid damage resulting from user mishandling.", "Support Guidance for Defective Apple AirPods", "Before seeking assistance for faulty Apple AirPods under the Apple One (1) Year Apple Limited Warranty, end-users need to verify that the AirPods were bought in Ariba within the current year. To check the purchase date, click Check your device's coverage and input the AirPods Serial Number, which is located on the underside of the lid of your charging case. This portal displays the purchase date and informs users about warranty status and available services.", "EMEA INT and Germany", "In regions where Bechtle acts as the Procurement supplier (EMEA INT and Germany), SAP end-users should submit a Procure to Pay (P2P) ticket in Unified Ticketing. Make sure the Ticket Type is set to “Procure to Pay” instead of “IT Ticket.” Use the Description template “Broken AirPod – Warranty.” Bechtle will collaborate with Apple and the end-user to address the issue.", "AMER and APJ", "End-users in the Americas and APJ region (except India and areas without an Apple Store) can contact Apple Support for broken or defective devices. Alternatively, they can visit an Apple Store with their AirPods and accessories for help.", "In India and APJ offices without a nearby Apple Store, SAP IT Client Service Desk and On-Site Support will facilitate communication with the Apple reseller, similar to support for general IT devices. Contact SAP IT Support or visit your local IT Link Center.", "SAP end-users cannot buy new AirPods through Ariba within three years from the original order date.", "If an AirPods is lost, stolen, or damaged during this time, the end-user must replace it at their own expense.", "For more information, please refer to the Updated Apple AirPods Ordering Guidance/ Policy for Employees (incl. Concur).", "Apple Care for Enterprise Phone Numbers", "Although AirPods aren't covered by ACE, Apple Enterprise Advisors can still help clients with any Apple device issues.", "The ACE phone numbers around the world are:", "Australia : 130 076 0237", "Austria : 0800 070266", "Belgium : 0800 81 519", "Canada : 866 752 7753", "China : 400 056 0710", "Denmark : 80251620", "Finland : 0800 774220", "France : 0805 540 103", "Germany : 0800 6645 308", "Hong Kong : 2112 9968", "India : 000800 1009009", "Ireland : 1 800805005", "Israel : (02) 375-2135", "Italy : 800798644", "Japan : 012 099 6477", "Kingdom of Saudi Arabia: 800844 8008", "Luxembourg : 800 27790", "Netherlands : 0800 3949020", "New Zealand : 0800 387931", "Norway : 240 55 186", "Poland : 800 707 347", "Portugal : 800781367", "Singapore : 800 186 1015", "South Korea : 080 500 0017", "Spain : 900812689", "Sweden : 020 160 5636", "Switzerland : 0800 00 0467", "Turkey : 00800 448829876", "United Arab Emirates: 800 0444 9014", "United Kingdom : 0800 912 7301", "United States : 866 752 7753", "And the PIN for the different regions we have spit the ACE contract for SAP are:", "SAP Germany - 3193", "SAP EMEA INT - 3226", "SAP APJ - 3228", "SAP AMER - 3227"], "content": "Apple AirPods are not included in SAP’s Apple Care for Enterprise (ACE) program, which does cover MacBooks, iPhones, iPads in participating countries. Additionally, these devices do not have Apple Care Plus (AC+) coverage. If your Apple AirPods or accessories have defects and the issue isn't due to mishandling or accidents, the Apple One (1) Year Apple Limited Warranty may cover repair or replacement. For country-specific legal warranty details and Apple Support contact information, please refer to the Apple One (1) Year Limited Warranty Accessory document Legal - Accessory Warranty English - Apple . Accidental Physical or Liquid Damage The Apple Limited Warranty does not cover AirPods that have physical or liquid damage resulting from user mishandling. Support Guidance for Defective Apple AirPods Before seeking assistance for faulty Apple AirPods under the Apple One (1) Year Apple Limited Warranty, end-users need to verify that the AirPods were bought in Ariba within the current year. To check the purchase date, click Check your device's coverage and input the AirPods Serial Number, which is located on the underside of the lid of your charging case. This portal displays the purchase date and informs users about warranty status and available services. EMEA INT and Germany In regions where Bechtle acts as the Procurement supplier (EMEA INT and Germany), SAP end-users should submit a Procure to Pay (P2P) ticket in Unified Ticketing. Make sure the Ticket Type is set to “Procure to Pay” instead of “IT Ticket.” Use the Description template “Broken AirPod – Warranty.” Bechtle will collaborate with Apple and the end-user to address the issue. AMER and APJ End-users in the Americas and APJ region (except India and areas without an Apple Store) can contact Apple Support for broken or defective devices. Alternatively, they can visit an Apple Store with their AirPods and accessories for help. In India and APJ offices without a nearby Apple Store, SAP IT Client Service Desk and On-Site Support will facilitate communication with the Apple reseller, similar to support for general IT devices. Contact SAP IT Support or visit your local IT Link Center. SAP end-users cannot buy new AirPods through Ariba within three years from the original order date. If an AirPods is lost, stolen, or damaged during this time, the end-user must replace it at their own expense. For more information, please refer to the Updated Apple AirPods Ordering Guidance/ Policy for Employees (incl. Concur). Apple Care for Enterprise Phone Numbers Although AirPods aren't covered by ACE, Apple Enterprise Advisors can still help clients with any Apple device issues. The ACE phone numbers around the world are: Australia : 130 076 0237 Austria : 0800 070266 Belgium : 0800 81 519 Canada : 866 752 7753 China : 400 056 0710 Denmark : 80251620 Finland : 0800 774220 France : 0805 540 103 Germany : 0800 6645 308 Hong Kong : 2112 9968 India : 000800 1009009 Ireland : 1 800805005 Israel : (02) 375-2135 Italy : 800798644 Japan : 012 099 6477 Kingdom of Saudi Arabia: 800844 8008 Luxembourg : 800 27790 Netherlands : 0800 3949020 New Zealand : 0800 387931 Norway : 240 55 186 Poland : 800 707 347 Portugal : 800781367 Singapore : 800 186 1015 South Korea : 080 500 0017 Spain : 900812689 Sweden : 020 160 5636 Switzerland : 0800 00 0467 Turkey : 00800 448829876 United Arab Emirates: 800 0444 9014 United Kingdom : 0800 912 7301 United States : 866 752 7753 And the PIN for the different regions we have spit the ACE contract for SAP are: SAP Germany - 3193 SAP EMEA INT - 3226 SAP APJ - 3228 SAP AMER - 3227", "source": "Asset management", "id": 19}, {"topic": "", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["ONE Support", "Internal- SAP Only", "Version control", "If you find any content in this document is out of date, feel free to contact the Authors for feedback!", "Thanks for your cooperation in advance!"], "content": "ONE Support Internal- SAP Only Version control If you find any content in this document is out of date, feel free to contact the Authors for feedback! Thanks for your cooperation in advance!", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 20}, {"topic": "Microsoft license", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Can I use my Office 365 subscription on a private device at home?", "Although each Office 365 subscription is entitled for usage on 5 devices (Windows, macOS), using a company provided license on a private device is considered a monetary benefit (Geldwerter Vorteil) by tax and revenue offices - this was checked in the 15 countries with the biggest SAP workforce. If the employee doesn't declare this benefit correctly, SAP would/could be held responsible. Negotiations are ongoing (but not very likely to succeed) so installing / using Office365 with a company license on private devices is currently prohibited.", "Refer to IKB0011435 - Microsoft 365 - General FAQ for Click to Run Office Applications", "Can I own a HUP license for Microsoft Office? What is the organization program code?", "Since SAP has switched completely to Microsoft Office 365, we are no longer eligible to participate in the Microsoft Home Use Program (HUP). Office 365 is a subscription; HUP is only granted to customer purchasing the Office 2019 and previous licenses", "Refer to IKB0010595 - Microsoft 365 - Home Use Program HUP has stopped for SAP"], "content": "Can I use my Office 365 subscription on a private device at home? Although each Office 365 subscription is entitled for usage on 5 devices (Windows, macOS), using a company provided license on a private device is considered a monetary benefit (Geldwerter Vorteil) by tax and revenue offices - this was checked in the 15 countries with the biggest SAP workforce. If the employee doesn't declare this benefit correctly, SAP would/could be held responsible. Negotiations are ongoing (but not very likely to succeed) so installing / using Office365 with a company license on private devices is currently prohibited. Refer to IKB0011435 - Microsoft 365 - General FAQ for Click to Run Office Applications Can I own a HUP license for Microsoft Office? What is the organization program code? Since SAP has switched completely to Microsoft Office 365, we are no longer eligible to participate in the Microsoft Home Use Program (HUP). Office 365 is a subscription; HUP is only granted to customer purchasing the Office 2019 and previous licenses Refer to IKB0010595 - Microsoft 365 - Home Use Program HUP has stopped for SAP", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 21}, {"topic": "Teams - Microsoft Teams - Built for hybrid work", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Meet, chat, call, and share video and files, all from one place. Plus, communicate one-on-one, with part of a team, a full team, or groups from different organizations in the company.", "Teams enables people to work together at the same time or at different times, so they can collaborate from virtually anywhere without missing something important. With shared documents and files available when and where they need them, it is easier to keep projects and tasks moving forward."], "content": "Meet, chat, call, and share video and files, all from one place. Plus, communicate one-on-one, with part of a team, a full team, or groups from different organizations in the company. Teams enables people to work together at the same time or at different times, so they can collaborate from virtually anywhere without missing something important. With shared documents and files available when and where they need them, it is easier to keep projects and tasks moving forward.", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 22}, {"topic": "Teams - Microsoft Teams - Built for hybrid work", "section": "How to create a team", "paragraphs": ["Open the Teams client or access Teams on the web. On the left side of the app, Select Teams , click the drop-down arrow icon, and select \"New team\".", "Name your team and add an optional description.", "Decide what kind of team you want this to be. To limit content and talk to a certain group of people, choose Private. For a community or topic that anyone in the org can join, choose Public.", "And you can create team from template or from another existing team and group.", "Note: Every team has at least one channel. We create the first one for you; however, you must provide a name to get started. Its description is the same as your team's description.", "If needed, you can add more channels, but you will always have this first channel. Your first channel cannot be archived or deleted."], "content": "Open the Teams client or access Teams on the web. On the left side of the app, Select Teams , click the drop-down arrow icon, and select \"New team\". Name your team and add an optional description. Decide what kind of team you want this to be. To limit content and talk to a certain group of people, choose Private. For a community or topic that anyone in the org can join, choose Public. And you can create team from template or from another existing team and group. Note: Every team has at least one channel. We create the first one for you; however, you must provide a name to get started. Its description is the same as your team's description. If needed, you can add more channels, but you will always have this first channel. Your first channel cannot be archived or deleted.", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 23}, {"topic": "Teams - Microsoft Teams - Built for hybrid work", "section": "Private Channel Limit Increase", "paragraphs": ["One of the most significant updates coming at the end of October 2025 is the increased limit for private channels and their memberships. Previously, Teams restricted private channels to 250 users and 30 channels per team, which sometimes hampered large projects or complex organizational structures.", "What’s changing?", "Private Channels Membership: The user limit per private channel is increasing from 250 to a whopping 5,000 users.", "Number of Private Channels: A single team can now host up to 1,000 private channels, a substantial jump from the former limit of 30.", "Meetings in Private Channels: You can now schedule meetings directly within private channels, streamlining coordination and communication for focused groups.", "These improvements give far more flexibility in organizing your workspaces, supporting larger teams, and managing projects with granular access controls.", "More about Private Channels, please refer to IT for You SharePoint page.", "Microsoft Teams _ Private Channels"], "content": "One of the most significant updates coming at the end of October 2025 is the increased limit for private channels and their memberships. Previously, Teams restricted private channels to 250 users and 30 channels per team, which sometimes hampered large projects or complex organizational structures. What’s changing? Private Channels Membership: The user limit per private channel is increasing from 250 to a whopping 5,000 users. Number of Private Channels: A single team can now host up to 1,000 private channels, a substantial jump from the former limit of 30. Meetings in Private Channels: You can now schedule meetings directly within private channels, streamlining coordination and communication for focused groups. These improvements give far more flexibility in organizing your workspaces, supporting larger teams, and managing projects with granular access controls. More about Private Channels, please refer to IT for You SharePoint page. Microsoft Teams _ Private Channels", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 24}, {"topic": "Teams - Microsoft Teams - Built for hybrid work", "section": "How to Join a team", "paragraphs": ["Open Teams, press the drop-down arrow icon, and select “Join team”.", "To join a Public Team, use the Search Box to find the team and then click on Join Team from the search results.", "To join a private team, use a code or ask the team owner to add you as a member.", "Teams Owner can generate the Team code from Manage Team -> Settings -> Team Code"], "content": "Open Teams, press the drop-down arrow icon, and select “Join team”. To join a Public Team, use the Search Box to find the team and then click on Join Team from the search results. To join a private team, use a code or ask the team owner to add you as a member. Teams Owner can generate the Team code from Manage Team -> Settings -> Team Code", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 25}, {"topic": "Teams - Microsoft Teams - Built for hybrid work", "section": "Teams for Channels", "paragraphs": ["Channels in Microsoft Teams help you to organize your conversations by topic, project, or even along organizational lines depending on your needs. With private and shared channels, you have even more possibilities for collaborating with internal and external partners.", "Keep everyone informed at once.", "Channels in Microsoft Teams give you the unique opportunity to update anyone within your project or team at the same time.", "Simply start a new conversation in the respective channel and @-notify your colleagues, if necessary. Everyone can read the conversation in their own time, reply with questions or suggestions, and stay up to date on developments after absences.", "Private channels.", "Use a private channel if you have certain areas within your project that not all team members need to see, e.g., budget allocation. As private channels will only be accessible to invited members and as they come with a separate SharePoint for file storage, your private or confidential items are safely tugged away.", "Customize your channel with tabs.", "At the top of each channel, you will find the tabs Posts, Files by default. But you can also add documents, links to websites or other apps as tabs there to customize the channel to your needs. These could be project overview documents or a simple welcome message with housekeeping rules for new members.", "How to restore accidentally deleted team in Microsoft Teams", "IT admins can recover deleted teams for up to 30 days.", "To request the restore:", "Create a request on https://itsupport.sap.com – Request catalog - Microsoft Teams restore.", "Or use the direct link to raise request – Restore a deleted team", "When a team is restored, the following content is restored:", "Teams team", "Azure Active Directory (AAD) Microsoft 365 Groups object, properties and members", "Group SMTP address", "Exchange Online shared inbox and calendar", "SharePoint Online team site and files", "OneNote notebook", "Planner", "How to restore accidentally deleted team channel in Microsoft Teams", "To restore the accidentally deleted team channel, you may go to Manage team, click on Channels -> More -> Deleted", "Select the deleted team channel and click on Restore", "Change a channel name in Microsoft Teams", "Team owners and members can change the name of a channel by selecting the channel in the list, and then select More Channel options button > Edit Channel.", "If you don't see the option “Edit channel”, that means that a team owner has changed the permissions that members have. Also note that you cannot change the name of the General channel(the first named channel).", "The General channel can also be renamed from the Manage channel settings page by teams owners.", "General is a reserved string, and no new channels can be named General.", "The first-created channel in a new team will have the same description as the team by default.", "Refer to Microsoft community - Give a custom name to the General channel in Microsoft Teams"], "content": "Channels in Microsoft Teams help you to organize your conversations by topic, project, or even along organizational lines depending on your needs. With private and shared channels, you have even more possibilities for collaborating with internal and external partners. Keep everyone informed at once. Channels in Microsoft Teams give you the unique opportunity to update anyone within your project or team at the same time. Simply start a new conversation in the respective channel and @-notify your colleagues, if necessary. Everyone can read the conversation in their own time, reply with questions or suggestions, and stay up to date on developments after absences. Private channels. Use a private channel if you have certain areas within your project that not all team members need to see, e.g., budget allocation. As private channels will only be accessible to invited members and as they come with a separate SharePoint for file storage, your private or confidential items are safely tugged away. Customize your channel with tabs. At the top of each channel, you will find the tabs Posts, Files by default. But you can also add documents, links to websites or other apps as tabs there to customize the channel to your needs. These could be project overview documents or a simple welcome message with housekeeping rules for new members. How to restore accidentally deleted team in Microsoft Teams IT admins can recover deleted teams for up to 30 days. To request the restore: Create a request on https://itsupport.sap.com – Request catalog - Microsoft Teams restore. Or use the direct link to raise request – Restore a deleted team When a team is restored, the following content is restored: Teams team Azure Active Directory (AAD) Microsoft 365 Groups object, properties and members Group SMTP address Exchange Online shared inbox and calendar SharePoint Online team site and files OneNote notebook Planner How to restore accidentally deleted team channel in Microsoft Teams To restore the accidentally deleted team channel, you may go to Manage team, click on Channels -> More -> Deleted Select the deleted team channel and click on Restore Change a channel name in Microsoft Teams Team owners and members can change the name of a channel by selecting the channel in the list, and then select More Channel options button > Edit Channel. If you don't see the option “Edit channel”, that means that a team owner has changed the permissions that members have. Also note that you cannot change the name of the General channel(the first named channel). The General channel can also be renamed from the Manage channel settings page by teams owners. General is a reserved string, and no new channels can be named General. The first-created channel in a new team will have the same description as the team by default. Refer to Microsoft community - Give a custom name to the General channel in Microsoft Teams", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 26}, {"topic": "Teams - Microsoft Teams - Built for hybrid work", "section": "Teams for Meetings", "paragraphs": ["Microsoft Teams is the standard tool for meetings with internal and external stakeholders at SAP. Experience audio and video-optimized state-of-the-art meetings with enhanced screen sharing quality and stability."], "content": "Microsoft Teams is the standard tool for meetings with internal and external stakeholders at SAP. Experience audio and video-optimized state-of-the-art meetings with enhanced screen sharing quality and stability.", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 27}, {"topic": "Teams - Microsoft Teams - Built for hybrid work", "section": "Teams Meeting limitation.", "paragraphs": ["Teams Meetings have a limit of 1,000 participants.", "Teams Live Events support up to 10,000 view-only participants."], "content": "Teams Meetings have a limit of 1,000 participants. Teams Live Events support up to 10,000 view-only participants.", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 28}, {"topic": "Teams - Microsoft Teams - Built for hybrid work", "section": "Can external participants outside SAP be invited t​​​o a Teams Meeting?", "paragraphs": ["Yes, you can invite participants outside SAP. They can join with the Teams client or the Teams web app which launches automatically if no client is present. They can also use the dial-in numbers in the invitation (Local numbers for the complete list) to join by phone."], "content": "Yes, you can invite participants outside SAP. They can join with the Teams client or the Teams web app which launches automatically if no client is present. They can also use the dial-in numbers in the invitation (Local numbers for the complete list) to join by phone.", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 29}, {"topic": "Teams - Microsoft Teams - Built for hybrid work", "section": "How to join a Teams meeting?", "paragraphs": ["Join Teams meetings anytime, anywhere, from any device.", "Teams meetings are best when you join them from the Teams app or Teams on the web, and there are a bunch of ways to do that—read on for details about joining by link, from your calendar, and more. If you cannot use the app or the web, some meetings let you call in using a phone number.", "Join by link", "Join from calendar or ID", "Join in a channel", "Join from chat", "Call in", "Connect to a room while you join", "More details you could find via Microsoft article - Join a meeting in Teams"], "content": "Join Teams meetings anytime, anywhere, from any device. Teams meetings are best when you join them from the Teams app or Teams on the web, and there are a bunch of ways to do that—read on for details about joining by link, from your calendar, and more. If you cannot use the app or the web, some meetings let you call in using a phone number. Join by link Join from calendar or ID Join in a channel Join from chat Call in Connect to a room while you join More details you could find via Microsoft article - Join a meeting in Teams", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 30}, {"topic": "Teams - Microsoft Teams - Built for hybrid work", "section": "Is it possible to schedule a Teams meeting for a ​manager?", "paragraphs": ["Yes, simply open the manager's calendar and schedule the meeting there. There are no additional permissions required; you only need the Outlook delegate permissions."], "content": "Yes, simply open the manager's calendar and schedule the meeting there. There are no additional permissions required; you only need the Outlook delegate permissions.", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 31}, {"topic": "Teams - Microsoft Teams - Built for hybrid work", "section": "Who can start and stop Teams recording?", "paragraphs": ["Anyone from SAP can start or stop a recording, even if the meeting organizer is not present. Also, you do not have to be the same person who started the recording to stop it.", "Person from another organization or company (federated users), or someone joined as Guest or Anonymous cannot start/stop recording."], "content": "Anyone from SAP can start or stop a recording, even if the meeting organizer is not present. Also, you do not have to be the same person who started the recording to stop it. Person from another organization or company (federated users), or someone joined as Guest or Anonymous cannot start/stop recording.", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 32}, {"topic": "Teams - Microsoft Teams - Built for hybrid work", "section": "Where is the recording saved and who has access to it?", "paragraphs": ["Please note that only the people who have joined the roster in the meeting will have access to the meeting recording without any action from the organizer or the one who has recorded it.", "There is a known limitation that if a Distribution List is invited, only 150 of the members are joining the meeting roster.", "Nested groups are not supported either.", "Refer to IKB0011156 - Microsoft Teams - Teams meeting FAQ Recording your meeting"], "content": "Please note that only the people who have joined the roster in the meeting will have access to the meeting recording without any action from the organizer or the one who has recorded it. There is a known limitation that if a Distribution List is invited, only 150 of the members are joining the meeting roster. Nested groups are not supported either. Refer to IKB0011156 - Microsoft Teams - Teams meeting FAQ Recording your meeting", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 33}, {"topic": "Teams - Microsoft Teams - Built for hybrid work", "section": "Retention Policy for Cloud Meeting Recordings", "paragraphs": ["It is implemented by applying a retention period of 90 days to all recordings for our main conferencing solutions Microsoft Teams and Zoom. For a quick overview, you can watch ours SAP WORX Knowledge Bite video.", "This policy is in alignment with best practices to reduce data storage at SAP and to remove so called “dark data” (e.g., unused and forgotten meeting recordings). It also adds significantly to SAP’s security and data protection efforts as well as to the company’s Green IT strategy by saving CO2 emissions through the reduction of data storage.", "Refer to IT for You - The Great Clean-up! New Policy for Cloud Meeting Recordings"], "content": "It is implemented by applying a retention period of 90 days to all recordings for our main conferencing solutions Microsoft Teams and Zoom. For a quick overview, you can watch ours SAP WORX Knowledge Bite video. This policy is in alignment with best practices to reduce data storage at SAP and to remove so called “dark data” (e.g., unused and forgotten meeting recordings). It also adds significantly to SAP’s security and data protection efforts as well as to the company’s Green IT strategy by saving CO2 emissions through the reduction of data storage. Refer to IT for You - The Great Clean-up! New Policy for Cloud Meeting Recordings", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 34}, {"topic": "Teams - Microsoft Teams - Built for hybrid work", "section": "How long can I extend the expiration date for Teams meeting recording?", "paragraphs": ["The expiration can be adjusted in the details pane of the recording file in OneDrive or SharePoint, and it can be set to 7, 30, 60 days, a specific date in the future or \"Remove expiration\" can be selected as well."], "content": "The expiration can be adjusted in the details pane of the recording file in OneDrive or SharePoint, and it can be set to 7, 30, 60 days, a specific date in the future or \"Remove expiration\" can be selected as well.", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 35}, {"topic": "Teams - Microsoft Teams - Built for hybrid work", "section": "What happens if it was forgotten to keep a recording?", "paragraphs": ["When the expiration date occurs and the recording is automatically deleted, an email like this will be received and it will provide the option to restore the recording if needed.", "Refer to IKB0013169 - FAQ for Retention Policy for Cloud Meeting Recordings"], "content": "When the expiration date occurs and the recording is automatically deleted, an email like this will be received and it will provide the option to restore the recording if needed. Refer to IKB0013169 - FAQ for Retention Policy for Cloud Meeting Recordings", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 36}, {"topic": "Teams - Microsoft Teams - Built for hybrid work", "section": "Teams Webinars feature", "paragraphs": ["A specific feature to handle webinars in Teams is available on demand (see below for further information on the request process). With the feature activated you can create Webinars in the Teams client. It does not imply further costs to the requester. Microsoft describes the feature in their Knowledge Base articles.", "How to activate Teams webinar feature?", "In order to activate the feature please use the UC Cockpit.", "Refer to KB - Microsoft Teams Meetings - Best Practice for Webinars"], "content": "A specific feature to handle webinars in Teams is available on demand (see below for further information on the request process). With the feature activated you can create Webinars in the Teams client. It does not imply further costs to the requester. Microsoft describes the feature in their Knowledge Base articles. How to activate Teams webinar feature? In order to activate the feature please use the UC Cockpit. Refer to KB - Microsoft Teams Meetings - Best Practice for Webinars", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 37}, {"topic": "Teams - Microsoft Teams - Built for hybrid work", "section": "Live transcript", "paragraphs": ["Enable the live transcript during your calls (or meetings) to better follow what's been said. If the language in the call is changed from English to another, you can simply adjust the language for the live transcript as well — no need to restart the transcript, it will simply continue in the new language."], "content": "Enable the live transcript during your calls (or meetings) to better follow what's been said. If the language in the call is changed from English to another, you can simply adjust the language for the live transcript as well — no need to restart the transcript, it will simply continue in the new language.", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 38}, {"topic": "Teams - Microsoft Teams - Built for hybrid work", "section": "Easy transfer to mobile app", "paragraphs": ["Sometimes a call or a meeting runs longer than anticipated. In these situations, it is often necessary to flexibly transfer the call to your mobile device. This can be done from within the call without the need to leave and dial back in. Your peers won't even notice you are gone, and you won't miss a word of what's been said!"], "content": "Sometimes a call or a meeting runs longer than anticipated. In these situations, it is often necessary to flexibly transfer the call to your mobile device. This can be done from within the call without the need to leave and dial back in. Your peers won't even notice you are gone, and you won't miss a word of what's been said!", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 39}, {"topic": "Teams - Microsoft Teams - Built for hybrid work", "section": "Delegation settings and call transfer", "paragraphs": ["Easily set up a call delegation and transfer calls to someone else. This can be set up so that you can either first consult with whomever you want to transfer the caller to, or you can simply transfer the call to the person whose delegate you are without a consultation first."], "content": "Easily set up a call delegation and transfer calls to someone else. This can be set up so that you can either first consult with whomever you want to transfer the caller to, or you can simply transfer the call to the person whose delegate you are without a consultation first.", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 40}, {"topic": "Teams - Microsoft Teams - Built for hybrid work", "section": "Voicemail", "paragraphs": ["Microsoft Teams Direct Calling offers a standard voicemail functionality that is enabled by default and can be configured in the Teams client (Settings / Calls).", "New voicemails are signaled ​​in the Teams Activity Feed, ​with a red dot on the Calls tab, and you will also receive an e-mail notification with the recording.", "Existing and new voicemails can be accessed on the Calls tab in the Teams client.", "Note: this is synchronized with the voicemails you received on Skype for Business, you can also access the Teams Direct Calling voicemails from your Skype for Business client accordingly.​", "You can adjust the settings for Voicemail in the Teams Client, Settings, Calls.", "You can configure Teams so that unanswered calls should go to Voicemail. If you select Do nothing, the calls will not be routed to voicemail. Under Configure Voicemail, you can adjust the greetings, answering rules, and even configure out of office greetings aligned with your Outlook settings!", "Refer to KB - Microsoft Teams – Calling – Voice Mail"], "content": "Microsoft Teams Direct Calling offers a standard voicemail functionality that is enabled by default and can be configured in the Teams client (Settings / Calls). New voicemails are signaled ​​in the Teams Activity Feed, ​with a red dot on the Calls tab, and you will also receive an e-mail notification with the recording. Existing and new voicemails can be accessed on the Calls tab in the Teams client. Note: this is synchronized with the voicemails you received on Skype for Business, you can also access the Teams Direct Calling voicemails from your Skype for Business client accordingly.​ You can adjust the settings for Voicemail in the Teams Client, Settings, Calls. You can configure Teams so that unanswered calls should go to Voicemail. If you select Do nothing, the calls will not be routed to voicemail. Under Configure Voicemail, you can adjust the greetings, answering rules, and even configure out of office greetings aligned with your Outlook settings! Refer to KB - Microsoft Teams – Calling – Voice Mail", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 41}, {"topic": "Teams - Microsoft Teams - Built for hybrid work", "section": "Teams for Chat", "paragraphs": ["Stay in the know! Use chat rather than lengthy E-Mail conversations with multiple recipients - get started with persistent group chats. With group chats in Microsoft Teams, you can easily keep track of a conversation, share the previous conversation with newly added members, and even share files.", "Persistent chat", "Profit from the persistent chats dedicated to your Teams meetings with easier follow-ups as the chat remains visible even after your meeting has ended and for as long as your meeting series lasts.", "Share files with cloud storage", "Any file you share within a chat is automatically stored in your OneDrive if you didn't share the link directly from cloud storage. You can make sure that all chat members work on the same file all the time - no duplication, less confusion!", "Engage with your peers using emojis and gifs", "Microsoft Teams Chat gives you plenty of options to engage with your colleagues in a light-hearted way by using built-in emojis and gifs. Share your joy about a successful project or underscore a joke with a wink-emoji.", "Find General information of Chat with below contents.", "Short comparison", "One-on-one chat", "Looking for a chat from the past?", "Group chat", "Leaving a group chat", "Edit/Delete a Sent Message", "Delete chat history", "Pop out chat", "FAQ"], "content": "Stay in the know! Use chat rather than lengthy E-Mail conversations with multiple recipients - get started with persistent group chats. With group chats in Microsoft Teams, you can easily keep track of a conversation, share the previous conversation with newly added members, and even share files. Persistent chat Profit from the persistent chats dedicated to your Teams meetings with easier follow-ups as the chat remains visible even after your meeting has ended and for as long as your meeting series lasts. Share files with cloud storage Any file you share within a chat is automatically stored in your OneDrive if you didn't share the link directly from cloud storage. You can make sure that all chat members work on the same file all the time - no duplication, less confusion! Engage with your peers using emojis and gifs Microsoft Teams Chat gives you plenty of options to engage with your colleagues in a light-hearted way by using built-in emojis and gifs. Share your joy about a successful project or underscore a joke with a wink-emoji. Find General information of Chat with below contents. Short comparison One-on-one chat Looking for a chat from the past? Group chat Leaving a group chat Edit/Delete a Sent Message Delete chat history Pop out chat FAQ", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 42}, {"topic": "Teams - Microsoft Teams - Built for hybrid work", "section": "Teams for Document Sharing", "paragraphs": ["Every team within Microsoft Teams comes with a separate SharePoint site allocated to it. This is where all the files from the Files tab within your Teams group's channels are stored. Everyone within the Teams group automatically has access to them.", "Separate SharePoint with every Teams group", "Every team within Microsoft Teams comes with a separate SharePoint site allocated to it. This is where all the files from the Files tab within your Teams group's channels are stored. Everyone within the Teams group automatically has access to them.", "Real-time collaboration within documents", "Benefit from the SharePoint cloud storage behind file storage in Teams and collaborate on files in real-time. Choose whether you want to work on your Microsoft 365 files within the Teams client, the browser version, or the desktop app.", "Additionally, you can even start a meeting from a document with your team members to collaborate there.", "Version history", "Due to the SharePoint storage allocated to each Teams group, you can benefit from the version history feature in the same way as with any other document stored on a separate SharePoint. Check who updated the document last, restore a previous version, and easily share your documents via link for better collaboration."], "content": "Every team within Microsoft Teams comes with a separate SharePoint site allocated to it. This is where all the files from the Files tab within your Teams group's channels are stored. Everyone within the Teams group automatically has access to them. Separate SharePoint with every Teams group Every team within Microsoft Teams comes with a separate SharePoint site allocated to it. This is where all the files from the Files tab within your Teams group's channels are stored. Everyone within the Teams group automatically has access to them. Real-time collaboration within documents Benefit from the SharePoint cloud storage behind file storage in Teams and collaborate on files in real-time. Choose whether you want to work on your Microsoft 365 files within the Teams client, the browser version, or the desktop app. Additionally, you can even start a meeting from a document with your team members to collaborate there. Version history Due to the SharePoint storage allocated to each Teams group, you can benefit from the version history feature in the same way as with any other document stored on a separate SharePoint. Check who updated the document last, restore a previous version, and easily share your documents via link for better collaboration.", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 43}, {"topic": "Teams - Microsoft Teams - Built for hybrid work", "section": "How to restore deleted files and folders", "paragraphs": ["Files restore for SharePoint and Microsoft Teams is a complete self-service recovery solution that allows site owners to restore files from any point in time during the last 30 days.", "Go to the channel where the files or folders have been deleted.", "​​In the Files tab, click on Open in SharePoint", "Click Recycle Bin in the Quick Launch bar on the left side of the screen.", "On the Recycle Bin page, click the box to the left of the files or folders you want to restore.", "Click Restore.", "Note: If you don’t see the item you’re looking for, and it was deleted recently, a site collection administrator might be able to restore it from the site collection recycle bin. If you're the site collection administrator, see Restore deleted items from the site collection recycle bin.", "Note: When an item is restored, it is restored to the same location that it was deleted from. Deleted items are retained in recycle bins for a certain period. For SharePoint Online, the retention time is 93 days. It begins when you delete the item from its original location. When you delete the item from the site recycle bin, it goes into the site collection recycle bin. It stays there for the remainder of the 93 days, and then is permanently deleted.", "Refer to IKB0011128 - Microsoft Teams - Files - Restore deleted files", "Microsoft Teams – Released Features as SAP - 2025"], "content": "Files restore for SharePoint and Microsoft Teams is a complete self-service recovery solution that allows site owners to restore files from any point in time during the last 30 days. Go to the channel where the files or folders have been deleted. ​​In the Files tab, click on Open in SharePoint Click Recycle Bin in the Quick Launch bar on the left side of the screen. On the Recycle Bin page, click the box to the left of the files or folders you want to restore. Click Restore. Note: If you don’t see the item you’re looking for, and it was deleted recently, a site collection administrator might be able to restore it from the site collection recycle bin. If you're the site collection administrator, see Restore deleted items from the site collection recycle bin. Note: When an item is restored, it is restored to the same location that it was deleted from. Deleted items are retained in recycle bins for a certain period. For SharePoint Online, the retention time is 93 days. It begins when you delete the item from its original location. When you delete the item from the site recycle bin, it goes into the site collection recycle bin. It stays there for the remainder of the 93 days, and then is permanently deleted. Refer to IKB0011128 - Microsoft Teams - Files - Restore deleted files Microsoft Teams – Released Features as SAP - 2025", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 44}, {"topic": "SharePoint & OneDrive", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["SharePoint Online is a web-based collaborative platform that integrates with Microsoft Office. SharePoint is primarily used as a document storage and management system, but the product is highly configurable and provides web pages which may be edited in-browser. You can build Intranet sites where you can format and customize your content to share information.", "SharePoint Online is your building block to perform advanced tasks and automation using Web parts and app parts, which are components that can be inserted into pages to tailor your Team Site. Some of the more advanced apps available are Planner, Power Automate (Flow) and PowerApps.", "OneDrive allows users to store files and personal data in the cloud, share files, and sync files across Android, Windows Phone, and iOS mobile devices, Windows and macOS computers. Users can upload Microsoft Office documents directly to OneDrive. It can be used for sharing files and concurrent co-editing (several users can edit the same document at the same time).", "SharePoint and OneDrive use the same underlying Microsoft technology. The main difference is that OneDrive is for personal use, whereas SharePoint is made for teams."], "content": "SharePoint Online is a web-based collaborative platform that integrates with Microsoft Office. SharePoint is primarily used as a document storage and management system, but the product is highly configurable and provides web pages which may be edited in-browser. You can build Intranet sites where you can format and customize your content to share information. SharePoint Online is your building block to perform advanced tasks and automation using Web parts and app parts, which are components that can be inserted into pages to tailor your Team Site. Some of the more advanced apps available are Planner, Power Automate (Flow) and PowerApps. OneDrive allows users to store files and personal data in the cloud, share files, and sync files across Android, Windows Phone, and iOS mobile devices, Windows and macOS computers. Users can upload Microsoft Office documents directly to OneDrive. It can be used for sharing files and concurrent co-editing (several users can edit the same document at the same time). SharePoint and OneDrive use the same underlying Microsoft technology. The main difference is that OneDrive is for personal use, whereas SharePoint is made for teams.", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 45}, {"topic": "SharePoint & OneDrive", "section": "Microsoft SharePoint - Create a new SharePoint site", "paragraphs": ["You can create a Site in SharePoint Online by the SharePoint self-service portal tool - Navigator", "You will be asked for the following details:", "A title, responsible users, a cost center and your preferred site template. An initial quota (capacity) is 1 TB for all new sites (it can be changed by administrators later if needed).", "Details about Administrators: add min 2 (max 6) user IDs. Responsible users will be allowed to manage/delete the site in the self-service portal, and they will be added to Owners group in the SharePoint Online. The creator is added to responsible users automatically.", "Details about cost center: the cost center manager is the information owner of all data stored in the site -> every site must be assigned to a valid Cost center. There is no cross charging involved for SharePoint Sites.", "The following templates are available:", "Document Library to use the Site only to share documents. The other template includes a Document Library as well.", "Classic Team site to quickly create, organize, and share information for your team. The site also includes Notebook, Discussion Board (Newsfeed) and a Document Library.", "Project site to provide an easy way to manage projects. It contains the same apps as the Team site plus additional ones: Tasks, Calendar and the Projects summary web part that is connected to the default Task list.", "Modern Team site (modern experience) to integrate with Office 365 groups and associated Office 365 apps.", "Communication Site (modern experience) to integrate web parts - to share information with others in a visually compelling format.", "Project Web App, known as Microsoft Project Online (is licensed).", "When you create a Classic Team site from the 'Team Site' template, web parts for Announcements, Calendar, and Links are automatically added to the home page, while on a modern site, you get a section for News, Quick links, Site activity, and a Document library. More details about differences between classic and modern experiences: here", "You cannot change from one template to another after creation.", "To change SharePoint name, please go to SharePoint self-service portal tool - Navigator to change the name that you are the owner."], "content": "You can create a Site in SharePoint Online by the SharePoint self-service portal tool - Navigator You will be asked for the following details: A title, responsible users, a cost center and your preferred site template. An initial quota (capacity) is 1 TB for all new sites (it can be changed by administrators later if needed). Details about Administrators: add min 2 (max 6) user IDs. Responsible users will be allowed to manage/delete the site in the self-service portal, and they will be added to Owners group in the SharePoint Online. The creator is added to responsible users automatically. Details about cost center: the cost center manager is the information owner of all data stored in the site -> every site must be assigned to a valid Cost center. There is no cross charging involved for SharePoint Sites. The following templates are available: Document Library to use the Site only to share documents. The other template includes a Document Library as well. Classic Team site to quickly create, organize, and share information for your team. The site also includes Notebook, Discussion Board (Newsfeed) and a Document Library. Project site to provide an easy way to manage projects. It contains the same apps as the Team site plus additional ones: Tasks, Calendar and the Projects summary web part that is connected to the default Task list. Modern Team site (modern experience) to integrate with Office 365 groups and associated Office 365 apps. Communication Site (modern experience) to integrate web parts - to share information with others in a visually compelling format. Project Web App, known as Microsoft Project Online (is licensed). When you create a Classic Team site from the 'Team Site' template, web parts for Announcements, Calendar, and Links are automatically added to the home page, while on a modern site, you get a section for News, Quick links, Site activity, and a Document library. More details about differences between classic and modern experiences: here You cannot change from one template to another after creation. To change SharePoint name, please go to SharePoint self-service portal tool - Navigator to change the name that you are the owner.", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 46}, {"topic": "SharePoint & OneDrive", "section": "Microsoft SharePoint – Sharing", "paragraphs": ["How to setup sharing and permissions of files and folders", "The permissions must be set for the Site Collection. In SAP standard all the necessary permission is given for the One Drive for Business. For Share Point Online there is an additional request necessary to allow external sharing."], "content": "How to setup sharing and permissions of files and folders The permissions must be set for the Site Collection. In SAP standard all the necessary permission is given for the One Drive for Business. For Share Point Online there is an additional request necessary to allow external sharing.", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 47}, {"topic": "SharePoint & OneDrive", "section": "Step-by-step Instructions to setup sharing and permissions for files and folders", "paragraphs": ["Step 1) In the top bar on a document library select Share.", "There are 3 different ways to share files or folders", "1. People in SAP SE:", "Gives access to everyone in your organization to the link, whether they receive it directly from you or forwarded from someone else.", "The users get specified are only the users that get an email with the link", "2. People with existing access:", "Only send the existing link to the users that already have the permission", "3. People you choose:", "Only specific people identified by their email address and using authenticated access", "Step 2) By default, Send Link is selected with option People you choose, after clicking on Apply, you can enter username or mail address for the uses, and you can set the access permission. It should be the preferred solution and works with SAP internal people as well as external people.", "Refer to KB0887701 - Microsoft SharePoint - How to Share Files and Folders with all of SAP"], "content": "Step 1) In the top bar on a document library select Share. There are 3 different ways to share files or folders 1. People in SAP SE: Gives access to everyone in your organization to the link, whether they receive it directly from you or forwarded from someone else. The users get specified are only the users that get an email with the link 2. People with existing access: Only send the existing link to the users that already have the permission 3. People you choose: Only specific people identified by their email address and using authenticated access Step 2) By default, Send Link is selected with option People you choose, after clicking on Apply, you can enter username or mail address for the uses, and you can set the access permission. It should be the preferred solution and works with SAP internal people as well as external people. Refer to KB0887701 - Microsoft SharePoint - How to Share Files and Folders with all of SAP", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 48}, {"topic": "SharePoint & OneDrive", "section": "Step-by-step Instructions to setup external sharing and permissions for files and folders", "paragraphs": ["The way external sharing with specific people works, depends on the status of these external people:", "1. Enterprise:", "They are members of another Office 365 tenant.", "They authenticate against their own tenant and can access the link directly, like SAP employees could do.", "2. Consumer with MS mail:", "They have a consumer/live account assigned to their email address, and the email address is hosted on a Microsoft service (outlook.com, live.com, hotmail.com etc.)", "They authenticate against live.com and can access the link directly.", "3. Consumer with private mail domain:", "They have a consumer/live account assigned to their email address, and the email address is hosted on a private service (myname.com, anydomain.com).", "They cannot use the link. In this case they need to provide an email address which is not assigned to any Microsoft consumer account.", "4. Generic email address, no assignment to any Microsoft service:", "They have to authenticate using the email address which was used for sharing and a one-time passcode sent to the same email address. Using this way, it is at least checked that the person who wants to use the link does have access to the related mailbox. It cannot check the security standard of that mailbox, so e.g. if a mailbox is used by multiple people, the link access is not limited to a specific person but to the group of people who have access to the mailbox.", "Example for one-time code authentication:", "Step 1) Select the file or folder you want to share, and then select Share.", "Step 2) Select People you choose, click on Apply", "Enter user name or mail address that you want to share, set the share permission (Can edit, Can view, Can’t download), then click on Send.", "External users will receive invitation mail to access the shared file or folder.", "Refer to IKB0010361 - Microsoft SharePoint - External sharing of SharePoint files or folders", "Additional Information for the \"Anyone\" Option", "The option \"Anyone\", has being disabled in SAP. The reasons behind this are shared in this knowledge article. This option creates an anonymous accessible link, will show an expiration date. The default is 10 days and maximum possible time range is 90 days.", "Keep in mind that such link can be used, distributed by mail or posted somewhere by anybody who just has the link/URL. There is also a “set password” option - When a user clicks the link, they will be prompted to enter a password before they can access the file. You'll need to provide this password separately to users. ​ This means such links are a risk and should be used only if no other option is possible.", "Refer to KB0887752 - How to share files with external users without authentication"], "content": "The way external sharing with specific people works, depends on the status of these external people: 1. Enterprise: They are members of another Office 365 tenant. They authenticate against their own tenant and can access the link directly, like SAP employees could do. 2. Consumer with MS mail: They have a consumer/live account assigned to their email address, and the email address is hosted on a Microsoft service (outlook.com, live.com, hotmail.com etc.) They authenticate against live.com and can access the link directly. 3. Consumer with private mail domain: They have a consumer/live account assigned to their email address, and the email address is hosted on a private service (myname.com, anydomain.com). They cannot use the link. In this case they need to provide an email address which is not assigned to any Microsoft consumer account. 4. Generic email address, no assignment to any Microsoft service: They have to authenticate using the email address which was used for sharing and a one-time passcode sent to the same email address. Using this way, it is at least checked that the person who wants to use the link does have access to the related mailbox. It cannot check the security standard of that mailbox, so e.g. if a mailbox is used by multiple people, the link access is not limited to a specific person but to the group of people who have access to the mailbox. Example for one-time code authentication: Step 1) Select the file or folder you want to share, and then select Share. Step 2) Select People you choose, click on Apply Enter user name or mail address that you want to share, set the share permission (Can edit, Can view, Can’t download), then click on Send. External users will receive invitation mail to access the shared file or folder. Refer to IKB0010361 - Microsoft SharePoint - External sharing of SharePoint files or folders Additional Information for the \"Anyone\" Option The option \"Anyone\", has being disabled in SAP. The reasons behind this are shared in this knowledge article. This option creates an anonymous accessible link, will show an expiration date. The default is 10 days and maximum possible time range is 90 days. Keep in mind that such link can be used, distributed by mail or posted somewhere by anybody who just has the link/URL. There is also a “set password” option - When a user clicks the link, they will be prompted to enter a password before they can access the file. You'll need to provide this password separately to users. ​ This means such links are a risk and should be used only if no other option is possible. Refer to KB0887752 - How to share files with external users without authentication", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 49}, {"topic": "SharePoint & OneDrive", "section": "File Size and File Count", "paragraphs": ["There's a 250-gigabyte (GB) file size limit for each file that's uploaded. Technically, OneDrive for Business has a limit of 30 million documents in total and 5.000 files per folder and 3 TB of space per user.", "Note: You might be unable to sync files to a device if the data to be synced is greater than the free space on your device. You may define which folders are synchronized to a device following the instructions in the First Steps: Get started with OneDrive... for your device.", "Note: Recent document versions also count into your 3 TB of space in OneDrive. In case you have twenty versions of a 20 MB file, it will use 400 MB of your storage quota. Also, the recycle bin counts into your quota, deleted files disappear from there automatically 93 days after deletion. The quota can be extended on request.", "Note: If you upload large files to OneDrive, they will be downloaded to synchronized folders on your other devices. Also, if colleagues chose to synchronize a shared folder, they would receive the files. This may lead to unexpected download activities."], "content": "There's a 250-gigabyte (GB) file size limit for each file that's uploaded. Technically, OneDrive for Business has a limit of 30 million documents in total and 5.000 files per folder and 3 TB of space per user. Note: You might be unable to sync files to a device if the data to be synced is greater than the free space on your device. You may define which folders are synchronized to a device following the instructions in the First Steps: Get started with OneDrive... for your device. Note: Recent document versions also count into your 3 TB of space in OneDrive. In case you have twenty versions of a 20 MB file, it will use 400 MB of your storage quota. Also, the recycle bin counts into your quota, deleted files disappear from there automatically 93 days after deletion. The quota can be extended on request. Note: If you upload large files to OneDrive, they will be downloaded to synchronized folders on your other devices. Also, if colleagues chose to synchronize a shared folder, they would receive the files. This may lead to unexpected download activities.", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 50}, {"topic": "SharePoint & OneDrive", "section": "Naming Conventions", "paragraphs": ["However, there are other limits on viewing by using the web that may limit how you structure your files in OneDrive.", "File names including the paths and the extension are limited in length and some characters aren't supported in the file names when you sync.", "Unsupported characters: <, >, \", |,?, *, /, \\", "Maximum combined path and file name length on the web-interface: ~ 300 characters (in reality it's 400 characters minus the domain name, full path, and your e-mail address)", "Maximum path length on Windows Explorer: 247 characters counting from the root directory of your file system for folders, plus 12 more characters for files. This is a limitation in Windows Explorer.", "Maximum combined path and file name length in Excel: 218 characters, as Excel limits links to other worksheets to max. 218 characters for the Excel filename plus max. 31 for the worksheet name plus cell reference information. There is also a file size limitation of 10 MB to edit Excel files from OneDrive in Excel Online (read more). Both are limitations in Excel.", "Refer to IKB0010485 - Microsoft OneDrive - What are the limits for files folders and links"], "content": "However, there are other limits on viewing by using the web that may limit how you structure your files in OneDrive. File names including the paths and the extension are limited in length and some characters aren't supported in the file names when you sync. Unsupported characters: <, >, \", |,?, *, /, \\ Maximum combined path and file name length on the web-interface: ~ 300 characters (in reality it's 400 characters minus the domain name, full path, and your e-mail address) Maximum path length on Windows Explorer: 247 characters counting from the root directory of your file system for folders, plus 12 more characters for files. This is a limitation in Windows Explorer. Maximum combined path and file name length in Excel: 218 characters, as Excel limits links to other worksheets to max. 218 characters for the Excel filename plus max. 31 for the worksheet name plus cell reference information. There is also a file size limitation of 10 MB to edit Excel files from OneDrive in Excel Online (read more). Both are limitations in Excel. Refer to IKB0010485 - Microsoft OneDrive - What are the limits for files folders and links", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 51}, {"topic": "SharePoint & OneDrive", "section": "Microsoft OneDrive - How to set automatic backup for OneDrive Windows client", "paragraphs": ["You can back up your important folders (your Desktop, Documents, Music, Pictures, and Video folders) on your device with OneDrive folder backup, so they're protected and available on other devices.", "Open OneDrive Settings", "Go to the Sync and Back tab", "Select Manage back up", "Select folder you need to backup"], "content": "You can back up your important folders (your Desktop, Documents, Music, Pictures, and Video folders) on your device with OneDrive folder backup, so they're protected and available on other devices. Open OneDrive Settings Go to the Sync and Back tab Select Manage back up Select folder you need to backup", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 52}, {"topic": "SharePoint & OneDrive", "section": "Microsoft OneDrive - Recovering Deleted Files from OneDrive", "paragraphs": ["Any files that have been stored in OneDrive which were removed and/or deleted will be held in the OneDrive recycling bin for 90 days, then after that they will go to the secondary bin for further potential recovery. Though please note any files that have not first been successfully sync'd to OneDrive will not appear in these locations if deleted or removed. Other missing files may still be on your computer in other folders, however if anything has been deleted from your system directly and from the Windows recycling bin cannot be recovered unless there was a copy successfully synced to OneDrive. SAP does not have any tools for file recovery, only OneDrive recycling bin would be closest file recovery option."], "content": "Any files that have been stored in OneDrive which were removed and/or deleted will be held in the OneDrive recycling bin for 90 days, then after that they will go to the secondary bin for further potential recovery. Though please note any files that have not first been successfully sync'd to OneDrive will not appear in these locations if deleted or removed. Other missing files may still be on your computer in other folders, however if anything has been deleted from your system directly and from the Windows recycling bin cannot be recovered unless there was a copy successfully synced to OneDrive. SAP does not have any tools for file recovery, only OneDrive recycling bin would be closest file recovery option.", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 53}, {"topic": "SharePoint & OneDrive", "section": "You can recover your files for OneDrive using the following steps", "paragraphs": ["Open the OneDrive application (from the system tray)", "click view online.", "Or go directly to https://sap-my.sharepoint.com.", "Go to your Recycling bin.", "Find the files and simply recover them", "Check if the missing files are there, if they are you can simply recover them.", "If you do not see the restore button below, please ensure that you have selected the files you want to recover first.", "If this still does not work, please then test in another browser.", "If the files not in recycling bin, go to the secondary stage recycle bin.", "Check if the missing files are there, if they are you can simply recover them.", "If not in the secondary bin you can check your local system and move them to OneDrive.", "If there are no files in your folders, check your windows recycling bin and restore from there.", "If there are no files in your recovery bin, then unfortunately there is no other means to recover your files."], "content": "Open the OneDrive application (from the system tray) click view online. Or go directly to https://sap-my.sharepoint.com. Go to your Recycling bin. Find the files and simply recover them Check if the missing files are there, if they are you can simply recover them. If you do not see the restore button below, please ensure that you have selected the files you want to recover first. If this still does not work, please then test in another browser. If the files not in recycling bin, go to the secondary stage recycle bin. Check if the missing files are there, if they are you can simply recover them. If not in the secondary bin you can check your local system and move them to OneDrive. If there are no files in your folders, check your windows recycling bin and restore from there. If there are no files in your recovery bin, then unfortunately there is no other means to recover your files.", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 54}, {"topic": "SharePoint & OneDrive", "section": "Restore this library", "paragraphs": ["This feature allows you to restore an entire shared document library to a previous time. The restore will undo all the actions that occurred on both files and folders in the last 30 days. You cannot select single files or actions - it works like \"undo all actions before xx amount of time\"", "This applies for deleted, infected, corrupted and/or overwritten files.", "Keep in mind that while it provides a history-like list of changes made to the files, it will only display deleted files that are in the recycle bin (e.g. if you haven't found your deleted file in the Recycle bin, you will unlikely find it with this feature as well; instead, try looking in the Second Stage Recycle bin). This means that deleted files can’t be restored after they’ve been removed from the site collection recycle bin - either by manual delete or by emptying the recycle bin.", "Restoring files uses version history and the recycle bin. When version history is turned off, you won’t be able to restore files to a previous version.", "Keep in mind that this feature requires site admin permission (Site Collection Administrator). By default, users are admins of their personal OneDrive, but owners of SharePoint Online sites aren't by default site admins (can become by creating an IT ticket).", "Please note if you have deleted a large number of files and you try to scroll down to the earliest, you might experience performance issues, because of the default item threshold limit in SharePoint Online for displaying more than 5000 items at once.", "In order to use the feature:", "Navigate to the SharePoint document library you'd like to restore. (You can use that for OneDrive as well - to do so, you need to open OneDrive in the browser):", "Select Settings (cogwheel/gear button on top right) > Restore this library.", "On the Restore page, select a date from the dropdown list, such as Yesterday, or select Custom date and time.", "Use the activity chart and activity feed to review the recent activities that you want to undo.", "The daily activity chart shows the volume of file activities in each day for the last 30 days. It gives you an overview of what has happened to your library over time and can help you identify any unusual activities, such as when your files were infected by malware.", "The activity feed shows individual file and folder operations in reverse chronological order. You can scroll down to see previous days or move the slider below the daily activity chart to quickly move to a specific day.", "If you're selecting a custom date and time, select the earliest activity that you want to undo. When you select an activity, all other activities that occurred after that are selected automatically.", "When you’re ready to restore your library, select Restore to undo all the activities you selected. The time it takes to perform the restoration depends on the number of the actions you chose to undo.", "Your library will be restored to the state it was in before the first activity you selected. If you change your mind about the restore you just did, you can select Restore this library to undo the restore by selecting the restore action you just did.", "Refer to IKB0010994 - Microsoft OneDrive - Recovering Deleted Files From OneDrive"], "content": "This feature allows you to restore an entire shared document library to a previous time. The restore will undo all the actions that occurred on both files and folders in the last 30 days. You cannot select single files or actions - it works like \"undo all actions before xx amount of time\" This applies for deleted, infected, corrupted and/or overwritten files. Keep in mind that while it provides a history-like list of changes made to the files, it will only display deleted files that are in the recycle bin (e.g. if you haven't found your deleted file in the Recycle bin, you will unlikely find it with this feature as well; instead, try looking in the Second Stage Recycle bin). This means that deleted files can’t be restored after they’ve been removed from the site collection recycle bin - either by manual delete or by emptying the recycle bin. Restoring files uses version history and the recycle bin. When version history is turned off, you won’t be able to restore files to a previous version. Keep in mind that this feature requires site admin permission (Site Collection Administrator). By default, users are admins of their personal OneDrive, but owners of SharePoint Online sites aren't by default site admins (can become by creating an IT ticket). Please note if you have deleted a large number of files and you try to scroll down to the earliest, you might experience performance issues, because of the default item threshold limit in SharePoint Online for displaying more than 5000 items at once. In order to use the feature: Navigate to the SharePoint document library you'd like to restore. (You can use that for OneDrive as well - to do so, you need to open OneDrive in the browser): Select Settings (cogwheel/gear button on top right) > Restore this library. On the Restore page, select a date from the dropdown list, such as Yesterday, or select Custom date and time. Use the activity chart and activity feed to review the recent activities that you want to undo. The daily activity chart shows the volume of file activities in each day for the last 30 days. It gives you an overview of what has happened to your library over time and can help you identify any unusual activities, such as when your files were infected by malware. The activity feed shows individual file and folder operations in reverse chronological order. You can scroll down to see previous days or move the slider below the daily activity chart to quickly move to a specific day. If you're selecting a custom date and time, select the earliest activity that you want to undo. When you select an activity, all other activities that occurred after that are selected automatically. When you’re ready to restore your library, select Restore to undo all the activities you selected. The time it takes to perform the restoration depends on the number of the actions you chose to undo. Your library will be restored to the state it was in before the first activity you selected. If you change your mind about the restore you just did, you can select Restore this library to undo the restore by selecting the restore action you just did. Refer to IKB0010994 - Microsoft OneDrive - Recovering Deleted Files From OneDrive", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 55}, {"topic": "SharePoint & OneDrive", "section": "How to Sync SharePoint/OneDrive folders to user’s PC", "paragraphs": ["This Guide can be used for syncing SharePoint sites and OneDrive folders that have been shared to you by your colleagues.", "Once added the folders will show under SAP SE in File Explorer (OneDrive - Shared Libraries - SAP SE for Finder on MacOS", "User must have OneDrive client is installed, then open SharePoint documents library or OneDrive folder then click on Sync.", "Open your SharePoint site Documents Library or a colleagues Shared OneDrive folder", "Click on Sync", "Select which folders / files you want to sync", "Click on Start Sync", "You will now find the SharePoint Documents Library listed under \"SAP SE\" in File Explorer", "MacOS: Listed under \"OneDrive - Shared Libraries - SAP SE\" in Finder", "If you want to open the SharePoint Library in a browser, Right-click > View Online"], "content": "This Guide can be used for syncing SharePoint sites and OneDrive folders that have been shared to you by your colleagues. Once added the folders will show under SAP SE in File Explorer (OneDrive - Shared Libraries - SAP SE for Finder on MacOS User must have OneDrive client is installed, then open SharePoint documents library or OneDrive folder then click on Sync. Open your SharePoint site Documents Library or a colleagues Shared OneDrive folder Click on Sync Select which folders / files you want to sync Click on Start Sync You will now find the SharePoint Documents Library listed under \"SAP SE\" in File Explorer MacOS: Listed under \"OneDrive - Shared Libraries - SAP SE\" in Finder If you want to open the SharePoint Library in a browser, Right-click > View Online", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 56}, {"topic": "SharePoint & OneDrive", "section": "Manage/Remove SharePoint and OneDrive Folders/files you have synced", "paragraphs": ["Right-click the OneDrive icon in your system tray (bottom right) > Open Settings", "MacOS: Right-click OneDrive icon in top bar > Open Preferences", "Select the Account tab and you will see a list of locations you are syncing, including your own OneDrive folder", "Use \"Choose folders\" to pick which folders inside the synced location to sync", "Use \"Stop sync\" to remove the sync.", "The local versions of the files will be leftover in your file explorer/finder, but any changes to them will no longer be uploaded to the server version in SharePoint Online.", "Once the sync is removed you can safely delete the folder from SAP SE without affecting the SharePoint site."], "content": "Right-click the OneDrive icon in your system tray (bottom right) > Open Settings MacOS: Right-click OneDrive icon in top bar > Open Preferences Select the Account tab and you will see a list of locations you are syncing, including your own OneDrive folder Use \"Choose folders\" to pick which folders inside the synced location to sync Use \"Stop sync\" to remove the sync. The local versions of the files will be leftover in your file explorer/finder, but any changes to them will no longer be uploaded to the server version in SharePoint Online. Once the sync is removed you can safely delete the folder from SAP SE without affecting the SharePoint site.", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 57}, {"topic": "SharePoint & OneDrive", "section": "Save Storage Space by using Files On-Demand Feature", "paragraphs": ["With the Files On-Demand function, you can see all your cloud files as if they were on your local hard drive.", "To save space on your disk, you can define which files are permanently synchronized to your disk - other files will be downloaded from the cloud only when you access them.", "OneDrive Files On-Demand helps you access all the files in your cloud storage in OneDrive without having to download them and use storage space on your computer.", "When you turn on Files On-Demand, you’ll still see all your files as online-only files in File Explorer, but they won't take up space. When you’re connected to the Internet, you’ll be able to use the files like every other file on your device.", "Starting with OneDrive build 23.066 Files On-Demand is enabled by default for all users", "Right click on OneDrive icon on the taskbar -> Settings, at Sync and Backup tab, click on advanced settings."], "content": "With the Files On-Demand function, you can see all your cloud files as if they were on your local hard drive. To save space on your disk, you can define which files are permanently synchronized to your disk - other files will be downloaded from the cloud only when you access them. OneDrive Files On-Demand helps you access all the files in your cloud storage in OneDrive without having to download them and use storage space on your computer. When you turn on Files On-Demand, you’ll still see all your files as online-only files in File Explorer, but they won't take up space. When you’re connected to the Internet, you’ll be able to use the files like every other file on your device. Starting with OneDrive build 23.066 Files On-Demand is enabled by default for all users Right click on OneDrive icon on the taskbar -> Settings, at Sync and Backup tab, click on advanced settings.", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 58}, {"topic": "SharePoint & OneDrive", "section": "How to disable sync for a SharePoint site", "paragraphs": ["Microsoft SharePoint files are usually available to sync to a folder on your computer. In some cases, you may want to prevent people from using a sync app with a site or library.", "To restrict syncing of all document libraries within a site, only the site administrator is authorized to perform the following steps:", "On the site, click Settings > Site Settings.", "Under Search, click Search and offline availability.", "In the Offline Client Availability section, select No."], "content": "Microsoft SharePoint files are usually available to sync to a folder on your computer. In some cases, you may want to prevent people from using a sync app with a site or library. To restrict syncing of all document libraries within a site, only the site administrator is authorized to perform the following steps: On the site, click Settings > Site Settings. Under Search, click Search and offline availability. In the Offline Client Availability section, select No.", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 59}, {"topic": "SharePoint & OneDrive", "section": "Navigator", "paragraphs": ["Navigator helps you control your Microsoft 365 experience. With it, you can create new collaborative spaces, manage existing experiences and, if you’re uncertain of which tool you need, get recommendations for the best solutions for you and your team,", "For detail, please check from IT for You Navigator site", "https://sap.sharepoint.com/sites/ITforYou/SitePages/Navigator.aspx", "More Useful Information", "IKB0012928 - Microsoft SharePoint/OneDrive - Sync SharePoint/Shared OneDrive folders to File Explorer/Finder", "IKB0012930 - Navigator FAQ", "IKB0011940 - Microsoft SharePoint - Getting Started", "IKB0010547 - Microsoft OneDrive - Getting Started", "Microsoft article - Save disk space with OneDrive Files On-Demand for Windows"], "content": "Navigator helps you control your Microsoft 365 experience. With it, you can create new collaborative spaces, manage existing experiences and, if you’re uncertain of which tool you need, get recommendations for the best solutions for you and your team, For detail, please check from IT for You Navigator site https://sap.sharepoint.com/sites/ITforYou/SitePages/Navigator.aspx More Useful Information IKB0012928 - Microsoft SharePoint/OneDrive - Sync SharePoint/Shared OneDrive folders to File Explorer/Finder IKB0012930 - Navigator FAQ IKB0011940 - Microsoft SharePoint - Getting Started IKB0010547 - Microsoft OneDrive - Getting Started Microsoft article - Save disk space with OneDrive Files On-Demand for Windows", "source": "Cloud Collaboration", "id": 60}, {"topic": "", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["ONE Support", "Internal- SAP Only", "Version control", "If you find any content in this document is out of date, feel free to contact the Authors for feedback!", "Thanks for your cooperation in advance!"], "content": "ONE Support Internal- SAP Only Version control If you find any content in this document is out of date, feel free to contact the Authors for feedback! Thanks for your cooperation in advance!", "source": "Core Technologies", "id": 61}, {"topic": "Exchange & Outlook", "section": "1.1 Exchange Online Limits", "paragraphs": ["With Exchange Online there is a full list of limits available that provides guidelines for users. You will find below some of the key points and associated limits set in Exchange Online that we are frequently asked about.", "Important: SAP uses an Office 365 Enterprise E5 License.", "User Mailbox Storage Limits", "Mailbox Storage Warning Alerts", "Employee mailbox quota", "Warning 98 GB", "Send limit 99 GB", "Receive limit 100 GB", "Receiving Email Limits", "Sending Email Limits", "Recipient Rate Limit: To discourage the delivery of unsolicited bulk messages, Exchange Online has recipient limits that prevent users and applications from sending large volumes of email. These limits are applied per-user to all outbound and internal messages.", "Recipient Limit: This is the maximum number of recipients allowed in the To:, Cc:, and Bcc: fields for a single email message.", "Message Rate Limit: Message rate limits determine how many messages a user can send from their Exchange Online account within a specified period of time.", "Email Retention Limits", "These limits control the length of time that items in specific folders in the Inbox can be accessed.", "Deleted Items folder retention period: The maximum number of days that items can remain in the Deleted Items folder before they're automatically removed.", "Retention period for items removed from the Deleted Items folder: The maximum numbers of days that items removed from the Deleted Items folder are retained before they're permanently deleted.", "Refer to IKB0010550 - Exchange Online Limits"], "content": "With Exchange Online there is a full list of limits available that provides guidelines for users. You will find below some of the key points and associated limits set in Exchange Online that we are frequently asked about. Important: SAP uses an Office 365 Enterprise E5 License. User Mailbox Storage Limits Mailbox Storage Warning Alerts Employee mailbox quota Warning 98 GB Send limit 99 GB Receive limit 100 GB Receiving Email Limits Sending Email Limits Recipient Rate Limit: To discourage the delivery of unsolicited bulk messages, Exchange Online has recipient limits that prevent users and applications from sending large volumes of email. These limits are applied per-user to all outbound and internal messages. Recipient Limit: This is the maximum number of recipients allowed in the To:, Cc:, and Bcc: fields for a single email message. Message Rate Limit: Message rate limits determine how many messages a user can send from their Exchange Online account within a specified period of time. Email Retention Limits These limits control the length of time that items in specific folders in the Inbox can be accessed. Deleted Items folder retention period: The maximum number of days that items can remain in the Deleted Items folder before they're automatically removed. Retention period for items removed from the Deleted Items folder: The maximum numbers of days that items removed from the Deleted Items folder are retained before they're permanently deleted. Refer to IKB0010550 - Exchange Online Limits", "source": "Core Technologies", "id": 62}, {"topic": "Exchange & Outlook", "section": "1.2 Email attachment", "paragraphs": ["To address the increased risk of attacks, SAP Global Security (SGS) has requested that certain file types get blocked. Additionally, McAfee also applies specific algorithms and policies to block certain file types and attachment types.", "See below for a list of blocked file extensions. This list is subject to change by Security (SGS).", "Blocked File Types", "Depending on the mail being sent to internal or external recipients, if the email contains any of the blocked file types listed below, the sender will be notified via a non-deliverable report from SAP Postmaster.", "Recipient is Internal - below attachments are not permitted from internal or external senders.", "Recipient is External - the email is not blocked by SAP.", "Blocked File Types are:", ".386, .ace, .acm, .acv, .ade, .adp, .adt, .ani, .app, .arc, .arj, .asd, .asp, .avb, .ax, .bas, .bat, .boo, .btm, .cab, .cbt, .cdr, .cer, .chm, .cla, .cmd, .cnv, .com, .cpl, .crt, .csc, .csh, .dll, .docm, .drv, .dvb, .email, .eml, .exe, .fon, .fxp, .gms, .gvb, .hlp, .ht, .hta, .htlp, .htt, .inf, .ini, .ins, .iqy, .iso, .isp, .its, .jar, .job, .js, .jse, .ksh, .lib, .lnk, .maf, .mam, .maq, .mar, .mat, .mau, .mav, .maw, .mch, .mda, .mdb, .mde, .mdt, .mdw, .mdz, .mht, .mhtm, .mhtml, .mpd, .mpt, .msc, .msi, .mso, .msp, .mst, .nws, .obd, .obj, .obt, .obz, .ocx, .ops, .ovl, .ovr, .pcd, .pci, .perl, .pgm, .pif, .pl, .pot, .prf, .prg, .ps1, .pub, .pwz, .qpw, .reg, .rtf, .sbf, .scf, .scr, .sct, .sfx, .sh, .shb, .shs, .shtml, .shw, .smm, .svg, .swf, .sys, .td0, .tlb, .tmp, .torrent, .tsk, .tsp, .tt6, .url, .vb, .vbe, .vbs, .vbx, .vom, .vsmacro, .vss, .vst, .vsw, .vwp, .vxd, .vxe, .wbk, .wbt, .wIz, .wk, .wmf, .wml, .wms, .wpc, .wpd, .ws, .wsc, .wsf, .wsh, .xlsm", "NOTE: The blocked file types are subject to change upon direction from SGS.", "Workarounds", "As an alternative to sending the blocked attachment via email please use one the following options:", "- OneDrive/SharePoint", "Additional information", "Email Attachment Limits", "Internal 35MB", "External 25MB", "Refer to IKB0012488 - Exchange Online - Attachment Blocking"], "content": "To address the increased risk of attacks, SAP Global Security (SGS) has requested that certain file types get blocked. Additionally, McAfee also applies specific algorithms and policies to block certain file types and attachment types. See below for a list of blocked file extensions. This list is subject to change by Security (SGS). Blocked File Types Depending on the mail being sent to internal or external recipients, if the email contains any of the blocked file types listed below, the sender will be notified via a non-deliverable report from SAP Postmaster. Recipient is Internal - below attachments are not permitted from internal or external senders. Recipient is External - the email is not blocked by SAP. Blocked File Types are: .386, .ace, .acm, .acv, .ade, .adp, .adt, .ani, .app, .arc, .arj, .asd, .asp, .avb, .ax, .bas, .bat, .boo, .btm, .cab, .cbt, .cdr, .cer, .chm, .cla, .cmd, .cnv, .com, .cpl, .crt, .csc, .csh, .dll, .docm, .drv, .dvb, .email, .eml, .exe, .fon, .fxp, .gms, .gvb, .hlp, .ht, .hta, .htlp, .htt, .inf, .ini, .ins, .iqy, .iso, .isp, .its, .jar, .job, .js, .jse, .ksh, .lib, .lnk, .maf, .mam, .maq, .mar, .mat, .mau, .mav, .maw, .mch, .mda, .mdb, .mde, .mdt, .mdw, .mdz, .mht, .mhtm, .mhtml, .mpd, .mpt, .msc, .msi, .mso, .msp, .mst, .nws, .obd, .obj, .obt, .obz, .ocx, .ops, .ovl, .ovr, .pcd, .pci, .perl, .pgm, .pif, .pl, .pot, .prf, .prg, .ps1, .pub, .pwz, .qpw, .reg, .rtf, .sbf, .scf, .scr, .sct, .sfx, .sh, .shb, .shs, .shtml, .shw, .smm, .svg, .swf, .sys, .td0, .tlb, .tmp, .torrent, .tsk, .tsp, .tt6, .url, .vb, .vbe, .vbs, .vbx, .vom, .vsmacro, .vss, .vst, .vsw, .vwp, .vxd, .vxe, .wbk, .wbt, .wIz, .wk, .wmf, .wml, .wms, .wpc, .wpd, .ws, .wsc, .wsf, .wsh, .xlsm NOTE: The blocked file types are subject to change upon direction from SGS. Workarounds As an alternative to sending the blocked attachment via email please use one the following options: - OneDrive/SharePoint Additional information Email Attachment Limits Internal 35MB External 25MB Refer to IKB0012488 - Exchange Online - Attachment Blocking", "source": "Core Technologies", "id": 63}, {"topic": "Exchange & Outlook", "section": "1.3 What is Mass mailing limits", "paragraphs": ["At SAP sending to a distribution list (DL) with less than 500 members is open to all internal e-mail addresses. This means that all SAP users and Shared Mailboxes can send to any DL with less than 500 members.", "SAP Distribution lists (DL) with More than 500 members are restricted.", "Only users with mass mailing permissions will be able to send to these distribution lists. It is not necessary to be a member of the distribution list you want to send to.", "Restricted distribution lists", "When a distribution list has 500 members or more, sending to this DL automatically becomes restricted to the mass mailing security group.", "If a user without mass mailing permission tries to send to such a distribution list, they will receive a reply notifying them that sending has failed as they are not on the \"allowed sending list.\"", "How to check if Sender has mass mailing permissions", "To check if a sender has mass mailing permissions, loop up the sender from outlook address book and select the “Member of”", "If the sender is a member of either AllowDLsGT500_TEMP or AllowDLsGT500_PERM, then the sender has been permission to send mail to DL with more than 500 members.", "Applying for mass mailing permissions", "When applying for mass mailing permission, please note:", "If you are not sending to a distribution list, then mass mailing permissions will not help.", "If you are 'Sending as' another user or shared mailbox, they will need the mass mailing rights applied to their account.", "If sending 'on behalf of' another user, you will need the mass mailing rights applied to your User ID.", "Please check carefully who needs the permission? Is it you, or another address?", "There are 2 types of mass mailing permissions available to request.", "Temporary", "Permanent", "Temporary mass mailing permissions last 30 days and do not require an approval.", "Permanent mass mailing permissions require a business case, which will be submitted to SAP Corporate Affairs for approval.", "Use Mass Mailling Self Service App to request mass mailing permission", "Open the App", "Type the UserID, or email address of the mailbox, or the Lastname, Firstname of the user you are looking for in the Search box.", "Select the correct mailbox from the list.", "The tool will then show the current status:", "Temporary Access – includes an expiration date.", "Permanent Access – no expiration.", "No Access – you can request access directly from the app.", "Click on Request to raise request", "You can apply for two types of mass mailing access:", "Temporary Access (no approval needed)", "Best for short-term use.", "Just enter a short reason (use case) and click Submit.", "Access is granted right away and expires after 30 days.", "Permanent Access (approval required)", "Best for ongoing or frequent mass emails.", "Enter your reason and submit your request.", "The request goes through an approval process.", "Once approved, access does not expire.", "Refer to KB1287998 - Mass Mailing Self-Service App", "Refer to IKB0012522 - Mass mailing / mass e-mail permissions request"], "content": "At SAP sending to a distribution list (DL) with less than 500 members is open to all internal e-mail addresses. This means that all SAP users and Shared Mailboxes can send to any DL with less than 500 members. SAP Distribution lists (DL) with More than 500 members are restricted. Only users with mass mailing permissions will be able to send to these distribution lists. It is not necessary to be a member of the distribution list you want to send to. Restricted distribution lists When a distribution list has 500 members or more, sending to this DL automatically becomes restricted to the mass mailing security group. If a user without mass mailing permission tries to send to such a distribution list, they will receive a reply notifying them that sending has failed as they are not on the \"allowed sending list.\" How to check if Sender has mass mailing permissions To check if a sender has mass mailing permissions, loop up the sender from outlook address book and select the “Member of” If the sender is a member of either AllowDLsGT500_TEMP or AllowDLsGT500_PERM, then the sender has been permission to send mail to DL with more than 500 members. Applying for mass mailing permissions When applying for mass mailing permission, please note: If you are not sending to a distribution list, then mass mailing permissions will not help. If you are 'Sending as' another user or shared mailbox, they will need the mass mailing rights applied to their account. If sending 'on behalf of' another user, you will need the mass mailing rights applied to your User ID. Please check carefully who needs the permission? Is it you, or another address? There are 2 types of mass mailing permissions available to request. Temporary Permanent Temporary mass mailing permissions last 30 days and do not require an approval. Permanent mass mailing permissions require a business case, which will be submitted to SAP Corporate Affairs for approval. Use Mass Mailling Self Service App to request mass mailing permission Open the App Type the UserID, or email address of the mailbox, or the Lastname, Firstname of the user you are looking for in the Search box. Select the correct mailbox from the list. The tool will then show the current status: Temporary Access – includes an expiration date. Permanent Access – no expiration. No Access – you can request access directly from the app. Click on Request to raise request You can apply for two types of mass mailing access: Temporary Access (no approval needed) Best for short-term use. Just enter a short reason (use case) and click Submit. Access is granted right away and expires after 30 days. Permanent Access (approval required) Best for ongoing or frequent mass emails. Enter your reason and submit your request. The request goes through an approval process. Once approved, access does not expire. Refer to KB1287998 - Mass Mailing Self-Service App Refer to IKB0012522 - Mass mailing / mass e-mail permissions request", "source": "Core Technologies", "id": 64}, {"topic": "Exchange & Outlook", "section": "1.4.1. Shared Mailbox Self Service Guide", "paragraphs": ["The Shared Mailbox Self Service Tool helps to simplify the administration task associated with Shared Mailboxes by giving back control to the mailbox owners.", "We would like to inform you that from January 1, 2023, an annual fee of €36 will be introduced for each existing & newly requested shared mailbox.", "The fee will be charged monthly to the cost center of the primary owner of the shared mailbox.", "Now you can manage user access, request additional SMTP addresses, change the display name of a mailbox and more.", "When working with a shared mailbox, it's important to understand the type of address you require or is existing on a mailbox. The type of address you assign will determine the functionality of the mailbox.", "More information can be found here: Internal vs External Email Addresses.", "Initial Questions you may ask about the Self-Service Tool", "What is an Owner?", "The owner of a mailbox is responsible for it. They are the only ones who can request changes to the mailbox and manage its permissions.", "By default, an Owner will be added to the Full Access User list on the mailbox.", "How to find the owner of a shared mailbox", "Go to RMMT Self Service tool, select the Search Mailbox Tile.", "Enter the shared mailbox name or mail address and click on Search, select the mailbox, you may find the owners of the mailbox.", "And you can request the access by clicking on the envelop icon.", "What happens when you connect to the Self-Service Tool?", "When you first connect you will see a list of mailboxes that you are the owner of. If this is your first time connecting and you are not an owner of any mailboxes, it will appear empty. From here you can select a mailbox and view/change the properties associated with it. Some properties can be changed without the need of a ticket, helping to speed up the processing of certain changes. While other changes will require approval from IT before they can be changed.", "What can I manage without a ticket?", "You can perform the following changes:", "Add/Remove additional users to the mailbox", "Add/Remove additional owners to the mailbox", "Configure the Spam Policy", "The above changes do not require a ticket to be performed and can be done by any owner assigned to a mailbox.", "What changes require a ticket?", "Certain restricted properties will require the creation of a ticket before they can be changed. This is to ensure that the changes adhere to SAP policies.", "Changing the Display Name of the mailbox", "Adding additional E-mail addresses (Alias)", "Setting a new Primary SMTP address for the mailbox", "Hiding the mailbox from the Address Book in Outlook", "We've made it as simple as possible for you to request changes that require a ticket. They can be created directly from within the Self-Service Tool.", "Refer to IKB0010470 | Exchange Online - Shared Mailbox Self Service - FAQ"], "content": "The Shared Mailbox Self Service Tool helps to simplify the administration task associated with Shared Mailboxes by giving back control to the mailbox owners. We would like to inform you that from January 1, 2023, an annual fee of €36 will be introduced for each existing & newly requested shared mailbox. The fee will be charged monthly to the cost center of the primary owner of the shared mailbox. Now you can manage user access, request additional SMTP addresses, change the display name of a mailbox and more. When working with a shared mailbox, it's important to understand the type of address you require or is existing on a mailbox. The type of address you assign will determine the functionality of the mailbox. More information can be found here: Internal vs External Email Addresses. Initial Questions you may ask about the Self-Service Tool What is an Owner? The owner of a mailbox is responsible for it. They are the only ones who can request changes to the mailbox and manage its permissions. By default, an Owner will be added to the Full Access User list on the mailbox. How to find the owner of a shared mailbox Go to RMMT Self Service tool, select the Search Mailbox Tile. Enter the shared mailbox name or mail address and click on Search, select the mailbox, you may find the owners of the mailbox. And you can request the access by clicking on the envelop icon. What happens when you connect to the Self-Service Tool? When you first connect you will see a list of mailboxes that you are the owner of. If this is your first time connecting and you are not an owner of any mailboxes, it will appear empty. From here you can select a mailbox and view/change the properties associated with it. Some properties can be changed without the need of a ticket, helping to speed up the processing of certain changes. While other changes will require approval from IT before they can be changed. What can I manage without a ticket? You can perform the following changes: Add/Remove additional users to the mailbox Add/Remove additional owners to the mailbox Configure the Spam Policy The above changes do not require a ticket to be performed and can be done by any owner assigned to a mailbox. What changes require a ticket? Certain restricted properties will require the creation of a ticket before they can be changed. This is to ensure that the changes adhere to SAP policies. Changing the Display Name of the mailbox Adding additional E-mail addresses (Alias) Setting a new Primary SMTP address for the mailbox Hiding the mailbox from the Address Book in Outlook We've made it as simple as possible for you to request changes that require a ticket. They can be created directly from within the Self-Service Tool. Refer to IKB0010470 | Exchange Online - Shared Mailbox Self Service - FAQ", "source": "Core Technologies", "id": 65}, {"topic": "Exchange & Outlook", "section": "1.4.2. How to Add a Shared Mailbox (Windows)", "paragraphs": ["As there are two options for adding a shared mailbox in Outlook, take care that both options have not been applied at the same time. You need to remove the shared mailbox and restart Outlook before re-adding with a different option.", "Option A: Adding a shared mailbox as an additional account", "Step 1: Click on File.", "Step 2: Click on the Account Settings -> then Account Settings again.", "Step 3: Click New.", "Step 4: Enter the email address of the shared mailbox into the Email Address field and then click on Next.", "If prompted for a username and password, enter in your email and your C/D/I user password. Click here for steps: Shared mailbox prompting for password when adding the mailbox.", "Step 5: Outlook will connect to the mailbox, and it should look like below.", "If prompted for a username and password, enter in your email and your C/D/I user password.", "Step 6: Click on Finish and you will be prompted to restart Outlook.", "It will take some time for Outlook to populate for the first time.", "Once Outlook has been restarted, the shared mailbox will appear in the left-hand side of outlook as seen here.", "**Note**", "Using this method the display name of the left side in Outlook will show up as the mailbox's email address and not the display name such as: shared_mailbox@sap.com or shared_mailbox@global.corp.sap. BUT the recipient will still see the mailbox display name when they receive the email.", "Advantages of adding a shared mailbox as an additional account.", "Sent e-mails will appear in the Sent folder of the shared mailbox.", "Private items are visible in the shared mailbox.", "You can manage the rules of the shared mailbox.", "You can manage the Out of Office response of the shared mailbox.", "The shared mailbox no longer shares .ost files with the primary mailbox and therefore reduces sync issues.", "Better functionality with Microsoft Teams.", "Option B: Adding a shared mailbox as an additional mailbox to an existing account", "Step 1: Right click on your email address in the left column and select properties:", "Step 2: The \"Outlook Today\" screen will pop up. Please click on the Advanced button.", "Step 3: On the following window click on the Advanced tab and then the Add button.", "Step 4: An \"Add Mailbox\" window will appear. Type in the name of the mailbox and click OK.", "Step 5: The shared mailbox will now appear in the list of mailboxes added.", "Step 6: Click Apply and OK on the preceding windows.", "Step 7: The mailbox should now appear in the left-hand column of your Outlook.", "**Note**", "Using this method, the display name in Outlook will show up as the mailbox's actual DisplayName, such as \"SAP Shared Mailbox Name\".", "Caveats of Option B:", "Sent Items and Deleted Items from the shared mailbox appear in YOUR own mailbox, Sent and Deleted Items folders, and not the shared mailbox.", "To send from the mailbox you must manually add the FROM option while composing the email, then add the mailbox from the address book.", "The mailbox's total size will be added to your own OST file (the offline cache) possibly pushing it beyond the 50GB limit. This can be mitigated by reducing the cached slider in your account properties.", "Limited functionality when working with Microsoft Teams.", "Refer to IKB0012803 | Exchange Online - Shared mailboxes - How to's", "Additional info for using a shared mailbox with Microsoft Teams", "If you use Microsoft Teams with a shared mailbox, its recommended to use \"Option A: Adding a shared mailbox as an additional account\"", "Please refer to IKB0011030- Microsoft Teams - Meeting FAQ - Scheduling a Meeting Q6"], "content": "As there are two options for adding a shared mailbox in Outlook, take care that both options have not been applied at the same time. You need to remove the shared mailbox and restart Outlook before re-adding with a different option. Option A: Adding a shared mailbox as an additional account Step 1: Click on File. Step 2: Click on the Account Settings -> then Account Settings again. Step 3: Click New. Step 4: Enter the email address of the shared mailbox into the Email Address field and then click on Next. If prompted for a username and password, enter in your email and your C/D/I user password. Click here for steps: Shared mailbox prompting for password when adding the mailbox. Step 5: Outlook will connect to the mailbox, and it should look like below. If prompted for a username and password, enter in your email and your C/D/I user password. Step 6: Click on Finish and you will be prompted to restart Outlook. It will take some time for Outlook to populate for the first time. Once Outlook has been restarted, the shared mailbox will appear in the left-hand side of outlook as seen here. **Note** Using this method the display name of the left side in Outlook will show up as the mailbox's email address and not the display name such as: shared_mailbox@sap.com or shared_mailbox@global.corp.sap. BUT the recipient will still see the mailbox display name when they receive the email. Advantages of adding a shared mailbox as an additional account. Sent e-mails will appear in the Sent folder of the shared mailbox. Private items are visible in the shared mailbox. You can manage the rules of the shared mailbox. You can manage the Out of Office response of the shared mailbox. The shared mailbox no longer shares .ost files with the primary mailbox and therefore reduces sync issues. Better functionality with Microsoft Teams. Option B: Adding a shared mailbox as an additional mailbox to an existing account Step 1: Right click on your email address in the left column and select properties: Step 2: The \"Outlook Today\" screen will pop up. Please click on the Advanced button. Step 3: On the following window click on the Advanced tab and then the Add button. Step 4: An \"Add Mailbox\" window will appear. Type in the name of the mailbox and click OK. Step 5: The shared mailbox will now appear in the list of mailboxes added. Step 6: Click Apply and OK on the preceding windows. Step 7: The mailbox should now appear in the left-hand column of your Outlook. **Note** Using this method, the display name in Outlook will show up as the mailbox's actual DisplayName, such as \"SAP Shared Mailbox Name\". Caveats of Option B: Sent Items and Deleted Items from the shared mailbox appear in YOUR own mailbox, Sent and Deleted Items folders, and not the shared mailbox. To send from the mailbox you must manually add the FROM option while composing the email, then add the mailbox from the address book. The mailbox's total size will be added to your own OST file (the offline cache) possibly pushing it beyond the 50GB limit. This can be mitigated by reducing the cached slider in your account properties. Limited functionality when working with Microsoft Teams. Refer to IKB0012803 | Exchange Online - Shared mailboxes - How to's Additional info for using a shared mailbox with Microsoft Teams If you use Microsoft Teams with a shared mailbox, its recommended to use \"Option A: Adding a shared mailbox as an additional account\" Please refer to IKB0011030- Microsoft Teams - Meeting FAQ - Scheduling a Meeting Q6", "source": "Core Technologies", "id": 66}, {"topic": "Exchange & Outlook", "section": "1.5.1 What is the Online Archive?", "paragraphs": ["The Online Archive is a feature in Office 365 that provides users with an additional archive storage space of 100 GB.", "Users can access and store messages in their Online Archive using the Microsoft or Mac Outlook client.", "A user's Online Archive acts somewhat like a second account in Outlook with its own folder structure. As a result, it isn't included in searches performed from the Inbox.", "Note: The archive mailbox will be configured 31 days after the creation of the primary mailbox."], "content": "The Online Archive is a feature in Office 365 that provides users with an additional archive storage space of 100 GB. Users can access and store messages in their Online Archive using the Microsoft or Mac Outlook client. A user's Online Archive acts somewhat like a second account in Outlook with its own folder structure. As a result, it isn't included in searches performed from the Inbox. Note: The archive mailbox will be configured 31 days after the creation of the primary mailbox.", "source": "Core Technologies", "id": 67}, {"topic": "Exchange & Outlook", "section": "1.5.2 What is the Purpose of the Online Archive?", "paragraphs": ["It provides an additional 100 GB of storage space for all users.", "It provides usage of the Default Archive Policy (1 year to 3 years or 5 years).", "Auto-expanding feature: Once your Online Archive is enabled, the auto-expanding feature will apply additional storage as soon as the initial Online Archive quota reaches 100 GB, and subsequently up to 1 TB.", "Online Archive is not available for shared mailbox."], "content": "It provides an additional 100 GB of storage space for all users. It provides usage of the Default Archive Policy (1 year to 3 years or 5 years). Auto-expanding feature: Once your Online Archive is enabled, the auto-expanding feature will apply additional storage as soon as the initial Online Archive quota reaches 100 GB, and subsequently up to 1 TB. Online Archive is not available for shared mailbox.", "source": "Core Technologies", "id": 68}, {"topic": "Exchange & Outlook", "section": "1.5.3 Overview of the Online Archive Mailbox", "paragraphs": ["The Online Archive comes with the following three default folders/functions:", "Deleted Items: To manage deleted items from within the archive.", "Archive: PLEASE NOTE! The default Online Archive folder has no connection to your primary mailbox's Archive button in your Outlook ribbon. This folder is created by default, based on the existing Archive folder in your primary mailbox.", "Search Folder: Allows users to perform searches for items located in the Online Archive, searches started from the primary mailbox do not include search results from the Online Archive. Searches need to be performed directly from there."], "content": "The Online Archive comes with the following three default folders/functions: Deleted Items: To manage deleted items from within the archive. Archive: PLEASE NOTE! The default Online Archive folder has no connection to your primary mailbox's Archive button in your Outlook ribbon. This folder is created by default, based on the existing Archive folder in your primary mailbox. Search Folder: Allows users to perform searches for items located in the Online Archive, searches started from the primary mailbox do not include search results from the Online Archive. Searches need to be performed directly from there.", "source": "Core Technologies", "id": 69}, {"topic": "Exchange & Outlook", "section": "1.5.4 Working with Your Online Archive Using Policies (Recommended)", "paragraphs": ["You can let archive policies automatically move email messages from your primary mailbox to the Online Archive by assigning an archive policy to items or folders using the Assign Policy button in the Outlook ribbon and the Set Folder Policy option. Once assigned, the items/folders will be automatically archived to the Online Archive based on the policy selected. It is important to note that this will replicate your physical mailbox folder structure based on your selection; the same applies to sub folders.", "Assign an Archive Policy to Items", "Archive Policies control how long your messages are left in a primary mailbox before they are moved to your Online Archive.", "Select some items in your inbox, as seen below, and then use the quick link in the Outlook ribbon to assign one of the three policies available. In this example, one year was selected.", "Assign an Archive Policy to Folders", "Select the folder you want to assign the policy to. In the example, two folders were selected.", "PLEASE NOTE! The folder policy cannot be set using the quick link option as described above, as this is used for assigning the policy quickly to items.", "You will see that there is an option in the Assign Policy button named Set Folder Policy. Select this option and you can now assign the desired policy to the folder.", "After the policy is assigned, the Inbox and its subsequent sub folders to which the policy were applied are now created. Any subsequent folders you apply the policy to will also appear."], "content": "You can let archive policies automatically move email messages from your primary mailbox to the Online Archive by assigning an archive policy to items or folders using the Assign Policy button in the Outlook ribbon and the Set Folder Policy option. Once assigned, the items/folders will be automatically archived to the Online Archive based on the policy selected. It is important to note that this will replicate your physical mailbox folder structure based on your selection; the same applies to sub folders. Assign an Archive Policy to Items Archive Policies control how long your messages are left in a primary mailbox before they are moved to your Online Archive. Select some items in your inbox, as seen below, and then use the quick link in the Outlook ribbon to assign one of the three policies available. In this example, one year was selected. Assign an Archive Policy to Folders Select the folder you want to assign the policy to. In the example, two folders were selected. PLEASE NOTE! The folder policy cannot be set using the quick link option as described above, as this is used for assigning the policy quickly to items. You will see that there is an option in the Assign Policy button named Set Folder Policy. Select this option and you can now assign the desired policy to the folder. After the policy is assigned, the Inbox and its subsequent sub folders to which the policy were applied are now created. Any subsequent folders you apply the policy to will also appear.", "source": "Core Technologies", "id": 70}, {"topic": "Exchange & Outlook", "section": "1.5.5 Working Manually with the Online Archive", "paragraphs": ["Users can also create their own folder hierarchy within the Online Archive and move / copy / drag and drop items from their primary mailbox into the Online Archive. In the example shown below, a folder called My Archive was created, where items were moved / copied / dragged and dropped to. Additionally, a number of sub folders were created. It is possible to move / copy an entire folder from your primary mailbox to your Online Archive. Consequently, working manually with the archive requires some more effort in creating the sub folders. When policies are applied this is not required.", "IKB0010631 - Exchange Online - Archive"], "content": "Users can also create their own folder hierarchy within the Online Archive and move / copy / drag and drop items from their primary mailbox into the Online Archive. In the example shown below, a folder called My Archive was created, where items were moved / copied / dragged and dropped to. Additionally, a number of sub folders were created. It is possible to move / copy an entire folder from your primary mailbox to your Online Archive. Consequently, working manually with the archive requires some more effort in creating the sub folders. When policies are applied this is not required. IKB0010631 - Exchange Online - Archive", "source": "Core Technologies", "id": 71}, {"topic": "Exchange & Outlook", "section": "1.6 How to create new outlook profile", "paragraphs": ["IKB0010691 - Microsoft Outlook - Create a new profile"], "content": "IKB0010691 - Microsoft Outlook - Create a new profile", "source": "Core Technologies", "id": 72}, {"topic": "Exchange & Outlook", "section": "1.7 New Outlook Feature", "paragraphs": ["Delete invitations from Inbox after responding - You can enable/disable this new meeting invite option by visiting the Seetings > Calendar > Events and invitations > Invitations from other people.", "Folder icon colors - You can now customize folder icon colors in the new Outlook, making it easier to distinguish and personalize your folders.", "Right click on the Folder Name, Select Change color", "S/MIME encryption support - S/MIME signing and encryption are now supported, with all configurations working automatically without administrator intervention.", "Settings > Mail > S/MIME", "Manage emails in PST files - Move, copy, delete, flag/unflag, mark as read/unread, and set categories for emails within .pst files. You can also create, delete, move, and rename folders within .pst files.", "Move (drag and drop) emails from a .pst file to a mailbox.", "To add .pst files to the new Outlook, go to Settings > Files > Outlook Data Files > Add file", "KB0726226 -Availability of the New Outlook for Windows Application"], "content": "Delete invitations from Inbox after responding - You can enable/disable this new meeting invite option by visiting the Seetings > Calendar > Events and invitations > Invitations from other people. Folder icon colors - You can now customize folder icon colors in the new Outlook, making it easier to distinguish and personalize your folders. Right click on the Folder Name, Select Change color S/MIME encryption support - S/MIME signing and encryption are now supported, with all configurations working automatically without administrator intervention. Settings > Mail > S/MIME Manage emails in PST files - Move, copy, delete, flag/unflag, mark as read/unread, and set categories for emails within .pst files. You can also create, delete, move, and rename folders within .pst files. Move (drag and drop) emails from a .pst file to a mailbox. To add .pst files to the new Outlook, go to Settings > Files > Outlook Data Files > Add file KB0726226 -Availability of the New Outlook for Windows Application", "source": "Core Technologies", "id": 73}, {"topic": "Service Account", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Request service account via the Thycotic ALM tool", "https://dewdfalm01.wdf.global.corp.sap/#/requests", "https://wiki.one.int.sap/wiki/display/globsecu/IT+-+Service+Account+Provisioning", "How to enroll a SSO G2 certificate for Service Accounts – Click here."], "content": "Request service account via the Thycotic ALM tool https://dewdfalm01.wdf.global.corp.sap/#/requests https://wiki.one.int.sap/wiki/display/globsecu/IT+-+Service+Account+Provisioning How to enroll a SSO G2 certificate for Service Accounts – Click here.", "source": "Core Technologies", "id": 74}, {"topic": "Anti Spam/Junk", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["To handle SPAM filtering in the future easier and in a single place, SAP's previous third-party SPAM filter service will be replaced by a centralized Anti-SPAM solution within the Microsoft cloud services."], "content": "To handle SPAM filtering in the future easier and in a single place, SAP's previous third-party SPAM filter service will be replaced by a centralized Anti-SPAM solution within the Microsoft cloud services.", "source": "Core Technologies", "id": 75}, {"topic": "4. Report a phishing email", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["SAP IT provided a new Outlook add-in button available for all SAP employees named as \"Report Phishing\" - that SAP colleagues can easily send samples of phishing emails or spam emails to our Cyber Security team.", "Here are the steps to use the tools.", "Installing the add- in", "1) Click the \"Get Add-ins\" button in your Outlook ribbon", "2) Look under \"Admin-managed\" in the left-hand navigation. Select the add-in and click \"Add\"", "Using the button to report suspicious e-mails once installed.", "Highlight the e-mail you want to report", "Click on the \"Report Phishing\" button in your Outlook ribbon", "Confirm your selection by clicking \"Report\" button", "Note:", "After reporting, you will receive an e-mail from SAP's security team confirming whether the e-mail was phishing, junk, or a legitimate message.", "The reported e-mail will be moved to your deleted items folder, in case you need to retrieve it.", "IKB0011112 - Microsoft 365 Apps - Report a phishing e-mail", "IKB0012814 - Exchange Online - Anti Spam/Junk settings using Outlook Web Access (OWA)"], "content": "SAP IT provided a new Outlook add-in button available for all SAP employees named as \"Report Phishing\" - that SAP colleagues can easily send samples of phishing emails or spam emails to our Cyber Security team. Here are the steps to use the tools. Installing the add- in 1) Click the \"Get Add-ins\" button in your Outlook ribbon 2) Look under \"Admin-managed\" in the left-hand navigation. Select the add-in and click \"Add\" Using the button to report suspicious e-mails once installed. Highlight the e-mail you want to report Click on the \"Report Phishing\" button in your Outlook ribbon Confirm your selection by clicking \"Report\" button Note: After reporting, you will receive an e-mail from SAP's security team confirming whether the e-mail was phishing, junk, or a legitimate message. The reported e-mail will be moved to your deleted items folder, in case you need to retrieve it. IKB0011112 - Microsoft 365 Apps - Report a phishing e-mail IKB0012814 - Exchange Online - Anti Spam/Junk settings using Outlook Web Access (OWA)", "source": "Core Technologies", "id": 76}, {"topic": "", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["ONE Support", "Internal- SAP Only", "Version control", "If you find any content in this document is out of date, feel free to contact the Authors for feedback!", "Thanks for your cooperation in advance!"], "content": "ONE Support Internal- SAP Only Version control If you find any content in this document is out of date, feel free to contact the Authors for feedback! Thanks for your cooperation in advance!", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 77}, {"topic": "About Your Mac", "section": "1.1 File System", "paragraphs": ["File system formats available in Disk Utility on Mac", "Disk Utility on Mac supports several file system formats:", "Apple File System (APFS): The file system used by macOS 10.13 or later.", "Mac OS Extended: The file system used by macOS 10.12 or earlier.", "MS-DOS (FAT) and ExFAT: File systems that are compatible with Windows.", "Apple File System (APFS)", "Apple File System (APFS), the default file system for Mac computers using macOS 10.13 or later, features strong encryption, space sharing, snapshots, fast directory sizing, and improved file system fundamentals. While APFS is optimized for the Flash/SSD storage used in recent Mac computers, it can also be used with older systems with traditional hard disk drives (HDD) and external, direct-attached storage. macOS 10.13 or later supports APFS for both bootable and data volumes.", "APFS allocates disk space within a container (partition) on demand. When a single APFS container has multiple volumes, the container’s free space is shared and is automatically allocated to any of the individual volumes as needed. If desired, you can specify reserve and quota sizes for each volume. Each volume uses only part of the overall container, so the available space is the total size of the container, minus the size of all the volumes in the container.", "Choose one of the following APFS formats for Mac computers using macOS 10.13 or later.", "APFS: Uses the APFS format. Choose this option if you don’t need an encrypted or case-sensitive format.", "APFS (Encrypted): Uses the APFS format and encrypts the volume.", "APFS (Case-sensitive): Uses the APFS format and is case-sensitive to file and folder names. For example, folders named “Homework” and “HOMEWORK” are two different folders.", "APFS (Case-sensitive, Encrypted): Uses the APFS format, is case-sensitive to file and folder names, and encrypts the volume. For example, folders named “Homework” and “HOMEWORK” are two different folders.", "You can easily add or delete volumes in APFS containers. Each volume within an APFS container can have its own APFS format—APFS, APFS (Encrypted), APFS (Case-sensitive), or APFS (Case-sensitive, Encrypted).", "Mac OS Extended", "Choose one of the following Mac OS Extended file system formats for compatibility with Mac computers using macOS 10.12 or earlier.", "Mac OS Extended (Journaled): Uses the Mac format (Journaled HFS Plus) to protect the integrity of the hierarchical file system. Choose this option if you don’t need an encrypted or case-sensitive format.", "Mac OS Extended (Journaled, Encrypted): Uses the Mac format, requires a password, and encrypts the partition.", "Mac OS Extended (Case-sensitive, Journaled): Uses the Mac format and is case-sensitive to folder names. For example, folders named “Homework” and “HOMEWORK” are two different folders.", "Mac OS Extended (Case-sensitive, Journaled, Encrypted): Uses the Mac format, is case-sensitive to folder names, requires a password, and encrypts the partition.", "Windows-compatible formats", "Choose one of the following Windows-compatible file system formats if you are formatting a disk to use with Windows.", "MS-DOS (FAT): Use for Windows volumes that are 32 GB or less.", "ExFAT: Use for Windows volumes that are over 32 GB."], "content": "File system formats available in Disk Utility on Mac Disk Utility on Mac supports several file system formats: Apple File System (APFS): The file system used by macOS 10.13 or later. Mac OS Extended: The file system used by macOS 10.12 or earlier. MS-DOS (FAT) and ExFAT: File systems that are compatible with Windows. Apple File System (APFS) Apple File System (APFS), the default file system for Mac computers using macOS 10.13 or later, features strong encryption, space sharing, snapshots, fast directory sizing, and improved file system fundamentals. While APFS is optimized for the Flash/SSD storage used in recent Mac computers, it can also be used with older systems with traditional hard disk drives (HDD) and external, direct-attached storage. macOS 10.13 or later supports APFS for both bootable and data volumes. APFS allocates disk space within a container (partition) on demand. When a single APFS container has multiple volumes, the container’s free space is shared and is automatically allocated to any of the individual volumes as needed. If desired, you can specify reserve and quota sizes for each volume. Each volume uses only part of the overall container, so the available space is the total size of the container, minus the size of all the volumes in the container. Choose one of the following APFS formats for Mac computers using macOS 10.13 or later. APFS: Uses the APFS format. Choose this option if you don’t need an encrypted or case-sensitive format. APFS (Encrypted): Uses the APFS format and encrypts the volume. APFS (Case-sensitive): Uses the APFS format and is case-sensitive to file and folder names. For example, folders named “Homework” and “HOMEWORK” are two different folders. APFS (Case-sensitive, Encrypted): Uses the APFS format, is case-sensitive to file and folder names, and encrypts the volume. For example, folders named “Homework” and “HOMEWORK” are two different folders. You can easily add or delete volumes in APFS containers. Each volume within an APFS container can have its own APFS format—APFS, APFS (Encrypted), APFS (Case-sensitive), or APFS (Case-sensitive, Encrypted). Mac OS Extended Choose one of the following Mac OS Extended file system formats for compatibility with Mac computers using macOS 10.12 or earlier. Mac OS Extended (Journaled): Uses the Mac format (Journaled HFS Plus) to protect the integrity of the hierarchical file system. Choose this option if you don’t need an encrypted or case-sensitive format. Mac OS Extended (Journaled, Encrypted): Uses the Mac format, requires a password, and encrypts the partition. Mac OS Extended (Case-sensitive, Journaled): Uses the Mac format and is case-sensitive to folder names. For example, folders named “Homework” and “HOMEWORK” are two different folders. Mac OS Extended (Case-sensitive, Journaled, Encrypted): Uses the Mac format, is case-sensitive to folder names, requires a password, and encrypts the partition. Windows-compatible formats Choose one of the following Windows-compatible file system formats if you are formatting a disk to use with Windows. MS-DOS (FAT): Use for Windows volumes that are 32 GB or less. ExFAT: Use for Windows volumes that are over 32 GB.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 78}, {"topic": "About Your Mac", "section": "1.2 Apple ID", "paragraphs": ["You do not need an Apple ID to use or sign into a Mac. An ID is required for iCloud related devices and Mac App Store downloads. Syncing via Office 365 and OneDrive isn't related to anything on the Apple ID side. There are benefits however for security related items however with an Apple ID, just like an iPhone such as Activation Lock and Find My features.", "Apple ID isn't required unless you purchase/download Apps from the Store, if needed, please create your own personal account. The terms and conditions attached to the use of an Apple ID are 1:1 with you and your Apple devices.", "When you return a Mac to IT, please check if Find My Mac is configured and disable it from the Mac before returning the device"], "content": "You do not need an Apple ID to use or sign into a Mac. An ID is required for iCloud related devices and Mac App Store downloads. Syncing via Office 365 and OneDrive isn't related to anything on the Apple ID side. There are benefits however for security related items however with an Apple ID, just like an iPhone such as Activation Lock and Find My features. Apple ID isn't required unless you purchase/download Apps from the Store, if needed, please create your own personal account. The terms and conditions attached to the use of an Apple ID are 1:1 with you and your Apple devices. When you return a Mac to IT, please check if Find My Mac is configured and disable it from the Mac before returning the device", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 79}, {"topic": "About Your Mac", "section": "1.3 Connect a monitor", "paragraphs": ["Find out what your Mac supports", "Your external display will be dark if it exceeds the maximum number of external displays that your Mac can use at the same time. This limit varies by Mac model.", "Your external display will be dark or use a lower resolution or refresh rate if you configure it to exceed the maximum supported resolution or refresh rate. This limit varies by Mac model, display, the video cable and adapter used with the display, and the resolution and refresh rate of other connected displays. Learn what to do if your screen became dark after you changed its resolution or refresh rate.", "To find out how many external displays your Mac supports, and at which resolutions and refresh rates, check the specifications for your Mac model:", "Mac mini", "Mac Studio", "Mac Pro", "iMac", "MacBook Pro", "MacBook Air", "MacBook", "Detect your display", "If your Mac can't detect your external display, your external display will be dark. Use one or more of these steps to try again to detect your display.", "Disconnect the display from your Mac, then reconnect it. It might help to turn off the display first.", "Put your Mac to sleep, then wake it. On Mac laptop computers, you can close the lid for a few seconds, then open the lid again.", "Choose Apple menu > System Settings (or System Preferences), then click Displays. Press and hold the Option key to show the Detect Displays button, then click the button.", "Restart your Mac. If you can't restart your Mac, press and hold its power button for about 10 seconds to turn it off. Then press and release the power button to turn it back on.", "More on https://support.apple.com/en-us/HT201177"], "content": "Find out what your Mac supports Your external display will be dark if it exceeds the maximum number of external displays that your Mac can use at the same time. This limit varies by Mac model. Your external display will be dark or use a lower resolution or refresh rate if you configure it to exceed the maximum supported resolution or refresh rate. This limit varies by Mac model, display, the video cable and adapter used with the display, and the resolution and refresh rate of other connected displays. Learn what to do if your screen became dark after you changed its resolution or refresh rate. To find out how many external displays your Mac supports, and at which resolutions and refresh rates, check the specifications for your Mac model: Mac mini Mac Studio Mac Pro iMac MacBook Pro MacBook Air MacBook Detect your display If your Mac can't detect your external display, your external display will be dark. Use one or more of these steps to try again to detect your display. Disconnect the display from your Mac, then reconnect it. It might help to turn off the display first. Put your Mac to sleep, then wake it. On Mac laptop computers, you can close the lid for a few seconds, then open the lid again. Choose Apple menu > System Settings (or System Preferences), then click Displays. Press and hold the Option key to show the Detect Displays button, then click the button. Restart your Mac. If you can't restart your Mac, press and hold its power button for about 10 seconds to turn it off. Then press and release the power button to turn it back on. More on https://support.apple.com/en-us/HT201177", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 80}, {"topic": "Configure Your Mac", "section": "2.1 How to setup your Mac", "paragraphs": ["Let's set up your Mac!", "There are two methods to Install a Mac:", "ADE: Automated Device Enrollment.", "Your Mac is already registered (via serial number) in SAP's management system and after first power on, you will be enrolled automatically into MDM with Setup Assistant. Almost all new Macs are under ADE. Approximately 95% of all SAP Macs are under ADE today.", "DE: Device Enrollment.", "Your Mac is not registered in SAP's management system and you will need to manually enroll your Mac using a few extra manual steps. Only in exception cases would DE be used (a small number of countries are not covered today by ADE). Around 5% of SAP Macs will fall into device enrollment (manual).", "Pre-Requirement", "Multi Factor Authentication (MFA) is needed or a Temporary Access Pass (TAP) How to Setup Multi Factor Authentication (MFA)"], "content": "Let's set up your Mac! There are two methods to Install a Mac: ADE: Automated Device Enrollment. Your Mac is already registered (via serial number) in SAP's management system and after first power on, you will be enrolled automatically into MDM with Setup Assistant. Almost all new Macs are under ADE. Approximately 95% of all SAP Macs are under ADE today. DE: Device Enrollment. Your Mac is not registered in SAP's management system and you will need to manually enroll your Mac using a few extra manual steps. Only in exception cases would DE be used (a small number of countries are not covered today by ADE). Around 5% of SAP Macs will fall into device enrollment (manual). Pre-Requirement Multi Factor Authentication (MFA) is needed or a Temporary Access Pass (TAP) How to Setup Multi Factor Authentication (MFA)", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 81}, {"topic": "Configure Your Mac", "section": "2.2 Manual Provisioning Mac (MDM Profile)", "paragraphs": ["Note：Important", "When asked to create your computer account:", "If you are facing Enrollment profile is broken, you can try below steps Manual provisioning MDM", "Sometimes Self Service is not immediately available, sometimes taking up to 5-10 minutes to appear.", "When it’s missing after few hours, that means the enrollment profile is broken", "Please try the following steps:", "Make sure the account has Administrator rights via Privileges app", "Open the Terminal in your Mac and run the command:", "sudo jamf removeFramework", "​​", "Open Safari from the Dock at the bottom of your screen.", "Enter the URL https://apple.applebucket.int.sap/enroll into the address bar.", "Log in with your sap email account. Click Continue to download the MDM profile.", "Click on the Downloads folder at the right end of the Dock and select the file enrollmentProfile.mobileconfig to continue.", "A notification will show up, asking you to review the profile before installation.", "Open System Preferences by clicking its icon in the Dock. If System Preferences has opened, click on the Profiles icon at the bottom right.", "As soon as the Profiles pane of System Preferences shows up, click on the Install... button to continue.", "Start the installation of the MDM profile by clicking Install again.", "Finish the installation of the MDM profile by clicking Install again.", "When asked for your credentials, enter the password of your local user account(Global Domain Password ) and click Enroll", "The enrollment process is now complete.", "After some time, the Self-Service app launches automatically. Please select the Self-Service category For you on the left side and then click Continue for Set up my Mac to finish the setup process.", "You will be asked to Finish setup and log out and back into your Mac after a few minutes."], "content": "Note：Important When asked to create your computer account: If you are facing Enrollment profile is broken, you can try below steps Manual provisioning MDM Sometimes Self Service is not immediately available, sometimes taking up to 5-10 minutes to appear. When it’s missing after few hours, that means the enrollment profile is broken Please try the following steps: Make sure the account has Administrator rights via Privileges app Open the Terminal in your Mac and run the command: sudo jamf removeFramework ​​ Open Safari from the Dock at the bottom of your screen. Enter the URL https://apple.applebucket.int.sap/enroll into the address bar. Log in with your sap email account. Click Continue to download the MDM profile. Click on the Downloads folder at the right end of the Dock and select the file enrollmentProfile.mobileconfig to continue. A notification will show up, asking you to review the profile before installation. Open System Preferences by clicking its icon in the Dock. If System Preferences has opened, click on the Profiles icon at the bottom right. As soon as the Profiles pane of System Preferences shows up, click on the Install... button to continue. Start the installation of the MDM profile by clicking Install again. Finish the installation of the MDM profile by clicking Install again. When asked for your credentials, enter the password of your local user account(Global Domain Password ) and click Enroll The enrollment process is now complete. After some time, the Self-Service app launches automatically. Please select the Self-Service category For you on the left side and then click Continue for Set up my Mac to finish the setup process. You will be asked to Finish setup and log out and back into your Mac after a few minutes.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 82}, {"topic": "Configure Your Mac", "section": "2.3 Apple Care in SAP (APJ)", "paragraphs": ["What type of repair can I get?", "https://www.apple.com/legal/sales-support/applecare/applecareforenterprise/", "How to check if a device is covered with ACE", "• Type the s/n into: https://checkcoverage.apple.com"], "content": "What type of repair can I get? https://www.apple.com/legal/sales-support/applecare/applecareforenterprise/ How to check if a device is covered with ACE • Type the s/n into: https://checkcoverage.apple.com", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 83}, {"topic": "Data Migration", "section": "3.1 Migration Method", "paragraphs": ["Recommended Option: Using Office 365 + AirDrop", "The easiest option to migrate your data from an old Mac to a new Mac or from a Windows device to a Mac is to store all your data in the cloud.", "OneDrive", "Make sure all the documents and files you want to move to your new machine are synced with the OneDrive client on your old machine, whether it's a Windows or Mac device.", "On your new Mac, set up OneDrive as described in OneDrive for Mac.", "On your new Mac, sync all the content from your OneDrive storage.", "Outlook", "Ensure all of your mail is stored in your Exchange Online account.", "On your new Mac, Outlook will automatically sync to your account.", "💡Storing mail locally on your Mac (or Windows 10 device) is discouraged. You are strongly encouraged to store all your Exchange data in your Exchange Online account as this ensures data backup and access from anywhere and on any device, including your iPhone and iPad. This means: Do not use .PST file archive on your Windows device and do not use On My Computer local storage in Outlook for Mac.", "AirDrop", "Once you have set up your new Mac, installed your apps, and verified your Office 365 data (in the cloud) is good to go (Exchange mailbox, OneDrive, OneNote, etc.), if you have any remaining application data you need to migrate to your new Mac, the best option is to use AirDrop.", "Simply export your data needed in supported file format on your old Mac", "Using AirDrop on your Macs, send the data from the old Mac to the new Mac", "Import/place your data into the required location or application on your new Mac", "Use AirDrop on your Mac", "Alternative: Ethernet connection using Ethernet or Thunderbolt cable", "If you have your old Mac available and either a Thunderbolt 3 cable or ethernet cable, simply plugging the cable between the new Mac and old Mac will automatically create self-assigned addresses so the Macs can see each other.", "This option is not available between Windows and Mac unless you do additional manual configurations on the Windows side (outside of scope for this article, but in short, you'd want to enable sharing and setup correct networking information on the Windows device so your Mac can see it when connected via Ethernet cable).", "On your old Mac, simply Set up file sharing on Mac - Apple Support (IE) for the data you'd like to copy to your new Mac and use Finder to copy it to your new Mac.", "⚠️ Note: File Sharing will auto-disable on check-in to Jamf, which occurs once per day. If you enable File Sharing and it happens to check in and disable itself during your file transfers, you will need to re-enable file sharing and re-transfer at the point of interruption. Using the recommended approach (cloud services) or AirDrop will not face this edge use case.", "This method requires that you know the basic file system structure of macOS so you can transfer data from the old Mac to the new Mac into the correct, corresponding location.", "Alternative: Target Disk Mode", "For those who have a large amount of local data or Apps on their old Mac and Migration Assistant isn't working or you would prefer to manually move data over, Target Disk Mode is a good option.", "This method requires that you know the basic file system structure of macOS so you can transfer data from the old Mac to the new Mac into the correct, corresponding location.", "Target Disk Mode requires two Macs and a valid Thunderbolt cable between the two Macs.", "Old Mac (where the data currently resides): Boot the Mac into Target Disk Mode by pressing command-T while turning on the Mac. You will see a Target Disk Mode symbol on the screen.", "New Mac (where you want to migrate data to): Plug in the cable to the new Mac and the storage disk of the old Mac will display in Finder and/or the Desktop. If the volume is FileVault encrypted, provide a valid password or recovery key to decrypt the volume."], "content": "Recommended Option: Using Office 365 + AirDrop The easiest option to migrate your data from an old Mac to a new Mac or from a Windows device to a Mac is to store all your data in the cloud. OneDrive Make sure all the documents and files you want to move to your new machine are synced with the OneDrive client on your old machine, whether it's a Windows or Mac device. On your new Mac, set up OneDrive as described in OneDrive for Mac. On your new Mac, sync all the content from your OneDrive storage. Outlook Ensure all of your mail is stored in your Exchange Online account. On your new Mac, Outlook will automatically sync to your account. 💡Storing mail locally on your Mac (or Windows 10 device) is discouraged. You are strongly encouraged to store all your Exchange data in your Exchange Online account as this ensures data backup and access from anywhere and on any device, including your iPhone and iPad. This means: Do not use .PST file archive on your Windows device and do not use On My Computer local storage in Outlook for Mac. AirDrop Once you have set up your new Mac, installed your apps, and verified your Office 365 data (in the cloud) is good to go (Exchange mailbox, OneDrive, OneNote, etc.), if you have any remaining application data you need to migrate to your new Mac, the best option is to use AirDrop. Simply export your data needed in supported file format on your old Mac Using AirDrop on your Macs, send the data from the old Mac to the new Mac Import/place your data into the required location or application on your new Mac Use AirDrop on your Mac Alternative: Ethernet connection using Ethernet or Thunderbolt cable If you have your old Mac available and either a Thunderbolt 3 cable or ethernet cable, simply plugging the cable between the new Mac and old Mac will automatically create self-assigned addresses so the Macs can see each other. This option is not available between Windows and Mac unless you do additional manual configurations on the Windows side (outside of scope for this article, but in short, you'd want to enable sharing and setup correct networking information on the Windows device so your Mac can see it when connected via Ethernet cable). On your old Mac, simply Set up file sharing on Mac - Apple Support (IE) for the data you'd like to copy to your new Mac and use Finder to copy it to your new Mac. ⚠️ Note: File Sharing will auto-disable on check-in to Jamf, which occurs once per day. If you enable File Sharing and it happens to check in and disable itself during your file transfers, you will need to re-enable file sharing and re-transfer at the point of interruption. Using the recommended approach (cloud services) or AirDrop will not face this edge use case. This method requires that you know the basic file system structure of macOS so you can transfer data from the old Mac to the new Mac into the correct, corresponding location. Alternative: Target Disk Mode For those who have a large amount of local data or Apps on their old Mac and Migration Assistant isn't working or you would prefer to manually move data over, Target Disk Mode is a good option. This method requires that you know the basic file system structure of macOS so you can transfer data from the old Mac to the new Mac into the correct, corresponding location. Target Disk Mode requires two Macs and a valid Thunderbolt cable between the two Macs. Old Mac (where the data currently resides): Boot the Mac into Target Disk Mode by pressing command-T while turning on the Mac. You will see a Target Disk Mode symbol on the screen. New Mac (where you want to migrate data to): Plug in the cable to the new Mac and the storage disk of the old Mac will display in Finder and/or the Desktop. If the volume is FileVault encrypted, provide a valid password or recovery key to decrypt the volume.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 84}, {"topic": "Manage Your SSO", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Verifying your SSO certificate", "Open System Settings → Privacy & Security → Profiles.", "You will see your SSO certificate contained under Device Management, listed as Access & Authentication.", "Alternatively, you can also see your individual certificate in Keychain Access → My Certificates."], "content": "Verifying your SSO certificate Open System Settings → Privacy & Security → Profiles. You will see your SSO certificate contained under Device Management, listed as Access & Authentication. Alternatively, you can also see your individual certificate in Keychain Access → My Certificates.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 85}, {"topic": "Manage Your SSO", "section": "4.1 Remove your SSO certificate", "paragraphs": ["To remove your SSO, use Self Service → First Aid → Single Sign-On. Select Remove."], "content": "To remove your SSO, use Self Service → First Aid → Single Sign-On. Select Remove.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 86}, {"topic": "Manage Your SSO", "section": "4.2 Renew your SSO certificate", "paragraphs": ["To reinstall your SSO, use Self Service → First Aid → Single Sign-On. Select Renew."], "content": "To reinstall your SSO, use Self Service → First Aid → Single Sign-On. Select Renew.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 87}, {"topic": "Manage Your SSO", "section": "4.3 Manually check your SSO certificate status in Keychain Access", "paragraphs": ["To check your SSO certificate in macOS's Keychain Access (where all your passwords, certificates, etc. are securely stored), open Keychain Access.app. (/Applications/Utilities/Keychain Access.app)", "Under My Certificates, you will find your SSO certificate (your I/C/D#).", "Here you can also inspect the certificate, delete it or change settings for it."], "content": "To check your SSO certificate in macOS's Keychain Access (where all your passwords, certificates, etc. are securely stored), open Keychain Access.app. (/Applications/Utilities/Keychain Access.app) Under My Certificates, you will find your SSO certificate (your I/C/D#). Here you can also inspect the certificate, delete it or change settings for it.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 88}, {"topic": "Manage Your SSO", "section": "4.4 Unable to renew SSO on user mac", "paragraphs": ["Self Service does not resolve Single Sign-On (SSO) issues, additional troubleshooting data must be collected for review by the Mac team.", "Use this guide when:", "No new SSO - issues persist after running the first aid policy (Renew SSO).", "User Mac is not getting SSO and not passible to get SSO (make sure that macOS up to date and you did check compliancy-AV, FV)", "You need to provide diagnostic information to IT Support.", "Collect Logs", "Open the Self Service application on the Mac.", "Navigate to the First Aid category.", "Locate and click Gather data under Mac Entra ID (Azure AD) Cond Access diagnostics.", "Collect logs. If they save on Self Service, make sure to save a copy of it before you try to remove MDM. (How to collect logs)", "When logs are collected save them to OneDrive so Admins can review it as if you remove MDM logs will be gone too.", "Log in to jamf and get screenshot for history what policy was pushed to the device :", "enter affected user ID or Mac S/N", "when you see information for user computer select History and Policy Logs and add screenshot to the ticket"], "content": "Self Service does not resolve Single Sign-On (SSO) issues, additional troubleshooting data must be collected for review by the Mac team. Use this guide when: No new SSO - issues persist after running the first aid policy (Renew SSO). User Mac is not getting SSO and not passible to get SSO (make sure that macOS up to date and you did check compliancy-AV, FV) You need to provide diagnostic information to IT Support. Collect Logs Open the Self Service application on the Mac. Navigate to the First Aid category. Locate and click Gather data under Mac Entra ID (Azure AD) Cond Access diagnostics. Collect logs. If they save on Self Service, make sure to save a copy of it before you try to remove MDM. (How to collect logs) When logs are collected save them to OneDrive so Admins can review it as if you remove MDM logs will be gone too. Log in to jamf and get screenshot for history what policy was pushed to the device : enter affected user ID or Mac S/N when you see information for user computer select History and Policy Logs and add screenshot to the ticket", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 89}, {"topic": "Manage Your Printers", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["This app adds an SAP Printer to your Mac, automatically using the new cloud SAP Printing Tool.", "You can open the portal directly or open Add Printer app to be redirected to the SAP Printing Tool page.", "AirPrint functionality for all SAP office printers is planned for 2023"], "content": "This app adds an SAP Printer to your Mac, automatically using the new cloud SAP Printing Tool. You can open the portal directly or open Add Printer app to be redirected to the SAP Printing Tool page. AirPrint functionality for all SAP office printers is planned for 2023", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 90}, {"topic": "Manage Your Printers", "section": "5.1 Add your printer", "paragraphs": ["1.Open Add Printer (/Applications/Add Printer.app) or browser to the SAP Printing Tool.", "2. Use the left hand drill down to find your printer or simply enter your location or printer name into the search box.", "3. Choose Connect to Printer. Approve the request to open Add Printer.app", "4. The printer will be added and you will see a Notification on success.", "5. The printer will show up in System Preferences → Printers & Scanners."], "content": "1.Open Add Printer (/Applications/Add Printer.app) or browser to the SAP Printing Tool. 2. Use the left hand drill down to find your printer or simply enter your location or printer name into the search box. 3. Choose Connect to Printer. Approve the request to open Add Printer.app 4. The printer will be added and you will see a Notification on success. 5. The printer will show up in System Preferences → Printers & Scanners.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 91}, {"topic": "Install Windows 11 as VM in Fusion", "section": "6.1 Important information in advance", "paragraphs": ["On Apple Silicon Macs/M1-M5 Macs (ARM-based) you can only use ARM based guest OS's.", "If you are not sure which model you have, here's an Apple support article including all Macs with Apple Silicon: https://support.apple.com/en-us/HT211814", "You can access Windows Terminal Server (WTS) via http://access.sap.com from anywhere.", "You can self provision, in under 30 minutes, a Virtual Desktop infrastructure machine which is available to you, from anywhere. You have full control of your VDI image and can install additional software to it (compliant to normal SAP policies). See the Wiki for information.", "NOTE: Using Boot Camp to natively install Windows to your Mac is not allowed."], "content": "On Apple Silicon Macs/M1-M5 Macs (ARM-based) you can only use ARM based guest OS's. If you are not sure which model you have, here's an Apple support article including all Macs with Apple Silicon: https://support.apple.com/en-us/HT211814 You can access Windows Terminal Server (WTS) via http://access.sap.com from anywhere. You can self provision, in under 30 minutes, a Virtual Desktop infrastructure machine which is available to you, from anywhere. You have full control of your VDI image and can install additional software to it (compliant to normal SAP policies). See the Wiki for information. NOTE: Using Boot Camp to natively install Windows to your Mac is not allowed.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 92}, {"topic": "Install Windows 11 as VM in Fusion", "section": "6.2 Order VMWare Fusion and a Windows 11 license", "paragraphs": ["From Ariba Guided Buying (ABG), order a license for a Windows license.", "Microsoft Windows VM Image MAC € 0.01 per year", "Refer KB"], "content": "From Ariba Guided Buying (ABG), order a license for a Windows license. Microsoft Windows VM Image MAC € 0.01 per year Refer KB", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 93}, {"topic": "Install Windows 11 as VM in Fusion", "section": "6.3 Install VMWare Fusion from Self Service", "paragraphs": ["Once you have ordered VMWare Fusion and your Windows license, you will be notified that it has been issued to you. You can now open Self Service and log in. Under the Apps category, you will find the VMWare Fusion package to install to your Mac."], "content": "Once you have ordered VMWare Fusion and your Windows license, you will be notified that it has been issued to you. You can now open Self Service and log in. Under the Apps category, you will find the VMWare Fusion package to install to your Mac.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 94}, {"topic": "Privileges – MacOS", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Privileges allows users to work as a standard user for day-to-day tasks, by providing a quick and easy way to request administrator rights. Users can set a timeframe in the application's settings to perform specific tasks, such as installing or removing an application. To request admin rights, simply click on the Privileges icon in your dock. Privileges is open-sourced."], "content": "Privileges allows users to work as a standard user for day-to-day tasks, by providing a quick and easy way to request administrator rights. Users can set a timeframe in the application's settings to perform specific tasks, such as installing or removing an application. To request admin rights, simply click on the Privileges icon in your dock. Privileges is open-sourced.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 95}, {"topic": "Privileges – MacOS", "section": "7.1 Why can't I just have admin rights all the time?", "paragraphs": ["Working as a standard user instead of an administrator adds another layer of security to your Mac, protecting it from malware and other unauthorized changes, and is considered a security best practice.", "It also ensures compliance with the SAP Global Security requirements, which in turn makes sure you have access to all corporate resources."], "content": "Working as a standard user instead of an administrator adds another layer of security to your Mac, protecting it from malware and other unauthorized changes, and is considered a security best practice. It also ensures compliance with the SAP Global Security requirements, which in turn makes sure you have access to all corporate resources.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 96}, {"topic": "Privileges – MacOS", "section": "7.2 I'm a standard user and need admin rights to install an app", "paragraphs": ["Launch Privileges.", "You should see the following window:", "3. Click on Request Privileges.", "4. The Privileges dock icon should change to look like an orange padlock. A notification should appear saying that \"administrator rights were successfully granted\". The logged-in account should now have admin rights.", "Note: You can also request privilege rights via the icon in the dock. Simply right-click the icon and select Request Privileges."], "content": "Launch Privileges. You should see the following window: 3. Click on Request Privileges. 4. The Privileges dock icon should change to look like an orange padlock. A notification should appear saying that \"administrator rights were successfully granted\". The logged-in account should now have admin rights. Note: You can also request privilege rights via the icon in the dock. Simply right-click the icon and select Request Privileges.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 97}, {"topic": "Privileges – MacOS", "section": "7.3 The icon for Privileges changes in the dock.", "paragraphs": ["This is by design. The icon is green and with the padlock closed when you are a standard user. It looks like this:", "It becomes orange and the padlock opens when you are an admin. It looks like this:"], "content": "This is by design. The icon is green and with the padlock closed when you are a standard user. It looks like this: It becomes orange and the padlock opens when you are an admin. It looks like this:", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 98}, {"topic": "Privileges – MacOS", "section": "7.4 I want to make a change to the system and it asks me for an administrator account to proceed.", "paragraphs": ["Simply use Privileges to request admin rights. Then enter your username and password in the dialog."], "content": "Simply use Privileges to request admin rights. Then enter your username and password in the dialog.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 99}, {"topic": "Privileges – MacOS", "section": "7.5 I want to script or use Privileges from terminal.", "paragraphs": ["Privileges supports command line use.", "For Privileges, run /Applications/Privileges.app/Contents/Resources/PrivilegesCLI to see the usage syntax.", "For Privileges 2, run PrivilegesCLI to see the usage syntax.", "You should see the following window:"], "content": "Privileges supports command line use. For Privileges, run /Applications/Privileges.app/Contents/Resources/PrivilegesCLI to see the usage syntax. For Privileges 2, run PrivilegesCLI to see the usage syntax. You should see the following window:", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 100}, {"topic": "Privileges – MacOS", "section": "7.6 I want to uninstall Privileges.", "paragraphs": ["1. Open Self Service.", "2. Look for \"Privileges\". You should see the following:", "3. Click on Uninstall. You will be automatically reverted to a standard user.", "Important Note: Uninstalling Privileges will make your Mac non-compliant and you will lose access to certain SAP Corporate services."], "content": "1. Open Self Service. 2. Look for \"Privileges\". You should see the following: 3. Click on Uninstall. You will be automatically reverted to a standard user. Important Note: Uninstalling Privileges will make your Mac non-compliant and you will lose access to certain SAP Corporate services.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 101}, {"topic": "Privileges – MacOS", "section": "7.7 I see a locked black icon in the Dock and cannot elevate to Administrator.", "paragraphs": ["For some users, Privileges has been configured by SAP IT to prevent elevation to a local Administrator. You will see the warning \"You cannot use this app to change your privileges!\" if you try to elevate."], "content": "For some users, Privileges has been configured by SAP IT to prevent elevation to a local Administrator. You will see the warning \"You cannot use this app to change your privileges!\" if you try to elevate.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 102}, {"topic": "Privileges – MacOS", "section": "7.8 Privileges 2. What's new?", "paragraphs": ["Privileges 2 was officially released on November 20, 2024 and will be deployed automatically to all Macs in CW48 of 2024.", "Brand new icons:", "Remove admin rights upon login: To ensure that you are always a standard user after a restart, Privileges automatically revokes administrator rights after restart. This is a measure we have implemented at SAP to ensure security.", "Run actions on privilege change: You can now select an app that runs automatically after privileges have been changed.", "Localized in 40 languages: Privileges is now available in 40 different languages.", "Command line tool now also supports Touch ID.", "Webhooks.", "AppleScript Support."], "content": "Privileges 2 was officially released on November 20, 2024 and will be deployed automatically to all Macs in CW48 of 2024. Brand new icons: Remove admin rights upon login: To ensure that you are always a standard user after a restart, Privileges automatically revokes administrator rights after restart. This is a measure we have implemented at SAP to ensure security. Run actions on privilege change: You can now select an app that runs automatically after privileges have been changed. Localized in 40 languages: Privileges is now available in 40 different languages. Command line tool now also supports Touch ID. Webhooks. AppleScript Support.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 103}, {"topic": "Privileges – MacOS", "section": "7.9 New Privileges 2.2 features", "paragraphs": ["New menu bar icon", "To enable the new menu bar icon, go to Privileges' Settings > General > enable Show in Menu Bar.", "If the privileges have an expiration, the expiration time will show when the mouse hovers over the menu bar icon.", "Renew privileges via app icon", "To enable the new menu bar icon, go to Privileges' Settings > Privileges > enable Allow expiring administrator privileges to be renewed.", "You can now renew your privileges by right-clicking the icon in the menu bar or dock and pressing the Option-Key. Select Renew Privileges.", "Note: This only works if the privileges have an expiration time."], "content": "New menu bar icon To enable the new menu bar icon, go to Privileges' Settings > General > enable Show in Menu Bar. If the privileges have an expiration, the expiration time will show when the mouse hovers over the menu bar icon. Renew privileges via app icon To enable the new menu bar icon, go to Privileges' Settings > Privileges > enable Allow expiring administrator privileges to be renewed. You can now renew your privileges by right-clicking the icon in the menu bar or dock and pressing the Option-Key. Select Renew Privileges. Note: This only works if the privileges have an expiration time.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 104}, {"topic": "Self Service – MacOS", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Self Service is SAP's internal Mac App Store.", "It is preinstalled on your Mac and available anywhere with an Internet connection.", "You can use Self Service install SAP software or external software which allow for SAP owned machine."], "content": "Self Service is SAP's internal Mac App Store. It is preinstalled on your Mac and available anywhere with an Internet connection. You can use Self Service install SAP software or external software which allow for SAP owned machine.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 105}, {"topic": "Self Service – MacOS", "section": "8.1 How to use Self Service", "paragraphs": ["You can open Self Service from the Launchpad, Spotlight or by clicking its icon directly from /Applications:", "Self Service has several categories as shown on the left hand side. Some categories may not show up for all users or at all times (e.g. Compliance will only show if your Mac is non-compliant).", "Here are the descriptions for the categories:", "All Shows all packages in Self Service.", "Just Arrived Shows new packages just released from the Release Train (runs every 2 weeks)", "For You Shows all apps specifically relevant for you and your Mac such as new app versions", "Bookmarks Quick links to your most commonly used apps and sites", "Apps Shows all standard apps", "Compliance Shows items to fix your Mac's compliance issues (if any exist)", "First Aid Shows all packages for remediating and fixing your Mac if it becomes non-compliant", "For Techs Shows advanced packages for IT techs to use if your Mac becomes non-compliant or has other issues (login required for Self Service)", "Release Train Shows new packages being tested for release via the Release Train packaging process", "Hardware Return. Shows apps to ensure you properly sign out of your Mac if it is being returned, wiped or sent back to IT", "PoC Shows proof-of-concept apps being tested", "Click the info button ⓘ if you would like to see more information on the app or policy.", "You can easily search for any app or policy in the upper left corner.", "Each package for installation has a corresponding package for uninstallation."], "content": "You can open Self Service from the Launchpad, Spotlight or by clicking its icon directly from /Applications: Self Service has several categories as shown on the left hand side. Some categories may not show up for all users or at all times (e.g. Compliance will only show if your Mac is non-compliant). Here are the descriptions for the categories: All Shows all packages in Self Service. Just Arrived Shows new packages just released from the Release Train (runs every 2 weeks) For You Shows all apps specifically relevant for you and your Mac such as new app versions Bookmarks Quick links to your most commonly used apps and sites Apps Shows all standard apps Compliance Shows items to fix your Mac's compliance issues (if any exist) First Aid Shows all packages for remediating and fixing your Mac if it becomes non-compliant For Techs Shows advanced packages for IT techs to use if your Mac becomes non-compliant or has other issues (login required for Self Service) Release Train Shows new packages being tested for release via the Release Train packaging process Hardware Return. Shows apps to ensure you properly sign out of your Mac if it is being returned, wiped or sent back to IT PoC Shows proof-of-concept apps being tested Click the info button ⓘ if you would like to see more information on the app or policy. You can easily search for any app or policy in the upper left corner. Each package for installation has a corresponding package for uninstallation.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 106}, {"topic": "Self Service – MacOS", "section": "8.2 Notifications", "paragraphs": ["Self Service will send you notifications if actions are required from you. There are a few occasions where you might get these notifications."], "content": "Self Service will send you notifications if actions are required from you. There are a few occasions where you might get these notifications.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 107}, {"topic": "Self Service – MacOS", "section": "8.3 Non-compliant Mac", "paragraphs": ["If your Mac is non-compliant, you will be notified on a daily basis. This could be the case if your Mac has been changed and security mechanisms have been disabled or changed. For more information, see the section Compliancy.", "You will see the corresponding issue detected on your Mac with the ability to execute a remediation script to automatically fix your Mac."], "content": "If your Mac is non-compliant, you will be notified on a daily basis. This could be the case if your Mac has been changed and security mechanisms have been disabled or changed. For more information, see the section Compliancy. You will see the corresponding issue detected on your Mac with the ability to execute a remediation script to automatically fix your Mac.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 108}, {"topic": "SAP password sync – MacOS", "section": "9.1 How do I change my password with SAP password sync?", "paragraphs": ["Change your password on macOS Tahoe", "To change your account password with the built-in tool used for SAP password sync in macOS Tahoe or newer, follow these steps:", "For the best experience, quit all open apps on your Mac.", "Connect to SAP Corporate or VPN.", "Click on the key icon (Apple Kerberos) in the menu bar.", "Choose the \"Change Password\" command.", "Enter your current password as the \"Old Password.\"", "Type a new password in the \"New Password\" field. While you are typing in this field, an additional pop-up window will show whether or not what you have typed meets password requirements. The SAP password sync tool on macOS does not check for complexity on your device before submitting the password change to SAP systems. It does check for minimum password length.", "Enter the same new password in the \"Verify\" field.", "Click the \"Change Password\" button.", "The \"Password change successful\" dialog box appears when the password change is complete. This synchronizes your new SAP account password to your macOS account. Click the \"OK\" button.", "If the \"Password change failed\" dialog box appears, click the \"OK\" button and try to change your password again.", "After the password change is successful, it is a good idea to restart your Mac. This makes sure the password is completely in-sync and gives you a chance to verify it immediately."], "content": "Change your password on macOS Tahoe To change your account password with the built-in tool used for SAP password sync in macOS Tahoe or newer, follow these steps: For the best experience, quit all open apps on your Mac. Connect to SAP Corporate or VPN. Click on the key icon (Apple Kerberos) in the menu bar. Choose the \"Change Password\" command. Enter your current password as the \"Old Password.\" Type a new password in the \"New Password\" field. While you are typing in this field, an additional pop-up window will show whether or not what you have typed meets password requirements. The SAP password sync tool on macOS does not check for complexity on your device before submitting the password change to SAP systems. It does check for minimum password length. Enter the same new password in the \"Verify\" field. Click the \"Change Password\" button. The \"Password change successful\" dialog box appears when the password change is complete. This synchronizes your new SAP account password to your macOS account. Click the \"OK\" button. If the \"Password change failed\" dialog box appears, click the \"OK\" button and try to change your password again. After the password change is successful, it is a good idea to restart your Mac. This makes sure the password is completely in-sync and gives you a chance to verify it immediately.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 109}, {"topic": "SAP password sync – MacOS", "section": "SAP password sync on macOS Tahoe", "paragraphs": ["On macOS 13 or newer, SAP password sync uses a tool built-in to your Mac.", "The tool is activated when a key icon appears in the Mac menu bar.", "Once the new tool has been activated, it will provide the following features:", "automatically detect when are on or off SAP Corporate or VPN, as indicated by enabled or dimmed key icon in your menu bar", "automatically prompt to sign in after activation when connecting to SAP Corporate or VPN for the first time", "sync your SAP account password to your macOS account password during sign-in", "check if your SAP account and macOS account passwords are in sync whenever your Mac changes networks (when on SAP Corporate or VPN)", "allow you to change your SAP account password and sync the change to your macOS account", "The tool used for SAP password sync is not required for any other functionality and will appear dimmed and offline when you are not on SAP Corporate or VPN. This is normal behavior.", "This tool does not let you connect to file shares or a network home folder when it signs in and checks for password sync."], "content": "On macOS 13 or newer, SAP password sync uses a tool built-in to your Mac. The tool is activated when a key icon appears in the Mac menu bar. Once the new tool has been activated, it will provide the following features: automatically detect when are on or off SAP Corporate or VPN, as indicated by enabled or dimmed key icon in your menu bar automatically prompt to sign in after activation when connecting to SAP Corporate or VPN for the first time sync your SAP account password to your macOS account password during sign-in check if your SAP account and macOS account passwords are in sync whenever your Mac changes networks (when on SAP Corporate or VPN) allow you to change your SAP account password and sync the change to your macOS account The tool used for SAP password sync is not required for any other functionality and will appear dimmed and offline when you are not on SAP Corporate or VPN. This is normal behavior. This tool does not let you connect to file shares or a network home folder when it signs in and checks for password sync.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 110}, {"topic": "SAP password sync – MacOS", "section": "9.3 SAP password sync on earlier macOS versions", "paragraphs": ["Upgrade to macOS Tahoe to use SAP account sync."], "content": "Upgrade to macOS Tahoe to use SAP account sync.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 111}, {"topic": "SAP password sync – MacOS", "section": "9.4 Where is the SAP password sync tool on macOS Tahoe?", "paragraphs": ["The tool used for SAP Password sync is built-in to macOS. There is no app to install or open.", "Once SAP password sync has been activated, its key icon will appear in the menu bar. The key icon in the menu not surrounded by a circle, unlike an older similar tool."], "content": "The tool used for SAP Password sync is built-in to macOS. There is no app to install or open. Once SAP password sync has been activated, its key icon will appear in the menu bar. The key icon in the menu not surrounded by a circle, unlike an older similar tool.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 112}, {"topic": "SAP password sync – MacOS", "section": "9.5 How do I sign in for SAP password sync?", "paragraphs": ["The tool used for SAP password sync will sign in automatically after it is activated. You can also choose to sign in manually using its menu bar menu.", "It can only sign in successfully when on SAP Corporate or VPN."], "content": "The tool used for SAP password sync will sign in automatically after it is activated. You can also choose to sign in manually using its menu bar menu. It can only sign in successfully when on SAP Corporate or VPN.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 113}, {"topic": "SAP password sync – MacOS", "section": "9.6 Automatic sign-in", "paragraphs": ["SAP password sync tries to connect to SAP whenever your Mac changes network connections. If it can reach the resource it needs, it will try to sign in. If it cannot reach the resource it needs, you will need to connect to SAP Corporate or VPN first."], "content": "SAP password sync tries to connect to SAP whenever your Mac changes network connections. If it can reach the resource it needs, it will try to sign in. If it cannot reach the resource it needs, you will need to connect to SAP Corporate or VPN first.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 114}, {"topic": "SAP password sync – MacOS", "section": "9.7 First time sign-in", "paragraphs": ["If this is the first sign-in, the process starts by prompting you to enter the password for your SAP account, which is filled in for you. Enter your password and click the \"Sign In\" button. (You do not need to select any options from the \"Options\" pop-up menu.)", "After that, you will need to enter both of the following passwords. They may be the same, especially if you have just set up a new SAP computer.", "Your SAP account password", "The password for your macOS account, used to log into your Mac and unlock the screen saver", "Click the “Sync Password\" button. If you have entered both passwords correctly, SAP password sync will sync your SAP account (GLOBAL.CORP.SAP) password to your macOS user account password."], "content": "If this is the first sign-in, the process starts by prompting you to enter the password for your SAP account, which is filled in for you. Enter your password and click the \"Sign In\" button. (You do not need to select any options from the \"Options\" pop-up menu.) After that, you will need to enter both of the following passwords. They may be the same, especially if you have just set up a new SAP computer. Your SAP account password The password for your macOS account, used to log into your Mac and unlock the screen saver Click the “Sync Password\" button. If you have entered both passwords correctly, SAP password sync will sync your SAP account (GLOBAL.CORP.SAP) password to your macOS user account password.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 115}, {"topic": "SAP password sync – MacOS", "section": "9.8 Manual sign-in", "paragraphs": ["If SAP password sync does not sign in automatically, you may sign in manually.", "Connect to SAP Corporate or VPN.", "Click on the key icon in the menu bar.", "Choose one of the following commands from the key icon menu:", "How can I test the password for my local macOS account?", "If you suspect a password sync problem, try to confirm your local macOS account password. It may be best to do this without rebooting. To test the macOS account password without logging out of macOS, you have several choices.", "After a reboot, you may need to enter a FIleVault Recovery Key to unlock the disk encryption on your Mac and log in to your local macOS account.", "Once you verify your local macOS account password, you should know whether or not it is the same as your current SAP account password. That information is valuable when trying to get your SAP passwords synchronized or troubleshooting password-related problems on your Mac.", "Forget FileVault Recovery, refer to KB0528903", "If your local macOS account password and SAP account password are out-of-sync, you should use SAP password sync.", "For more information, refer to IKB0011533"], "content": "If SAP password sync does not sign in automatically, you may sign in manually. Connect to SAP Corporate or VPN. Click on the key icon in the menu bar. Choose one of the following commands from the key icon menu: How can I test the password for my local macOS account? If you suspect a password sync problem, try to confirm your local macOS account password. It may be best to do this without rebooting. To test the macOS account password without logging out of macOS, you have several choices. After a reboot, you may need to enter a FIleVault Recovery Key to unlock the disk encryption on your Mac and log in to your local macOS account. Once you verify your local macOS account password, you should know whether or not it is the same as your current SAP account password. That information is valuable when trying to get your SAP passwords synchronized or troubleshooting password-related problems on your Mac. Forget FileVault Recovery, refer to KB0528903 If your local macOS account password and SAP account password are out-of-sync, you should use SAP password sync. For more information, refer to IKB0011533", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 116}, {"topic": "Compliant Devices", "section": "10.1 Compliancy", "paragraphs": ["A compliant Mac is an SAP owned Mac running the latest version of macOS, properly enrolled into SAP IT management and with all SAP IT required apps and settings enabled.", "A non-compliant Mac means at least one of the following happened:", "No user is assigned to the Mac endpoint.", "Your Mac is unassigned to you in the MDM system.", "Your Mac is non-DEP and you have not approved UAMDM (User Approved Mobile Device Management)", "Your Mac is running an unsupported macOS version", "System Integrity Protection (SIP) has been disabled", "Privileges.app is not installed", "Endpoint Protection (\"anti-virus/anti-malware\") solution is not installed", "File Sharing has been enabled", "The macOS firewall has been disabled", "The root account has been enabled", "FileVault is disabled", "FileVault recovery key is missing from escrow", "Secure Boot Level is not set to Full Security mode (T2 enabled Macs only)", "External Boot Level is set to Allowed (T2 enabled Macs only)", "To fix any of the above items, simply open Self Service and click the \"Fix it\" button for the listed non-compliant item(s) to restore compliance for your Mac. In the event the issue cannot be auto-remediated for you, you will be presented with steps on how to remediate the issue. In some cases, your Mac may need to be restarted to apply the required changes.", "You can click on the \"i\" next to the item to view more information on why your Mac is non-compliant.", "You can click \"Fix It\" to remedy your Mac automatically. Once finished and restarted, Self Service will work as usual.", "The required macOS version is always the latest version available from Apple. Learn more about macOS.", "Secure Boot Level and External Boot Level require manual steps to remediate and cannot currently be automated.", "Non-compliance (\"Conditional Access\" or \"Limited Access\")", "In the event your Mac is non-compliant, your Mac may be subject to \"Conditional Access\" or \"Limited Access\" policies which will restricts access from your Mac to networks and services until your Mac is brought into compliance.", "Please use Self Service to remediate your non-compliance and bring your Mac into compliance. In the event your Mac is removed from network access and management, you must follow macOS - Self Service in order to re-enroll your Mac.", "All non-compliance issues can be remediated using any standard Internet connection."], "content": "A compliant Mac is an SAP owned Mac running the latest version of macOS, properly enrolled into SAP IT management and with all SAP IT required apps and settings enabled. A non-compliant Mac means at least one of the following happened: No user is assigned to the Mac endpoint. Your Mac is unassigned to you in the MDM system. Your Mac is non-DEP and you have not approved UAMDM (User Approved Mobile Device Management) Your Mac is running an unsupported macOS version System Integrity Protection (SIP) has been disabled Privileges.app is not installed Endpoint Protection (\"anti-virus/anti-malware\") solution is not installed File Sharing has been enabled The macOS firewall has been disabled The root account has been enabled FileVault is disabled FileVault recovery key is missing from escrow Secure Boot Level is not set to Full Security mode (T2 enabled Macs only) External Boot Level is set to Allowed (T2 enabled Macs only) To fix any of the above items, simply open Self Service and click the \"Fix it\" button for the listed non-compliant item(s) to restore compliance for your Mac. In the event the issue cannot be auto-remediated for you, you will be presented with steps on how to remediate the issue. In some cases, your Mac may need to be restarted to apply the required changes. You can click on the \"i\" next to the item to view more information on why your Mac is non-compliant. You can click \"Fix It\" to remedy your Mac automatically. Once finished and restarted, Self Service will work as usual. The required macOS version is always the latest version available from Apple. Learn more about macOS. Secure Boot Level and External Boot Level require manual steps to remediate and cannot currently be automated. Non-compliance (\"Conditional Access\" or \"Limited Access\") In the event your Mac is non-compliant, your Mac may be subject to \"Conditional Access\" or \"Limited Access\" policies which will restricts access from your Mac to networks and services until your Mac is brought into compliance. Please use Self Service to remediate your non-compliance and bring your Mac into compliance. In the event your Mac is removed from network access and management, you must follow macOS - Self Service in order to re-enroll your Mac. All non-compliance issues can be remediated using any standard Internet connection.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 117}, {"topic": "Compliant Devices", "section": "10.2 Notifications", "paragraphs": ["A non-compliant Mac will receive daily Notification Center notices, indicating non-compliance."], "content": "A non-compliant Mac will receive daily Notification Center notices, indicating non-compliance.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 118}, {"topic": "Compliant Devices", "section": "10.3 Assignment of Mac", "paragraphs": ["Your Mac must be assigned to you in the MDM management system.", "If your Mac is unassigned, you will be unable to get an SSO certificate issued to your Mac."], "content": "Your Mac must be assigned to you in the MDM management system. If your Mac is unassigned, you will be unable to get an SSO certificate issued to your Mac.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 119}, {"topic": "Compliant Devices", "section": "10.4 macOS version", "paragraphs": ["Your Mac must be running the latest version of macOS at all times (if some software not compatible with latest version of macOS, please contact software provider update software)", "You will be automatically notified when macOS updates are available directly in macOS and Notification Center.", "You will be automatically notified via email after 7 days of a release from Apple, if you have not updated your Mac yet.", "Mandatory Date For macOS:30 days after release (QEC aligned) the latest version becomes mandatory", "If you already update to latest version but still said you under old version in Self Service -> please run update inventory in Self Service"], "content": "Your Mac must be running the latest version of macOS at all times (if some software not compatible with latest version of macOS, please contact software provider update software) You will be automatically notified when macOS updates are available directly in macOS and Notification Center. You will be automatically notified via email after 7 days of a release from Apple, if you have not updated your Mac yet. Mandatory Date For macOS:30 days after release (QEC aligned) the latest version becomes mandatory If you already update to latest version but still said you under old version in Self Service -> please run update inventory in Self Service", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 120}, {"topic": "Compliant Devices", "section": "10.5 System Integrity Protection (SIP)", "paragraphs": ["Any Mac which has disabled SIP is non-compliant and SIP will automatically be re-enabled by MDM.", "Persistent disabling of SIP on your Mac may result in removal from all SAP Corporate services, network and MDM management.", "There is no exceptions to SIP enforcement. If you are disabling SIP on your Mac for any reason and don't understand how to resolve this, please contact IT Support."], "content": "Any Mac which has disabled SIP is non-compliant and SIP will automatically be re-enabled by MDM. Persistent disabling of SIP on your Mac may result in removal from all SAP Corporate services, network and MDM management. There is no exceptions to SIP enforcement. If you are disabling SIP on your Mac for any reason and don't understand how to resolve this, please contact IT Support.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 121}, {"topic": "Compliant Devices", "section": "10.6 Non Automated Enrollment", "paragraphs": ["If your Mac is not under Automated Device Enrolment (ADE), you will need to approve manually download and install and approve the MDM management profile to allow full management of your Mac.", "See Self Service - macOS for more details."], "content": "If your Mac is not under Automated Device Enrolment (ADE), you will need to approve manually download and install and approve the MDM management profile to allow full management of your Mac. See Self Service - macOS for more details.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 122}, {"topic": "Compliant Devices", "section": "10.7 Privileges.app", "paragraphs": ["Your Mac must have installed and running at all times."], "content": "Your Mac must have installed and running at all times.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 123}, {"topic": "Compliant Devices", "section": "10.8 Secure DNS", "paragraphs": ["Your Mac must have Cisco Secure Client installed and active to secure your DNS."], "content": "Your Mac must have Cisco Secure Client installed and active to secure your DNS.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 124}, {"topic": "Compliant Devices", "section": "10.9 Company Portal (Microsoft 365)", "paragraphs": ["Your Mac must be registered into Microsoft's Endpoint Manager, also known as the Company Portal app.", "See Company Portal - macOS for more information.", "Your Mac must be registered in order to access Microsoft 365 services (Outlook, Teams, etc.)."], "content": "Your Mac must be registered into Microsoft's Endpoint Manager, also known as the Company Portal app. See Company Portal - macOS for more information. Your Mac must be registered in order to access Microsoft 365 services (Outlook, Teams, etc.).", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 125}, {"topic": "Compliant Devices", "section": "10.10 Endpoint Protection", "paragraphs": ["Your Mac must have SAP IT provided endpoint protection software installed and active at all times.", "Endpoint protect software is the additional required level of protection for your Mac, behind the built-in macOS protections of Gatekeeper + XProtect and MRT."], "content": "Your Mac must have SAP IT provided endpoint protection software installed and active at all times. Endpoint protect software is the additional required level of protection for your Mac, behind the built-in macOS protections of Gatekeeper + XProtect and MRT.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 126}, {"topic": "Compliant Devices", "section": "10.11 Sharing Services", "paragraphs": ["Your Mac should not have Sharing services enabled, allowing your Mac to act as a server. Ensure you have disabled and sharing services (System Preferences → Sharing) and use approved SAP sharing services for your needs."], "content": "Your Mac should not have Sharing services enabled, allowing your Mac to act as a server. Ensure you have disabled and sharing services (System Preferences → Sharing) and use approved SAP sharing services for your needs.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 127}, {"topic": "Compliant Devices", "section": "10.12 macOS Firewall", "paragraphs": ["Your Mac must have the build in macOS firewall active at all times. The macOS firewall is designed to automatically leverage all signed macOS apps (with entitlements) to automatically set your firewall rules."], "content": "Your Mac must have the build in macOS firewall active at all times. The macOS firewall is designed to automatically leverage all signed macOS apps (with entitlements) to automatically set your firewall rules.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 128}, {"topic": "Compliant Devices", "section": "10.13 root Account (enabled)", "paragraphs": ["Any Mac which has enabled the root account is non-compliant and the account will automatically be disabled by MDM.", "Persistent disabling of root on your Mac may result in removal from all SAP Corporate services, network and MDM management.", "There is no exceptions to root enablement. If you are enabling root on your Mac for any reason and don't understand how to resolve this, please contact IT Support."], "content": "Any Mac which has enabled the root account is non-compliant and the account will automatically be disabled by MDM. Persistent disabling of root on your Mac may result in removal from all SAP Corporate services, network and MDM management. There is no exceptions to root enablement. If you are enabling root on your Mac for any reason and don't understand how to resolve this, please contact IT Support.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 129}, {"topic": "Compliant Devices", "section": "10.14 Filevault & Filevault Recovery Key", "paragraphs": ["Your Mac must have Filevault enabled at all times and there must be an escrowed encryption key stored in the SAP IT MDM management system. In the event your Mac is found to be missing a recovery key, you will be notified of non-compliance and you can use Self Service to generate a new key."], "content": "Your Mac must have Filevault enabled at all times and there must be an escrowed encryption key stored in the SAP IT MDM management system. In the event your Mac is found to be missing a recovery key, you will be notified of non-compliance and you can use Self Service to generate a new key.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 130}, {"topic": "Compliant Devices", "section": "10.15 Secure Boot Level", "paragraphs": ["Secure Boot is a feature native to your Mac.", "It ensures that your Mac only starts up from an OS that is trusted by Apple.", "Secure Boot must be set to \"Full Security\" on your Mac at all times."], "content": "Secure Boot is a feature native to your Mac. It ensures that your Mac only starts up from an OS that is trusted by Apple. Secure Boot must be set to \"Full Security\" on your Mac at all times.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 131}, {"topic": "Compliant Devices", "section": "10.16 External Boot Level", "paragraphs": ["External Boot Level is a feature native to your Mac.", "It ensures that your Mac is not allowed to boot from USB or Thunderbolt.", "External Boot Level must be set to \"Disallow booting...\" on your Mac at all times."], "content": "External Boot Level is a feature native to your Mac. It ensures that your Mac is not allowed to boot from USB or Thunderbolt. External Boot Level must be set to \"Disallow booting...\" on your Mac at all times.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 132}, {"topic": "Erase All Content and Settings", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["With macOS Monterey, Apple introduced a feature called Erase All Content and Settings to securely erase all of your apps and personal data while the operating system remains untouched.", "This feature makes it easier to hand over your Mac to another user, return it to IT or to erase your Mac and set it up again.", "Users should not hand over devices directly to other user and they should not erase their devices (LIT-Hold regulation)", "In case you need some data from this Mac, make sure that you back up your data first.", "Step-by-step Instructions", "How to use Erase All Content and Settings", "Your personal data is erased. In case you want to hand the Mac over to another user or return it to IT, you can now shut down the Mac."], "content": "With macOS Monterey, Apple introduced a feature called Erase All Content and Settings to securely erase all of your apps and personal data while the operating system remains untouched. This feature makes it easier to hand over your Mac to another user, return it to IT or to erase your Mac and set it up again. Users should not hand over devices directly to other user and they should not erase their devices (LIT-Hold regulation) In case you need some data from this Mac, make sure that you back up your data first. Step-by-step Instructions How to use Erase All Content and Settings Your personal data is erased. In case you want to hand the Mac over to another user or return it to IT, you can now shut down the Mac.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 133}, {"topic": "SAP GUI", "section": "12.1 Requirements", "paragraphs": ["SAP Single Sign-On (SSO) must be configured on your Mac before you proceed with setting up SAP GUI. For more information, see macOS - Single Sign-On."], "content": "SAP Single Sign-On (SSO) must be configured on your Mac before you proceed with setting up SAP GUI. For more information, see macOS - Single Sign-On.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 134}, {"topic": "SAP GUI", "section": "12.2 Installation of latest version of SAP GUI for Java", "paragraphs": ["Step 1: Install Secure Login Client", "Open Self Service → Apps and install SAP Secure Login Client.", "Step 2: Install the latest version of SAP GUI for Java", "Install SAP GUI for Java from Self Service.", "Once the installation is completed, launch SAP GUI from Applications→ SAP Clients → SAP GUI."], "content": "Step 1: Install Secure Login Client Open Self Service → Apps and install SAP Secure Login Client. Step 2: Install the latest version of SAP GUI for Java Install SAP GUI for Java from Self Service. Once the installation is completed, launch SAP GUI from Applications→ SAP Clients → SAP GUI.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 135}, {"topic": "SAP GUI", "section": "12.3 Where does SAP GUI for Java store my connection settings?", "paragraphs": ["~/Library/Preferences/SAP/"], "content": "~/Library/Preferences/SAP/", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 136}, {"topic": "SAP GUI", "section": "12.4 SAP GUI for Java", "paragraphs": ["macOS - SAP GUI for Java", "12.5 I need to create a custom connection string in SAP GUI for Java", "Cause: N/A", "Solution:", "The way you define a new SAP Connection in SAP GUI For Java differs slightly from SAP GUI For Windows. Let’s assume that you have the following connection information:", "Address: 10.1.3.40 System No: 02 In SAP GUI For Java, you need to get to the “Advanced” tab, click “Expert mode” and enter the following connection string:", "conn=/H/10.1.3.40/S/3202", "The address goes between /H/ and /S/ and the system number goes to the end of the string. If your system ID is 00, you need to enter 3200. If your system ID is 07, you need to enter 3207. In our case, your system ID is 02 so you need to enter 3202.", "Your connection string can contain additional parameters; such as your user name, client number, etc. Here are some sample connection strings:", "conn=/H/sapsrv/S/3204&jenc=MacTurkish&jloc=tr&cpg=1607&clnt=100&user=kerem", "Here are some sample connection strings going over routers (IP’s changed for security reasons):", "conn=/H/88.249.244.45/H/10.0.0.5/S/3200", "conn=/H/78.186.178.12/W/golive2013/H/192.168.2.10/S/3200"], "content": "macOS - SAP GUI for Java 12.5 I need to create a custom connection string in SAP GUI for Java Cause: N/A Solution: The way you define a new SAP Connection in SAP GUI For Java differs slightly from SAP GUI For Windows. Let’s assume that you have the following connection information: Address: 10.1.3.40 System No: 02 In SAP GUI For Java, you need to get to the “Advanced” tab, click “Expert mode” and enter the following connection string: conn=/H/10.1.3.40/S/3202 The address goes between /H/ and /S/ and the system number goes to the end of the string. If your system ID is 00, you need to enter 3200. If your system ID is 07, you need to enter 3207. In our case, your system ID is 02 so you need to enter 3202. Your connection string can contain additional parameters; such as your user name, client number, etc. Here are some sample connection strings: conn=/H/sapsrv/S/3204&jenc=MacTurkish&jloc=tr&cpg=1607&clnt=100&user=kerem Here are some sample connection strings going over routers (IP’s changed for security reasons): conn=/H/88.249.244.45/H/10.0.0.5/S/3200 conn=/H/78.186.178.12/W/golive2013/H/192.168.2.10/S/3200", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 137}, {"topic": "macOS - Microsoft Defender for Mac", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Microsoft Defender for Mac will start automatically on your Mac.", "You will also find an app under /Applications/Microsoft Defender.app.", "There is no visible indication in your Dock or menu bar that Defender is running unless you open the actual Microsoft Defender.app itself.", "Threat Detection and Response Requirements", "Defender builds on the already built-in protections in macOS and meets the requirements from SAP Global Security for Threat Detection and Response requirements as well as the macOS - Security Procedure and Workstation requirements. Specially it covers the following requirements:", "Centralized, managed endpoint protection service for addressing malware (EPP or Endpoint Protection)", "Endpoint Detection and Response functionalities (EDR) for SAP Global Security for telemetry data from the Mac endpoint including network and file and OS events", "Additional endpoint data loss prevention functionalities (DLP/eDLP) such as file monitoring", "Exclusions", "Exclusions can be seen in the configuration profile installed on your Mac for Defender.", "Settings → Security & Privacy → Profiles. Microsoft Defender Settings.", "Additional Resources", "Overview of Microsoft Defender for Endpoint on macOS", "Microsoft Defender for macOS - Endpoint Protection - Wiki@SAP", "Troubleshooting", "Troubleshoot performance issues for Microsoft Defender for Endpoint on macOS", "To report an issue", "To report an issue, please open a ticket with first level support. Make sure to include all relevant information, such as logs and screenshots of the error. Also, specify the name of the application that is affected by Defender or when Defender is affecting your work. If all the necessary information is provided, the first level support team will forward your case to the security team for further investigation."], "content": "Microsoft Defender for Mac will start automatically on your Mac. You will also find an app under /Applications/Microsoft Defender.app. There is no visible indication in your Dock or menu bar that Defender is running unless you open the actual Microsoft Defender.app itself. Threat Detection and Response Requirements Defender builds on the already built-in protections in macOS and meets the requirements from SAP Global Security for Threat Detection and Response requirements as well as the macOS - Security Procedure and Workstation requirements. Specially it covers the following requirements: Centralized, managed endpoint protection service for addressing malware (EPP or Endpoint Protection) Endpoint Detection and Response functionalities (EDR) for SAP Global Security for telemetry data from the Mac endpoint including network and file and OS events Additional endpoint data loss prevention functionalities (DLP/eDLP) such as file monitoring Exclusions Exclusions can be seen in the configuration profile installed on your Mac for Defender. Settings → Security & Privacy → Profiles. Microsoft Defender Settings. Additional Resources Overview of Microsoft Defender for Endpoint on macOS Microsoft Defender for macOS - Endpoint Protection - Wiki@SAP Troubleshooting Troubleshoot performance issues for Microsoft Defender for Endpoint on macOS To report an issue To report an issue, please open a ticket with first level support. Make sure to include all relevant information, such as logs and screenshots of the error. Also, specify the name of the application that is affected by Defender or when Defender is affecting your work. If all the necessary information is provided, the first level support team will forward your case to the security team for further investigation.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 138}, {"topic": "14. MacOS - How to add Input Language on MacOS", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["1. Access System Settings", "Click on the Apple logo at the top-left corner of your screen. Select System Settings.", "2. Navigate to Keyboard", "Click on Keyboard in the System Settings sidebar.", "Then click on Edit... beside Input Sources in the right side field.", "3. Add new languages", "Click the + button at the bottom of the Input Sources list.", "On the next popup window, select the desired language(s) from the list.", "Click Add to add the selected languages."], "content": "1. Access System Settings Click on the Apple logo at the top-left corner of your screen. Select System Settings. 2. Navigate to Keyboard Click on Keyboard in the System Settings sidebar. Then click on Edit... beside Input Sources in the right side field. 3. Add new languages Click the + button at the bottom of the Input Sources list. On the next popup window, select the desired language(s) from the list. Click Add to add the selected languages.", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 139}, {"topic": "15．Mac FAQ", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Q1: SAP & SAP-Corporate & SAP-Internet Wi-Fi EAP-TLS authentication", "Your Mac is automatically configured to use your SSO certificate to authenticate using TLS to SAP-Corporate. This removes your need to manually connect to SAP-Corporate using your GLOBAL username and password. It also removes the issue of needing to update your password when you change your GLOBAL password.", "This configuration is automatically done when your SSO certificate is installed.", "Q2: How am I connected to the Internet?", "Your Mac's internet connection will route through a firewall (Palo Alto Network Next Generation Internet firewall). Your Mac is issued a default route to the Internet (your default gateway). Services such as Messages, FaceTime and Push Notifications will \"just work\" as expected. In the event you are using a non-approved service such as Peer to Peer applications or bit torrents or smtp (email), these are blocked at the firewall level and will not work.", "The network firewall includes advanced threat protection and IPS as well as several other supporting network services such as network acceleration. This is all transparent and seamless to you.", "Q3: Can I use a proxy?", "No. Generally speaking proxy access in is blocked by default. This means that the routing to an SAP IT provided proxy is blocked by default on the network ACL.", "Q4: Do I need any proxy settings enabled on my Mac?", "No.", "Q5: The profile “Access & Authentication” is installed, but there’s no SSO certificate in Keychain.", "To get a new certificate, opt-out from SSO (using Self Service -> First Aid). This will remove the profile “Access & Authentication”. As soon as the profile disappeared, you can opt-in again using the same policy in Self Service. This will push the profile again, as well as a new certificate.", "Q6: I am prompted to enter my password in a dialog from an app, such as Safari or Chrome. It states '(The app) wants to sign using key \"Configuration Profiles\" in your Keychain.'", "This is normal. The Configuration Profile contains your SSO certificate. By design, macOS has an Access Control List to a certificate stored in your Keychain. When an app wants to access this certificate (such as when automatically authenticates you to a website), you will be prompted to authenticate if no prior approval is given. In this case, enter your password and click Always Allow to permanently approve the request.", "Q7: I can Add Printer even when I'm not connect to SAP-Corporate network, but I can't print.", "Normal Behavior, Currently, you still have to be connected to SAP-Corporate network to print to an office printer. Use VPN or connect to SAP-Corporate and your print job will succeed.", "Q8: Can Mac with M1/M2 install VMware Fusion?", "Yes, VMware Fusion 13pro support ARM based guest OS’s", "Q9: Did Mac with M1/M2 can install ARM based Win11 image right now?", "No, Win11 ARM Based still under Beta or Developer version, need wait release a public version", "Q10: Connection Failed. The connection shows an error of \"Unable to load GSS-API dyld Shared Library\" and Secure Login Client.app may not have loaded properly.", "The environment variables are missing from your Mac or you do not have Secure Login Client.app installed.", "Solution", "First verify you have installed Secure Login Client.app from Self Service. If you do not have it installed, install it from Self Service.", "If the issue persists:", "Option 1:", "In SAP GUI for Java, open the about dialog and press the \"More information\" button.", "Scroll down to or search for \"Environment Variables defining special directories\".", "There should be an entry like shown below and the exists value should be true. Likely this is not the case.", "-----------------------------------------------------------", "Environment Variables defining special directories", "—————————————————————————————", "...", "SNC_LIB = \"/Applications/Secure Login Client.app/Contents/MacOS/lib/libsapcrypto.dylib\" (exists: true)", "In case the entry is missing or exists is set to false, uninstall Secure Login Client and reinstall it from the Self-Service.", "After that, log off your Mac and back into your Mac.", "Start SAP GUI for Java and double check again in \"More information\" for the SNC_LIB entry.", "Now it should be there and exists should be true. Also connecting using SNC should work now.", "Option 2: (Note: This manual method using Terminal commands may resolve the issue but may not be persistent after a restart)", "Open Terminal and issue these three commands:", "launchctl setenv SNC_LIB /Applications/Secure\\ Login\\ Client.app/Contents/MacOS/lib/libsapcrypto.dylib;launchctl setenv SNC_LIB_64 /Applications/Secure\\ Login\\ Client.app/Contents/MacOS/lib/libsapcrypto.dylib", "launchctl setenv SSF_LIBRARY_PATH /Applications/Secure\\ Login\\ Client.app/Contents/MacOS/lib/libsapcrypto.dylib", "launchctl setenv SSF_LIBRARY_PATH_64 /Applications/Secure\\ Login\\ Client.app/Contents/MacOS/lib/libsapcrypto.dylib", "Close and re-open SAP GUI for Java and your connection should now work. If the issue persists, uninstall and re-install SAP Secure Login Client from Self Service.", "Q11:If Self Service shows \"This items is no longer available\" when I try to install a package.", "The previous installation and download failed or was corrupted.Wait 60 seconds and try to install the package again.", "Q12: I changed my SAP account password on another device. How do I get my Mac password set and in sync with my new SAP account password?", "Startup and log into your Mac using your old password (as your Mac doesn't know you changed your password yet). Connect to SAP Corporate or VPN. The SAP password sync tool will automatically check. During the check, it will see that your password doesn't match and ask you update it", ".", "Q13: Does SAP password sync check my SAP account when I am not on the SAP network?", "No. You must be on the SAP Corporate network or using SAP VPN.", "Q14: I changed my password without using SAP password sync. SAP password sync won't recognize the new password. What's going on?", "Possible password change replication delay", "There could be a few different things happening.", "SAP password sync on your Mac does not continuously poll or check your SAP GLOBAL account. It checks during specific triggering events. You will need to trigger one of those events for the next check to take place.", "If you change your SAP password through Office.com or other means external to your Mac, that password change needs to be replicated throughout SAP infrastructure first. You may need to wait for password replication to complete, so that the closest domain controller server has been informed about your new password.", "So, to get SAP password sync to recognize the new password:", "Create one of the triggering events — either make a network change, or choose the Reconnect command in the SAP password sync key menu. If this doesn't work and it has not been at least 45 minutes since your password change, try the next step.", "Wait at least 45-60 minutes after the last password change. Then, create one of the triggering events that causes SAP password sync to check your account.", "Q15:Does Apple Care for Enterprise available for every country?", "No", "Q16:Why I can’t find Apple Care for Enterprise activate for my SAP device", "There is a delay of some weeks until the Apple Care Subscription is activated for the device", "Q17:If CSD help user reset SAP Global Password, did Mac can direct get sync when Mac under login windows?", "No, user need enter machine using FileValut key and sync password using Apple Kerberos", "Q18: Raccount or Rescue account available for Mac?", "No, Raccount or Rescue account is for Windows", "Q19: If someone report their Mac has been stolen, do they need open lost Mode", "Yes, Need turn on Lost mode and create security Ticket"], "content": "Q1: SAP & SAP-Corporate & SAP-Internet Wi-Fi EAP-TLS authentication Your Mac is automatically configured to use your SSO certificate to authenticate using TLS to SAP-Corporate. This removes your need to manually connect to SAP-Corporate using your GLOBAL username and password. It also removes the issue of needing to update your password when you change your GLOBAL password. This configuration is automatically done when your SSO certificate is installed. Q2: How am I connected to the Internet? Your Mac's internet connection will route through a firewall (Palo Alto Network Next Generation Internet firewall). Your Mac is issued a default route to the Internet (your default gateway). Services such as Messages, FaceTime and Push Notifications will \"just work\" as expected. In the event you are using a non-approved service such as Peer to Peer applications or bit torrents or smtp (email), these are blocked at the firewall level and will not work. The network firewall includes advanced threat protection and IPS as well as several other supporting network services such as network acceleration. This is all transparent and seamless to you. Q3: Can I use a proxy? No. Generally speaking proxy access in is blocked by default. This means that the routing to an SAP IT provided proxy is blocked by default on the network ACL. Q4: Do I need any proxy settings enabled on my Mac? No. Q5: The profile “Access & Authentication” is installed, but there’s no SSO certificate in Keychain. To get a new certificate, opt-out from SSO (using Self Service -> First Aid). This will remove the profile “Access & Authentication”. As soon as the profile disappeared, you can opt-in again using the same policy in Self Service. This will push the profile again, as well as a new certificate. Q6: I am prompted to enter my password in a dialog from an app, such as Safari or Chrome. It states '(The app) wants to sign using key \"Configuration Profiles\" in your Keychain.' This is normal. The Configuration Profile contains your SSO certificate. By design, macOS has an Access Control List to a certificate stored in your Keychain. When an app wants to access this certificate (such as when automatically authenticates you to a website), you will be prompted to authenticate if no prior approval is given. In this case, enter your password and click Always Allow to permanently approve the request. Q7: I can Add Printer even when I'm not connect to SAP-Corporate network, but I can't print. Normal Behavior, Currently, you still have to be connected to SAP-Corporate network to print to an office printer. Use VPN or connect to SAP-Corporate and your print job will succeed. Q8: Can Mac with M1/M2 install VMware Fusion? Yes, VMware Fusion 13pro support ARM based guest OS’s Q9: Did Mac with M1/M2 can install ARM based Win11 image right now? No, Win11 ARM Based still under Beta or Developer version, need wait release a public version Q10: Connection Failed. The connection shows an error of \"Unable to load GSS-API dyld Shared Library\" and Secure Login Client.app may not have loaded properly. The environment variables are missing from your Mac or you do not have Secure Login Client.app installed. Solution First verify you have installed Secure Login Client.app from Self Service. If you do not have it installed, install it from Self Service. If the issue persists: Option 1: In SAP GUI for Java, open the about dialog and press the \"More information\" button. Scroll down to or search for \"Environment Variables defining special directories\". There should be an entry like shown below and the exists value should be true. Likely this is not the case. ----------------------------------------------------------- Environment Variables defining special directories ————————————————————————————— ... SNC_LIB = \"/Applications/Secure Login Client.app/Contents/MacOS/lib/libsapcrypto.dylib\" (exists: true) In case the entry is missing or exists is set to false, uninstall Secure Login Client and reinstall it from the Self-Service. After that, log off your Mac and back into your Mac. Start SAP GUI for Java and double check again in \"More information\" for the SNC_LIB entry. Now it should be there and exists should be true. Also connecting using SNC should work now. Option 2: (Note: This manual method using Terminal commands may resolve the issue but may not be persistent after a restart) Open Terminal and issue these three commands: launchctl setenv SNC_LIB /Applications/Secure\\ Login\\ Client.app/Contents/MacOS/lib/libsapcrypto.dylib;launchctl setenv SNC_LIB_64 /Applications/Secure\\ Login\\ Client.app/Contents/MacOS/lib/libsapcrypto.dylib launchctl setenv SSF_LIBRARY_PATH /Applications/Secure\\ Login\\ Client.app/Contents/MacOS/lib/libsapcrypto.dylib launchctl setenv SSF_LIBRARY_PATH_64 /Applications/Secure\\ Login\\ Client.app/Contents/MacOS/lib/libsapcrypto.dylib Close and re-open SAP GUI for Java and your connection should now work. If the issue persists, uninstall and re-install SAP Secure Login Client from Self Service. Q11:If Self Service shows \"This items is no longer available\" when I try to install a package. The previous installation and download failed or was corrupted.Wait 60 seconds and try to install the package again. Q12: I changed my SAP account password on another device. How do I get my Mac password set and in sync with my new SAP account password? Startup and log into your Mac using your old password (as your Mac doesn't know you changed your password yet). Connect to SAP Corporate or VPN. The SAP password sync tool will automatically check. During the check, it will see that your password doesn't match and ask you update it . Q13: Does SAP password sync check my SAP account when I am not on the SAP network? No. You must be on the SAP Corporate network or using SAP VPN. Q14: I changed my password without using SAP password sync. SAP password sync won't recognize the new password. What's going on? Possible password change replication delay There could be a few different things happening. SAP password sync on your Mac does not continuously poll or check your SAP GLOBAL account. It checks during specific triggering events. You will need to trigger one of those events for the next check to take place. If you change your SAP password through Office.com or other means external to your Mac, that password change needs to be replicated throughout SAP infrastructure first. You may need to wait for password replication to complete, so that the closest domain controller server has been informed about your new password. So, to get SAP password sync to recognize the new password: Create one of the triggering events — either make a network change, or choose the Reconnect command in the SAP password sync key menu. If this doesn't work and it has not been at least 45 minutes since your password change, try the next step. Wait at least 45-60 minutes after the last password change. Then, create one of the triggering events that causes SAP password sync to check your account. Q15:Does Apple Care for Enterprise available for every country? No Q16:Why I can’t find Apple Care for Enterprise activate for my SAP device There is a delay of some weeks until the Apple Care Subscription is activated for the device Q17:If CSD help user reset SAP Global Password, did Mac can direct get sync when Mac under login windows? No, user need enter machine using FileValut key and sync password using Apple Kerberos Q18: Raccount or Rescue account available for Mac? No, Raccount or Rescue account is for Windows Q19: If someone report their Mac has been stolen, do they need open lost Mode Yes, Need turn on Lost mode and create security Ticket", "source": "MacOS Topic", "id": 140}, {"topic": "", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["ONE Support", "Internal- SAP Only", "Version control", "If you find any content in this document is out of date, feel free to contact the Authors for feedback!", "Thanks for your cooperation in advance!", "Contents", "1 SAP Meeting Rooms Standards 5", "1.1 Meeting Room Type - XS (1-2 Seat) 5", "1.2 Meeting Room Type - S (3-4 Seat) 5", "1.3 Meeting Room Type - M (5-8 Seat) 6", "1.4 Meeting Room Type : L (9-12 Seat) 6", "1.5 Meeting Room Type: XL (13-20 Seat) 6", "1.6 Meeting Room Type - Mobile Solution (5-12 Seat) 7", "1.7 Meeting Room Type: Customer Demo Room (9-12 Seat) 7", "1.8 Meeting Room Type: Open Spaces (2-10 Seat) 7", "1.9 Event Room/Multipurpose Room 7", "1.10 Meeting Room Type : BoardRoom/VIP 8", "2 Room types and how to book 8", "2.1 Meeting Room Types 8", "2.2 Standard Meeting Room Naming Convention at SAP 9", "2.2.1 Room Categories 9", "2.2.2 Room Technology 10", "2.3 How to Book a Meeting Room 11", "2.3.1 Directly via Microsoft Outlook Application 11", "2.3.2 Via SAP Room Booker Outlook Add-in 12", "2.3.3 Via FlexConnect Application 17", "2.3.4 Tips 17", "3 Meeting Room Checker tool 19", "3.1 Meeting Room Checker 19", "3.2 MRC Mobile App 34", "3.3 Meeting Room Checker - Planned Maintenance Process (KB1263842) 42", "4 Meeting Room Experience QR code sticker 44", "4.1 How does it work? 44", "​​​​​​​4.2 Sticker guidelines – How many and where the stickers should be pasted? 45", "4.3 How to request QR code stickers? 46", "5 eDoorpanels (Crestron) 47", "5.1 Teams panel User guide 47", "5.1.1 Check Room Availability 47", "5.1.2 Book an Ad-Hoc Meeting 47", "5.1.3 Book via QR Code (Optional) 48", "5.2 Logitech Sync Portal 49", "5.3 eDoorpanels Crestron 49", "5.3.1 What is a Crestron eDoorplate? 50", "5.3.2 What's in it for me? 50", "5.3.3 How to use a Crestron eDoorplate? 50", "5.3.4 Good to know 53", "5.3.5 Need Help? 53", "5.3.6 Internal IT Handling 53", "6 Surface hub 53", "7 Reactive Meeting Room Support 53", "7.1 Overview 54", "7.2 Step by Step Guide 54", "8 Microsoft Teams - FAQ Meeting in Meeting Rooms 56", "9 Meeting Room - How to use a (Video, BYOD) meeting room? 57", "9.1 What is a (Video, BYOD) meeting room? 57", "9.2 What's in it for me? 58", "9.3 How to use a (Video, BYOD) meeting room? 58", "10 Meeting Room - Ticket Handling Process 59", "11 FAQ 62", "SAP Meeting Rooms Standards"], "content": "ONE Support Internal- SAP Only Version control If you find any content in this document is out of date, feel free to contact the Authors for feedback! Thanks for your cooperation in advance! Contents 1 SAP Meeting Rooms Standards 5 1.1 Meeting Room Type - XS (1-2 Seat) 5 1.2 Meeting Room Type - S (3-4 Seat) 5 1.3 Meeting Room Type - M (5-8 Seat) 6 1.4 Meeting Room Type : L (9-12 Seat) 6 1.5 Meeting Room Type: XL (13-20 Seat) 6 1.6 Meeting Room Type - Mobile Solution (5-12 Seat) 7 1.7 Meeting Room Type: Customer Demo Room (9-12 Seat) 7 1.8 Meeting Room Type: Open Spaces (2-10 Seat) 7 1.9 Event Room/Multipurpose Room 7 1.10 Meeting Room Type : BoardRoom/VIP 8 2 Room types and how to book 8 2.1 Meeting Room Types 8 2.2 Standard Meeting Room Naming Convention at SAP 9 2.2.1 Room Categories 9 2.2.2 Room Technology 10 2.3 How to Book a Meeting Room 11 2.3.1 Directly via Microsoft Outlook Application 11 2.3.2 Via SAP Room Booker Outlook Add-in 12 2.3.3 Via FlexConnect Application 17 2.3.4 Tips 17 3 Meeting Room Checker tool 19 3.1 Meeting Room Checker 19 3.2 MRC Mobile App 34 3.3 Meeting Room Checker - Planned Maintenance Process (KB1263842) 42 4 Meeting Room Experience QR code sticker 44 4.1 How does it work? 44 ​​​​​​​4.2 Sticker guidelines – How many and where the stickers should be pasted? 45 4.3 How to request QR code stickers? 46 5 eDoorpanels (Crestron) 47 5.1 Teams panel User guide 47 5.1.1 Check Room Availability 47 5.1.2 Book an Ad-Hoc Meeting 47 5.1.3 Book via QR Code (Optional) 48 5.2 Logitech Sync Portal 49 5.3 eDoorpanels Crestron 49 5.3.1 What is a Crestron eDoorplate? 50 5.3.2 What's in it for me? 50 5.3.3 How to use a Crestron eDoorplate? 50 5.3.4 Good to know 53 5.3.5 Need Help? 53 5.3.6 Internal IT Handling 53 6 Surface hub 53 7 Reactive Meeting Room Support 53 7.1 Overview 54 7.2 Step by Step Guide 54 8 Microsoft Teams - FAQ Meeting in Meeting Rooms 56 9 Meeting Room - How to use a (Video, BYOD) meeting room? 57 9.1 What is a (Video, BYOD) meeting room? 57 9.2 What's in it for me? 58 9.3 How to use a (Video, BYOD) meeting room? 58 10 Meeting Room - Ticket Handling Process 59 11 FAQ 62 SAP Meeting Rooms Standards", "source": "Meeting Room Technologies", "id": 141}, {"topic": "", "section": "1.6 Meeting Room Type - Mobile Solution (5-12 Seat)", "paragraphs": ["Meeting Room Type: Customer Demo Room (9-12 Seat)", "Meeting Room Type: Open Spaces (2-10 Seat)", "Event Room/Multipurpose Room", "Meeting Room Type : BoardRoom/VIP", "More details could be found via below URL.", "Room types and how to book"], "content": "Meeting Room Type: Customer Demo Room (9-12 Seat) Meeting Room Type: Open Spaces (2-10 Seat) Event Room/Multipurpose Room Meeting Room Type : BoardRoom/VIP More details could be found via below URL. Room types and how to book", "source": "Meeting Room Technologies", "id": 142}, {"topic": "", "section": "2.1 Meeting Room Types", "paragraphs": ["Micro Meeting Rooms, Small Meeting Rooms, and Medium to Large Meeting Rooms, these 3 room types represent the most common meeting rooms globally we can find in SAP offices.", "2.2 Standard Meeting Room Naming Convention at SAP", "This standard naming convention makes it easy to find and reserve meeting rooms in any SAP office worldwide.", "Review the details below to understand how it works:"], "content": "Micro Meeting Rooms, Small Meeting Rooms, and Medium to Large Meeting Rooms, these 3 room types represent the most common meeting rooms globally we can find in SAP offices. 2.2 Standard Meeting Room Naming Convention at SAP This standard naming convention makes it easy to find and reserve meeting rooms in any SAP office worldwide. Review the details below to understand how it works:", "source": "Meeting Room Technologies", "id": 143}, {"topic": "", "section": "2.2.1 Room Categories", "paragraphs": ["The following are the meeting room categories:"], "content": "The following are the meeting room categories:", "source": "Meeting Room Technologies", "id": 144}, {"topic": "", "section": "2.2.2 Room Technology", "paragraphs": ["The following list is of the current room technologies:", "Note:", "Restricted rooms are indicated by an “R” at the end of the Room Category (e.g. SWR, DRR). To maximize meeting room availability for everyone, MRRs will no longer be created.", "BYOD: Bring Your Own Device – Referring to the room technology, your SAP device is required (no private device)"], "content": "The following list is of the current room technologies: Note: Restricted rooms are indicated by an “R” at the end of the Room Category (e.g. SWR, DRR). To maximize meeting room availability for everyone, MRRs will no longer be created. BYOD: Bring Your Own Device – Referring to the room technology, your SAP device is required (no private device)", "source": "Meeting Room Technologies", "id": 145}, {"topic": "", "section": "2.3 How to Book a Meeting Room", "paragraphs": ["2.3.1 Directly via Microsoft Outlook Application", "(Tip, you can add several rooms to a Meeting but uncheck the checkmark on all and set the checkmark only for the free Room which will be invited. Advantage: You can see in the schedule the free/busy status for all added rooms)", "Click on “New Items” then “Meeting” in Outlook.", "Select accordingly the meeting “Start time” and “End time”.", "Click on ”Scheduling Assistant” to easily view the availability of selected meeting rooms afterwards.", "Click on “Add Rooms”.", "Search Meeting Rooms:", "Type “MR” or “MRR” (for Restricted meeting rooms) followed by building code in the search field. All meeting rooms found in the building will be listed.", "Double-click the desired room/s (depending on the needed technology and capacity) from the list of rooms and click “OK” to check for room availability.", "You will be able to see the selected room/s availability. Proceed to make your decision on which meeting room to book and untick the other selected rooms.", "Click on the “Meeting” tab and proceed to schedule your meeting as per usual by adding the “Title”, “Required”, “Optional” participants ... then send the meeting request.", "You will receive a confirmation email for the booking of the room.", "2.3.2 Via SAP Room Booker Outlook Add-in", "First time using the SAP Room Booker Add-in? Ensure that you have installed the “Room Booker outlook Add-in”( IES Knowledge Base - SAP Room Booker - Installation and User Guide).", "Before opening SAP Room Booker, set a date and time for the meeting or meeting series you want to create. In the Rooms-tab, you can select and see the availability of up to 20 rooms, where you can review available dates and times.", "Search for a meeting room", "If you have specific rooms in mind, you can simply search for and select them in the search box at the bottom. If not, you can filter all meeting rooms by their category, equipment, and capacity. Below the search box, all rooms that match your filter criteria will be displayed.", "They are sorted by region, country, city, and building.", "Select the country, city, and building. Once a country is expanded, you can select the area within that country. When selecting 'Dublin, IE,' there is a choice of two buildings. Other countries may have more areas and more building to choose from within.", "Selecting a specific room automatically marks off its country and area.", "2. Check for availability", "Select the rooms you want to check for availability. Then, click on the ‘Check availability’ button further up on the page.", "In the ‘Schedules’ tab, you can select the rooms you want to book for the dates/times selected. Then, click on the right button on the top to book the rooms. Rooms that are not available, cannot be selected. For a larger view, you can click on the left button on top.", "Mark the meeting room and click 'Book.'", "Then, the window will close, and a confirmation email will be sent to your inbox.", "Review the reservation.", "Show Room Pictures", "You can check the Room Pictures before book as well", "How to add a meeting room to your favorites", "When selecting the rooms to be checked for availability in the rooms-tab, you can use the ‘Add to favorites’-button, to add the selected rooms to a group of favorite rooms:", "After naming the new group of favorite rooms or selecting a group to add the rooms to, click on the ‘+’-button:", "That group will now be shown in the ‘Favorites’-tab where it can be selected quickly without having to filter through all the other rooms.", "To quickly add or remove a room from your favorites, click on the star icon next to the room name. To delete a whole group of favorites at once, just click on the minus next to the group name.", "2.3.3 Via FlexConnect Application", "Please find the step-by-step guide on how to use the FlexConnect app here."], "content": "2.3.1 Directly via Microsoft Outlook Application (Tip, you can add several rooms to a Meeting but uncheck the checkmark on all and set the checkmark only for the free Room which will be invited. Advantage: You can see in the schedule the free/busy status for all added rooms) Click on “New Items” then “Meeting” in Outlook. Select accordingly the meeting “Start time” and “End time”. Click on ”Scheduling Assistant” to easily view the availability of selected meeting rooms afterwards. Click on “Add Rooms”. Search Meeting Rooms: Type “MR” or “MRR” (for Restricted meeting rooms) followed by building code in the search field. All meeting rooms found in the building will be listed. Double-click the desired room/s (depending on the needed technology and capacity) from the list of rooms and click “OK” to check for room availability. You will be able to see the selected room/s availability. Proceed to make your decision on which meeting room to book and untick the other selected rooms. Click on the “Meeting” tab and proceed to schedule your meeting as per usual by adding the “Title”, “Required”, “Optional” participants ... then send the meeting request. You will receive a confirmation email for the booking of the room. 2.3.2 Via SAP Room Booker Outlook Add-in First time using the SAP Room Booker Add-in? Ensure that you have installed the “Room Booker outlook Add-in”( IES Knowledge Base - SAP Room Booker - Installation and User Guide). Before opening SAP Room Booker, set a date and time for the meeting or meeting series you want to create. In the Rooms-tab, you can select and see the availability of up to 20 rooms, where you can review available dates and times. Search for a meeting room If you have specific rooms in mind, you can simply search for and select them in the search box at the bottom. If not, you can filter all meeting rooms by their category, equipment, and capacity. Below the search box, all rooms that match your filter criteria will be displayed. They are sorted by region, country, city, and building. Select the country, city, and building. Once a country is expanded, you can select the area within that country. When selecting 'Dublin, IE,' there is a choice of two buildings. Other countries may have more areas and more building to choose from within. Selecting a specific room automatically marks off its country and area. 2. Check for availability Select the rooms you want to check for availability. Then, click on the ‘Check availability’ button further up on the page. In the ‘Schedules’ tab, you can select the rooms you want to book for the dates/times selected. Then, click on the right button on the top to book the rooms. Rooms that are not available, cannot be selected. For a larger view, you can click on the left button on top. Mark the meeting room and click 'Book.' Then, the window will close, and a confirmation email will be sent to your inbox. Review the reservation. Show Room Pictures You can check the Room Pictures before book as well How to add a meeting room to your favorites When selecting the rooms to be checked for availability in the rooms-tab, you can use the ‘Add to favorites’-button, to add the selected rooms to a group of favorite rooms: After naming the new group of favorite rooms or selecting a group to add the rooms to, click on the ‘+’-button: That group will now be shown in the ‘Favorites’-tab where it can be selected quickly without having to filter through all the other rooms. To quickly add or remove a room from your favorites, click on the star icon next to the room name. To delete a whole group of favorites at once, just click on the minus next to the group name. 2.3.3 Via FlexConnect Application Please find the step-by-step guide on how to use the FlexConnect app here.", "source": "Meeting Room Technologies", "id": 146}, {"topic": "", "section": "2.3.4 Tips", "paragraphs": ["If you already know the meeting room name you want to reserve, you can enter it directly into the meeting request “Required” field and then open the “Scheduling Assistant” to check the room availability.", "When you reserve a room, Outlook adds it to your frequently used names list, so the next time you wish to use the same room, you only need to type the first few characters of the name.", "More details could be found via URL.", "Meeting Room Checker tool", "Meeting Room Checker", "This part is to provide an overview of the Meeting Room Checker and the requirements surrounding the required use of the tool.", "The process for MR checks per room type can be found here. The checking process is being updated to allow for the new MR tools and standards.", "Please ensure you flag the check is compete while in the room, bring an appropriate device to complete the checks. Alternate testing technology between a MAC and a Windows device", "Meeting Room Checker should be used multiple times per day as UI to check on the status of rooms in a location.", "3.1 Meeting Room Checker", "Refer to KB0972740", "MRC Dashboard User Interface", "The Meeting Room Checker (MRC) has an interactive view of the room with live information on what is happening with the room.", "You can identify if the room is in use, if there are any alerts from the room, plus the inventory in the room, also you can check the number of the rooms are due to be checked and the one are completed.", "Banners are displayed with three colors, either in blue (informational), yellow (Warning/Attention) or red (Warning High Criticality) Please ensure you review the banner as it is information related to all MR items that impact operations.", "Meeting Room Details", "The top of this page will display the Information Panel Meeting Room Details", "Events and Tickets", "IT is OSS responsibility to action all Events that occur in the MRC Dashboard. After determining an Event's cause and deciding to take action, Events may be used to create Tickets.", "Depending on the events that have occurred for a room, these need to grouped and batched together when opening a ticket. For example, all events impacting an MTR are combined into a single ticket during.", "Note: Events which have different completion methods (Web vs. Mobile) may not be mixed.", "Tickets created through MRC Events will open their counterpart in SNOW.", "These tickets, then indicated by the Desktop or Mobile Symbol must be closed in the application(s).", "DO NOT CLOSE INC VIA SNOW", "Tickets created through MRC have their own Templates and Logic in regard to KB Article attachments. Henceforth, they must not be added retroactively in SNOW.", "Incidents will be displayed with their INC number. Service Requests, which will be introduced in the near future, but at the current time, are indicated by n/a.", "Upon selecting either an Event, or a Ticket, the details for the selected item and its correlations may be reviewed.", "DO NOT CLOSE INC VIA SNOW", "Information Buttons for support", "The information button accompanying Events aim to provide assistance with troubleshooting the issue you are facing and referencing a KB article which correlate to the issue at hand.", "Dashboard Application", "Creating and closing a Ticket intended for the Dashboard Application differs from the Mobile UI. Dashboard is normally a data driven task such as a Serial Number Mismatch, AV Room Type Change or Room Booker Creation/Change.", "The resolution for closing a Service Request in MRC aims for simplicity and efficiency.", "Given below example, a Service Request for an AV Type Change would take place.", "This Event Item is selected (1) and a popup for selection of items and values will appear (2). In mentioned example of something as an AV Type Change, this is listed singularly. After selecting Create Ticket, the confirmation for Ticket screen will then appear (3).", "Upon confirming the ticket creation with displayed items, a Ticket is created (4).", "Here, steps to resolve the issue at hand are completed, in below mentioned case, the AV Type change (KB0909160 Meeting Room Naming)would take place successfully.", "The In Progress Ticket may then be selected (4) and the Ticket Information popup will appear (5). Here, upon selection resolve, a resolution category for the issue must be selected from the dropdown (6)", "Upon completion, your Ticket in the Dashboard Interface will now be set to closed (7)", "Note : At the current time, it is not possible to create a Service Request in SNOW. This is a development item and upon completion, n/a will no longer be displayed as a Ticket Number.", "Tickets and their Resolution method/application are displayed via the Desktop and Mobile Symbol in the Tickets information Line", "For more information on the Mobile Application Event/Ticket Creation and Closure, please refer to - KB0972713 - MRC Mobile APP -", "Monitored Devices and Unmonitored Devices", "Monitored and Unmonitored Devices in your Meeting Room Details page show you which devices are cloud connected (Monitored) and which ones are managed manually (Unmonitored).", "Devices that must appear in the monitored devices list include LG screens, all Logitech devices, MTR rooms, eDoorplates (Crestron and Logitech), and WolfVision.", "Understanding the difference between the two is important when attempting to troubleshoot issues you may be facing in the field", "Monitored Devices have a cloud connection and as the name implies, are able to be monitored. Cloud connectivity allows the status of the device to be read/extracted so Events may populate your dashboard.", "Identifying where a problem stems from is oftentimes the difference between a quick fix and extended troubleshooting with various involved parties. If your MRC is displaying a state and you have access to the cloud, such as with Logitech Sync Portal, look at what information is displayed there, as this is the information it is communicating to the Meeting Room Checker application.", "Unmonitored Devices do not have established Cloud enviroment and therefore cannot be monitored.", "Data Management for these Devices is completed manually. These devices, unlike Monitored devices, may be se to inactive or have their status changed with documentation of the reason for this being mandator (written further below in Device Details).", "Device Details", "Clicking on a device in your Meeting room Details page will take you to the Meeting room Device page where you will find various bits of information correlating to your selection.", "Among the information displayed, the Equipment and Serial Number may also be saved.", "Upon selecting the magnifying glass symbol next to these numbers, pendant on access rights to Equipment Management in ISP, you will be able to query it and extract information.", "The Activity of the selected device may also be set here. If setting a device to inactive, a reasoning will be required.", "time and party who set this trigger will be recorded for reference.", "Monitored devices, such as displayed on the right receive their activity status automatically and must not be managed.", "Unmonitored Devices, however, may have this setting changed, such as below, where they have a separate trigger for denoting the status of the device.", "The Events History can help you determine trends or notice if some of your equipment has re-occurring problems to further escalate and/or raise awareness of it.", "Meeting Room Admin", "The Meeting Room Admin section provides additional in-depth information about Meeting Rooms not required for everyday utility, hence not in your dashboard Interface.", "Important points to note include noting the Meeting room Type, checking the rooms capacity or things as determining a rooms usage.", "Public Spaces (PUB) added manually should always have Auto Sync De-activated.", "Active state for the Public Spaces (PUB) should then be set to Activated.", "Meeting room Usage - Mandatory for OSS to Update", "Meeting Room Usage is a required set of information relevant to all Meeting Rooms in a Location. When selected, you will be given the option to choose what type of environment and/or specialities this room has. Ranging from Coffee Corners, Auditoriums, L1 or Board Support area's, or also, if the room has limited access in any way. Multiple Usages may be selected.", "The Usage should always be kept up to date and changed if the selected Meeting Rooms usage changes.", "Depending on the type of room (or due to other reasons), it may be required that checks and/or monitoring are deactivated. Both of these will however require valid reasoning and are tracked.", "Please note: If you disable checks or monitoring, you are responsible for ensuring they are reactivated. In the event of an escalation caused by a meeting room issue, the OSS technician who suppressed these items must be able to provide a valid justification.", "Always make sure to press the save button on your Meeting room Interface after selecting Usages. Dropdown requires the save function to ensure selected items stay populated", "Disabling Monitoring will initiate the suppression of Events for your Meeting Room Checker application.", "This means, that any Events triggered, regardless of source (Elastic/ISP/SAP Room Booker) will be disabled and no longer populate your Dashboard interface.", "Upon selecting the switch, a remark field will pop up where reasoning behind decision is requested.", "After submitting, you will then have the option to view (but not edit) this information as it will then be retrievable next to whoever submitted it.", "If you set something to this state due to common factors such as construction or short time on-premises outages, please confirm that this suppression has been lifted after completion and re-activation of room", "Disabling Checks", "Depending on Room Usage, there may not be a need for checks or the rooms themselves are inaccessible to OSS staff(this should be recored in the Meeting Room Usage area).", "These rooms may be excluded from future checks by disabling the Checks switch.", "All rooms and spaces require at least one check per month, unless approved with the local MR Champion (See Contacts Directory).", "Much like by the suppression of Events, this must also have valid reasoning behind it hence the reason for the request for more information upon selection.", "Remark alongside whoever had set this status will then be displayed next to the switch.", "3.2 MRC Mobile App", "MRC Mobile App is the app where the technician should perform the regular meeting room checks.", "To access the MRC Mobile app, you should use the following link : MeetingRoomChecker App", "Besides the Mobile App there is also the Dashboard, a separate KB - check KB0972740", "Before checking a room", "You'll get an overview of the pending checks and tickets opened, Available or Busy rooms will also be highlighted. Sorting order can also be adjusted alternating between using room name or check date.", "Confirm the location, on top you can see the selected location and Building. If you need to change, just tap on the settings icon on the upper right corner and select the desired Building in case you are responsible for more than one.", "Checking Rooms", "To start a check, simply tap on the desired room from the list or search for a typing room name using the search icon on bottom right of the screen.", "Observing the information", "You can then view a summary of the room, name, contact number, account and occupation; If the room is currently being used, and if there are open problems or events, this can be helpful while checking the room so you can already address those issues on the spot. Next check date and also the check interval.", "Devices A list of the devices in the room with the respective current status on real time under the Devices section.", "Events", "A list of open events or problems related to a device in the room, if we click on one of those events, we can review its information and current status from Elastic.", "Checks", "This is where the checklist is located, with the actions to perform on the check, that will need to actioned and marked as complete.", "Actions", "You'll need to tap Call Room, to perform a test call and confirm its working fine, and lastly Take a Picture of the meeting room taking directly with the phone.", "If by any chance, the room you are checking does not have technology that is not able to receive the test call, the Call button shall be greyed.", "Additionally, need to mark if room is OTX complaint.", "Once all is completed, the room check can be completed by tapping on the button.", "Resolving Tickets on the MRC App", "Selecting Tickets tab will show us all opened tickets for the selected location. To act on an opened ticket, simply tap on the desired one.", "Each ticket will have an icon, depending on if it’s intended to be solved in the Mobile App or MRC Dashboard.", "MRC Dashboard", "Mobile App", "We have relevant Room information and ticket information, you can proceed to review and check the opened events , can click on it, review and set resolution for each, as the example below", "You can also set the resolution in the very end, after clicking in Resolve you'll be able to select resolution for all Events too:", "Once all the issues are resolved onsite, proceed with the resolution of the Ticket, calling the room, taking a photo and mark it as OTX compliant or not.", "There can be cases where resolving the ticket is not possible from the Mobile App, such as, when we have a Meeting Room name mismatch or serial number, these have to be resolved within the Meeting Room Checker Admin Web page."], "content": "If you already know the meeting room name you want to reserve, you can enter it directly into the meeting request “Required” field and then open the “Scheduling Assistant” to check the room availability. When you reserve a room, Outlook adds it to your frequently used names list, so the next time you wish to use the same room, you only need to type the first few characters of the name. More details could be found via URL. Meeting Room Checker tool Meeting Room Checker This part is to provide an overview of the Meeting Room Checker and the requirements surrounding the required use of the tool. The process for MR checks per room type can be found here. The checking process is being updated to allow for the new MR tools and standards. Please ensure you flag the check is compete while in the room, bring an appropriate device to complete the checks. Alternate testing technology between a MAC and a Windows device Meeting Room Checker should be used multiple times per day as UI to check on the status of rooms in a location. 3.1 Meeting Room Checker Refer to KB0972740 MRC Dashboard User Interface The Meeting Room Checker (MRC) has an interactive view of the room with live information on what is happening with the room. You can identify if the room is in use, if there are any alerts from the room, plus the inventory in the room, also you can check the number of the rooms are due to be checked and the one are completed. Banners are displayed with three colors, either in blue (informational), yellow (Warning/Attention) or red (Warning High Criticality) Please ensure you review the banner as it is information related to all MR items that impact operations. Meeting Room Details The top of this page will display the Information Panel Meeting Room Details Events and Tickets IT is OSS responsibility to action all Events that occur in the MRC Dashboard. After determining an Event's cause and deciding to take action, Events may be used to create Tickets. Depending on the events that have occurred for a room, these need to grouped and batched together when opening a ticket. For example, all events impacting an MTR are combined into a single ticket during. Note: Events which have different completion methods (Web vs. Mobile) may not be mixed. Tickets created through MRC Events will open their counterpart in SNOW. These tickets, then indicated by the Desktop or Mobile Symbol must be closed in the application(s). DO NOT CLOSE INC VIA SNOW Tickets created through MRC have their own Templates and Logic in regard to KB Article attachments. Henceforth, they must not be added retroactively in SNOW. Incidents will be displayed with their INC number. Service Requests, which will be introduced in the near future, but at the current time, are indicated by n/a. Upon selecting either an Event, or a Ticket, the details for the selected item and its correlations may be reviewed. DO NOT CLOSE INC VIA SNOW Information Buttons for support The information button accompanying Events aim to provide assistance with troubleshooting the issue you are facing and referencing a KB article which correlate to the issue at hand. Dashboard Application Creating and closing a Ticket intended for the Dashboard Application differs from the Mobile UI. Dashboard is normally a data driven task such as a Serial Number Mismatch, AV Room Type Change or Room Booker Creation/Change. The resolution for closing a Service Request in MRC aims for simplicity and efficiency. Given below example, a Service Request for an AV Type Change would take place. This Event Item is selected (1) and a popup for selection of items and values will appear (2). In mentioned example of something as an AV Type Change, this is listed singularly. After selecting Create Ticket, the confirmation for Ticket screen will then appear (3). Upon confirming the ticket creation with displayed items, a Ticket is created (4). Here, steps to resolve the issue at hand are completed, in below mentioned case, the AV Type change (KB0909160 Meeting Room Naming)would take place successfully. The In Progress Ticket may then be selected (4) and the Ticket Information popup will appear (5). Here, upon selection resolve, a resolution category for the issue must be selected from the dropdown (6) Upon completion, your Ticket in the Dashboard Interface will now be set to closed (7) Note : At the current time, it is not possible to create a Service Request in SNOW. This is a development item and upon completion, n/a will no longer be displayed as a Ticket Number. Tickets and their Resolution method/application are displayed via the Desktop and Mobile Symbol in the Tickets information Line For more information on the Mobile Application Event/Ticket Creation and Closure, please refer to - KB0972713 - MRC Mobile APP - Monitored Devices and Unmonitored Devices Monitored and Unmonitored Devices in your Meeting Room Details page show you which devices are cloud connected (Monitored) and which ones are managed manually (Unmonitored). Devices that must appear in the monitored devices list include LG screens, all Logitech devices, MTR rooms, eDoorplates (Crestron and Logitech), and WolfVision. Understanding the difference between the two is important when attempting to troubleshoot issues you may be facing in the field Monitored Devices have a cloud connection and as the name implies, are able to be monitored. Cloud connectivity allows the status of the device to be read/extracted so Events may populate your dashboard. Identifying where a problem stems from is oftentimes the difference between a quick fix and extended troubleshooting with various involved parties. If your MRC is displaying a state and you have access to the cloud, such as with Logitech Sync Portal, look at what information is displayed there, as this is the information it is communicating to the Meeting Room Checker application. Unmonitored Devices do not have established Cloud enviroment and therefore cannot be monitored. Data Management for these Devices is completed manually. These devices, unlike Monitored devices, may be se to inactive or have their status changed with documentation of the reason for this being mandator (written further below in Device Details). Device Details Clicking on a device in your Meeting room Details page will take you to the Meeting room Device page where you will find various bits of information correlating to your selection. Among the information displayed, the Equipment and Serial Number may also be saved. Upon selecting the magnifying glass symbol next to these numbers, pendant on access rights to Equipment Management in ISP, you will be able to query it and extract information. The Activity of the selected device may also be set here. If setting a device to inactive, a reasoning will be required. time and party who set this trigger will be recorded for reference. Monitored devices, such as displayed on the right receive their activity status automatically and must not be managed. Unmonitored Devices, however, may have this setting changed, such as below, where they have a separate trigger for denoting the status of the device. The Events History can help you determine trends or notice if some of your equipment has re-occurring problems to further escalate and/or raise awareness of it. Meeting Room Admin The Meeting Room Admin section provides additional in-depth information about Meeting Rooms not required for everyday utility, hence not in your dashboard Interface. Important points to note include noting the Meeting room Type, checking the rooms capacity or things as determining a rooms usage. Public Spaces (PUB) added manually should always have Auto Sync De-activated. Active state for the Public Spaces (PUB) should then be set to Activated. Meeting room Usage - Mandatory for OSS to Update Meeting Room Usage is a required set of information relevant to all Meeting Rooms in a Location. When selected, you will be given the option to choose what type of environment and/or specialities this room has. Ranging from Coffee Corners, Auditoriums, L1 or Board Support area's, or also, if the room has limited access in any way. Multiple Usages may be selected. The Usage should always be kept up to date and changed if the selected Meeting Rooms usage changes. Depending on the type of room (or due to other reasons), it may be required that checks and/or monitoring are deactivated. Both of these will however require valid reasoning and are tracked. Please note: If you disable checks or monitoring, you are responsible for ensuring they are reactivated. In the event of an escalation caused by a meeting room issue, the OSS technician who suppressed these items must be able to provide a valid justification. Always make sure to press the save button on your Meeting room Interface after selecting Usages. Dropdown requires the save function to ensure selected items stay populated Disabling Monitoring will initiate the suppression of Events for your Meeting Room Checker application. This means, that any Events triggered, regardless of source (Elastic/ISP/SAP Room Booker) will be disabled and no longer populate your Dashboard interface. Upon selecting the switch, a remark field will pop up where reasoning behind decision is requested. After submitting, you will then have the option to view (but not edit) this information as it will then be retrievable next to whoever submitted it. If you set something to this state due to common factors such as construction or short time on-premises outages, please confirm that this suppression has been lifted after completion and re-activation of room Disabling Checks Depending on Room Usage, there may not be a need for checks or the rooms themselves are inaccessible to OSS staff(this should be recored in the Meeting Room Usage area). These rooms may be excluded from future checks by disabling the Checks switch. All rooms and spaces require at least one check per month, unless approved with the local MR Champion (See Contacts Directory). Much like by the suppression of Events, this must also have valid reasoning behind it hence the reason for the request for more information upon selection. Remark alongside whoever had set this status will then be displayed next to the switch. 3.2 MRC Mobile App MRC Mobile App is the app where the technician should perform the regular meeting room checks. To access the MRC Mobile app, you should use the following link : MeetingRoomChecker App Besides the Mobile App there is also the Dashboard, a separate KB - check KB0972740 Before checking a room You'll get an overview of the pending checks and tickets opened, Available or Busy rooms will also be highlighted. Sorting order can also be adjusted alternating between using room name or check date. Confirm the location, on top you can see the selected location and Building. If you need to change, just tap on the settings icon on the upper right corner and select the desired Building in case you are responsible for more than one. Checking Rooms To start a check, simply tap on the desired room from the list or search for a typing room name using the search icon on bottom right of the screen. Observing the information You can then view a summary of the room, name, contact number, account and occupation; If the room is currently being used, and if there are open problems or events, this can be helpful while checking the room so you can already address those issues on the spot. Next check date and also the check interval. Devices A list of the devices in the room with the respective current status on real time under the Devices section. Events A list of open events or problems related to a device in the room, if we click on one of those events, we can review its information and current status from Elastic. Checks This is where the checklist is located, with the actions to perform on the check, that will need to actioned and marked as complete. Actions You'll need to tap Call Room, to perform a test call and confirm its working fine, and lastly Take a Picture of the meeting room taking directly with the phone. If by any chance, the room you are checking does not have technology that is not able to receive the test call, the Call button shall be greyed. Additionally, need to mark if room is OTX complaint. Once all is completed, the room check can be completed by tapping on the button. Resolving Tickets on the MRC App Selecting Tickets tab will show us all opened tickets for the selected location. To act on an opened ticket, simply tap on the desired one. Each ticket will have an icon, depending on if it’s intended to be solved in the Mobile App or MRC Dashboard. MRC Dashboard Mobile App We have relevant Room information and ticket information, you can proceed to review and check the opened events , can click on it, review and set resolution for each, as the example below You can also set the resolution in the very end, after clicking in Resolve you'll be able to select resolution for all Events too: Once all the issues are resolved onsite, proceed with the resolution of the Ticket, calling the room, taking a photo and mark it as OTX compliant or not. There can be cases where resolving the ticket is not possible from the Mobile App, such as, when we have a Meeting Room name mismatch or serial number, these have to be resolved within the Meeting Room Checker Admin Web page.", "source": "Meeting Room Technologies", "id": 147}, {"topic": "", "section": "3.3 Meeting Room Checker - Planned Maintenance Process (KB1263842)", "paragraphs": ["This article provides guidance for handling meeting rooms that are currently under maintenance or undergoing renovation. It ensures proper tracking and closure of impacted devices until the MRC transitions to the new maintenance model in Q4 2025. This is also applicable for circumstances where a room needs to be closed due to hardware failure for unplanned maintenance.", "This is applicable to OSS Technicians and Meeting Room Champions that are responsible for monitoring and ticket management in the MRC v2 Dashboard and SNOW.", "There is currently no process to place an entire site into Maintenance Mode via MRC, this is planned for 2026.", "Maintenance Steps", "Where a meeting room will be offline for renovation or planned maintenance, please ensure you follow the following guidelines.", "Ensure that room cannot be bookable. Contact GRF (GRF-Room-Reservation Team) to turn off booking of Meeting Rooms.", "Work with GRF to clear all bookings made during construction time.", "Add ‘Under Construction’ poster to entryway(s) of room. (Posters)", "(For ONT Works like SMON Migration or Power Works from Facilities each room must be set to suppress events via the admin section)", "Before beginning any work in a meeting room, please follow these steps via the main MRC dashboard:", "Access the Room Admin Section", "Navigate to the required room in the dashboard.", "Open the Admin section for that room.", "Disable Monitoring:", "Use the Monitoring toggle to disable monitoring for the room.", "Enter a valid reason for disabling monitoring.", "Click Save before proceeding with any other changes.", "Disable Checks (if required):", "You may also disable meeting room checks for a room that is undergoing works.", "Enter a valid reason for disabling checks and then hit save before moving to the next step.", "Add Meeting Room Usage", "Ensure that the meeting room usage information is entered and recorded in the system.", "The room may look like this where both options are disabled, and the room is under construction.", "Any hardware actions that are required me be completed i.e. devices that need to be brought offline during the works or removed from the room.", "Power Down Devices:", "Ensure all devices in the affected meeting room are powered down and offline.", "Securely store any hardware removed from the room.", "Once the renovation is complete and the room is ready for use:", "Bring all relevant MR equipment back online.", "Update devices to ensure the latest firmware/software is applied.", "Check functionality of all components, including:", "Test calls and audio/video quality", "Screen sharing and displays, touch functions.", "Naming conventions of devices are correct", "Cloud enablement of hardware, LG SYNC Portal etc", "Confirm device health in MRC, ensuring all devices show online and healthy.", "Check to ensure all relevant meeting room equipment is accurately maintained", "Verification & Closure", "Once the renovation or works are complete and devices are confirmed to be functioning, please ensure you add meeting room monitoring and checks back again", "This is an high priority step to ensure the monitoring and checks are back to the expected behavior.", "Additional Notes", "This process ensures that planned works can temporarily pause event creation, preventing unnecessary events during renovations or upgrades. OSS Technicians are responsible for the final verification of equipment, as well as re-enabling meeting room checks and monitoring.", "Please also ensure you complete the remaining steps:", "Remove ‘Under Construction’ posters from outside the room.", "Clear booking block with Facilities.", "Ensure that room can be booked normally.", "Management for unplanned Maintenance", "Unplanned Maintenance Events", "All above best practices and steps for planned maintenance are still applicable .", "When events occur due to ongoing unplanned maintenance issues such as defective device that requires a replacement or AV installer to come onsite to complete a support request. The following steps are also required.", "Dismiss Open Events", "Dismiss all open events for the affected room.", "Disable events for the room to prevent additional alerts.", "Add a note to the distinguish that the room is closed and has unplanned maintenance.", "Suppress Further Events", "This process ensures that no new events are generated and suppresses any further occurrences during the maintenance period", "Meeting Room Experience QR code sticker", "To further enhance their experience, the OTX team has decided to adopt a globalized solution that incorporated a single QR code for all meeting rooms. This Meeting Room QR code sticker shall be the single point of entry for any meeting room needs.", "4.1 How does it work?", "When the end users scan the Meeting Room QR code sticker, they will be connected to the Meeting Room Experience home page. There, they can choose what type of support they need by clicking on the “IT Office Technology Experience” or “Global Real Estate & Facilities” icon.", "OTX icon will lead the end users to the OTX landing page, where they can choose between 4 options:", "Ask for immediate support", "Create an IT Ticket", "Onsite support channel on IT support portal", "Access the user guides", "Give their feedback"], "content": "This article provides guidance for handling meeting rooms that are currently under maintenance or undergoing renovation. It ensures proper tracking and closure of impacted devices until the MRC transitions to the new maintenance model in Q4 2025. This is also applicable for circumstances where a room needs to be closed due to hardware failure for unplanned maintenance. This is applicable to OSS Technicians and Meeting Room Champions that are responsible for monitoring and ticket management in the MRC v2 Dashboard and SNOW. There is currently no process to place an entire site into Maintenance Mode via MRC, this is planned for 2026. Maintenance Steps Where a meeting room will be offline for renovation or planned maintenance, please ensure you follow the following guidelines. Ensure that room cannot be bookable. Contact GRF (GRF-Room-Reservation Team) to turn off booking of Meeting Rooms. Work with GRF to clear all bookings made during construction time. Add ‘Under Construction’ poster to entryway(s) of room. (Posters) (For ONT Works like SMON Migration or Power Works from Facilities each room must be set to suppress events via the admin section) Before beginning any work in a meeting room, please follow these steps via the main MRC dashboard: Access the Room Admin Section Navigate to the required room in the dashboard. Open the Admin section for that room. Disable Monitoring: Use the Monitoring toggle to disable monitoring for the room. Enter a valid reason for disabling monitoring. Click Save before proceeding with any other changes. Disable Checks (if required): You may also disable meeting room checks for a room that is undergoing works. Enter a valid reason for disabling checks and then hit save before moving to the next step. Add Meeting Room Usage Ensure that the meeting room usage information is entered and recorded in the system. The room may look like this where both options are disabled, and the room is under construction. Any hardware actions that are required me be completed i.e. devices that need to be brought offline during the works or removed from the room. Power Down Devices: Ensure all devices in the affected meeting room are powered down and offline. Securely store any hardware removed from the room. Once the renovation is complete and the room is ready for use: Bring all relevant MR equipment back online. Update devices to ensure the latest firmware/software is applied. Check functionality of all components, including: Test calls and audio/video quality Screen sharing and displays, touch functions. Naming conventions of devices are correct Cloud enablement of hardware, LG SYNC Portal etc Confirm device health in MRC, ensuring all devices show online and healthy. Check to ensure all relevant meeting room equipment is accurately maintained Verification & Closure Once the renovation or works are complete and devices are confirmed to be functioning, please ensure you add meeting room monitoring and checks back again This is an high priority step to ensure the monitoring and checks are back to the expected behavior. Additional Notes This process ensures that planned works can temporarily pause event creation, preventing unnecessary events during renovations or upgrades. OSS Technicians are responsible for the final verification of equipment, as well as re-enabling meeting room checks and monitoring. Please also ensure you complete the remaining steps: Remove ‘Under Construction’ posters from outside the room. Clear booking block with Facilities. Ensure that room can be booked normally. Management for unplanned Maintenance Unplanned Maintenance Events All above best practices and steps for planned maintenance are still applicable . When events occur due to ongoing unplanned maintenance issues such as defective device that requires a replacement or AV installer to come onsite to complete a support request. The following steps are also required. Dismiss Open Events Dismiss all open events for the affected room. Disable events for the room to prevent additional alerts. Add a note to the distinguish that the room is closed and has unplanned maintenance. Suppress Further Events This process ensures that no new events are generated and suppresses any further occurrences during the maintenance period Meeting Room Experience QR code sticker To further enhance their experience, the OTX team has decided to adopt a globalized solution that incorporated a single QR code for all meeting rooms. This Meeting Room QR code sticker shall be the single point of entry for any meeting room needs. 4.1 How does it work? When the end users scan the Meeting Room QR code sticker, they will be connected to the Meeting Room Experience home page. There, they can choose what type of support they need by clicking on the “IT Office Technology Experience” or “Global Real Estate & Facilities” icon. OTX icon will lead the end users to the OTX landing page, where they can choose between 4 options: Ask for immediate support Create an IT Ticket Onsite support channel on IT support portal Access the user guides Give their feedback", "source": "Meeting Room Technologies", "id": 148}, {"topic": "", "section": "​​​​​​​4.2 Sticker guidelines – How many and where the stickers should be pasted?", "paragraphs": ["Depending of the size of the meeting room, from 1 up to 2 stickers are required. It is also asked to add a number of spare stickers to anticipate any degradation or internal move...", "4.3 How to request QR code stickers?", "*For local sticker printing, please provide the following technical information to your provider:", "Separation: CMYK / Material: SK-Folie (polymer)", "Schutzlaminat (polymer,matt) - (self-adhesive foil + protective laminate) ​​​", "Disinfection and cleaning is possible", "More details could be found via URL.", "eDoorpanels (Crestron)", "Teams panel User guide"], "content": "Depending of the size of the meeting room, from 1 up to 2 stickers are required. It is also asked to add a number of spare stickers to anticipate any degradation or internal move... 4.3 How to request QR code stickers? *For local sticker printing, please provide the following technical information to your provider: Separation: CMYK / Material: SK-Folie (polymer) Schutzlaminat (polymer,matt) - (self-adhesive foil + protective laminate) ​​​ Disinfection and cleaning is possible More details could be found via URL. eDoorpanels (Crestron) Teams panel User guide", "source": "Meeting Room Technologies", "id": 149}, {"topic": "", "section": "5.1.1 Check Room Availability", "paragraphs": ["Walk up to the Teams Panel mounted outside the meeting room.", "Available – Green LEDs Booked – Red LEDs", "The panel displays:", "Room name", "Current availability (green = available, red = occupied)", "Upcoming meetings for the day"], "content": "Walk up to the Teams Panel mounted outside the meeting room. Available – Green LEDs Booked – Red LEDs The panel displays: Room name Current availability (green = available, red = occupied) Upcoming meetings for the day", "source": "Meeting Room Technologies", "id": 150}, {"topic": "", "section": "5.1.2 Book an Ad-Hoc Meeting", "paragraphs": ["If the room is available:", "Tap \"Reserve\" on the screen.", "Select the duration (e.g., 15, 30, or 60 minutes).", "If you need it to start later, please scan the QR code with your SAP phone.", "Confirm the booking.", "Your meeting will be added to the room’s calendar, starting immediately."], "content": "If the room is available: Tap \"Reserve\" on the screen. Select the duration (e.g., 15, 30, or 60 minutes). If you need it to start later, please scan the QR code with your SAP phone. Confirm the booking. Your meeting will be added to the room’s calendar, starting immediately.", "source": "Meeting Room Technologies", "id": 151}, {"topic": "", "section": "5.1.3 Book via QR Code (Optional)", "paragraphs": ["If enabled, scan the QR code on the panel using your mobile device.", "This opens the room’s calendar in Teams.", "You can book the room for a later time slot.", "5.1.4 Useful Tips", "Extend a Meeting: Tap \"Extend\" or \"Manage\" on the panel if your meeting is running long (as long as there is availability).", "No Check-In Needed: The check-in button has been removed to simplify the experience.", "For more information, please see How to use Microsoft Teams panels devices - Microsoft Teams | Microsoft Learn", "5.2 Logitech Sync Portal", "The Logitech Sync Portal is a cloud-based device management platform designed for IT administrators to manage and monitor Logitech meeting room devices remotely.", "It works in conjunction with the Logitech Sync App, which is installed on meeting room computers.", "Key Features", "Remote Device Management: Monitor the health and status of Logitech devices across multiple rooms and locations.", "Alerts and Notifications: Receive alerts for device issues to minimize downtime.", "Refer KB1304095", "5.3 eDoorpanels Crestron", "The Crestron XiO Cloud® based eDoorplate is the next generation of meeting room scheduler at SAP. Crestron XiO Cloud management platform offers simple infrastructure, zero touch installation for local IT and is ready for SAP's network of the future.", "In the first phase the UI run on the Exchange UI.", "In the second phase the UI switch to the Teams Panel APP to align the user experience inside (MTR) and outside the room.", "The eDoorplate is directly communicating with the Exchange/Teams Cloud infrastructure.", "It can be used in different areas, at SAP, like Internal meeting rooms, customer rooms, training rooms and other.", "The new era of eDoorplate provides you native experience with the ability to view room and meeting details, reserve a meeting room, view upcoming reservations, and easily identify current meeting room availability status.", "With Crestron eDoorplate you can have a seamless meeting room booking experience throughout your workday!", "Important: Before entering the meeting room, remember to press the check-in button on the eDoorplate screen, so your reservation is not cancelled.", "Below you will find out the new features with Crestron eDoorplates."], "content": "If enabled, scan the QR code on the panel using your mobile device. This opens the room’s calendar in Teams. You can book the room for a later time slot. 5.1.4 Useful Tips Extend a Meeting: Tap \"Extend\" or \"Manage\" on the panel if your meeting is running long (as long as there is availability). No Check-In Needed: The check-in button has been removed to simplify the experience. For more information, please see How to use Microsoft Teams panels devices - Microsoft Teams | Microsoft Learn 5.2 Logitech Sync Portal The Logitech Sync Portal is a cloud-based device management platform designed for IT administrators to manage and monitor Logitech meeting room devices remotely. It works in conjunction with the Logitech Sync App, which is installed on meeting room computers. Key Features Remote Device Management: Monitor the health and status of Logitech devices across multiple rooms and locations. Alerts and Notifications: Receive alerts for device issues to minimize downtime. Refer KB1304095 5.3 eDoorpanels Crestron The Crestron XiO Cloud® based eDoorplate is the next generation of meeting room scheduler at SAP. Crestron XiO Cloud management platform offers simple infrastructure, zero touch installation for local IT and is ready for SAP's network of the future. In the first phase the UI run on the Exchange UI. In the second phase the UI switch to the Teams Panel APP to align the user experience inside (MTR) and outside the room. The eDoorplate is directly communicating with the Exchange/Teams Cloud infrastructure. It can be used in different areas, at SAP, like Internal meeting rooms, customer rooms, training rooms and other. The new era of eDoorplate provides you native experience with the ability to view room and meeting details, reserve a meeting room, view upcoming reservations, and easily identify current meeting room availability status. With Crestron eDoorplate you can have a seamless meeting room booking experience throughout your workday! Important: Before entering the meeting room, remember to press the check-in button on the eDoorplate screen, so your reservation is not cancelled. Below you will find out the new features with Crestron eDoorplates.", "source": "Meeting Room Technologies", "id": 152}, {"topic": "", "section": "5.3.1 What is a Crestron eDoorplate?", "paragraphs": ["A Crestron eDoorplate does more than make it easy to book a space. It gathers intelligence, facilitates productivity and opens up possibilities to a better meeting experience. It enables you to quickly determine the room availability and book free meeting room on the fly.", "With this new generation of technology, you can have a seamless meeting room booking experience throughout your workday!", "5.3.2 What's in it for me?", "The user-friendly touch-screen panel is based on SAP Room Booker, it therefore automatically sync to display all bookings that have been made.", "The process of booking a room via SAP Room Booker is not changing, however this new solution allows better management of internal bookings and improve the transparency of occupation and vacancy for you as the end user."], "content": "A Crestron eDoorplate does more than make it easy to book a space. It gathers intelligence, facilitates productivity and opens up possibilities to a better meeting experience. It enables you to quickly determine the room availability and book free meeting room on the fly. With this new generation of technology, you can have a seamless meeting room booking experience throughout your workday! 5.3.2 What's in it for me? The user-friendly touch-screen panel is based on SAP Room Booker, it therefore automatically sync to display all bookings that have been made. The process of booking a room via SAP Room Booker is not changing, however this new solution allows better management of internal bookings and improve the transparency of occupation and vacancy for you as the end user.", "source": "Meeting Room Technologies", "id": 153}, {"topic": "", "section": "5.3.3 How to use a Crestron eDoorplate?", "paragraphs": ["How to extend a meeting", "If you need more time and the meeting room is not reserved after your meeting, you can easily extend your meeting.", "Simply press the “Extend” button on the eDoorplate screen and select a new end time for your meeting given that there is no adjoining meeting scheduled.", "How to book an ad-hoc meeting? In case of an immediate need, you can also book a room directly from the screen when you are standing in front of a free meeting room. Press the \"+\" button and make your booking in 30-minute increments up to two hours. For any bookings longer then two hours please book via SAP Room Booker.", "For a same-day reservation, you can book a meeting using the timeline area:", "Quickly locate available rooms:", "The color of light around the Crestron eDoorplates indicates the status of the meeting room.", "Green: The room is free to book.", "Red: The room is booked and occupied"], "content": "How to extend a meeting If you need more time and the meeting room is not reserved after your meeting, you can easily extend your meeting. Simply press the “Extend” button on the eDoorplate screen and select a new end time for your meeting given that there is no adjoining meeting scheduled. How to book an ad-hoc meeting? In case of an immediate need, you can also book a room directly from the screen when you are standing in front of a free meeting room. Press the \"+\" button and make your booking in 30-minute increments up to two hours. For any bookings longer then two hours please book via SAP Room Booker. For a same-day reservation, you can book a meeting using the timeline area: Quickly locate available rooms: The color of light around the Crestron eDoorplates indicates the status of the meeting room. Green: The room is free to book. Red: The room is booked and occupied", "source": "Meeting Room Technologies", "id": 154}, {"topic": "", "section": "5.3.4 Good to know", "paragraphs": ["Please note restricted meeting rooms (MRR) can be booked via outlook only by special authorization (authorization can be granted by the meeting room admin of the room).", "To improve meeting room utilization, for restricted meeting rooms (MRR) it is now possible to make an ad-hoc booking via the Creston/Evoko e-Doorplate if the meeting room is not booked.", "No preauthorization is required for an ad-hoc booking."], "content": "Please note restricted meeting rooms (MRR) can be booked via outlook only by special authorization (authorization can be granted by the meeting room admin of the room). To improve meeting room utilization, for restricted meeting rooms (MRR) it is now possible to make an ad-hoc booking via the Creston/Evoko e-Doorplate if the meeting room is not booked. No preauthorization is required for an ad-hoc booking.", "source": "Meeting Room Technologies", "id": 155}, {"topic": "", "section": "5.3.5 Need Help?", "paragraphs": ["Crestron \"How to videos\" are available in the Crestron - Meeting Room Experience page", "For any question or assistance, go to itsupport.sap.com"], "content": "Crestron \"How to videos\" are available in the Crestron - Meeting Room Experience page For any question or assistance, go to itsupport.sap.com", "source": "Meeting Room Technologies", "id": 156}, {"topic": "", "section": "5.3.6 Internal IT Handling", "paragraphs": ["For local IT eDoorplate troubleshooting guides for automated INC please refer to the internal KB articles provided. Attach this KB ONLY to automated INC regarding eDoorplates(both crestron and Evoko) that are created from elastic or for INC created by customers.", "More details could be found via IKB0012962", "Surface hub", "Surface Hub Replacement 2025", "​This year, Microsoft will end support for the Surface Hub OS. As a result, we need to replace all Surface Hubs, both Gen 1 and Gen 2. We are targeting to have this replacement 100% complete by June 1st, 2025, to avoid any interruption of services in the spaces that have active Surface Hubs. All Surface Hubs must be replaced even if they are just being used as touch screen TVs.", "Most Surface Hubs should be replaced with LG touch screens connected to a BYOD Video Bar. However, that may not be the best solution for all spaces. Please refer to the 2025 OTX standards to determine the best fit for each room at your location. In some cases, disposal without replacement may make sense.", "Please update the tracker as you progress through the replacement: Surface Hub Upgrade Tracker - 2025.xlsx. (Note: Even if the Surface Hub is being replaced under a different project, please update the status in this tracker as well.)", "The tracker is based on Surface Hubs that have been logged into a room account in 2025. If there is a device at your site missing, please insert a line as needed.", "Given the tight timelines, we are asking that you start working with vendors to get all needed quotes and raise orders as soon as possible.", "Reactive Meeting Room Support"], "content": "For local IT eDoorplate troubleshooting guides for automated INC please refer to the internal KB articles provided. Attach this KB ONLY to automated INC regarding eDoorplates(both crestron and Evoko) that are created from elastic or for INC created by customers. More details could be found via IKB0012962 Surface hub Surface Hub Replacement 2025 ​This year, Microsoft will end support for the Surface Hub OS. As a result, we need to replace all Surface Hubs, both Gen 1 and Gen 2. We are targeting to have this replacement 100% complete by June 1st, 2025, to avoid any interruption of services in the spaces that have active Surface Hubs. All Surface Hubs must be replaced even if they are just being used as touch screen TVs. Most Surface Hubs should be replaced with LG touch screens connected to a BYOD Video Bar. However, that may not be the best solution for all spaces. Please refer to the 2025 OTX standards to determine the best fit for each room at your location. In some cases, disposal without replacement may make sense. Please update the tracker as you progress through the replacement: Surface Hub Upgrade Tracker - 2025.xlsx. (Note: Even if the Surface Hub is being replaced under a different project, please update the status in this tracker as well.) The tracker is based on Surface Hubs that have been logged into a room account in 2025. If there is a device at your site missing, please insert a line as needed. Given the tight timelines, we are asking that you start working with vendors to get all needed quotes and raise orders as soon as possible. Reactive Meeting Room Support", "source": "Meeting Room Technologies", "id": 157}, {"topic": "", "section": "7.1 Overview", "paragraphs": ["Important Update: Previously Reactive Meeting Room Support calls to CSD Hotline where the MR is included in the Power BI Dashboard were logged under the IES-CS-Reactive Meeting Room Support. This is no longer applicable.", "The IES-CS-Reactive Meeting Room Support Service Offering will no longer be used and is now retired as of 11/10/2024", "All Meeting Room Support and technology relevant support processes need to use IES-CS-Meeting Room Support & Technology as of 11/10/2024.", "For specific user issues see the following article:", "Meeting Room – IT CSD Troubleshooting Guide"], "content": "Important Update: Previously Reactive Meeting Room Support calls to CSD Hotline where the MR is included in the Power BI Dashboard were logged under the IES-CS-Reactive Meeting Room Support. This is no longer applicable. The IES-CS-Reactive Meeting Room Support Service Offering will no longer be used and is now retired as of 11/10/2024 All Meeting Room Support and technology relevant support processes need to use IES-CS-Meeting Room Support & Technology as of 11/10/2024. For specific user issues see the following article: Meeting Room – IT CSD Troubleshooting Guide", "source": "Meeting Room Technologies", "id": 158}, {"topic": "", "section": "7.2 Step by Step Guide", "paragraphs": ["Call received for Meeting Room Support. Gather ALL information before proceeding to the next step:", "Caller Name", "User ID", "Location", "Issues Experience etc.", "Attempt to resolve the issue remotely by utilising: Meeting Room – IT CSD Troubleshooting Guide", "If Resolved: Log the relevant information in an Incident and place in the \"IES-CS-Meeting Room Support & Technology\" Service Offering to close", "If Unresolved: Continue with step 3", "If the issue cannot be solved remotely, please follow the next steps to place a call via Microsoft Teams to Onsite Support (Note: All available Onsite Support Agents will receive the call!)", "Confirm the location of the End User again and open the Onsite Support Dashboard.", "Only locations visible in the dashboard are in scope.", "Search for the users location on the dashboard – filtering can be done by Region, Country, City and Building code. Ensuring location is in scope.", "Inform the End User that they will be placed on hold while you contact Onsite Support Team for additional support.", "Place end user on hold in Sinch Contact Centre.", "Do not end the call with the user as you may require more information also.", "Find the relevant location in Power Bi and click the \"Call\" button to place a call via Microsoft Teams to the local Onsite Support Team.", "If the call fails:", "We are aware that some CSD Agents experience issues when switching between CC365 and MS TEAMS calls. So, if you experience this please take the mobile number of the end-user and explain that you will close out the CC365 call while you contact Onsite Support in order to send someone down. And they will receive a call-back to confirm that Onsite Support are on the way.", "If there is no answer from Onsite Support Team please select the Notify Team button to notify the onsite team that there was no answer. This posts a missed call notice.", "Once the call is connected, provide the Onsite technician with all the relevant information in relation to the issue the End User is facing with Meeting Room Technology, including the severity and the Meeting Room location. Once all information has been provided to Onsite Support you can then proceed to the next step.", "Confirm that the Onsite Support agent is on the way to offer support to the End User and end the call.", "Resume the call with the End User on Sinch Contact Centre and advise them that the Onsite Support Agent is on the way.", "Update the status of the INC and pass the ticket to the Onsite Support Agent.", "1st level support is complete.", "More details could be found via KB0515985"], "content": "Call received for Meeting Room Support. Gather ALL information before proceeding to the next step: Caller Name User ID Location Issues Experience etc. Attempt to resolve the issue remotely by utilising: Meeting Room – IT CSD Troubleshooting Guide If Resolved: Log the relevant information in an Incident and place in the \"IES-CS-Meeting Room Support & Technology\" Service Offering to close If Unresolved: Continue with step 3 If the issue cannot be solved remotely, please follow the next steps to place a call via Microsoft Teams to Onsite Support (Note: All available Onsite Support Agents will receive the call!) Confirm the location of the End User again and open the Onsite Support Dashboard. Only locations visible in the dashboard are in scope. Search for the users location on the dashboard – filtering can be done by Region, Country, City and Building code. Ensuring location is in scope. Inform the End User that they will be placed on hold while you contact Onsite Support Team for additional support. Place end user on hold in Sinch Contact Centre. Do not end the call with the user as you may require more information also. Find the relevant location in Power Bi and click the \"Call\" button to place a call via Microsoft Teams to the local Onsite Support Team. If the call fails: We are aware that some CSD Agents experience issues when switching between CC365 and MS TEAMS calls. So, if you experience this please take the mobile number of the end-user and explain that you will close out the CC365 call while you contact Onsite Support in order to send someone down. And they will receive a call-back to confirm that Onsite Support are on the way. If there is no answer from Onsite Support Team please select the Notify Team button to notify the onsite team that there was no answer. This posts a missed call notice. Once the call is connected, provide the Onsite technician with all the relevant information in relation to the issue the End User is facing with Meeting Room Technology, including the severity and the Meeting Room location. Once all information has been provided to Onsite Support you can then proceed to the next step. Confirm that the Onsite Support agent is on the way to offer support to the End User and end the call. Resume the call with the End User on Sinch Contact Centre and advise them that the Onsite Support Agent is on the way. Update the status of the INC and pass the ticket to the Onsite Support Agent. 1st level support is complete. More details could be found via KB0515985", "source": "Meeting Room Technologies", "id": 159}, {"topic": "8 Microsoft Teams - FAQ Meeting in Meeting Rooms", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["For a general overview please check our article Microsoft Teams - Meeting in Meeting Rooms.", "Q1: How can I join Teams Meetings in Meeting Rooms ​​with MTR (Microsoft Teams Room) if the room has not been invited to the Teams Meeting?", "Whenever possible, it is recommended to invite the meeting room(s) directly to the Teams Meeting for best experience and simple \"one-tap-join\" from the meeting room. Even considering the limitation to book meeting rooms only up to 180 days in advance, it is still recommended to do this and renew the complete meeting series regularly and not book the room in parallel.", "If it is not possible to invite the meeting room, use the following options to include the room into the meeting:", "Add the room as participant during the meeting", "After joining the meeting on any device, open the Participant list (roster)", "Enter the room name in the \"Invite someone or dial a number\" box - the room name should be visible on the screen", "Accept the Video call on the device", "(MTR only, Windows only) Use the \"Add a room\" option", "Click \"Add a room\" on the pre-join meeting dialog", "The room should be automatically detected - select the room and continue with the meeting join", "​​If the room is not automatically detected, please use the option described above", "Accept the Video call on the device", "Q2: Is it possible to invite restricted rooms (\"xxR\") to Teams Meetings?", "Generally, yes, but restricted rooms cannot be invited to Channel Meetings in this case, the channel is the owner of the meeting and it is not possible to grant permissions based on channels in Roombooker. Channel meetings are meetings created in a channel, or a channel is selected when creating the meeting in the Teams client.​", "Note: The same restrictions, as described for public meeting rooms above, apply for some meeting room types and devices.", "Refer IKB0011185"], "content": "For a general overview please check our article Microsoft Teams - Meeting in Meeting Rooms. Q1: How can I join Teams Meetings in Meeting Rooms ​​with MTR (Microsoft Teams Room) if the room has not been invited to the Teams Meeting? Whenever possible, it is recommended to invite the meeting room(s) directly to the Teams Meeting for best experience and simple \"one-tap-join\" from the meeting room. Even considering the limitation to book meeting rooms only up to 180 days in advance, it is still recommended to do this and renew the complete meeting series regularly and not book the room in parallel. If it is not possible to invite the meeting room, use the following options to include the room into the meeting: Add the room as participant during the meeting After joining the meeting on any device, open the Participant list (roster) Enter the room name in the \"Invite someone or dial a number\" box - the room name should be visible on the screen Accept the Video call on the device (MTR only, Windows only) Use the \"Add a room\" option Click \"Add a room\" on the pre-join meeting dialog The room should be automatically detected - select the room and continue with the meeting join ​​If the room is not automatically detected, please use the option described above Accept the Video call on the device Q2: Is it possible to invite restricted rooms (\"xxR\") to Teams Meetings? Generally, yes, but restricted rooms cannot be invited to Channel Meetings in this case, the channel is the owner of the meeting and it is not possible to grant permissions based on channels in Roombooker. Channel meetings are meetings created in a channel, or a channel is selected when creating the meeting in the Teams client.​ Note: The same restrictions, as described for public meeting rooms above, apply for some meeting room types and devices. Refer IKB0011185", "source": "Meeting Room Technologies", "id": 160}, {"topic": "Meeting Room - How to use a (Video, BYOD) meeting room?", "section": "9.1 What is a (Video, BYOD) meeting room?", "paragraphs": ["A (Video, BYOD) meeting room is a room with Video Call solution where Bring Your Own Device* is required.", "Typically, in BYOD Rooms you will find displays with videobars and USB-C cables to connect.", "* BYOD: Bring Your Own Device - To Join an online meeting any Device can be used."], "content": "A (Video, BYOD) meeting room is a room with Video Call solution where Bring Your Own Device* is required. Typically, in BYOD Rooms you will find displays with videobars and USB-C cables to connect. * BYOD: Bring Your Own Device - To Join an online meeting any Device can be used.", "source": "Meeting Room Technologies", "id": 161}, {"topic": "Meeting Room - How to use a (Video, BYOD) meeting room?", "section": "9.2 What's in it for me?", "paragraphs": ["Technology available in this room enables you to connect to your video meeting easily by connecting a USB-C cable to your device.", "One Cable connection with USB-C for all features", "Presenting Content to the screen in the room", "Shared Audio / Video from the room to your device", "Charging up to 100W"], "content": "Technology available in this room enables you to connect to your video meeting easily by connecting a USB-C cable to your device. One Cable connection with USB-C for all features Presenting Content to the screen in the room Shared Audio / Video from the room to your device Charging up to 100W", "source": "Meeting Room Technologies", "id": 162}, {"topic": "Meeting Room - How to use a (Video, BYOD) meeting room?", "section": "9.3 How to use a (Video, BYOD) meeting room?", "paragraphs": ["1- Simply connect your device using the USB-C cable available in the meeting room:", "2- Start your meeting from your device, Teams Client, Zoom Client, Webex Client…", "Tips:", "To ensure that your audio, video and microphone selection is correctly configured, click on “More actions”, “Device settings”, and select the correct Speaker/Microphone and Video source:", "You can mute your microphone directly in the client on your device.", "You can check the videos below explaining how to use (it will open on a new window)", "Refer KB0835926"], "content": "1- Simply connect your device using the USB-C cable available in the meeting room: 2- Start your meeting from your device, Teams Client, Zoom Client, Webex Client… Tips: To ensure that your audio, video and microphone selection is correctly configured, click on “More actions”, “Device settings”, and select the correct Speaker/Microphone and Video source: You can mute your microphone directly in the client on your device. You can check the videos below explaining how to use (it will open on a new window) Refer KB0835926", "source": "Meeting Room Technologies", "id": 163}, {"topic": "10 Meeting Room - Ticket Handling Process", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Please follow the standards below when managing meeting room incident (INC) tickets:", "1. Internal IT Knowledge Articles:", "Internal IT knowledge articles cannot be attached to INC tickets (including those raised by customers, Elastic, or MRC tools) and are intentionally restricted.", "These articles contain sensitive, internal-only IT information that must not be shared externally.", "Do not raise KB gaps or flags related to attaching internal IT knowledge to INC, as this information is not intended for INC ticket attachments.", "2. Customer-Created INC Tickets:", "For all customer-reported INC tickets, you must attach one of the approved knowledge articles listed in the section below.", "These articles are public-facing and designed to support the business in using MR hardware.", "Knowledge attachments are required only for business-originated MR INC tickets.", "3. Internal IT Support Tickets:", "For INC tickets raised internally within IT, there is no requirement to attach knowledge articles when closing the ticket.", "Tickets created via the MRC tool do not require you to attach any KB articles when closing.", "This will not impact the OKRs for the Meeting Room service offering.", "A future update, planned for October 2025, will address this permanently.", "Attaching KB's to INC - Guidelines", "Please note the following guidance for attaching KB’s to INC in SNOW for customer generated INC.", "Internal IT support information cannot and should never be shared with customers.", "To support customer awareness and self-service, specific external KBs have been created.", "These articles do not contain sensitive internal IT information and are intended to help customers learn about meeting rooms and use the related technology effectively.", "This is intended to enable our customers to learn about Meeting rooms.", "Only these approved external KBs may be attached to INC tickets and are externally available to be attached.", "eDoorplate issues :", "Use the external KB0012962 to attach to INC from Elastic for eDoorplate issues.", "Use the KB0976092 to support you in troubleshooting eDoorplates INC and you cannot attach this to an INC as its internal IT article. (internal IT article, not to be shared with customers)", "Wolfvisions Issues :", "Use the external KB0948890 to attach to INC rom Elastic for WolfVision issues.", "Use the KB0946158 to support you in troubleshooting WolfVision INC and you cannot attach this to an INC as its internal IT article. (internal IT article, not to be shared with customers)", "MTR related Issues:", "Use the external KB0968022 to attach to INC from Elastic for MTR issues.", "Use the KB0875138 to support you in troubleshooting MTR INC and you cannot attach this to any INC as its internal IT article. (internal IT article, not to be shared with customers)", "BYOD ROOMS:", "Use the external KB0835926 to attach to INC from Customers", "Use the Following link which contains multiple BYOD related KBs to support you in troubleshooting BYOD INC and you cannot attach these to any INC as its internal IT article. (internal IT article, not to be shared with customers)", "Customer Incident: Use the external KB0516288 Reactive Meeting Room Support, for remaining customer incidents, as this includes information on how to request support and how to use the rooms.", "MRC Ticket Process", "Important - Closing INCs Created via the MRC Application", "For any tickets created through the MRC application, it is essential that you follow the relevant application process to close the incident.", "If you see a mobile symbol beside the ticket, you must use the mobile application to close the INC following the correct process.", "Do not close the INC directly in SNOW. ONLY VIA MRC MOBILE APP", "Serial Number Mismatches & Meeting Room (MR) Name Changes", "For any serial number mismatches or MR name changes, you will create a Service Request for the required updates via MRC tool (This process will be available planned October 1st).Until then, you will see an N/A symbol, this is expected.", "These events must be closed on the MRC Dashboard.", "They are represented by a desktop symbol.", "Planned Updates – Effective October 31st", "To improve the process and resolve current issues, the following changes will be implemented:", "The Assigned To field will be automatically updated during the initial creation of the INC. Resolving an known issue.", "When closing the INC via the mobile application, the Resolved Category will automatically update to the new category:", "Solved (Internal IT Knowledge Required)", "This new category provides support agents with a method to close incidents without attaching knowledge articles in cases where an Internal IT Knowledge article was used", "Refer KB1259004"], "content": "Please follow the standards below when managing meeting room incident (INC) tickets: 1. Internal IT Knowledge Articles: Internal IT knowledge articles cannot be attached to INC tickets (including those raised by customers, Elastic, or MRC tools) and are intentionally restricted. These articles contain sensitive, internal-only IT information that must not be shared externally. Do not raise KB gaps or flags related to attaching internal IT knowledge to INC, as this information is not intended for INC ticket attachments. 2. Customer-Created INC Tickets: For all customer-reported INC tickets, you must attach one of the approved knowledge articles listed in the section below. These articles are public-facing and designed to support the business in using MR hardware. Knowledge attachments are required only for business-originated MR INC tickets. 3. Internal IT Support Tickets: For INC tickets raised internally within IT, there is no requirement to attach knowledge articles when closing the ticket. Tickets created via the MRC tool do not require you to attach any KB articles when closing. This will not impact the OKRs for the Meeting Room service offering. A future update, planned for October 2025, will address this permanently. Attaching KB's to INC - Guidelines Please note the following guidance for attaching KB’s to INC in SNOW for customer generated INC. Internal IT support information cannot and should never be shared with customers. To support customer awareness and self-service, specific external KBs have been created. These articles do not contain sensitive internal IT information and are intended to help customers learn about meeting rooms and use the related technology effectively. This is intended to enable our customers to learn about Meeting rooms. Only these approved external KBs may be attached to INC tickets and are externally available to be attached. eDoorplate issues : Use the external KB0012962 to attach to INC from Elastic for eDoorplate issues. Use the KB0976092 to support you in troubleshooting eDoorplates INC and you cannot attach this to an INC as its internal IT article. (internal IT article, not to be shared with customers) Wolfvisions Issues : Use the external KB0948890 to attach to INC rom Elastic for WolfVision issues. Use the KB0946158 to support you in troubleshooting WolfVision INC and you cannot attach this to an INC as its internal IT article. (internal IT article, not to be shared with customers) MTR related Issues: Use the external KB0968022 to attach to INC from Elastic for MTR issues. Use the KB0875138 to support you in troubleshooting MTR INC and you cannot attach this to any INC as its internal IT article. (internal IT article, not to be shared with customers) BYOD ROOMS: Use the external KB0835926 to attach to INC from Customers Use the Following link which contains multiple BYOD related KBs to support you in troubleshooting BYOD INC and you cannot attach these to any INC as its internal IT article. (internal IT article, not to be shared with customers) Customer Incident: Use the external KB0516288 Reactive Meeting Room Support, for remaining customer incidents, as this includes information on how to request support and how to use the rooms. MRC Ticket Process Important - Closing INCs Created via the MRC Application For any tickets created through the MRC application, it is essential that you follow the relevant application process to close the incident. If you see a mobile symbol beside the ticket, you must use the mobile application to close the INC following the correct process. Do not close the INC directly in SNOW. ONLY VIA MRC MOBILE APP Serial Number Mismatches & Meeting Room (MR) Name Changes For any serial number mismatches or MR name changes, you will create a Service Request for the required updates via MRC tool (This process will be available planned October 1st).Until then, you will see an N/A symbol, this is expected. These events must be closed on the MRC Dashboard. They are represented by a desktop symbol. Planned Updates – Effective October 31st To improve the process and resolve current issues, the following changes will be implemented: The Assigned To field will be automatically updated during the initial creation of the INC. Resolving an known issue. When closing the INC via the mobile application, the Resolved Category will automatically update to the new category: Solved (Internal IT Knowledge Required) This new category provides support agents with a method to close incidents without attaching knowledge articles in cases where an Internal IT Knowledge article was used Refer KB1259004", "source": "Meeting Room Technologies", "id": 164}, {"topic": "11 FAQ", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Q1: How to share a Surface Hub screen to remote participants?", "To start sharing content, click on “Share content”, then the remote participants can view shared content in their own Teams client window", "Similar to your Teams Client, you may request access to control (the Surface Hub) by click on “…..”.", "Q2: How to project audio and video content?", "From your computer, tablet, or phone, use either the HDMI cable (where available) or wirelessly.", "Q3: How to use the Whiteboard feature on the Surface Hub?", "To start using the Whiteboard, click on Whiteboard tile, then you will be able to draw and write on a whiteboard like OneNote page.", "Q4: How to use the Built-in apps on the Surface Hub?", "To start using the built-in apps, click on”?”, then you will be able to work with Microsoft Edge, Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and OneNote."], "content": "Q1: How to share a Surface Hub screen to remote participants? To start sharing content, click on “Share content”, then the remote participants can view shared content in their own Teams client window Similar to your Teams Client, you may request access to control (the Surface Hub) by click on “…..”. Q2: How to project audio and video content? From your computer, tablet, or phone, use either the HDMI cable (where available) or wirelessly. Q3: How to use the Whiteboard feature on the Surface Hub? To start using the Whiteboard, click on Whiteboard tile, then you will be able to draw and write on a whiteboard like OneNote page. Q4: How to use the Built-in apps on the Surface Hub? To start using the built-in apps, click on”?”, then you will be able to work with Microsoft Edge, Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and OneNote.", "source": "Meeting Room Technologies", "id": 165}, {"topic": "", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["ONE Support", "Internal- SAP Only", "Version control", "If you find any content in this document is out of date, feel free to contact the Authors for feedback!", "Thanks for your cooperation in advance!", "Area: Network"], "content": "ONE Support Internal- SAP Only Version control If you find any content in this document is out of date, feel free to contact the Authors for feedback! Thanks for your cooperation in advance! Area: Network", "source": "Network", "id": 166}, {"topic": "1.Wireless LAN (WLAN)/ Wi-Fi​​​​​​​", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["A wireless network is a computer network that uses wireless data connections between network nodes. Examples of wireless networks include cell phone networks, wireless local area networks (WLANs), wireless sensor networks, etc.", "Wi-Fi Availability", "Wi-Fi is globally available in standard office spaces, meeting rooms, and coffee corners. Coverage may be limited or non-existent in areas like restrooms, stairways, elevators, parent-child offices, canteens, kitchens, sport areas, crosswalks between buildings, and outdoors.", "The following Wireless network are available in SAP offices:", "-SAP-", "SAP-GUEST", "SAP-IOT", "1.1 -SAP-", "Access: Only for SAP devices", "Encryption: Advanced (user/device certificate)", "Intended Use: General office tasks and daily work", "Security: Prevents cyber threats; Internet access limited to corporate purposes", "Note: We're introducing the new SAP Managed Office Network. After the migration to the SAP Managed Office Network, the network will change from SAP to -SAP- ('dash SAP dash'). For more information and an overview of migrated vs. non-migrated locations, see the Getting Started knowledge article."], "content": "A wireless network is a computer network that uses wireless data connections between network nodes. Examples of wireless networks include cell phone networks, wireless local area networks (WLANs), wireless sensor networks, etc. Wi-Fi Availability Wi-Fi is globally available in standard office spaces, meeting rooms, and coffee corners. Coverage may be limited or non-existent in areas like restrooms, stairways, elevators, parent-child offices, canteens, kitchens, sport areas, crosswalks between buildings, and outdoors. The following Wireless network are available in SAP offices: -SAP- SAP-GUEST SAP-IOT 1.1 -SAP- Access: Only for SAP devices Encryption: Advanced (user/device certificate) Intended Use: General office tasks and daily work Security: Prevents cyber threats; Internet access limited to corporate purposes Note: We're introducing the new SAP Managed Office Network. After the migration to the SAP Managed Office Network, the network will change from SAP to -SAP- ('dash SAP dash'). For more information and an overview of migrated vs. non-migrated locations, see the Getting Started knowledge article.", "source": "Network", "id": 167}, {"topic": "1.Wireless LAN (WLAN)/ Wi-Fi​​​​​​​", "section": "1.2 SAP-GUEST", "paragraphs": ["Access: Temporary Internet access for guests and test devices", "Encryption: Unencrypted", "Intended Use: Easy guest access with low restrictions", "Note: We're introducing the new SAP Managed Office Network. After the migration to the SAP Managed Office Network, the network will change from SAP-Guest to SAP-GUEST (all caps). The SAP-GUEST network comes with an updated network portal for login, including new sponsor links. For more information and an overview of migrated vs. non-migrated locations, see the Getting Started knowledge article."], "content": "Access: Temporary Internet access for guests and test devices Encryption: Unencrypted Intended Use: Easy guest access with low restrictions Note: We're introducing the new SAP Managed Office Network. After the migration to the SAP Managed Office Network, the network will change from SAP-Guest to SAP-GUEST (all caps). The SAP-GUEST network comes with an updated network portal for login, including new sponsor links. For more information and an overview of migrated vs. non-migrated locations, see the Getting Started knowledge article.", "source": "Network", "id": 168}, {"topic": "1.Wireless LAN (WLAN)/ Wi-Fi​​​​​​​", "section": "1.3 SAP-IOT", "paragraphs": ["The wireless and wired network SAP-IOT is designed specifically for non-standard devices, wired or wireless, belonging to SAP such as sensors or digital signage. Generally, the Internet of Things (IoT) refers to devices that exclusively communicate with the Internet and are centrally managed through a cloud-based instance.", "To use the SAP-IOT network, make sure that your IoT devices meet the following criteria:", "Access: Internet-only for IoT devices", "Encryption: Based on dedicated pre-shared keys", "Intended Use: IoT projects with non-standard devices", "Security: Basic security; no access to corporate resources/other networks", "How to onboard a device to SAP-IOT", "For information on how to onboard your IoT devices, see How to Onboard Your IoT Devices on the “SAP-IOT” Network.", "Miscellaneous information on the SAP-IOT network", "Before connecting your devices to the SAP-IOT network, you need to read and agree to the terms of use.", "Also, IoT projects need to provide the Security Self Service Application ID.", "Please note that all devices of a project:", "need to be registered with their MAC address (be careful if you use MAC randomization).", "will use the same pre-shared key (PSK) to connect to the wireless SSID SAP-IOT.", "require a primary and backup owner (project owner requires D-/I- or selected C-Users, backup users can be D-/I-/C-Users - DLs are not allowed).", "generate email reminders to the owners to extend their lifetime.", "can ignore the PSK if the device is connected wired.", "for large/regional projects requiring identical PSKs - please clone an initial project and name it accordingly (cloned projects use identical PSKs)", "devices need to request IP addresses via DHCP, no static leases allowed.", "If you require a static DHCP lease for your device, please open a ticket", "The PSK is auto generated to assure it is compliant with security requirements.", "How does the SAP-IOT network operate?", "Wireless IoT devices need to connect to the WLAN SSID SAP-IOT and use the PSK that is mapped to the project.", "Wired IoT devices need to get their wired port configured to be a member of the IOT-VLAN. This requires a ticket and needs to be requested here.", "Access from the Internet to SAP-IOT is not possible, communication to the Internet must start from the device being in SAP-IOT not vice versa.", "Internet access is supervised by a corporate firewall. Direct access to corporate resources from SAP-IOT is not possible.", "Please note that access for devices might be blocked, for example on request of SGS.", "For more information on SAP-IOT, see SAP-IOT Getting Started."], "content": "The wireless and wired network SAP-IOT is designed specifically for non-standard devices, wired or wireless, belonging to SAP such as sensors or digital signage. Generally, the Internet of Things (IoT) refers to devices that exclusively communicate with the Internet and are centrally managed through a cloud-based instance. To use the SAP-IOT network, make sure that your IoT devices meet the following criteria: Access: Internet-only for IoT devices Encryption: Based on dedicated pre-shared keys Intended Use: IoT projects with non-standard devices Security: Basic security; no access to corporate resources/other networks How to onboard a device to SAP-IOT For information on how to onboard your IoT devices, see How to Onboard Your IoT Devices on the “SAP-IOT” Network. Miscellaneous information on the SAP-IOT network Before connecting your devices to the SAP-IOT network, you need to read and agree to the terms of use. Also, IoT projects need to provide the Security Self Service Application ID. Please note that all devices of a project: need to be registered with their MAC address (be careful if you use MAC randomization). will use the same pre-shared key (PSK) to connect to the wireless SSID SAP-IOT. require a primary and backup owner (project owner requires D-/I- or selected C-Users, backup users can be D-/I-/C-Users - DLs are not allowed). generate email reminders to the owners to extend their lifetime. can ignore the PSK if the device is connected wired. for large/regional projects requiring identical PSKs - please clone an initial project and name it accordingly (cloned projects use identical PSKs) devices need to request IP addresses via DHCP, no static leases allowed. If you require a static DHCP lease for your device, please open a ticket The PSK is auto generated to assure it is compliant with security requirements. How does the SAP-IOT network operate? Wireless IoT devices need to connect to the WLAN SSID SAP-IOT and use the PSK that is mapped to the project. Wired IoT devices need to get their wired port configured to be a member of the IOT-VLAN. This requires a ticket and needs to be requested here. Access from the Internet to SAP-IOT is not possible, communication to the Internet must start from the device being in SAP-IOT not vice versa. Internet access is supervised by a corporate firewall. Direct access to corporate resources from SAP-IOT is not possible. Please note that access for devices might be blocked, for example on request of SGS. For more information on SAP-IOT, see SAP-IOT Getting Started.", "source": "Network", "id": 169}, {"topic": "1.Wireless LAN (WLAN)/ Wi-Fi​​​​​​​", "section": "1.4 Which Wi-Fi Network to Use Depending on Your Device", "paragraphs": ["Here’s a list of SAP’s Wi-Fi networks and which one you can use depending on your device.", "-SAP-", "* Login to SAP Wi-Fi with SAP user ID and password has been replaced by a certificate on the device.", "SAP-IOT", "SAP-GUEST", "* We're introducing the new SAP Managed Office Network. After the migration to the SAP Managed Office Network, the network will change from SAP-Guest to SAP-GUEST (all caps). The SAP-GUEST network comes with an updated network portal for login, including new sponsor links", "Which Wi-Fi network can I use?", "Depending on your device, you can use the following Wi-Fi networks:", "KB Network - Wireless LAN - Which Wi-Fi Network to Use Depending on Your Device"], "content": "Here’s a list of SAP’s Wi-Fi networks and which one you can use depending on your device. -SAP- * Login to SAP Wi-Fi with SAP user ID and password has been replaced by a certificate on the device. SAP-IOT SAP-GUEST * We're introducing the new SAP Managed Office Network. After the migration to the SAP Managed Office Network, the network will change from SAP-Guest to SAP-GUEST (all caps). The SAP-GUEST network comes with an updated network portal for login, including new sponsor links Which Wi-Fi network can I use? Depending on your device, you can use the following Wi-Fi networks: KB Network - Wireless LAN - Which Wi-Fi Network to Use Depending on Your Device", "source": "Network", "id": 170}, {"topic": "1.Wireless LAN (WLAN)/ Wi-Fi​​​​​​​", "section": "1.5.1 Windows: Selecting a Default Wireless Connection for SAP Networks", "paragraphs": ["Network Connections Available", "Over the past few years our networks have changed to ensure all employees can connect directly to all applications protected by the next generation firewalls. As a result, SAP buildings went through a complete restructuring of the wireless landscape. The following is a list of available networks in every SAP office:", "-SAP-: internal to employees serving the majority of requirements", "SAP-GUEST*: intended for visitor use cases", "* SAP-Guest network should be used by Concur employees in an SAP office who are using Concur VPNs to avoid connectivity interruption.", "Setting Default Network", "Open the Network and Internet Setting in your task bar by clicking the Wi-Fi icon.", "Click the right-facing arrow next to the Wi-Fi icon in the settings window.", "By default, the last network that was connected will reconnect upon return to the office. To change the network, select either -SAP- or SAP-GUEST from the dropdown. Select the \"Connect automatically\" option to set a network as your default. To switch networks, disconnect and choose a preferred network."], "content": "Network Connections Available Over the past few years our networks have changed to ensure all employees can connect directly to all applications protected by the next generation firewalls. As a result, SAP buildings went through a complete restructuring of the wireless landscape. The following is a list of available networks in every SAP office: -SAP-: internal to employees serving the majority of requirements SAP-GUEST*: intended for visitor use cases * SAP-Guest network should be used by Concur employees in an SAP office who are using Concur VPNs to avoid connectivity interruption. Setting Default Network Open the Network and Internet Setting in your task bar by clicking the Wi-Fi icon. Click the right-facing arrow next to the Wi-Fi icon in the settings window. By default, the last network that was connected will reconnect upon return to the office. To change the network, select either -SAP- or SAP-GUEST from the dropdown. Select the \"Connect automatically\" option to set a network as your default. To switch networks, disconnect and choose a preferred network.", "source": "Network", "id": 171}, {"topic": "1.Wireless LAN (WLAN)/ Wi-Fi​​​​​​​", "section": "1.5.2 macOS: Wi-Fi network selection for macOS", "paragraphs": ["Setting Default Network", "Open the Network Setting from the taskbar by clicking the Wi-Fi icon.", "Select the preferred network from the Other Networks dropdown (if not listed under Known Networks). Once selected, the network will show up under Known Networks.", "By connecting to a network Auto-Join will be enabled for that network. (Ex: user was previously connected to SAP network in the office, upon return to the office the SAP network will automatically join when the device is started). To switch networks, click Wi-Fi Settings.", "In order to connect to a specific network, the Auto-Join feature must be disabled for all other networks listed for a specific location or office. Click the three dots in the tree next to the network name and uncheck Auto-Join.", "KB macOS - WiFi network selection for macOS"], "content": "Setting Default Network Open the Network Setting from the taskbar by clicking the Wi-Fi icon. Select the preferred network from the Other Networks dropdown (if not listed under Known Networks). Once selected, the network will show up under Known Networks. By connecting to a network Auto-Join will be enabled for that network. (Ex: user was previously connected to SAP network in the office, upon return to the office the SAP network will automatically join when the device is started). To switch networks, click Wi-Fi Settings. In order to connect to a specific network, the Auto-Join feature must be disabled for all other networks listed for a specific location or office. Click the three dots in the tree next to the network name and uncheck Auto-Join. KB macOS - WiFi network selection for macOS", "source": "Network", "id": 172}, {"topic": "1.Wireless LAN (WLAN)/ Wi-Fi​​​​​​​", "section": "1.6.1 Wireless LAN - How to connect Guests to Wi-Fi at SAP legacy locations", "paragraphs": ["The Guest wireless network is currently undergoing a tech refresh project. Depending on the guest's location, two different technologies and slightly varied processes are used. You can refer to this article to verify whether your location employs the legacy process or the new one.", "Note: We are introducing the new SAP Managed Office Network. Following the migration to the SAP Managed Office Network, the network name will be updated from SAP-Guest to SAP-GUEST (in all caps). The revamped SAP-GUEST network includes an enhanced network portal for login, with new sponsor links. For more details and a comparison of migrated vs. non-migrated locations, see the following articles:", "Getting Started knowledge article.", "Migration Status of Locations", "For devices connecting to the new SAP-GUEST (in all caps) Wi-Fi, a slightly modified portal will open.", "Log in ➊", "To log in to either portal, guests must enter:", "E-mail address (used during registration - see sections 3 and 4) along with the password retrieved.", "Username/code and password provided by the SAP sponsor or reception desk.", "Access Code from the reception desk for migrated locations (SMON).", "SAP employees should log in using their SAP user ID and password.", "After accepting the terms of use, click Log In.", "Forgot password ➋", "If guests cannot remember their password, they choose Forgot password. They enter their username and choose Request new password, which will trigger an email containing their access data.", "Register via text/SMS ➌", "Guests can register for an account via text/SMS verification by providing a mobile phone number. They need to fill out the entire form, accept the terms of use, and select Register. A text message (SMS) with a PIN will be sent to their mobile phone for verification purposes.", "Entering the PIN in the SAP-Guest or SAP-GUEST Wi-Fi portal followed by selecting Log In will validate the account, which remains active for one day.", "If the text/SMS is delayed or not received, guests shall opt for SAP sponsor registration (see section 4).", "Delivery of an SMS is dependent on many external factors and must be judged as the best effort approach. A delivery cannot be guaranteed and may fail due to multiple reasons outside of SAPs responsibility.", "*Tip: * Guests can log in with any device, independent of which device was used for initial registration.", "Register via SAP sponsor ➍", "If guests do not have a mobile phone or if the text/SMS method is ineffective, they can register for an account through SAP sponsor approval. Guests need the SAP company e-mail address of their sponsor—the SAP employee who is hosting them. They must complete the entire form, specify their password and the desired account expiration period, then accept the terms of use and select Register.", "Initially, the status will display as Disabled in the SAP GUEST Wi-Fi portal.", "At migrated SAP-GUEST locations, the sponsor will get an email requesting confirmation of the guest's registration.", "*Important Tip:* The sponsor is required to connect to the SAP office network to click the confirmation link in the email. This link directs the sponsor to a webpage where they can approve or reject the guest's request.", "After the sponsor's confirmation, the access status in the Wi-Fi portal will change to Active, allowing the guest to connect to the SAP-GUEST Wi-Fi.", "Create account as sponsor", "Fill all required fields and select Create Account.", "For sites that are migrated to the SAP Managed Office Network (SAP-GUEST)", "This link takes you to a website where you can create an account as a sponsor.", "Global", "The homepage of the new sponsor portal allows for voucher creation for known visitors and facilitates the ability to generate multiple vouchers randomly. Different templates exist for various guest types depending on the length of stay (e.g., SAP_Contractor, SAP_Daily, SAP_Employee, SAP_Weekly).", "From this portal you can also select Pending Accounts tab at the top to approve pending access requests where you are named the sponsor or Manage Accounts to delete unused access permissions.", "You can read more SAP-Guest from IKB0010212 Wireless LAN - How to connect Guests to Wi-Fi at SAP locations"], "content": "The Guest wireless network is currently undergoing a tech refresh project. Depending on the guest's location, two different technologies and slightly varied processes are used. You can refer to this article to verify whether your location employs the legacy process or the new one. Note: We are introducing the new SAP Managed Office Network. Following the migration to the SAP Managed Office Network, the network name will be updated from SAP-Guest to SAP-GUEST (in all caps). The revamped SAP-GUEST network includes an enhanced network portal for login, with new sponsor links. For more details and a comparison of migrated vs. non-migrated locations, see the following articles: Getting Started knowledge article. Migration Status of Locations For devices connecting to the new SAP-GUEST (in all caps) Wi-Fi, a slightly modified portal will open. Log in ➊ To log in to either portal, guests must enter: E-mail address (used during registration - see sections 3 and 4) along with the password retrieved. Username/code and password provided by the SAP sponsor or reception desk. Access Code from the reception desk for migrated locations (SMON). SAP employees should log in using their SAP user ID and password. After accepting the terms of use, click Log In. Forgot password ➋ If guests cannot remember their password, they choose Forgot password. They enter their username and choose Request new password, which will trigger an email containing their access data. Register via text/SMS ➌ Guests can register for an account via text/SMS verification by providing a mobile phone number. They need to fill out the entire form, accept the terms of use, and select Register. A text message (SMS) with a PIN will be sent to their mobile phone for verification purposes. Entering the PIN in the SAP-Guest or SAP-GUEST Wi-Fi portal followed by selecting Log In will validate the account, which remains active for one day. If the text/SMS is delayed or not received, guests shall opt for SAP sponsor registration (see section 4). Delivery of an SMS is dependent on many external factors and must be judged as the best effort approach. A delivery cannot be guaranteed and may fail due to multiple reasons outside of SAPs responsibility. *Tip: * Guests can log in with any device, independent of which device was used for initial registration. Register via SAP sponsor ➍ If guests do not have a mobile phone or if the text/SMS method is ineffective, they can register for an account through SAP sponsor approval. Guests need the SAP company e-mail address of their sponsor—the SAP employee who is hosting them. They must complete the entire form, specify their password and the desired account expiration period, then accept the terms of use and select Register. Initially, the status will display as Disabled in the SAP GUEST Wi-Fi portal. At migrated SAP-GUEST locations, the sponsor will get an email requesting confirmation of the guest's registration. *Important Tip:* The sponsor is required to connect to the SAP office network to click the confirmation link in the email. This link directs the sponsor to a webpage where they can approve or reject the guest's request. After the sponsor's confirmation, the access status in the Wi-Fi portal will change to Active, allowing the guest to connect to the SAP-GUEST Wi-Fi. Create account as sponsor Fill all required fields and select Create Account. For sites that are migrated to the SAP Managed Office Network (SAP-GUEST) This link takes you to a website where you can create an account as a sponsor. Global The homepage of the new sponsor portal allows for voucher creation for known visitors and facilitates the ability to generate multiple vouchers randomly. Different templates exist for various guest types depending on the length of stay (e.g., SAP_Contractor, SAP_Daily, SAP_Employee, SAP_Weekly). From this portal you can also select Pending Accounts tab at the top to approve pending access requests where you are named the sponsor or Manage Accounts to delete unused access permissions. You can read more SAP-Guest from IKB0010212 Wireless LAN - How to connect Guests to Wi-Fi at SAP locations", "source": "Network", "id": 173}, {"topic": "1.Wireless LAN (WLAN)/ Wi-Fi​​​​​​​", "section": "1.7 Wireless LAN - Sponsor Portal for SMON Migrated Sites", "paragraphs": ["With the introduction of the SAP Managed Office Network (SMON), the SAP-GUEST Wi-Fi will be available as well as an enhanced network portal for logging in and creating new sponsored accounts. To access the new portal for creating accounts, you may refer to the link below:", "SAP Guest Portal", "Logging In", "Navigate to SAP Guest Portal and login using your D, I, or C-number then click sign on.", "Create Accounts Tab", "The Create Accounts tab is where guest accounts are created", "There are 4 types of accounts with varying maximum durations:", "SAP Contractor - Maximum duration of 1 year (when creating this type of account, you can specify the start and end date for the access duration)", "SAP_Daily - 12 Hours", "SAP_Employee - 1 day", "SAP_Weekly - 14 days", "There are 3 ways to Populate Guest Information:", "Known - input all the details of your guest", "Random - input the desired number of accounts and your desired prefix (e.g. your name-guest)", "Import - download and fill out the csv template and upload the filled-out file", "Manage Accounts Tab", "Manage Accounts tab allows you to manage your created accounts.", "Pending Accounts Tab", "Pending Accounts tab allows you to either Approve, Deny, or Delete Guest accounts created thru “Register via SAP Sponsor” in SAP-GUEST SSID", "Notices Tab", "Notices Tab displays information on whether the creation of accounts are successful or not", "Important Notes", "When creating SAP_Contractor account, the From and To time follows Germany Timezone and the times need to be adjusted accordingly based on your local timezone. Example: For PH, we need to substract 7 hours from the preset time for the access to be granted immediately.", "When using the Import option when creating accounts, it is recommended to leave the “Phone Number” column blank in the csv template to avoid errors during the account creation process.", "You will get more information for KB1256107 Sponsor Portal for SMON Migrated Site"], "content": "With the introduction of the SAP Managed Office Network (SMON), the SAP-GUEST Wi-Fi will be available as well as an enhanced network portal for logging in and creating new sponsored accounts. To access the new portal for creating accounts, you may refer to the link below: SAP Guest Portal Logging In Navigate to SAP Guest Portal and login using your D, I, or C-number then click sign on. Create Accounts Tab The Create Accounts tab is where guest accounts are created There are 4 types of accounts with varying maximum durations: SAP Contractor - Maximum duration of 1 year (when creating this type of account, you can specify the start and end date for the access duration) SAP_Daily - 12 Hours SAP_Employee - 1 day SAP_Weekly - 14 days There are 3 ways to Populate Guest Information: Known - input all the details of your guest Random - input the desired number of accounts and your desired prefix (e.g. your name-guest) Import - download and fill out the csv template and upload the filled-out file Manage Accounts Tab Manage Accounts tab allows you to manage your created accounts. Pending Accounts Tab Pending Accounts tab allows you to either Approve, Deny, or Delete Guest accounts created thru “Register via SAP Sponsor” in SAP-GUEST SSID Notices Tab Notices Tab displays information on whether the creation of accounts are successful or not Important Notes When creating SAP_Contractor account, the From and To time follows Germany Timezone and the times need to be adjusted accordingly based on your local timezone. Example: For PH, we need to substract 7 hours from the preset time for the access to be granted immediately. When using the Import option when creating accounts, it is recommended to leave the “Phone Number” column blank in the csv template to avoid errors during the account creation process. You will get more information for KB1256107 Sponsor Portal for SMON Migrated Site", "source": "Network", "id": 174}, {"topic": "1.Wireless LAN (WLAN)/ Wi-Fi​​​​​​​", "section": "1.8.1 What is IP address", "paragraphs": ["An Internet Protocol address (IP address) is numerical label such as 192.0.2.1 that is connected to a computer network that uses an Internet Protocol for communication. An IP address servers two main functions: network interface identification and location addressing. There are two IP versions: IPv4 and IPv6", "The important thing is it’s mandatory to obtain IP address for each SAP computer to connect to the Internet. You can get one PC IP address with methods:", "Precheck with command ipconfig/all to see if network connection is going through.", "Right click on Start button -> Run -> open \"cmd\".", "Enter command ipconfig/all and you will get below screen.", "You can get the example PC IP address 10.59.190.248. SAP computers IP address starts from 10.X.X.X. Meanwhile, SAP computers’ IP address is automatically assigned by SAP DHCP server.", "IPV4 address", "Example: SAP network ipv4 address like 10.58.x.x or 10.59.x.x or 10.207.x.x etc.", "Home WIFI ipv4 addresses like 192.168.x.x etc.", "Mobile Hotspot ipv4 addresses like 172.0.x.x etc.", "If not show like above, you need check if the network is connected or not.", "Default Gateway", "It should be similar to the ipv4pv4 address.", "Example: if Ipv4 address is 10.58.x.x, Default Gateway should be similar like 10.58.x.x", "DNS Servers", "(A DNS server is a computer server containing a directory of fully qualified domain names (FQDN) and the corresponding public IP addresses for that domain.)", "Should be set to automatic or correct DNS address."], "content": "An Internet Protocol address (IP address) is numerical label such as 192.0.2.1 that is connected to a computer network that uses an Internet Protocol for communication. An IP address servers two main functions: network interface identification and location addressing. There are two IP versions: IPv4 and IPv6 The important thing is it’s mandatory to obtain IP address for each SAP computer to connect to the Internet. You can get one PC IP address with methods: Precheck with command ipconfig/all to see if network connection is going through. Right click on Start button -> Run -> open \"cmd\". Enter command ipconfig/all and you will get below screen. You can get the example PC IP address 10.59.190.248. SAP computers IP address starts from 10.X.X.X. Meanwhile, SAP computers’ IP address is automatically assigned by SAP DHCP server. IPV4 address Example: SAP network ipv4 address like 10.58.x.x or 10.59.x.x or 10.207.x.x etc. Home WIFI ipv4 addresses like 192.168.x.x etc. Mobile Hotspot ipv4 addresses like 172.0.x.x etc. If not show like above, you need check if the network is connected or not. Default Gateway It should be similar to the ipv4pv4 address. Example: if Ipv4 address is 10.58.x.x, Default Gateway should be similar like 10.58.x.x DNS Servers (A DNS server is a computer server containing a directory of fully qualified domain names (FQDN) and the corresponding public IP addresses for that domain.) Should be set to automatic or correct DNS address.", "source": "Network", "id": 175}, {"topic": "1.Wireless LAN (WLAN)/ Wi-Fi​​​​​​​", "section": "1.8.2 What is MAC address", "paragraphs": ["MAC addresses are primarily assigned by device manufacturers, and are therefore often referred to as the burned-in address, or as an Ethernet hardware address, hardware address, or physical address. Each address can be stored in the interface hardware, such as its read-only memory, or by a firmware mechanism. Many network interfaces, however, support changing their MAC addresses. The address typically includes a manufacturer's organizationally unique identifier (OUI)", "How is a MAC Address Formatted?", "A MAC address is a sequence of 12 hexadecimal digits (0-9 and A-F). These digits are usually split into pairs and separated by colons or hyphens, like this: 00:1A:2B:3C:4D:5E.", "Why are MAC Address Important", "Network Management: Network administrators use MAC addresses to configure and manage networks, set up filters, and assign permissions.", "Security: MAC addresses can help restrict network access to known devices or identify unauthorized devices trying to connect to a network.", "Troubleshooting: When diagnosing network issues, knowing the MAC addresses involved can help pinpoint where problems are occurring.", "Finding Your MAC Address on Windows", "Press the Windows key + R to open the Run dialog box.", "Type cmd and press Enter to open the Command Prompt.", "In the Command Prompt, type ipconfig /all and press Enter.", "Scroll through the results until you find the network adapter you're using (Wi-Fi or Ethernet). The MAC address will be listed next to \"Physical Address\" and will look something like 00-1A-2B-3C-4D-5E", "Finding Your MAC Address on Mac/iPhone/iPad", "On a Mac computer (MacOS):", "Click on the Apple icon in the top left corner of the screen and select \"System Preferences\".", "Click on \"Network\" and choose the network connection you want to check on the left side (WiFi, Wired, etc.).", "Click on \"Advanced\" and go to the \"Hardware\" tab. The MAC address will be listed as the \"MAC Address\" at the top of the window.", "On an iPhone or iPad:", "Open the \"Settings\" app.", "Tap on \"General\" and then \"About\".", "Scroll down to find \"Wi-Fi Address,\" which is the MAC address of your device.", "Finding Your MAC Address on Android", "To locate the MAC address on an Android smartphone or tablet, you can use the following steps:", "Open the \"Settings\" app on your Android device.", "Scroll down and select \"About Phone\" or \"About Device\" (the exact wording can vary depending on the device).", "Tap on \"Status\" or \"Hardware Information.\"", "Look for \"Wi-Fi MAC address\" or simply \"MAC address.\" This will display the MAC address of your Wi-Fi network interface."], "content": "MAC addresses are primarily assigned by device manufacturers, and are therefore often referred to as the burned-in address, or as an Ethernet hardware address, hardware address, or physical address. Each address can be stored in the interface hardware, such as its read-only memory, or by a firmware mechanism. Many network interfaces, however, support changing their MAC addresses. The address typically includes a manufacturer's organizationally unique identifier (OUI) How is a MAC Address Formatted? A MAC address is a sequence of 12 hexadecimal digits (0-9 and A-F). These digits are usually split into pairs and separated by colons or hyphens, like this: 00:1A:2B:3C:4D:5E. Why are MAC Address Important Network Management: Network administrators use MAC addresses to configure and manage networks, set up filters, and assign permissions. Security: MAC addresses can help restrict network access to known devices or identify unauthorized devices trying to connect to a network. Troubleshooting: When diagnosing network issues, knowing the MAC addresses involved can help pinpoint where problems are occurring. Finding Your MAC Address on Windows Press the Windows key + R to open the Run dialog box. Type cmd and press Enter to open the Command Prompt. In the Command Prompt, type ipconfig /all and press Enter. Scroll through the results until you find the network adapter you're using (Wi-Fi or Ethernet). The MAC address will be listed next to \"Physical Address\" and will look something like 00-1A-2B-3C-4D-5E Finding Your MAC Address on Mac/iPhone/iPad On a Mac computer (MacOS): Click on the Apple icon in the top left corner of the screen and select \"System Preferences\". Click on \"Network\" and choose the network connection you want to check on the left side (WiFi, Wired, etc.). Click on \"Advanced\" and go to the \"Hardware\" tab. The MAC address will be listed as the \"MAC Address\" at the top of the window. On an iPhone or iPad: Open the \"Settings\" app. Tap on \"General\" and then \"About\". Scroll down to find \"Wi-Fi Address,\" which is the MAC address of your device. Finding Your MAC Address on Android To locate the MAC address on an Android smartphone or tablet, you can use the following steps: Open the \"Settings\" app on your Android device. Scroll down and select \"About Phone\" or \"About Device\" (the exact wording can vary depending on the device). Tap on \"Status\" or \"Hardware Information.\" Look for \"Wi-Fi MAC address\" or simply \"MAC address.\" This will display the MAC address of your Wi-Fi network interface.", "source": "Network", "id": 176}, {"topic": "1.Wireless LAN (WLAN)/ Wi-Fi​​​​​​​", "section": "1.8.3 Gateway", "paragraphs": ["A default gateway is the node in a computer network using the Internet protocol suites that servers as the forwarding host to other networks when no other router specification matches the destination IP address of packet. In SAP network, Default gateway address is also automatically assigned by SAP DHCP servers, and the gateway address starts from 10.X.X.X."], "content": "A default gateway is the node in a computer network using the Internet protocol suites that servers as the forwarding host to other networks when no other router specification matches the destination IP address of packet. In SAP network, Default gateway address is also automatically assigned by SAP DHCP servers, and the gateway address starts from 10.X.X.X.", "source": "Network", "id": 177}, {"topic": "1.Wireless LAN (WLAN)/ Wi-Fi​​​​​​​", "section": "1.8.4 DNS server", "paragraphs": ["The most important function of DNS servers is the translation (resolution) of human-memorable domain names (example.com) into the corresponding numeric Internet Protocol, the second principal name space of the Internet, which is used to identify and locate computer systems and resources on the Internet. But in SAP network environment, it is mandatory to choose Obtain DNS server address automatically.", "Important: In SAP network, it is not required manually to add Proxy server in Devices. If so, it would lead to network connection failure. Make sure Obtain an IP address automatically.", "Open Control Panel and Click on View network status and tasks.", "On the left navigation list, click on \"Change adapter settings\".", "Choose Ethernet (LAN cable connection) or Wi-Fi (It depends on which network you are connected to.) Right click on it and go to \"Properties\".", "Under Networking tab, highlight \"Internet Protocol Version 4 (TCP /IPv4)\" and then click on \"Properties\". (Sometimes, uncheck Internet Protocol Version 6 (TCP/IPV6) would solve some network connection issue.)", "Remove any IP address under DNS and select \"Obtain DNS Server address automatically\".", "Stay in the same window and go to \"Advanced...\" button. Remove gateway under Default gateways.", "Click on \"OK\" to all the windows and close the last one. Now you may run command ipconfig/all to check if Default Gateways and DNS are back to normal.", "Note: Some home Wi-Fi DNS settings are set up on Router. Please suggest users contact the network provider to help remove it.", "You can get more information from KB Network - No internet available through cable/Wi-Fi is connected"], "content": "The most important function of DNS servers is the translation (resolution) of human-memorable domain names (example.com) into the corresponding numeric Internet Protocol, the second principal name space of the Internet, which is used to identify and locate computer systems and resources on the Internet. But in SAP network environment, it is mandatory to choose Obtain DNS server address automatically. Important: In SAP network, it is not required manually to add Proxy server in Devices. If so, it would lead to network connection failure. Make sure Obtain an IP address automatically. Open Control Panel and Click on View network status and tasks. On the left navigation list, click on \"Change adapter settings\". Choose Ethernet (LAN cable connection) or Wi-Fi (It depends on which network you are connected to.) Right click on it and go to \"Properties\". Under Networking tab, highlight \"Internet Protocol Version 4 (TCP /IPv4)\" and then click on \"Properties\". (Sometimes, uncheck Internet Protocol Version 6 (TCP/IPV6) would solve some network connection issue.) Remove any IP address under DNS and select \"Obtain DNS Server address automatically\". Stay in the same window and go to \"Advanced...\" button. Remove gateway under Default gateways. Click on \"OK\" to all the windows and close the last one. Now you may run command ipconfig/all to check if Default Gateways and DNS are back to normal. Note: Some home Wi-Fi DNS settings are set up on Router. Please suggest users contact the network provider to help remove it. You can get more information from KB Network - No internet available through cable/Wi-Fi is connected", "source": "Network", "id": 178}, {"topic": "1.Wireless LAN (WLAN)/ Wi-Fi​​​​​​​", "section": "1.9 Windows - SMON -SAP- WPA3 (Machine Certificate) vs. Non-SMON SAP WPA2 (User Certificate) Wi-Fi Connections", "paragraphs": ["It is important to select Computer authentication and, in the properties, to choose WPA3-Enterprise. The only difference between the screenshot and the XML file should be the Encryption Type value; in the exported XML, it must be set to AES. Both options are valid in the UI, but AES is required in the XML file.", "Please make sure that SAP Global Root CA is selected from the settings.", "Troubleshooting steps", "Make sure the affected computer is connected to SAP-Guest WiFi network To reset a WiFi profile, navigate to Network & internet > Wi-Fi > Manage known networks, and choose 'Forget' for the desired WiFi profile. Then, use the Network Profiles Setup / Recreation app in Company Portal to set up or recreate your network profiles.", "Avoid using the 'forget' connection option in the WiFi UI when accessing the WiFi icon near the clock in the taskbar. If you manually connect to -SAP-, you'll only see user certificates available for selection, not machine certificates.", "The machine certificate is installed automatically during enrollment, and successful enrollment depends on this certificate being deployed.", "Note: The user does not need to manually select the machine certificate. Once Certificate authentication is configured for a WiFi profile, connecting to the network prompts the device to automatically use the valid machine certificate from the computer certificate store for the WiFi connection.", "Certlm.msc vs Certmgr.msc:", "You can verify that the machine certificate is installed by opening certlm.msc, as illustrated below.", "For user certificates, please use certmgr.msc.", "KB Windows - SMON -SAP- WPA3 (Machine Certificate) vs. Non-SMON SAP WPA2 (User Certificate) Wi-Fi Connections", "KB Article Network Profiles Setup / Recreation"], "content": "It is important to select Computer authentication and, in the properties, to choose WPA3-Enterprise. The only difference between the screenshot and the XML file should be the Encryption Type value; in the exported XML, it must be set to AES. Both options are valid in the UI, but AES is required in the XML file. Please make sure that SAP Global Root CA is selected from the settings. Troubleshooting steps Make sure the affected computer is connected to SAP-Guest WiFi network To reset a WiFi profile, navigate to Network & internet > Wi-Fi > Manage known networks, and choose 'Forget' for the desired WiFi profile. Then, use the Network Profiles Setup / Recreation app in Company Portal to set up or recreate your network profiles. Avoid using the 'forget' connection option in the WiFi UI when accessing the WiFi icon near the clock in the taskbar. If you manually connect to -SAP-, you'll only see user certificates available for selection, not machine certificates. The machine certificate is installed automatically during enrollment, and successful enrollment depends on this certificate being deployed. Note: The user does not need to manually select the machine certificate. Once Certificate authentication is configured for a WiFi profile, connecting to the network prompts the device to automatically use the valid machine certificate from the computer certificate store for the WiFi connection. Certlm.msc vs Certmgr.msc: You can verify that the machine certificate is installed by opening certlm.msc, as illustrated below. For user certificates, please use certmgr.msc. KB Windows - SMON -SAP- WPA3 (Machine Certificate) vs. Non-SMON SAP WPA2 (User Certificate) Wi-Fi Connections KB Article Network Profiles Setup / Recreation", "source": "Network", "id": 179}, {"topic": "2. Wired network", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["A wired network uses cables to connect devices, such as laptop or desktop computers, to the internet or another network. Similar to wireless network IP configuration, Wired network IP address is also automatically assigned by SAP DHCP servers.", "LAN at your workplace is probably disabled when the cable was removed by IT or you have a cable connected and the LAN port on your device doesn't show any activity - no blinking lights where this was normal before. Please be aware that there are certain areas where only WiFi is provided - here we cannot enable cabled access. (Note: For Mac it is recommended to use WiFi or LAN, not both simultaneously, due to issues with Network Access Control.)", "If WiFi is not sufficient and you require a LAN connection for your work:", "Please provide information enabling us to find the required LAN port: Country - SAP Building - room and place (which desk), and the equipment (choose).", "If the LAN cable is still connected and you can follow it to the outlet easily, please attach a picture of that outlet showing any visible information (port number etc.).", "IT Support will gather all missing information, provide a cable if necessary, then hand the ticket to Network support which re-enables the port(s).", "There is a pre-formatted request link which we can share with the users for them to request.", "ITSM Service Catalog - IT Support (services.sap)"], "content": "A wired network uses cables to connect devices, such as laptop or desktop computers, to the internet or another network. Similar to wireless network IP configuration, Wired network IP address is also automatically assigned by SAP DHCP servers. LAN at your workplace is probably disabled when the cable was removed by IT or you have a cable connected and the LAN port on your device doesn't show any activity - no blinking lights where this was normal before. Please be aware that there are certain areas where only WiFi is provided - here we cannot enable cabled access. (Note: For Mac it is recommended to use WiFi or LAN, not both simultaneously, due to issues with Network Access Control.) If WiFi is not sufficient and you require a LAN connection for your work: Please provide information enabling us to find the required LAN port: Country - SAP Building - room and place (which desk), and the equipment (choose). If the LAN cable is still connected and you can follow it to the outlet easily, please attach a picture of that outlet showing any visible information (port number etc.). IT Support will gather all missing information, provide a cable if necessary, then hand the ticket to Network support which re-enables the port(s). There is a pre-formatted request link which we can share with the users for them to request. ITSM Service Catalog - IT Support (services.sap)", "source": "Network", "id": 180}, {"topic": "3. Cisco Umbrella", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Overview", "Cisco Umbrella has been deployed on the SAP Corporate network and SAP managed endpoints. ​​​​​​​Additionally, some SAP cloud areas have also deployed Cisco Umbrella.", "Umbrella is a cloud-based service (SaaS) from Cisco to filter and resolve (as a recursive resolver) DNS requests. Malicious DNS requests are able to be blocked directly at the DNS level, preventing security incidents from reaching the endpoint and network. When using the Cisco Secure Client (Windows, Mac) or Cisco Security Connector (iOS, iPadOS) on your endpoint, it also provides encryption for your DNS requests to prevent spying or hijacking of your DNS."], "content": "Overview Cisco Umbrella has been deployed on the SAP Corporate network and SAP managed endpoints. ​​​​​​​Additionally, some SAP cloud areas have also deployed Cisco Umbrella. Umbrella is a cloud-based service (SaaS) from Cisco to filter and resolve (as a recursive resolver) DNS requests. Malicious DNS requests are able to be blocked directly at the DNS level, preventing security incidents from reaching the endpoint and network. When using the Cisco Secure Client (Windows, Mac) or Cisco Security Connector (iOS, iPadOS) on your endpoint, it also provides encryption for your DNS requests to prevent spying or hijacking of your DNS.", "source": "Network", "id": 181}, {"topic": "3. Cisco Umbrella", "section": "3.1 What is Umbrella", "paragraphs": ["Protecting SAP users and endpoints from anywhere with DNS-layer security", "Umbrella is comprised of two main areas for protection: 1. Network level (transparent DNS service) 2. Endpoint Protection (agent installed on SAP managed endpoints)", "SAP-Corporate Office Networks (Network level)", "SAP-Corporate office networks now use Umbrella for external DNS resolution (208.67.220.220, 208.67.222.222) instead of the local ISP provided DNS resolver. This is done on the network level and no other configurations or changes are needed by devices or clients. All devices resolving DNS requests from the SAP Corporate network are automatically under Umbrella's service and protection as the local DNS server used will forward all external requests to Umbrella.", "Further, udp/53 traffic seen on the network and egress firewalls is also transparently nat'd to Umbrella resolvers. This ensures other public resolving services are automatically redirected to use the required SAP Umbrella service for resolutions.", "Protecting Cloud and Production landscapes with Umbrella DNS", "Today, Umbrella is used with Network Level (transparent DNS service) for many cloud and production landscapes within SAP.", "SAP Cloud and Production landscapes (Network level)", "SAP Cloud and Production landscapes can now use Umbrella for external DNS resolution (208.67.220.220, 208.67.222.222) instead of the local ISP provided DNS resolver or other public resolvers. This is done on the network level and no other configurations or changes are needed by devices or clients. All devices resolving DNS requests from the egress network point are under Umbrella's service and protection in such an implementation. Alternatively Umbrella Virtual Appliances are also available to LOBs to use as local recursive resolvers in their landscapes.", "Umbrella for Cloud and Production landscapes is a pre approved central service offering and can be requested for an LOB following the SGSC DETECT Service Desk process. DTE will review and evaluate the request and work with the LOB through the onboarding process. SAP makes use of the Multi-Org feature of Umbrella, allowing LoBs to be delegated administrators of their own Umbrella tenant, under SAP's parent tenant and policies. In short, a SaaS based Umbrella tenant is created specifically for the LOB and setup and delegated with co-administration access. Umbrella logs are automatically brought into the LOBs SIEM as part of the onboarding process."], "content": "Protecting SAP users and endpoints from anywhere with DNS-layer security Umbrella is comprised of two main areas for protection: 1. Network level (transparent DNS service) 2. Endpoint Protection (agent installed on SAP managed endpoints) SAP-Corporate Office Networks (Network level) SAP-Corporate office networks now use Umbrella for external DNS resolution (208.67.220.220, 208.67.222.222) instead of the local ISP provided DNS resolver. This is done on the network level and no other configurations or changes are needed by devices or clients. All devices resolving DNS requests from the SAP Corporate network are automatically under Umbrella's service and protection as the local DNS server used will forward all external requests to Umbrella. Further, udp/53 traffic seen on the network and egress firewalls is also transparently nat'd to Umbrella resolvers. This ensures other public resolving services are automatically redirected to use the required SAP Umbrella service for resolutions. Protecting Cloud and Production landscapes with Umbrella DNS Today, Umbrella is used with Network Level (transparent DNS service) for many cloud and production landscapes within SAP. SAP Cloud and Production landscapes (Network level) SAP Cloud and Production landscapes can now use Umbrella for external DNS resolution (208.67.220.220, 208.67.222.222) instead of the local ISP provided DNS resolver or other public resolvers. This is done on the network level and no other configurations or changes are needed by devices or clients. All devices resolving DNS requests from the egress network point are under Umbrella's service and protection in such an implementation. Alternatively Umbrella Virtual Appliances are also available to LOBs to use as local recursive resolvers in their landscapes. Umbrella for Cloud and Production landscapes is a pre approved central service offering and can be requested for an LOB following the SGSC DETECT Service Desk process. DTE will review and evaluate the request and work with the LOB through the onboarding process. SAP makes use of the Multi-Org feature of Umbrella, allowing LoBs to be delegated administrators of their own Umbrella tenant, under SAP's parent tenant and policies. In short, a SaaS based Umbrella tenant is created specifically for the LOB and setup and delegated with co-administration access. Umbrella logs are automatically brought into the LOBs SIEM as part of the onboarding process.", "source": "Network", "id": 182}, {"topic": "3. Cisco Umbrella", "section": "3.2 SAP Managed Endpoints", "paragraphs": ["Windows 11 Cisco Secure Client (CSC): Available in Software Center. Automatically installed for new devices.", "Mac Cisco Secure Client (CSC): Available in Self Service. Automatically installed for new devices.", "Linux Currently there is no roaming client currently available for Linux. These devices are protected when on the SAP Corporate network (including VPN).", "Other landscapes, systems, servers While there is no software based agents available for other endpoint types, DNS requests sent to Umbrella will still be filtered and blocked for security categories as long as the endpoints are on the SAP Corporate network."], "content": "Windows 11 Cisco Secure Client (CSC): Available in Software Center. Automatically installed for new devices. Mac Cisco Secure Client (CSC): Available in Self Service. Automatically installed for new devices. Linux Currently there is no roaming client currently available for Linux. These devices are protected when on the SAP Corporate network (including VPN). Other landscapes, systems, servers While there is no software based agents available for other endpoint types, DNS requests sent to Umbrella will still be filtered and blocked for security categories as long as the endpoints are on the SAP Corporate network.", "source": "Network", "id": 183}, {"topic": "3. Cisco Umbrella", "section": "3.3 SAP iPhones and iPads (including BYOD)", "paragraphs": ["Installation for Security Connector", "Available in Self Service. Automatically installed for new devices during enrollment. Available for all supervised and managed devices.", "Cisco Secure Client - Basic Troubleshooting Steps for the Client Support", "Regarding Cisco Secure Client issues, reach out to the Client Support first. Service: Software Service Offering: IES-CS-Software-Cisco Umbrella Assignment Group: IES CS of your region", "You will get Cisco Client support knowledge from Umbrella@SAP"], "content": "Installation for Security Connector Available in Self Service. Automatically installed for new devices during enrollment. Available for all supervised and managed devices. Cisco Secure Client - Basic Troubleshooting Steps for the Client Support Regarding Cisco Secure Client issues, reach out to the Client Support first. Service: Software Service Offering: IES-CS-Software-Cisco Umbrella Assignment Group: IES CS of your region You will get Cisco Client support knowledge from Umbrella@SAP", "source": "Network", "id": 184}, {"topic": "4. macOS - Cisco Secure Client", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Overview", "Cisco Umbrella provides Secure DNS to your Mac.", "Specifically, it:", "Encrypts your DNS requests and prevents man-in-the-middle attacks and eavesdropping.", "Sends your external DNS requests to be resolved via Umbrella DNS services", "Protects you from clicking on known phishing and malicious links", "Protects you from downloading known malicious files", "Protects you from known crypto mining attacks and other security threats", "For users requiring \"eDLP\" applied security controls it can block access to prohibited sites and services", "Mac users use the Cisco Secure Client with the Umbrella module for the installed agent on all Mac endpoints:", "Cisco Secure Client = CSC", "The CSC will start automatically on your Mac as a System Extension and Network Extension. It has a launch agent for loading the GUI at startup (/Library/LaunchAgents/com.cisco.secureclient.csc_gui.plist). You will also find a folder with the apps under /Applications/Cisco/Cisco Secure Client.app.", "CSC will only show a menu bar icon if you actively have the UI open for app. Quitting CSC will close the menu bar icon, but CSC continues to run as a native macOS DNS Proxy system extension.", "As CSC with Umbrella utilizes a system extension, it will run on your Mac regardless of if open or closed as an app. As CSC is implemented as a native macOS DNS Proxy System Extension, there is virtually no performance impact on your Mac (under 1%), and it transparently handles DNS resolving at the macOS kernel level. It leaves your default set DNS resolvers unchanged. Behind the scenes, macOS is automatically proxying your DNS requests to Umbrella (transparently). There is no CSC icon displayed by default in your menu bar unless you open CSC UI.", "Utilizing Umbrella services will, in most cases, accelerate your Internet experience as it will provide faster resolutions and improved geo-location awareness to services such as Microsoft 365. Geek speak; it supports RFC7871(EDNS). It also increases your security as it encrypts DNS queries to and from the Umbrella service.", "KB macOS - Cisco Secure Client"], "content": "Overview Cisco Umbrella provides Secure DNS to your Mac. Specifically, it: Encrypts your DNS requests and prevents man-in-the-middle attacks and eavesdropping. Sends your external DNS requests to be resolved via Umbrella DNS services Protects you from clicking on known phishing and malicious links Protects you from downloading known malicious files Protects you from known crypto mining attacks and other security threats For users requiring \"eDLP\" applied security controls it can block access to prohibited sites and services Mac users use the Cisco Secure Client with the Umbrella module for the installed agent on all Mac endpoints: Cisco Secure Client = CSC The CSC will start automatically on your Mac as a System Extension and Network Extension. It has a launch agent for loading the GUI at startup (/Library/LaunchAgents/com.cisco.secureclient.csc_gui.plist). You will also find a folder with the apps under /Applications/Cisco/Cisco Secure Client.app. CSC will only show a menu bar icon if you actively have the UI open for app. Quitting CSC will close the menu bar icon, but CSC continues to run as a native macOS DNS Proxy system extension. As CSC with Umbrella utilizes a system extension, it will run on your Mac regardless of if open or closed as an app. As CSC is implemented as a native macOS DNS Proxy System Extension, there is virtually no performance impact on your Mac (under 1%), and it transparently handles DNS resolving at the macOS kernel level. It leaves your default set DNS resolvers unchanged. Behind the scenes, macOS is automatically proxying your DNS requests to Umbrella (transparently). There is no CSC icon displayed by default in your menu bar unless you open CSC UI. Utilizing Umbrella services will, in most cases, accelerate your Internet experience as it will provide faster resolutions and improved geo-location awareness to services such as Microsoft 365. Geek speak; it supports RFC7871(EDNS). It also increases your security as it encrypts DNS queries to and from the Umbrella service. KB macOS - Cisco Secure Client", "source": "Network", "id": 185}, {"topic": "5. Virtual Private Network", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["VPN is an acronym that stands for \"Virtual Private Network(ing)\". Internet plus security - as if it were a private network. A virtual private network (VPN) is a technology for using the Internet or another intermediate network to connect computers to isolated remote computer networks that would otherwise be inaccessible.", "Global Remote Access - F5 VPN with Microsoft Windows gives you full access to the entire SAP office network via a secure, encrypted virtual private network (VPN) connection.", "Available for C, D, and I users with SAP devices", "Internet access needed", "SecurID card required for Linux", "Today, F5 is only used in specific cases, such as SAP Learning Cloud, SAP Demo & Education, and Ariba PCI Landscape. By the end of Q1 2024, the following corporate F5 VPN gateways will still be available:", "Philadelphia", "Walldorf/Rot", "Bangalore", "Singapore", "Shanghai"], "content": "VPN is an acronym that stands for \"Virtual Private Network(ing)\". Internet plus security - as if it were a private network. A virtual private network (VPN) is a technology for using the Internet or another intermediate network to connect computers to isolated remote computer networks that would otherwise be inaccessible. Global Remote Access - F5 VPN with Microsoft Windows gives you full access to the entire SAP office network via a secure, encrypted virtual private network (VPN) connection. Available for C, D, and I users with SAP devices Internet access needed SecurID card required for Linux Today, F5 is only used in specific cases, such as SAP Learning Cloud, SAP Demo & Education, and Ariba PCI Landscape. By the end of Q1 2024, the following corporate F5 VPN gateways will still be available: Philadelphia Walldorf/Rot Bangalore Singapore Shanghai", "source": "Network", "id": 186}, {"topic": "5. Virtual Private Network", "section": "5.1 Global Remote Access with MacOS", "paragraphs": ["Connectivity to SAP Corporate network and services are offered with two VPN solutions: GlobalProtect and F5. These services are commonly referred to as \"SAP Seamless Access\".", "The default VPN solution should be GlobalProtect, with F5 BIG-IP VPN used only for special Use cases", "GlobalProtect is not working in People Republic of China as regulatory issues\"", "BIG-IP Edge Client allows you to connect to the SAP Corporate Network via a Virtual Private Network (VPN) connection. The BIG-IP Edge Client is preinstalled on your Mac. You can find it under /Applications. If you have uninstalled it, you can reinstall it in Self Service under the category Apps. You can see your connection status by clicking on the app icon in the menu bar."], "content": "Connectivity to SAP Corporate network and services are offered with two VPN solutions: GlobalProtect and F5. These services are commonly referred to as \"SAP Seamless Access\". The default VPN solution should be GlobalProtect, with F5 BIG-IP VPN used only for special Use cases GlobalProtect is not working in People Republic of China as regulatory issues\" BIG-IP Edge Client allows you to connect to the SAP Corporate Network via a Virtual Private Network (VPN) connection. The BIG-IP Edge Client is preinstalled on your Mac. You can find it under /Applications. If you have uninstalled it, you can reinstall it in Self Service under the category Apps. You can see your connection status by clicking on the app icon in the menu bar.", "source": "Network", "id": 187}, {"topic": "5. Virtual Private Network", "section": "5.1.1 How to Connect and Disconnect", "paragraphs": ["How do I connect?", "You will need:", "BIG-IP Edge Client on your Mac", "Your (compliant) Mac.", "Internet connection.", "To connect, follow these steps:", "1. On your Mac, open BIG-IP Edge Client.", "BIG-IP Edge Client: The app will open with a welcome screen and splash screen and then animate into your menu bar. The BIG-IP Edge Client icon in your dock will not show as launched (glowing dot underneath). This is normal. You will need to use the menu bar icon to access preferences and controls.", "2. BIG-IP Edge Client will automatically use the last connection settings and connect.", "3. If this is your first time connecting, you may be asked to allow BIG-IP to use your SSO certificate so you can be authenticated in SAP Cloud Identity. Enter your password and choose Always Allow. This allows the BIG-IP app to use your SSO certificate in the future, automatically.", "4. You will be connected to the SAP Corporate Network via VPN. The connection is full tunnel except for select SAP IT provided services which are automatically split out of the tunnel (e.g. Teams, Microsoft 365, etc.)", "5. If you'd like to automatically start F5 BIG-IP Edge Client when you log into your Mac, simply add the app into your Login Items using System Preferences → Users & Groups. Select Login Items for your account and add it. Alternatively, you can right click on the F5 BIG-IP Edge Client dock icon and select Options → Open at Login.", "How do I disconnect?", "1. In the menu bar, click on the f5 BIG-IP Edge Client icon.", "2. In the drop-down menu, click Turn VPN Off (BIG-IP)", "For More details, you may refer to this macOS – BIG Edge Client"], "content": "How do I connect? You will need: BIG-IP Edge Client on your Mac Your (compliant) Mac. Internet connection. To connect, follow these steps: 1. On your Mac, open BIG-IP Edge Client. BIG-IP Edge Client: The app will open with a welcome screen and splash screen and then animate into your menu bar. The BIG-IP Edge Client icon in your dock will not show as launched (glowing dot underneath). This is normal. You will need to use the menu bar icon to access preferences and controls. 2. BIG-IP Edge Client will automatically use the last connection settings and connect. 3. If this is your first time connecting, you may be asked to allow BIG-IP to use your SSO certificate so you can be authenticated in SAP Cloud Identity. Enter your password and choose Always Allow. This allows the BIG-IP app to use your SSO certificate in the future, automatically. 4. You will be connected to the SAP Corporate Network via VPN. The connection is full tunnel except for select SAP IT provided services which are automatically split out of the tunnel (e.g. Teams, Microsoft 365, etc.) 5. If you'd like to automatically start F5 BIG-IP Edge Client when you log into your Mac, simply add the app into your Login Items using System Preferences → Users & Groups. Select Login Items for your account and add it. Alternatively, you can right click on the F5 BIG-IP Edge Client dock icon and select Options → Open at Login. How do I disconnect? 1. In the menu bar, click on the f5 BIG-IP Edge Client icon. 2. In the drop-down menu, click Turn VPN Off (BIG-IP) For More details, you may refer to this macOS – BIG Edge Client", "source": "Network", "id": 188}, {"topic": "5. Virtual Private Network", "section": "5.1.2 Auto-Connect & On-Demand", "paragraphs": ["Auto-connect is an option for the F5 BIG-IP Edge Client to automatically connect in the event you are not connected to the SAP-Corporate network. While you are on SAP-Corporate, BIG-IP Edge Client will detect so and will not connect.", "To change your settings to turn on Auto-Connect, use the Preferences option in BIG-IP Edge Client:", "For More details, you may refer to this Network - Remote Access / VPN Client - F5 Big-IP Edge Client Auto-Connect VPN"], "content": "Auto-connect is an option for the F5 BIG-IP Edge Client to automatically connect in the event you are not connected to the SAP-Corporate network. While you are on SAP-Corporate, BIG-IP Edge Client will detect so and will not connect. To change your settings to turn on Auto-Connect, use the Preferences option in BIG-IP Edge Client: For More details, you may refer to this Network - Remote Access / VPN Client - F5 Big-IP Edge Client Auto-Connect VPN", "source": "Network", "id": 189}, {"topic": "5. Virtual Private Network", "section": "5.2 Global Remote Access - F5 VPN with Microsoft Windows", "paragraphs": ["GlobalProtect is the primary remote access solution at SAP. Only in very specific cases should F5 be used, such as SAP Education Cloud, Concur VPN and Ariba PCI landscape. This article will explain how to connect and disconnect BIG-IP Edge Client for these applications. GlobalProtect should be used for all other remote access requirements.", "Prerequisites", "Internet access", "Computer with SAP image", "Valid SSO and machine certificate"], "content": "GlobalProtect is the primary remote access solution at SAP. Only in very specific cases should F5 be used, such as SAP Education Cloud, Concur VPN and Ariba PCI landscape. This article will explain how to connect and disconnect BIG-IP Edge Client for these applications. GlobalProtect should be used for all other remote access requirements. Prerequisites Internet access Computer with SAP image Valid SSO and machine certificate", "source": "Network", "id": 190}, {"topic": "5. Virtual Private Network", "section": "5.2.1 Connecting", "paragraphs": ["Step 1.", "Start BIG-IP Edge Client. It's pre-installed on computers with an SAP image. If it's not available on your computer, install it from Company Portal.", "Step 2.", "Choose Change Server and select the city closest to your location.", "Always choose the nearest gateway from your location to connect VPN.", "Step 3.", "Choose Connect.", "You will be automatically connected. A certificate stored on your computer is used for authentication. Only if it fails, you'll be prompted to enter your user ID and a SecurID passcode.", "Please note: Since many applications and services are available on your Cloud workplace without VPN, we recommend that you only use the auto-connect feature if you constantly need VPN for your work, e.g. for ISP."], "content": "Step 1. Start BIG-IP Edge Client. It's pre-installed on computers with an SAP image. If it's not available on your computer, install it from Company Portal. Step 2. Choose Change Server and select the city closest to your location. Always choose the nearest gateway from your location to connect VPN. Step 3. Choose Connect. You will be automatically connected. A certificate stored on your computer is used for authentication. Only if it fails, you'll be prompted to enter your user ID and a SecurID passcode. Please note: Since many applications and services are available on your Cloud workplace without VPN, we recommend that you only use the auto-connect feature if you constantly need VPN for your work, e.g. for ISP.", "source": "Network", "id": 191}, {"topic": "5. Virtual Private Network", "section": "5.2.2 Disconnecting", "paragraphs": ["How to disconnect on Windows", "To turn OFF Big-IP Edge Client, click on the \"show hidden icons\" button as shown below", "Click on the F5 icon as shown below.", "For More details, you may refer to this Global Remote Access - F5 VPN with Microsoft Windows"], "content": "How to disconnect on Windows To turn OFF Big-IP Edge Client, click on the \"show hidden icons\" button as shown below Click on the F5 icon as shown below. For More details, you may refer to this Global Remote Access - F5 VPN with Microsoft Windows", "source": "Network", "id": 192}, {"topic": "6. SAP Seamless Access (GlobalProtect)", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["SAP's Seamless Access (GlobalProtect) is the next generation solution for seamless, secure, high-performance, \"designed for cloud\" connectivity at SAP, ensuring the best performance with optimized routing to SAP on-premise services via secure connection to SAP hub and branch locations, as well as Internet services like Fiori, Microsoft 365, Teams via a GlobalProtect gateway close to your location! With SSA, you can simply keep the connection \"always-on\" with seamless authentication without worrying about performance, as the cloud backend will always find the fastest path to all services for you, while ensuring all traffic is safe and secure!"], "content": "SAP's Seamless Access (GlobalProtect) is the next generation solution for seamless, secure, high-performance, \"designed for cloud\" connectivity at SAP, ensuring the best performance with optimized routing to SAP on-premise services via secure connection to SAP hub and branch locations, as well as Internet services like Fiori, Microsoft 365, Teams via a GlobalProtect gateway close to your location! With SSA, you can simply keep the connection \"always-on\" with seamless authentication without worrying about performance, as the cloud backend will always find the fastest path to all services for you, while ensuring all traffic is safe and secure!", "source": "Network", "id": 193}, {"topic": "6. SAP Seamless Access (GlobalProtect)", "section": "6.1 How to install GlobalProtect", "paragraphs": ["Here’s how to install GlobalProtect when you have already moved away from DirectAccess:", "Go to the Company portal (via the Windows icon in your taskbar and the Start menu).", "Install “Seamless Access (GlobalProtect)” from Company Portal.", "After the successful installation, you only need to start GlobalProtect once for a secure and fast connection. It will stay “always on” in the background providing you with a seamless access experience to internal services."], "content": "Here’s how to install GlobalProtect when you have already moved away from DirectAccess: Go to the Company portal (via the Windows icon in your taskbar and the Start menu). Install “Seamless Access (GlobalProtect)” from Company Portal. After the successful installation, you only need to start GlobalProtect once for a secure and fast connection. It will stay “always on” in the background providing you with a seamless access experience to internal services.", "source": "Network", "id": 194}, {"topic": "6. SAP Seamless Access (GlobalProtect)", "section": "6.2 Use cases", "paragraphs": ["SAP Seamless Access is currently primarily recommended for users mainly working with cloud services (Microsoft 365, SAP Cloud, …) and accessing SAP backend services in WDF/ROT, Newtown Square or Singapore (e.g., Corporate Portal, ISP, ...).​​​​​​​", "Please note: GlobalProtect has no license in China so you will not be able to use it. When in China, you need to use the Big-IP Edge Client.", "What is the gateway address?", "If you are missing the gateway / portal, use \"sap.gpcloudservice.com\".", "Don’t use cases", "Please continue using F5 Big-IP if you require access to the following scenarios:", "SAP Education Cloud", "Concur VPN", "Ariba PCI Landscape", "Important note:", "F5 VPN connection is blocked while Global Protect VPN client is enabled. It is by design, Global Protect VPN client is enabled by default, and if F5 client is launched manually or automatically – it will be blocked by the Firewall ruleset from reaching F5 APM/GTM servers.", "6.3 Interface icon status and meaning", "For more information", "You may visit Remote access on IT for you or SAP Seamless Access (GlobalProtect) FAQ", "7. SAP Seamless Access (GlobalProtect) for macOS", "SAP Seamless Access (GlobalProtect) is the next-generation VPN solution that is designed for the cloud and provides you with seamless, secure, and high-performance connectivity at SAP. It ensures the best performance with optimized routing to SAP on-premise services via a secure connection to SAP hub and branch locations, as well as Internet services like Fiori, Microsoft 365, Teams via a GlobalProtect gateway close to your location!", "With GlobalProtect, you can simply keep the connection always-on with seamless authentication without worrying about performance, as the cloud backend will always find the fastest path to all services for you, while ensuring all traffic is safe and secure!", "Please note: GlobalProtect has no license in China so you will not be able to use it. When in China, you need to use the BigIP Edge Client.", "7.1 How to get GlobalProtect?", "GlobalProtect uses central device compliance to grant you access to SAP Seamless Access. This is a harmonized solution across our cloud landscape.", "Some simple steps to get connected:", "1. Register your Mac for Entra ID Device Compliance", "2. After some minutes GlobalProtect will appear in your Self Service", "3. Run the Self Service", "4. Type in your email address on the GlobalProtect sign-in window", "5. GlobalProtect is connected", "7.2 What is the gateway address?", "If you are missing the gateway / portal, use \"sap.gpcloudservice.com\".", "You will get more GlobalProtect for macOS from KB0579189", "8. Network Support", "When there is a network related issue or outage, besides dispatching tickets to network support team, we can also find the local network contact from NIP Portal(Network Information Portal)", "The Network Information Portal (NIP) aims to provide operational tools for the networker's everyday processes as well as useful information about the company's structure, services and contacts as relevant from a networker's point of view.", "Global Network devices are managed centrally by Netlager of NIP, which provides access to network inventory data and allows for device management."], "content": "SAP Seamless Access is currently primarily recommended for users mainly working with cloud services (Microsoft 365, SAP Cloud, …) and accessing SAP backend services in WDF/ROT, Newtown Square or Singapore (e.g., Corporate Portal, ISP, ...).​​​​​​​ Please note: GlobalProtect has no license in China so you will not be able to use it. When in China, you need to use the Big-IP Edge Client. What is the gateway address? If you are missing the gateway / portal, use \"sap.gpcloudservice.com\". Don’t use cases Please continue using F5 Big-IP if you require access to the following scenarios: SAP Education Cloud Concur VPN Ariba PCI Landscape Important note: F5 VPN connection is blocked while Global Protect VPN client is enabled. It is by design, Global Protect VPN client is enabled by default, and if F5 client is launched manually or automatically – it will be blocked by the Firewall ruleset from reaching F5 APM/GTM servers. 6.3 Interface icon status and meaning For more information You may visit Remote access on IT for you or SAP Seamless Access (GlobalProtect) FAQ 7. SAP Seamless Access (GlobalProtect) for macOS SAP Seamless Access (GlobalProtect) is the next-generation VPN solution that is designed for the cloud and provides you with seamless, secure, and high-performance connectivity at SAP. It ensures the best performance with optimized routing to SAP on-premise services via a secure connection to SAP hub and branch locations, as well as Internet services like Fiori, Microsoft 365, Teams via a GlobalProtect gateway close to your location! With GlobalProtect, you can simply keep the connection always-on with seamless authentication without worrying about performance, as the cloud backend will always find the fastest path to all services for you, while ensuring all traffic is safe and secure! Please note: GlobalProtect has no license in China so you will not be able to use it. When in China, you need to use the BigIP Edge Client. 7.1 How to get GlobalProtect? GlobalProtect uses central device compliance to grant you access to SAP Seamless Access. This is a harmonized solution across our cloud landscape. Some simple steps to get connected: 1. Register your Mac for Entra ID Device Compliance 2. After some minutes GlobalProtect will appear in your Self Service 3. Run the Self Service 4. Type in your email address on the GlobalProtect sign-in window 5. GlobalProtect is connected 7.2 What is the gateway address? If you are missing the gateway / portal, use \"sap.gpcloudservice.com\". You will get more GlobalProtect for macOS from KB0579189 8. Network Support When there is a network related issue or outage, besides dispatching tickets to network support team, we can also find the local network contact from NIP Portal(Network Information Portal) The Network Information Portal (NIP) aims to provide operational tools for the networker's everyday processes as well as useful information about the company's structure, services and contacts as relevant from a networker's point of view. Global Network devices are managed centrally by Netlager of NIP, which provides access to network inventory data and allows for device management.", "source": "Network", "id": 195}, {"topic": "9. FAQ", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Q1: Why does VPN affect bandwidth?", "There are many factors that affect speed while connected to VPN, including encryption, geographical distance to the target server and its load, quality of service on the network, or multiple hops and provider peering points along the way.", "If you want to compare your speed with and without VPN, we recommend that you select the speed test server closest to the F5 VPN gateway you normally connect to. To ensure the comparability of the two speed values, please use the same speed test server for both tests.", "Q2: How can I ensure connection quality?", "The distance to the VPN gateway you connect to for remote access has a significant impact on the connection quality. The shorter the distance, the lower the latency, which can affect performance. Therefore, please use a VPN gateway that is as close as possible to your location. To change the gateway, in BIG-IP Edge Client choose Change Server and select a suitable gateway from the drop-down list.", "Q3: I'm on corporate wireless/wired Network and cannot access my applications. GlobalProtect shows the Internal icon.", "Click on the GlobalProtect icon, then the gear icon, and then Refresh Connection.", "This will force GlobalProtect to reassess the network it is connected to and automatically connect.", "Q4: As a Windows user, I used to connect remotely via connect.sap.com. Since this option is no longer available, how should I connect?", "To connect via a virtual private network (VPN), please use BIG-IP Edge Client. If you are using a non-SAP device, use the virtual desktop access WTS (Citrix) via access.sap.com.", "Q5: I'm on corporate wireless/wired Network and cannot access my applications. GlobalProtect shows the Internal icon.", "Click on the GlobalProtect icon, then the gear icon, and then Refresh Connection.", "This will force GlobalProtect to reassess the network it is connected to and automatically connect.", "Q6: Does BIG-IP Edge Client require a higher bandwidth than the previous browser access via connect.sap.com?", "No. Since both access types use the same back end and the same sources, there is no difference in bandwidth.", "Q7: In the manual you write that BIG-IP Edge Client connects automatically without requiring a SecurID password. However, I am still asked for one. Why?", "For the automatic (\"seamless\") connection, authentication is done via a certificate stored on your Windows computer (see rollout information). If this fails, you will be prompted to enter your SAP user ID and a SecurID password. If the automatic connection permanently fails, please create a Service Now ticket in Issue Category: Access / Network / Connectivity", "Q9: I am unable to authenticate or get logged in via GlobalProtect. The message 'Oops - You can't get to this yet' appears.", "Check your system compliance:", "For Windows devices check Device Health:", "Device Health Now Managing Your Windows 11 Compliance", "For macOS devices check compliance:", "MH9002 - Compliant Devices - macOS", "Contact IT Support on itsupport.sap.com.", "Q10: I cannot resolve DNS names, partially cannot access corporate sites or sites not reachable (DNS error).", "Issues might be:", "When you try to access sites or systems without FQDN or having issues accessing certain sites like https://one.int.sap/home even other internal corporate sites are accessible.", "Accessing sites or systems using non-FQDN names e.g. https://abc/site.html instead of https://abc.wdf.sap.corp/site.html", "Q11: When enabling GlobalProtect, I'm prompted for a multi-factor setup.", "For Seamless Access, SSO is required, and you need to have a valid SSO certificate enrolled. In case the SSO certificate is missing or expired/invalid see Knowledge base article How to manually enroll a SSO G2 user certificate (Windows platform)?", "GlobalProtect authentication is based on Microsoft authentication, similar to the office applications. To sign-in outside of SAP network, it may be required to use a multi-factor authentication (MFA). Therefore, you will be prompted to set up MFA if not done yet. Please follow the steps to complete the setup, then you can enable GlobalProtect.", "See Knowledge Base Article IKB0010510 for information on MFA.", "Q12: GlobalProtect does not connect and its always on \"connecting\" check if a proxy has been set.", "On Windows: Settings => Network & Internet => Proxy. Automatically detect settings should be on \"ON\" and \"Manual proxy\" on \"OFF\".", "Q13: A developer wants a desktop to be connected to a wired network in a location where the LAN port reduction project has been completed. Is this possible?", "Developer needs to raise an IT ticket with the workstation details and local IT will work with ONT to enable LAN ports.", "Q14: Employees would like to request a network port activation. What should he/she do?", "Create a ticket request in the IT support portal.", "Q15: If a network issue (with ticket created) needs to be escalated, where should I look for my office network contact?", "Access NIP Portal and look for an IT contact in the ONT Network Engineer category.", "Q16: Can I use SAP-IOT as a backup if I have trouble connecting to SAP?", "No, you cannot use SAP-IOT as a backup connection.", "Only registered and approved devices will be onboarded on the SAP-IOT wireless and wired LAN.", "Q17: My internet connection through GlobalProtect is significantly slower than other devices on the same network. Icon shows Connected.", "While we are always looking at ways of improving our network speeds, the way GlobalProtect creates a secure connection will cause your internet connection to be slower. Since you're connected to the SAP corporate network securely, your internet traffic has further to go and has to pass through more encryption/decryption processes.", "However, if you find that the connection speeds are impeding your ability to work, and other devices on the same network you're connected to are significantly faster, please contact IT Support on itsupport.sap.com for assistance.", "Q18: What are VPN protocols?", "IPSec", "Q19: Besides using the application, what is another way to connect to BIG-IP Edge Client?", "Entering the VPN URL directly into a web browser", "Q20: I'm seeing an issue whereas I'm trying to access a specific site but getting some type of \"blocked\" page that access is not possible because the site thinks I'm in a different country location (and this isn't the case).", "Some sites and services might block access from other countries for security reasons or legal reasons. Sites which are blocked because of legal reasons (e.g. I'm trying to access Hulu.com from Germany and it doesn't work), are usually \"normal\". However if you think it is the case they should work or have worked in the past, please follow the steps below to gather additional data for SAP IT to further investigate the issue.", "If you think you are getting incorrectly blocked from a particular site (and the block isn't because of Security reasons as indicated by the Umbrella block page), you can capture additional information to submit to IT to investigate further. Perform the following tests and collect all the data into screenshots to provide as part of your ServiceNow ticket.", "nslookup in Command Line or Terminal to the destination you are looking to connect to", "ping to the destination you are looking to connect to", "traceroute to the destination you are looking to connect to", "complete network stack information (ifconfig or ipconfig depending on platform) including DNS", "An overview of the device being used, current OS version, current application or browser and any other information (such as location services are enabled or disabled)", "Switch to another public Internet connection an verify the behavior isn't the same (while you can test against SAP-Internet and SAP-Guest, also ensure you test against a public Internet connection)", "Q21: I'm seeing some language issues whereas the country I'm in, the language from a site is incorrect. For example, I'm in the Paris office but my site is defaulting to German.", "Sites and services use many variables to attempt to identify your endpoint location against the service you are accessing. For example, if you go to Google.com, you would expect to be \"localized\" to the language of your current location (country). Most of the time, for major services, this occurs without issue. In some rare cases, things might add up behind the scenes which gives you a different default language. A good example of this is if you are in the US and your VPN connect to WDF. If you open the local Google News site, you will most likely be defaulted to the local German format. This is because your local client is connected and routing out to the Internet \"as if\" you are sitting in the WDF office location and routing out to the internet. In some cases, this would be normal behavior (as in the case of connecting to WDF over VPN from the US). In other cases, this may not be normal behavior. If you think you are getting incorrect language or location defaults from a particular business critical site, you can capture additional information to submit to IT to investigate further. Perform the following tests and collect all the data into screenshots to provide as part of your IT Direct ticket.", "nslookup in Command Line or Terminal to the destination you are looking to connect to", "ping to the destination you are looking to connect to", "traceroute to the destination you are looking to connect to", "complete network stack information (ifconfig or ipconfig depending on platform) including DNS", "An overview of the device being used, current OS version, current application or browser and any other information (such as location services are enabled or disabled)", "Switch to another public Internet connection an verify the behavior isn't the same (while you can test against SAP-Internet and SAP-Guest, also ensure you test against a public Internet connection)", "Q22: I'm tethering from my iOS device to my Mac and some resources can't be accessed (sap.com, etc.).", "While CSC supports IPv6, some ISP's have not fully deployed full IPv6 support. You can disable IPv6 on your endpoint which should resolve the issue. In the US, for example, T-Mobile only issues IPv6 cellular addresses. macOS: networksetup -setv6off Ethernet && networksetup -setv6off Wi-Fi", "Note: Ethernet / Wi-Fi is the name of your network adapter so you might have to change the name if it isn't correct such as a Thunderbolt bridge ethernet connection", "You can also disable in the GUI by selecting Advanced on the active Network adapter and under TCP/IP, under IPv6, choose \"Off\".", "Alternatively you can change your IPv6 setting on your WiFi adapter (through which you are tethering to your iOS device) to local-link only which will resolve the issue also.", "Q23: Is Umbrella protection applied to all the WiFi network areas?", "Yes, SAP, SAP-Guest, SAP-Corporate and SAP-Internet all route out and use the same external DNS settings which point to Umbrella for offices under Umbrella."], "content": "Q1: Why does VPN affect bandwidth? There are many factors that affect speed while connected to VPN, including encryption, geographical distance to the target server and its load, quality of service on the network, or multiple hops and provider peering points along the way. If you want to compare your speed with and without VPN, we recommend that you select the speed test server closest to the F5 VPN gateway you normally connect to. To ensure the comparability of the two speed values, please use the same speed test server for both tests. Q2: How can I ensure connection quality? The distance to the VPN gateway you connect to for remote access has a significant impact on the connection quality. The shorter the distance, the lower the latency, which can affect performance. Therefore, please use a VPN gateway that is as close as possible to your location. To change the gateway, in BIG-IP Edge Client choose Change Server and select a suitable gateway from the drop-down list. Q3: I'm on corporate wireless/wired Network and cannot access my applications. GlobalProtect shows the Internal icon. Click on the GlobalProtect icon, then the gear icon, and then Refresh Connection. This will force GlobalProtect to reassess the network it is connected to and automatically connect. Q4: As a Windows user, I used to connect remotely via connect.sap.com. Since this option is no longer available, how should I connect? To connect via a virtual private network (VPN), please use BIG-IP Edge Client. If you are using a non-SAP device, use the virtual desktop access WTS (Citrix) via access.sap.com. Q5: I'm on corporate wireless/wired Network and cannot access my applications. GlobalProtect shows the Internal icon. Click on the GlobalProtect icon, then the gear icon, and then Refresh Connection. This will force GlobalProtect to reassess the network it is connected to and automatically connect. Q6: Does BIG-IP Edge Client require a higher bandwidth than the previous browser access via connect.sap.com? No. Since both access types use the same back end and the same sources, there is no difference in bandwidth. Q7: In the manual you write that BIG-IP Edge Client connects automatically without requiring a SecurID password. However, I am still asked for one. Why? For the automatic (\"seamless\") connection, authentication is done via a certificate stored on your Windows computer (see rollout information). If this fails, you will be prompted to enter your SAP user ID and a SecurID password. If the automatic connection permanently fails, please create a Service Now ticket in Issue Category: Access / Network / Connectivity Q9: I am unable to authenticate or get logged in via GlobalProtect. The message 'Oops - You can't get to this yet' appears. Check your system compliance: For Windows devices check Device Health: Device Health Now Managing Your Windows 11 Compliance For macOS devices check compliance: MH9002 - Compliant Devices - macOS Contact IT Support on itsupport.sap.com. Q10: I cannot resolve DNS names, partially cannot access corporate sites or sites not reachable (DNS error). Issues might be: When you try to access sites or systems without FQDN or having issues accessing certain sites like https://one.int.sap/home even other internal corporate sites are accessible. Accessing sites or systems using non-FQDN names e.g. https://abc/site.html instead of https://abc.wdf.sap.corp/site.html Q11: When enabling GlobalProtect, I'm prompted for a multi-factor setup. For Seamless Access, SSO is required, and you need to have a valid SSO certificate enrolled. In case the SSO certificate is missing or expired/invalid see Knowledge base article How to manually enroll a SSO G2 user certificate (Windows platform)? GlobalProtect authentication is based on Microsoft authentication, similar to the office applications. To sign-in outside of SAP network, it may be required to use a multi-factor authentication (MFA). Therefore, you will be prompted to set up MFA if not done yet. Please follow the steps to complete the setup, then you can enable GlobalProtect. See Knowledge Base Article IKB0010510 for information on MFA. Q12: GlobalProtect does not connect and its always on \"connecting\" check if a proxy has been set. On Windows: Settings => Network & Internet => Proxy. Automatically detect settings should be on \"ON\" and \"Manual proxy\" on \"OFF\". Q13: A developer wants a desktop to be connected to a wired network in a location where the LAN port reduction project has been completed. Is this possible? Developer needs to raise an IT ticket with the workstation details and local IT will work with ONT to enable LAN ports. Q14: Employees would like to request a network port activation. What should he/she do? Create a ticket request in the IT support portal. Q15: If a network issue (with ticket created) needs to be escalated, where should I look for my office network contact? Access NIP Portal and look for an IT contact in the ONT Network Engineer category. Q16: Can I use SAP-IOT as a backup if I have trouble connecting to SAP? No, you cannot use SAP-IOT as a backup connection. Only registered and approved devices will be onboarded on the SAP-IOT wireless and wired LAN. Q17: My internet connection through GlobalProtect is significantly slower than other devices on the same network. Icon shows Connected. While we are always looking at ways of improving our network speeds, the way GlobalProtect creates a secure connection will cause your internet connection to be slower. Since you're connected to the SAP corporate network securely, your internet traffic has further to go and has to pass through more encryption/decryption processes. However, if you find that the connection speeds are impeding your ability to work, and other devices on the same network you're connected to are significantly faster, please contact IT Support on itsupport.sap.com for assistance. Q18: What are VPN protocols? IPSec Q19: Besides using the application, what is another way to connect to BIG-IP Edge Client? Entering the VPN URL directly into a web browser Q20: I'm seeing an issue whereas I'm trying to access a specific site but getting some type of \"blocked\" page that access is not possible because the site thinks I'm in a different country location (and this isn't the case). Some sites and services might block access from other countries for security reasons or legal reasons. Sites which are blocked because of legal reasons (e.g. I'm trying to access Hulu.com from Germany and it doesn't work), are usually \"normal\". However if you think it is the case they should work or have worked in the past, please follow the steps below to gather additional data for SAP IT to further investigate the issue. If you think you are getting incorrectly blocked from a particular site (and the block isn't because of Security reasons as indicated by the Umbrella block page), you can capture additional information to submit to IT to investigate further. Perform the following tests and collect all the data into screenshots to provide as part of your ServiceNow ticket. nslookup in Command Line or Terminal to the destination you are looking to connect to ping to the destination you are looking to connect to traceroute to the destination you are looking to connect to complete network stack information (ifconfig or ipconfig depending on platform) including DNS An overview of the device being used, current OS version, current application or browser and any other information (such as location services are enabled or disabled) Switch to another public Internet connection an verify the behavior isn't the same (while you can test against SAP-Internet and SAP-Guest, also ensure you test against a public Internet connection) Q21: I'm seeing some language issues whereas the country I'm in, the language from a site is incorrect. For example, I'm in the Paris office but my site is defaulting to German. Sites and services use many variables to attempt to identify your endpoint location against the service you are accessing. For example, if you go to Google.com, you would expect to be \"localized\" to the language of your current location (country). Most of the time, for major services, this occurs without issue. In some rare cases, things might add up behind the scenes which gives you a different default language. A good example of this is if you are in the US and your VPN connect to WDF. If you open the local Google News site, you will most likely be defaulted to the local German format. This is because your local client is connected and routing out to the Internet \"as if\" you are sitting in the WDF office location and routing out to the internet. In some cases, this would be normal behavior (as in the case of connecting to WDF over VPN from the US). In other cases, this may not be normal behavior. If you think you are getting incorrect language or location defaults from a particular business critical site, you can capture additional information to submit to IT to investigate further. Perform the following tests and collect all the data into screenshots to provide as part of your IT Direct ticket. nslookup in Command Line or Terminal to the destination you are looking to connect to ping to the destination you are looking to connect to traceroute to the destination you are looking to connect to complete network stack information (ifconfig or ipconfig depending on platform) including DNS An overview of the device being used, current OS version, current application or browser and any other information (such as location services are enabled or disabled) Switch to another public Internet connection an verify the behavior isn't the same (while you can test against SAP-Internet and SAP-Guest, also ensure you test against a public Internet connection) Q22: I'm tethering from my iOS device to my Mac and some resources can't be accessed (sap.com, etc.). While CSC supports IPv6, some ISP's have not fully deployed full IPv6 support. You can disable IPv6 on your endpoint which should resolve the issue. In the US, for example, T-Mobile only issues IPv6 cellular addresses. macOS: networksetup -setv6off Ethernet && networksetup -setv6off Wi-Fi Note: Ethernet / Wi-Fi is the name of your network adapter so you might have to change the name if it isn't correct such as a Thunderbolt bridge ethernet connection You can also disable in the GUI by selecting Advanced on the active Network adapter and under TCP/IP, under IPv6, choose \"Off\". Alternatively you can change your IPv6 setting on your WiFi adapter (through which you are tethering to your iOS device) to local-link only which will resolve the issue also. Q23: Is Umbrella protection applied to all the WiFi network areas? Yes, SAP, SAP-Guest, SAP-Corporate and SAP-Internet all route out and use the same external DNS settings which point to Umbrella for offices under Umbrella.", "source": "Network", "id": 196}, {"topic": "", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["ONE Support", "Internal- SAP Only", "Version control", "If you find any content in this document is out of date, feel free to contact the Authors for feedback!", "Thanks for your cooperation in advance!"], "content": "ONE Support Internal- SAP Only Version control If you find any content in this document is out of date, feel free to contact the Authors for feedback! Thanks for your cooperation in advance!", "source": "Onboarding & Offboarding", "id": 197}, {"topic": "1. Client Lifecycle Enterprise App (CLEA) - Onboarding manual", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Overview", "Lifecycle App (CLEA) is the platform that combines all your tools and automates processes regarding on/offboarding, general hardware return and lost or stolen devices to simplify your daily work, resulting in close to no human errors and fast and convenient routine tasks.", "URL: https://lifecycle.int.sap/", "Technical specifications", "Application is using following external systems to connect to and interact with (via APIs):", "SuccessFactors - Employee Central: Source of HR data for internal new hires Fieldglass : (Future) source of data for the external contractors ISP : Asset checks and assignments NEPRA : Checking the new employee password reset app’s status for the new hires HCSM ServiceNow : To auto-generate IT tickets", "ServiceNow: automated ticket creation & updating Exchange/O365: to generate e-mail notifications", "New-hire records appear in the app: as soon as they are visible/activated in HR systems – up to 3 months before the start date", "Synchronization with HR systems: every 4 hours.", "Locations management: Techs assigned to specific Countries with ability for the technician to adjust the cities for which they see new hires (based on their country assignments).", "Auto log-off from the app: 15 mins of inactivity", "Application access management: Internal IT-> via ARM role (“onoffboarding_itmember” on “CVP_IDD” system), DTMS staff-> managed by regional ASDMs via their own UI", "Tickets in HCSM ServiceNow created via technical user: INT_ONB2SN and tickets are maintained automatically by the app and auto-closed when the onboarding is marked completed or cancelled in the CLEA app.", "Platforms supported: Win/Mac/iOS/Android (SAP enrolled devices)", "ISP Roles required:", "in order to automated ISP asset assignment works correctly in CLEA application, please make sure you have all necessary ISP permissions:", "0000_ERP_LO_MOBILE_AUTH XX:PM_EQM:MT or XXXPM_EQM:MT XXXX_ERP_AM_MASTERDATA_MAINT XXXX_ERP_INVENTRY_MGMT_MAINT", "Where \"XX\" or \"XXXX\" equals the company code.", "Onboarding processing flow", "The goal of the application is to unify the sources of the new hire’s data for the IT onboarding teams so they do not have to rely on various SharePoint lists, e-mails and XLS sheets provided by local HR offices.", "The secondary goal is to offer a tool for IT onboarding teams in which they can process, track, and complete all their onboardings. Their work is also automatically recorded in ServiceNow in the form of tickets for the allocation of time, reporting and new hire feedback.", "In an ideal scenario, the onboarding processing in the app is as following:", "App limitations", "C-users are not included due to the missing data sets in Fieldglass side. We are now working with responsible teams on the future solution.", "Concur equipment ISP assignment is not working in the app now due to the Cost Center differences.", "Main screen & settings", "Since the Employee LifeCycle Application is covering both On- and Off-boarding, the main screen containing tiles for both processes depending on the technician’s permissions in the app. In this document, only the Onboarding part is described below", "Onboarding related and general tiles description:", "On-Boarding Joining Users – main user list for onboarding.", "On-Boarding Calendar – overview of the selected locations and number of the upcoming onboardings", "User Event (visible to certain roles only) – log for each new hire in the tool so you can check the detailed progress of the onboarding, when the e-mail notifications have been sent out, if the ServiceNow ticket was created successfully etc.", "On-boarding user list", "This is the main dashboard with all “active” new hires for the technician’s responsible locations. The list is updated every 4 hours, so the changes i.e. in start date are reflected automatically.", "Here the technician could manage the onboardings either on an individual basis (smaller locations) or via mass processing (larger locations). Depending on the number of available records, lists are dynamically populated while you scroll down in the UI.", "Mass Onboarding tile", "Mass Onboarding tile is designated for the onboarding of the larger groups of new hires. It allows the IT technicians to perform a mass HW Pre-assignment (either by manually providing EQ numbers of laptops or use XLS import/export feature), mass NEPRA check and ability to print labels with new hire details.", "New hire details page", "Here you can find all the necessary new hire (and his organization) information you need for onboarding.", "It’s also the page in which you can perform actions to manage the onboarding process such as assigning the prepared HW equipment, recording your notes and comments in the dedicated comment box, check NEPRA status and much more.", "For more information, refer to KB0759990", "SAP IT Onboarding tool & CLEA - HCSM Ticket handling support process", "If the issue is related to the CLEA/SAP IT Onboarding tool functionality (access issues, error messages, non-functional buttons etc), please use following service offering in HCSM: SAPIT-CS-ITAM Tools and route the corresponding ticket to the Onsite and then Advances ITAM Tools team.", "If the issue is related to the data quality (i.e. incorrect device assigned to the end-user), this should be routed to the local IT onsite teams to correct the IT Inventory records.", "Lifecycle Onboading App (CLEA) – FAQ"], "content": "Overview Lifecycle App (CLEA) is the platform that combines all your tools and automates processes regarding on/offboarding, general hardware return and lost or stolen devices to simplify your daily work, resulting in close to no human errors and fast and convenient routine tasks. URL: https://lifecycle.int.sap/ Technical specifications Application is using following external systems to connect to and interact with (via APIs): SuccessFactors - Employee Central: Source of HR data for internal new hires Fieldglass : (Future) source of data for the external contractors ISP : Asset checks and assignments NEPRA : Checking the new employee password reset app’s status for the new hires HCSM ServiceNow : To auto-generate IT tickets ServiceNow: automated ticket creation & updating Exchange/O365: to generate e-mail notifications New-hire records appear in the app: as soon as they are visible/activated in HR systems – up to 3 months before the start date Synchronization with HR systems: every 4 hours. Locations management: Techs assigned to specific Countries with ability for the technician to adjust the cities for which they see new hires (based on their country assignments). Auto log-off from the app: 15 mins of inactivity Application access management: Internal IT-> via ARM role (“onoffboarding_itmember” on “CVP_IDD” system), DTMS staff-> managed by regional ASDMs via their own UI Tickets in HCSM ServiceNow created via technical user: INT_ONB2SN and tickets are maintained automatically by the app and auto-closed when the onboarding is marked completed or cancelled in the CLEA app. Platforms supported: Win/Mac/iOS/Android (SAP enrolled devices) ISP Roles required: in order to automated ISP asset assignment works correctly in CLEA application, please make sure you have all necessary ISP permissions: 0000_ERP_LO_MOBILE_AUTH XX:PM_EQM:MT or XXXPM_EQM:MT XXXX_ERP_AM_MASTERDATA_MAINT XXXX_ERP_INVENTRY_MGMT_MAINT Where \"XX\" or \"XXXX\" equals the company code. Onboarding processing flow The goal of the application is to unify the sources of the new hire’s data for the IT onboarding teams so they do not have to rely on various SharePoint lists, e-mails and XLS sheets provided by local HR offices. The secondary goal is to offer a tool for IT onboarding teams in which they can process, track, and complete all their onboardings. Their work is also automatically recorded in ServiceNow in the form of tickets for the allocation of time, reporting and new hire feedback. In an ideal scenario, the onboarding processing in the app is as following: App limitations C-users are not included due to the missing data sets in Fieldglass side. We are now working with responsible teams on the future solution. Concur equipment ISP assignment is not working in the app now due to the Cost Center differences. Main screen & settings Since the Employee LifeCycle Application is covering both On- and Off-boarding, the main screen containing tiles for both processes depending on the technician’s permissions in the app. In this document, only the Onboarding part is described below Onboarding related and general tiles description: On-Boarding Joining Users – main user list for onboarding. On-Boarding Calendar – overview of the selected locations and number of the upcoming onboardings User Event (visible to certain roles only) – log for each new hire in the tool so you can check the detailed progress of the onboarding, when the e-mail notifications have been sent out, if the ServiceNow ticket was created successfully etc. On-boarding user list This is the main dashboard with all “active” new hires for the technician’s responsible locations. The list is updated every 4 hours, so the changes i.e. in start date are reflected automatically. Here the technician could manage the onboardings either on an individual basis (smaller locations) or via mass processing (larger locations). Depending on the number of available records, lists are dynamically populated while you scroll down in the UI. Mass Onboarding tile Mass Onboarding tile is designated for the onboarding of the larger groups of new hires. It allows the IT technicians to perform a mass HW Pre-assignment (either by manually providing EQ numbers of laptops or use XLS import/export feature), mass NEPRA check and ability to print labels with new hire details. New hire details page Here you can find all the necessary new hire (and his organization) information you need for onboarding. It’s also the page in which you can perform actions to manage the onboarding process such as assigning the prepared HW equipment, recording your notes and comments in the dedicated comment box, check NEPRA status and much more. For more information, refer to KB0759990 SAP IT Onboarding tool & CLEA - HCSM Ticket handling support process If the issue is related to the CLEA/SAP IT Onboarding tool functionality (access issues, error messages, non-functional buttons etc), please use following service offering in HCSM: SAPIT-CS-ITAM Tools and route the corresponding ticket to the Onsite and then Advances ITAM Tools team. If the issue is related to the data quality (i.e. incorrect device assigned to the end-user), this should be routed to the local IT onsite teams to correct the IT Inventory records. Lifecycle Onboading App (CLEA) – FAQ", "source": "Onboarding & Offboarding", "id": 198}, {"topic": "2. New CLEA IT Storage Room Scan Inventory App", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Overview", "During Inventory Week, all technicians are required to scan equipment in all SAP locations globally using the New Inventory Scanner Application. This tool is accessible via iPhone, iPad, or Laptop using the CLEA App.", "Key Benefits of the New Scanner App", "Increased Speed & Efficiency – Scan and process data faster than ever before.", "Real-Time Inventory Updates – Technicians can begin work immediately on the official inventory date, eliminating the need for manual snapshots.", "Seamless CLEA Integration – Directly sync with the CLEA system for streamlined operations", "Improve ISP Data Quality", "Supported Equipment Categories", "The following equipment must be scanned:", "LAPTOP (Windows Laptop)", "PC (Windows Desktop)", "MACBOOK (Apple Laptop)", "IMAC (Apple Desktop)", "PH_IPHONE (iPhone)", "PH_ANDROID (Android Phone)", "T_IOS (iOS Tablet)", "T_ANDROID (Android Tablet)", "TFT-DISP (Display Monitor)", "The following ABC Indicators are in scope for the IT Storage Room scanning process:", "N - New", "P - Pool", "R - ReUse", "S - Stock", "For more Step-by-Step Guide, refer to KB0977538"], "content": "Overview During Inventory Week, all technicians are required to scan equipment in all SAP locations globally using the New Inventory Scanner Application. This tool is accessible via iPhone, iPad, or Laptop using the CLEA App. Key Benefits of the New Scanner App Increased Speed & Efficiency – Scan and process data faster than ever before. Real-Time Inventory Updates – Technicians can begin work immediately on the official inventory date, eliminating the need for manual snapshots. Seamless CLEA Integration – Directly sync with the CLEA system for streamlined operations Improve ISP Data Quality Supported Equipment Categories The following equipment must be scanned: LAPTOP (Windows Laptop) PC (Windows Desktop) MACBOOK (Apple Laptop) IMAC (Apple Desktop) PH_IPHONE (iPhone) PH_ANDROID (Android Phone) T_IOS (iOS Tablet) T_ANDROID (Android Tablet) TFT-DISP (Display Monitor) The following ABC Indicators are in scope for the IT Storage Room scanning process: N - New P - Pool R - ReUse S - Stock For more Step-by-Step Guide, refer to KB0977538", "source": "Onboarding & Offboarding", "id": 199}, {"topic": "3. Temporary Access Pass (TAP)", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Overview", "A Temporary Access Pass (\"TAP\") is a passcode that is only valid for a certain timeframe, or for one-time use (OTP). It is a fallback possibility to perform a multi-factor authentication, if other methods fail or are not available.", "A TAP is usually required in two scenarios:", "1. in a support case", "request a TAP in case of any multi-factor authentication issues, if you have lost or forgotten the device you're using to authenticate (e.g. mobile phone with Microsoft Authenticator app), or if a secondary method is required for a \"Self Service Password Reset\".", "using the active TAP, you can then sign in and update or add further authentication methods (on https://url.sap/getmfa), e.g. to set up Microsoft Authenticator app on a new device", "2. during the onboarding of a new colleague who has not enrolled in multi-factor authentication (MFA) yet", "With the TAP, the new colleague can set up the required permanent authentication methods (on https://url.sap/getmfa).", "A TAP can also be pre-generated to become valid at a certain date time, e.g. for a planned device replacement.", "How to obtain a Temporary Access Pass (TAP)", "There are two ways to obtain a Temporary Access Pass (TAP)", "in a support case, create a service request, or reach out to IT Support via itsupport.sap.com.", "If you are a new hire, you usually receive a TAP automatically during onboarding.", "Please refer to KB How to get and use a Temporary Access Pass (TAP)"], "content": "Overview A Temporary Access Pass (\"TAP\") is a passcode that is only valid for a certain timeframe, or for one-time use (OTP). It is a fallback possibility to perform a multi-factor authentication, if other methods fail or are not available. A TAP is usually required in two scenarios: 1. in a support case request a TAP in case of any multi-factor authentication issues, if you have lost or forgotten the device you're using to authenticate (e.g. mobile phone with Microsoft Authenticator app), or if a secondary method is required for a \"Self Service Password Reset\". using the active TAP, you can then sign in and update or add further authentication methods (on https://url.sap/getmfa), e.g. to set up Microsoft Authenticator app on a new device 2. during the onboarding of a new colleague who has not enrolled in multi-factor authentication (MFA) yet With the TAP, the new colleague can set up the required permanent authentication methods (on https://url.sap/getmfa). A TAP can also be pre-generated to become valid at a certain date time, e.g. for a planned device replacement. How to obtain a Temporary Access Pass (TAP) There are two ways to obtain a Temporary Access Pass (TAP) in a support case, create a service request, or reach out to IT Support via itsupport.sap.com. If you are a new hire, you usually receive a TAP automatically during onboarding. Please refer to KB How to get and use a Temporary Access Pass (TAP)", "source": "Onboarding & Offboarding", "id": 200}, {"topic": "4. Password set-up process for new SAP employees & contractors", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Overview", "In this article, which is primarily targeted at managers in SAP who are about to hire new team members, you'll find a general description of the SAP password setup process for new hires and contractors. Please note that this process is not used for existing employees - they should refer to this KB article for self -service password reset", "How does the password set-up process work?", "Password tool for new hires uses the following process flow:", "The tool relies on data from HR SuccessFactors (for internal employees) or Fieldglass (for contractors). In the early hours of the start date, an initial email is sent to the new employee or contractor to trigger the process.", "The unique URL link in the initial email will take the new hire to the tool itself.", "In the \"Identity verification\" stage, based on the HR or Fieldglass data, the new employee is asked to enter the verification data and then use SMS or voice-call PIN code verification for an extra layer of security.", "Once the identity is successfully verified, the new SAP password needs to be defined by the employee. (according to current SAP password policy)", "Once the password is successfully set, the MFA authentication method is configured automatically. For internal employees, this is an optional step (they can choose to opt-out). For external contractors, this step is mandatory, and the tool does not ask for their consent.", "Who to contact if the password setup process is failing?", "In the initial email from the tool, there are phone contacts for IT remote support hotlines that the new employee should use if the process fails to set up the new SAP password. If the employee or contractor is being onboarded locally onsite, local IT technicians may also be able to check and assist with the process.", "For more Information, please visit KB0890410"], "content": "Overview In this article, which is primarily targeted at managers in SAP who are about to hire new team members, you'll find a general description of the SAP password setup process for new hires and contractors. Please note that this process is not used for existing employees - they should refer to this KB article for self -service password reset How does the password set-up process work? Password tool for new hires uses the following process flow: The tool relies on data from HR SuccessFactors (for internal employees) or Fieldglass (for contractors). In the early hours of the start date, an initial email is sent to the new employee or contractor to trigger the process. The unique URL link in the initial email will take the new hire to the tool itself. In the \"Identity verification\" stage, based on the HR or Fieldglass data, the new employee is asked to enter the verification data and then use SMS or voice-call PIN code verification for an extra layer of security. Once the identity is successfully verified, the new SAP password needs to be defined by the employee. (according to current SAP password policy) Once the password is successfully set, the MFA authentication method is configured automatically. For internal employees, this is an optional step (they can choose to opt-out). For external contractors, this step is mandatory, and the tool does not ask for their consent. Who to contact if the password setup process is failing? In the initial email from the tool, there are phone contacts for IT remote support hotlines that the new employee should use if the process fails to set up the new SAP password. If the employee or contractor is being onboarded locally onsite, local IT technicians may also be able to check and assist with the process. For more Information, please visit KB0890410", "source": "Onboarding & Offboarding", "id": 201}, {"topic": "5. Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA)", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Overview", "Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) is a security method that requires users to provide two or more forms of authentication before being granted access to an account or data. The goal of MFA is to provide an additional layer of security beyond just a password.", "There are three common types of authentication factors:", "Knowledge factors: Something only the user knows, such as a password, PIN, or answers to security questions.", "Possession factors: Something only the user possesses, such as a smart card, security token, or mobile phone.", "Inherence factors: Something inherent to the user, such as biometric data like fingerprints, face or iris scans.", "Which MFA methods are available?", "The following MFA methods are available and can be added via https://url.sap/getmfa:", "Microsoft Authenticator App", "Phone (Call, SMS)", "Alternate Phone (Call, SMS)", "Security Questions (only used for Self-Service Password Reset)", "In addition to these MFA methods, the following strong authentication methods (password-less) are available, which have MFA already embedded:", "Windows Hello for Business", "Recommended for Windows users, with Windows Hello for Business you can sign in with a PIN code or biometrics Please see here how to set up and use Hello for Business.", "Passwordless Sign-In (Android and iOS)", "Recommended for all users, please note you need to setup the Microsoft Authenticator app first (see below), then enable passwordless sign-in. Please see instructions for Android and iOS how to set up and use passwordless sign-in.", "FIDO2 Security key (FIDO2, please note that this currently is only available for Modern Authentication Early Adopter)", "Use this method ONLY if no other strong authentication method is available. It can only be set up after migration to Modern Authentication, when instructed in the migration announcement, or after joining the Early Adopter program. Please see here how to add and use a FIDO2 security key.", "Passkey in Microsoft Authenticator app", "Primarily for use on private devices, allows to store a passkey in the Microsoft Authenticator app on your mobile device, without the need for device registration, but generally available for all users. It can only be set up after migration to Modern Authentication, when instructed in the migration announcement, or after joining the Early Adopter program. Please see here how to set up and use Passkey in Microsoft Authenticator app.", "Please note that your sign-in and authentication flow differs depending on the methods you have enabled.", "Further Information", "For more information on MFA, visit Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) on IT for You.", "How to add an MFA method such as the Microsoft Authenticator app", "For more information about Self-Service Password Reset, refer to Authentication - Self-service password reset (SSPR) FAQ.", "If you need additional help, log an MFA Service Request or go to itsupport.sap.com.", "Common questions about MFA"], "content": "Overview Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) is a security method that requires users to provide two or more forms of authentication before being granted access to an account or data. The goal of MFA is to provide an additional layer of security beyond just a password. There are three common types of authentication factors: Knowledge factors: Something only the user knows, such as a password, PIN, or answers to security questions. Possession factors: Something only the user possesses, such as a smart card, security token, or mobile phone. Inherence factors: Something inherent to the user, such as biometric data like fingerprints, face or iris scans. Which MFA methods are available? The following MFA methods are available and can be added via https://url.sap/getmfa: Microsoft Authenticator App Phone (Call, SMS) Alternate Phone (Call, SMS) Security Questions (only used for Self-Service Password Reset) In addition to these MFA methods, the following strong authentication methods (password-less) are available, which have MFA already embedded: Windows Hello for Business Recommended for Windows users, with Windows Hello for Business you can sign in with a PIN code or biometrics Please see here how to set up and use Hello for Business. Passwordless Sign-In (Android and iOS) Recommended for all users, please note you need to setup the Microsoft Authenticator app first (see below), then enable passwordless sign-in. Please see instructions for Android and iOS how to set up and use passwordless sign-in. FIDO2 Security key (FIDO2, please note that this currently is only available for Modern Authentication Early Adopter) Use this method ONLY if no other strong authentication method is available. It can only be set up after migration to Modern Authentication, when instructed in the migration announcement, or after joining the Early Adopter program. Please see here how to add and use a FIDO2 security key. Passkey in Microsoft Authenticator app Primarily for use on private devices, allows to store a passkey in the Microsoft Authenticator app on your mobile device, without the need for device registration, but generally available for all users. It can only be set up after migration to Modern Authentication, when instructed in the migration announcement, or after joining the Early Adopter program. Please see here how to set up and use Passkey in Microsoft Authenticator app. Please note that your sign-in and authentication flow differs depending on the methods you have enabled. Further Information For more information on MFA, visit Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) on IT for You. How to add an MFA method such as the Microsoft Authenticator app For more information about Self-Service Password Reset, refer to Authentication - Self-service password reset (SSPR) FAQ. If you need additional help, log an MFA Service Request or go to itsupport.sap.com. Common questions about MFA", "source": "Onboarding & Offboarding", "id": 202}, {"topic": "6. New Employee Password Reset App (NEPRA)", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["How does NEPRA work?", "A video demo of the process can be found here", "Initial phase: Initial e-mail is sent to the new employee’s private e-mail address (previously provided to HR) in the early hours of Day 1. Verification HR data from SuccessFactors is synced to the app backend on a daily basis for all new employees.", "Initial phase: Initial e-mail contains personalized unique link to the verification part of the tool. This link could be used max. 3x (but only 1x successfully) and expires in 48 hours. End-users need to click on this link using his/her personal computer or mobile device.", "Verification part consists of using the unique link from the email, providing the birth date, last 4 digits from the phone number (previously provided to HR) and in the second step: verification SMS or phone call is used to receive verification code which user needs to enter to the app", "Password set-up phase: Once the verification process is successfully done, a new password setup page is displayed along with password requirements info.", "Confirmation phase: Once the new password is successfully set up, a confirmation e-mail is sent to the user’s private address with further instructions.", "MFA setup phase - Once the password process is completed, the new hire's phone number is added as an MFA authentication method (via SMS). For internal new hires, NEPRA asks their approval, for external hirings, this is done automatically. Optionally, NEPRA then also offers upgrading the SMS authentication method to the MFA Authenticator app.", "Using NEPRA support application", "Generate the TAP code for new hires using the NEPRA", "For the initial login to the new SAP laptop, each employee needs to have MFA authentication already set or the TAP (Temporary access pass) must be generated by the onboarding IT technician via NEPRA support application (New Employee Password reset application). Please refer to KB how to generate the TAP code for new hires using the NEPRA.", "Confirmation phase: it may take up to 15-60 mins before the new password and user’s AD OU membership are replicated across SAP systems and before we can proceed with the first login to the SAP laptop.", "How to request access to NEPRA Application", "You need to request access to the support application using the ARM:", "System name is: CTS_IDD Role name: Nepra-api-support-role-collection Please note: It might take up to 5 days to synchronize ARM Role to the NEPRA, so please have a patience.", "For more Information, please visit KB0013037", "IT Onboarding Slides location:", "Go to IT for You Hub – Getting Started – IT Onboarding. Review IT Onboarding Slides You can get more SAP IT Onboarding Process from SAP IT Onboarding Overview"], "content": "How does NEPRA work? A video demo of the process can be found here Initial phase: Initial e-mail is sent to the new employee’s private e-mail address (previously provided to HR) in the early hours of Day 1. Verification HR data from SuccessFactors is synced to the app backend on a daily basis for all new employees. Initial phase: Initial e-mail contains personalized unique link to the verification part of the tool. This link could be used max. 3x (but only 1x successfully) and expires in 48 hours. End-users need to click on this link using his/her personal computer or mobile device. Verification part consists of using the unique link from the email, providing the birth date, last 4 digits from the phone number (previously provided to HR) and in the second step: verification SMS or phone call is used to receive verification code which user needs to enter to the app Password set-up phase: Once the verification process is successfully done, a new password setup page is displayed along with password requirements info. Confirmation phase: Once the new password is successfully set up, a confirmation e-mail is sent to the user’s private address with further instructions. MFA setup phase - Once the password process is completed, the new hire's phone number is added as an MFA authentication method (via SMS). For internal new hires, NEPRA asks their approval, for external hirings, this is done automatically. Optionally, NEPRA then also offers upgrading the SMS authentication method to the MFA Authenticator app. Using NEPRA support application Generate the TAP code for new hires using the NEPRA For the initial login to the new SAP laptop, each employee needs to have MFA authentication already set or the TAP (Temporary access pass) must be generated by the onboarding IT technician via NEPRA support application (New Employee Password reset application). Please refer to KB how to generate the TAP code for new hires using the NEPRA. Confirmation phase: it may take up to 15-60 mins before the new password and user’s AD OU membership are replicated across SAP systems and before we can proceed with the first login to the SAP laptop. How to request access to NEPRA Application You need to request access to the support application using the ARM: System name is: CTS_IDD Role name: Nepra-api-support-role-collection Please note: It might take up to 5 days to synchronize ARM Role to the NEPRA, so please have a patience. For more Information, please visit KB0013037 IT Onboarding Slides location: Go to IT for You Hub – Getting Started – IT Onboarding. Review IT Onboarding Slides You can get more SAP IT Onboarding Process from SAP IT Onboarding Overview", "source": "Onboarding & Offboarding", "id": 203}, {"topic": "7. CLEA Offboarding and General Hardware Return Process", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Overview", "This KB is intended for OSS.", "You will find below the steps to be taken to return a device to IT via CLEA.", "This guide describes the process difference between offboarding and hardware return in general.", "Important notice: A device can be returned to IT on behalf of someone else. The most convenient way to process such a request is to have the client who wishes to return an asset to IT initiate the hardware return process from My IT Equipment as a self-service.", "CLEA will run into error if the owner of the to-be-returned device has been terminated already. (user account disabled / email inbox closed)", "In such cases OSS has to return to the legacy process and do the hardware return request manually. (Raise a hardware return ticket; check HRC (Hardware Return Checker), update master record (ISP))", "Please make sure to pick up and maintain all CLEA-generated tickets because the clients may use them as a channel for communication.", "Unreturned Hardware Action Timeline", "All devices must be returned to SAP IT by the last working day. If any hardware is not returned by the termination date, appropriate actions will be taken.", "Day 1: A first reminder email is sent to the manager.", "Day 7: A second reminder email is sent to the manager, and an IT incident is raised to disable the device.", "Day 14: A final reminder email is sent to the manager.", "Day 21: A Resolver incident is raised for GPS, and the pending hardware return ticket is closed.", "More information, refer to KB0837836"], "content": "Overview This KB is intended for OSS. You will find below the steps to be taken to return a device to IT via CLEA. This guide describes the process difference between offboarding and hardware return in general. Important notice: A device can be returned to IT on behalf of someone else. The most convenient way to process such a request is to have the client who wishes to return an asset to IT initiate the hardware return process from My IT Equipment as a self-service. CLEA will run into error if the owner of the to-be-returned device has been terminated already. (user account disabled / email inbox closed) In such cases OSS has to return to the legacy process and do the hardware return request manually. (Raise a hardware return ticket; check HRC (Hardware Return Checker), update master record (ISP)) Please make sure to pick up and maintain all CLEA-generated tickets because the clients may use them as a channel for communication. Unreturned Hardware Action Timeline All devices must be returned to SAP IT by the last working day. If any hardware is not returned by the termination date, appropriate actions will be taken. Day 1: A first reminder email is sent to the manager. Day 7: A second reminder email is sent to the manager, and an IT incident is raised to disable the device. Day 14: A final reminder email is sent to the manager. Day 21: A Resolver incident is raised for GPS, and the pending hardware return ticket is closed. More information, refer to KB0837836", "source": "Onboarding & Offboarding", "id": 204}, {"topic": "7. CLEA Offboarding and General Hardware Return Process", "section": "7.1 Offboarding process - Hardware return", "paragraphs": ["The offboarding process is composed of the following stages:", "Declare leaving SAP to HR or the manager.", "A hardware return ticket opens automatically: After an employee notifies HR or the manager about leaving SAP, hardware return tickets for all employee’s devices are opened automatically.", "Automated information flow: Leaver – Manager – HR – IT: After the ticket is opened, an email with the ticket link explaining the offboarding process is sent to the leaver, manager, and HR.", "Hardware return: The leaver returns the hardware to IT on their last day of work. The hardware can be returned in person at the office. If you cannot return the equipment in person:", "Go to My IT Equipment", "Select the device you would like to return. Note: If you do not see the equipment you intend to return, such as your monitor, create a ticket. Select \"Please contact me, I need help here...\"", "Choose \"Return Equipment.\" Return options for your location will be displayed.", "Select Return remote.", "Follow the instructions to request a remote return.", "Offboarding successful: After all the devices are returned to IT, an email is sent to the manager and HR confirming the offboarding process is complete and successful.", "More information, refer to KB0555342"], "content": "The offboarding process is composed of the following stages: Declare leaving SAP to HR or the manager. A hardware return ticket opens automatically: After an employee notifies HR or the manager about leaving SAP, hardware return tickets for all employee’s devices are opened automatically. Automated information flow: Leaver – Manager – HR – IT: After the ticket is opened, an email with the ticket link explaining the offboarding process is sent to the leaver, manager, and HR. Hardware return: The leaver returns the hardware to IT on their last day of work. The hardware can be returned in person at the office. If you cannot return the equipment in person: Go to My IT Equipment Select the device you would like to return. Note: If you do not see the equipment you intend to return, such as your monitor, create a ticket. Select \"Please contact me, I need help here...\" Choose \"Return Equipment.\" Return options for your location will be displayed. Select Return remote. Follow the instructions to request a remote return. Offboarding successful: After all the devices are returned to IT, an email is sent to the manager and HR confirming the offboarding process is complete and successful. More information, refer to KB0555342", "source": "Onboarding & Offboarding", "id": 205}, {"topic": "7. CLEA Offboarding and General Hardware Return Process", "section": "7.2 Hardware - How to return Equipment", "paragraphs": ["Overview", "This knowledge base article describes how to return SAP equipment (laptop, mobile, tablet, monitor, headset, mouse, keyboard, and other IT accessories …), and how to prepare the equipment for return.", "How to return your own equipment", "Go to the My IT Equipment app,", "Once there, click on “My device” It will display all your assigned Equipment such as laptop, monitor.", "Select the equipment you want to return", "Click on “Return Equipment”", "If your equipment for return is NOT listed under my device:", "In the same “My IT Equipment” app, click on “Create ticket” button located at the bottom right. This will take you to the “Personal Hardware – IT Equipment Data Maintenance” form.", "NOTE: The “Create Ticket” option within the “My IT Equipment” is different from “creating a ticket” for IT support via any other means. It is important you ensure you click this option from My IT Equipment page only. It is the fourth option next to “Lost or Stolen”.", "Alternatively, go directly to the Personal Hardware form via this link IT Equipment Data Maintenance Form, then follow the next steps.", "When the form page is open, choose the option that says, \"Please contact me, I need help here...\" and proceed to click the Submit button on the screen.", "Once submitted, you will be contacted by the Support team.", "If your equipment for return is listed under my device:", "Click on “Return Equipment”, you will be prompted with the available return options for your location:", "Choose Return onsite for returning your device with all provided accessories to IT staff at an IT Link Center in the country where it was issued.", "Return using Locker (not available for desktop screens): Based on availability/capacity, once you receive the email with drop-off instructions, you can return the device via the selected IT Locker", "Choose Return Remote (if available in your location) If you are unable to return the equipment personally, select the remote return option. The specific remote return method will depend on your country:", "For many regions, you may be asked to purchase an Ariba Return Box and receive a shipping label.", "For users in the US and Canada, the IT HW Box method is available.", "In other countries, a local process may apply; follow the instructions provided for your location.", "The onscreen instructions will guide you to the remote return method available in your location—simply follow the steps provided to complete the process.", "Notes:", "All hardware must be returned in the country where it was handed out.", "It can only be handed out in another SAP office if it is in the same country and IT Services are present. It can be found in SAP policies.", "Be aware, if you return the device personally without going through the above step, you will be asked by the IT personnel to provide an auto-generated PIN code which will be sent to your SAP email (not applicable for leaving Internal SAP employees).", "You will need an SAP-issued device during the return process to obtain the code. If you cannot provide the PIN code at the time of return, you will have to give it to the IT personnel remotely once you have access to your email.", "More information, refer to KB0013029"], "content": "Overview This knowledge base article describes how to return SAP equipment (laptop, mobile, tablet, monitor, headset, mouse, keyboard, and other IT accessories …), and how to prepare the equipment for return. How to return your own equipment Go to the My IT Equipment app, Once there, click on “My device” It will display all your assigned Equipment such as laptop, monitor. Select the equipment you want to return Click on “Return Equipment” If your equipment for return is NOT listed under my device: In the same “My IT Equipment” app, click on “Create ticket” button located at the bottom right. This will take you to the “Personal Hardware – IT Equipment Data Maintenance” form. NOTE: The “Create Ticket” option within the “My IT Equipment” is different from “creating a ticket” for IT support via any other means. It is important you ensure you click this option from My IT Equipment page only. It is the fourth option next to “Lost or Stolen”. Alternatively, go directly to the Personal Hardware form via this link IT Equipment Data Maintenance Form, then follow the next steps. When the form page is open, choose the option that says, \"Please contact me, I need help here...\" and proceed to click the Submit button on the screen. Once submitted, you will be contacted by the Support team. If your equipment for return is listed under my device: Click on “Return Equipment”, you will be prompted with the available return options for your location: Choose Return onsite for returning your device with all provided accessories to IT staff at an IT Link Center in the country where it was issued. Return using Locker (not available for desktop screens): Based on availability/capacity, once you receive the email with drop-off instructions, you can return the device via the selected IT Locker Choose Return Remote (if available in your location) If you are unable to return the equipment personally, select the remote return option. The specific remote return method will depend on your country: For many regions, you may be asked to purchase an Ariba Return Box and receive a shipping label. For users in the US and Canada, the IT HW Box method is available. In other countries, a local process may apply; follow the instructions provided for your location. The onscreen instructions will guide you to the remote return method available in your location—simply follow the steps provided to complete the process. Notes: All hardware must be returned in the country where it was handed out. It can only be handed out in another SAP office if it is in the same country and IT Services are present. It can be found in SAP policies. Be aware, if you return the device personally without going through the above step, you will be asked by the IT personnel to provide an auto-generated PIN code which will be sent to your SAP email (not applicable for leaving Internal SAP employees). You will need an SAP-issued device during the return process to obtain the code. If you cannot provide the PIN code at the time of return, you will have to give it to the IT personnel remotely once you have access to your email. More information, refer to KB0013029", "source": "Onboarding & Offboarding", "id": 206}, {"topic": "", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["ONE Support", "Internal- SAP Only", "Version control", "If you find any content in this document is out of date, feel free to contact the Authors for feedback!", "Thanks for your cooperation in advance!", "Area: Printing Services", "Contents: Main Concepts and FAQ"], "content": "ONE Support Internal- SAP Only Version control If you find any content in this document is out of date, feel free to contact the Authors for feedback! Thanks for your cooperation in advance! Area: Printing Services Contents: Main Concepts and FAQ", "source": "Printing Services", "id": 207}, {"topic": "Printing Services", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["GPS= Global Printing Services"], "content": "GPS= Global Printing Services", "source": "Printing Services", "id": 208}, {"topic": "Printing Services", "section": "1.1 Delivery of toner and other consumable material", "paragraphs": ["The respective current provider (General framework by GPS) delivers new toner and print drums to local IT if the following thresholds are reached: Toner below 15%, print drum below 5%.", "In case an additional toner or other consumable material is needed it should be ordered via the HP Inc Service Hotline (see chapter 3). If there is a problem with the device after you replaced toner or other consumables complain via the HP Inc Service Hotline.", "All printer kits (e. g. picture transfer, picture fixing etc.) are exchanged by HP technicians (monitoring by HP)."], "content": "The respective current provider (General framework by GPS) delivers new toner and print drums to local IT if the following thresholds are reached: Toner below 15%, print drum below 5%. In case an additional toner or other consumable material is needed it should be ordered via the HP Inc Service Hotline (see chapter 3). If there is a problem with the device after you replaced toner or other consumables complain via the HP Inc Service Hotline. All printer kits (e. g. picture transfer, picture fixing etc.) are exchanged by HP technicians (monitoring by HP).", "source": "Printing Services", "id": 209}, {"topic": "Printing Services", "section": "1.2 Toner Exchange", "paragraphs": ["In case of empty toners or consumed print drums an automatic email will be sent to the responsible IT colleagues mentioned in the monitoring system “WebJet”(notification at 2%, 1% and 0%). It is recommended to replace the toner only when the threshold is at 1% - as long as there is no compelling “Business Need”. Please check the level of the toner before the replacement via EWS e.g. https://STRA.str.sap.corp. If the replacement is necessary, check the level once again after the replacement if the status is now 100 %. If there is no change of the level a restart of the device is necessary. If there is a comment like “used cartridge is in use” for a new cartridge, please complain about this cartridge via the HP Inc Service Hotline for printer and MFP devices (see chapter 3). Please use for that the information of shipment from the packaging.", "To replace toner cartridges, take the oldest respective cartridge in storage for the printer model and ignore for which printer this was intended.", "Empty toner cartridges must collect in toner recycling containers (boxes) for the return to HP. The reason for that is: HP has the ownership of these and according to the contract the empty cartridges must be returned. For information about the process of cost free delivery and collection of the containers", "Please also notice: The collected empty cartridges must be sent back to HP in October every year, at the latest in November, even if the box is not yet full."], "content": "In case of empty toners or consumed print drums an automatic email will be sent to the responsible IT colleagues mentioned in the monitoring system “WebJet”(notification at 2%, 1% and 0%). It is recommended to replace the toner only when the threshold is at 1% - as long as there is no compelling “Business Need”. Please check the level of the toner before the replacement via EWS e.g. https://STRA.str.sap.corp. If the replacement is necessary, check the level once again after the replacement if the status is now 100 %. If there is no change of the level a restart of the device is necessary. If there is a comment like “used cartridge is in use” for a new cartridge, please complain about this cartridge via the HP Inc Service Hotline for printer and MFP devices (see chapter 3). Please use for that the information of shipment from the packaging. To replace toner cartridges, take the oldest respective cartridge in storage for the printer model and ignore for which printer this was intended. Empty toner cartridges must collect in toner recycling containers (boxes) for the return to HP. The reason for that is: HP has the ownership of these and according to the contract the empty cartridges must be returned. For information about the process of cost free delivery and collection of the containers Please also notice: The collected empty cartridges must be sent back to HP in October every year, at the latest in November, even if the box is not yet full.", "source": "Printing Services", "id": 210}, {"topic": "Printing Services", "section": "1.3 Printer Move or get a new printer", "paragraphs": ["Please contact the GPS Team before you move a printer. The GPS Team will then prepare the device for the move. There are some necessary steps to do before the move as e. g. opening the administrative menu and setting the correct new IP address.", "Regarding a new printer you must connect it to an active network port and check the network connection with the ping command. If the printer is online, please contact the GPS Team. Then you will get the name and the planed IP address for the new device."], "content": "Please contact the GPS Team before you move a printer. The GPS Team will then prepare the device for the move. There are some necessary steps to do before the move as e. g. opening the administrative menu and setting the correct new IP address. Regarding a new printer you must connect it to an active network port and check the network connection with the ping command. If the printer is online, please contact the GPS Team. Then you will get the name and the planed IP address for the new device.", "source": "Printing Services", "id": 211}, {"topic": "Printing Services", "section": "1.4 Printer Return", "paragraphs": ["Before returning printers, all data held on the device must be deleted (wiped).", "For HP devices this is controlled by security settings applied by the GPS team - the data is deleted permanently after each printout (deletion of data and not only flag).", "For other devices the service owner for SAP IT printing services needs to be contacted for each individual case via GPS Team."], "content": "Before returning printers, all data held on the device must be deleted (wiped). For HP devices this is controlled by security settings applied by the GPS team - the data is deleted permanently after each printout (deletion of data and not only flag). For other devices the service owner for SAP IT printing services needs to be contacted for each individual case via GPS Team.", "source": "Printing Services", "id": 212}, {"topic": "Printing Services", "section": "1.5 End user support regarding printing issues", "paragraphs": ["Please use the Knowledge Section on the right side of this page and IT for You - Printing @ SAP.", "For Details, you may refer to “Printer Support”"], "content": "Please use the Knowledge Section on the right side of this page and IT for You - Printing @ SAP. For Details, you may refer to “Printer Support”", "source": "Printing Services", "id": 213}, {"topic": "Printing Services", "section": "1.6 Create Printer labels​", "paragraphs": ["Each printer at SAP should have the correct label with the physical name for unique identification.", "The service owner for SAP IT printing services defines the physical names. Ask for names MOS-GPS Team.", "This article describes how to create the IT Onsite Support (2nd level) a printer label included troubleshooting.", "Classification of the name for printer queues and physical printers in the SAP printing environment", "We differentiate between BadgePrint / virtual printer queues and physical printers in the printing environment.", "a) BadgePrint- / virtual printer queues", "We see these logical names in the SAP Printing tool: e.g. PWDF_BWS, PWDF_COS, PEM1_BWS, PAM2_COS,… These are the names of virtual printer queues, that a user has to connect for Badge Printing at SAP. That‘s no name of a physical device.", "The name of the virtual printer queue, that supports HP AC Badge Printing, consists the following signs:", "P – Pull Printing", "Location = 3 Letters of the location e. g. LON, WDF, PAL (Building code from Facility Management)", "or 2 Letters of a region and a number 1- 4 (AM for region AMER, AP for region APJ or EM for region EMEA, e. g. PAM1_, PAM2_, PAP3_, PEM1_, …)", "BWS = Black/White Secure", "COS = Color Secure", "b) Physical printers", "Every printer should have a label with a right name with 4 characters, e. g. FRAB, DD20, T283,…", "The MOS-GPS team defines the names.", "You have to create a label with this name for each printer and adhesive the label onto a fixed part of the printer (e. g. not on the scanner unit).", "Important: When there is a device name change then you have to create a new label with the correct new name.", "You may have to ask for the correct name the MOS-GPS Team: DL SAPIT-POP-TEC-GLOBAL", "Creating of the printer labels", "The documentation you find here. Most important for the printer labels are chapter 1 - 4, 9 and 10.", "You should select the FORM SAPZ10 (included the building code) or SAPZ15, please.", "SAPZ10 / Printer label or SAPZ15 / Printer label small", "Troubleshooting for Label printers", "Chapter 12 of the documentation contains typical problems with the Zebra label printer and information for Troubleshooting", "additional to the IT internal KBA KB0571730."], "content": "Each printer at SAP should have the correct label with the physical name for unique identification. The service owner for SAP IT printing services defines the physical names. Ask for names MOS-GPS Team. This article describes how to create the IT Onsite Support (2nd level) a printer label included troubleshooting. Classification of the name for printer queues and physical printers in the SAP printing environment We differentiate between BadgePrint / virtual printer queues and physical printers in the printing environment. a) BadgePrint- / virtual printer queues We see these logical names in the SAP Printing tool: e.g. PWDF_BWS, PWDF_COS, PEM1_BWS, PAM2_COS,… These are the names of virtual printer queues, that a user has to connect for Badge Printing at SAP. That‘s no name of a physical device. The name of the virtual printer queue, that supports HP AC Badge Printing, consists the following signs: P – Pull Printing Location = 3 Letters of the location e. g. LON, WDF, PAL (Building code from Facility Management) or 2 Letters of a region and a number 1- 4 (AM for region AMER, AP for region APJ or EM for region EMEA, e. g. PAM1_, PAM2_, PAP3_, PEM1_, …) BWS = Black/White Secure COS = Color Secure b) Physical printers Every printer should have a label with a right name with 4 characters, e. g. FRAB, DD20, T283,… The MOS-GPS team defines the names. You have to create a label with this name for each printer and adhesive the label onto a fixed part of the printer (e. g. not on the scanner unit). Important: When there is a device name change then you have to create a new label with the correct new name. You may have to ask for the correct name the MOS-GPS Team: DL SAPIT-POP-TEC-GLOBAL Creating of the printer labels The documentation you find here. Most important for the printer labels are chapter 1 - 4, 9 and 10. You should select the FORM SAPZ10 (included the building code) or SAPZ15, please. SAPZ10 / Printer label or SAPZ15 / Printer label small Troubleshooting for Label printers Chapter 12 of the documentation contains typical problems with the Zebra label printer and information for Troubleshooting additional to the IT internal KBA KB0571730.", "source": "Printing Services", "id": 214}, {"topic": "2. User Menu", "section": "2.1 Printer Overview", "paragraphs": ["With the HP AC Badge Printing solution, you can send print jobs to an internal SAP “Printer Cloud”. The job can be printed by using the standard SAP access (SIPORT - Appendix 1) or a chip on every printer that has a card reader installed and activated.", "This solution will be available on multifunctional printers in public printer rooms (excludes printers with limited access).", "Advantages of Badge Printing:", "Secure Printing, User data protection", "No uncollected, unnecessary printouts in the printer rooms (Exception Appendix 2).", "Print jobs that have not been printed within 24 hours will be automatically deleted.", "Badge Printing = Follow me concept: You can pick up your print jobs on any printer with an activated card reader, no matter what virtual printer connection (worldwide) is used. Example: If a device is currently out of order or is occupied by another printout you can pick up your printouts on the next device with a card reader. That also means if your installed printer queue has a problem, you can use every other virtual printer queue worldwide.", "Benefits of the new SAPprinting UI5:", "Now we have only one tool for printing from Windows and Mac computers and it works with different browsers.", "https://sapprinting.wdf.sap.corp:1080/", "Printing Terms", "BadgePrint = naming for standard print via server based printer queue.", "P – Pull Printing.", "Location = 3 Letters of your location i.e. LON, WDF, PAL (Building code from Facility Management).", "BW = Black/White", "CO = Color", "S = SECURE.", "Note: _BADGE, _USB or _EQUI not have connect to printer, it’s just the view to show the location where you can find them", "Printers install environment", "Only on Corporate Network or Company VPN (Global Protect or F5)", "Examples", "PHAM_BWS = Black/White-Printer in Hamburg.", "PPAL_COS = Color-Printer in Palo Alto.", "*SAP Standard is a _BWS connection that supports the Green IT goals of SAP.", "The names of the physical printers (4 characters, e. g. HAMD) will remain in the SAP Printing Tool in order to show the physical location of the printer. You will connect virtually to BADGEPRINT."], "content": "With the HP AC Badge Printing solution, you can send print jobs to an internal SAP “Printer Cloud”. The job can be printed by using the standard SAP access (SIPORT - Appendix 1) or a chip on every printer that has a card reader installed and activated. This solution will be available on multifunctional printers in public printer rooms (excludes printers with limited access). Advantages of Badge Printing: Secure Printing, User data protection No uncollected, unnecessary printouts in the printer rooms (Exception Appendix 2). Print jobs that have not been printed within 24 hours will be automatically deleted. Badge Printing = Follow me concept: You can pick up your print jobs on any printer with an activated card reader, no matter what virtual printer connection (worldwide) is used. Example: If a device is currently out of order or is occupied by another printout you can pick up your printouts on the next device with a card reader. That also means if your installed printer queue has a problem, you can use every other virtual printer queue worldwide. Benefits of the new SAPprinting UI5: Now we have only one tool for printing from Windows and Mac computers and it works with different browsers. https://sapprinting.wdf.sap.corp:1080/ Printing Terms BadgePrint = naming for standard print via server based printer queue. P – Pull Printing. Location = 3 Letters of your location i.e. LON, WDF, PAL (Building code from Facility Management). BW = Black/White CO = Color S = SECURE. Note: _BADGE, _USB or _EQUI not have connect to printer, it’s just the view to show the location where you can find them Printers install environment Only on Corporate Network or Company VPN (Global Protect or F5) Examples PHAM_BWS = Black/White-Printer in Hamburg. PPAL_COS = Color-Printer in Palo Alto. *SAP Standard is a _BWS connection that supports the Green IT goals of SAP. The names of the physical printers (4 characters, e. g. HAMD) will remain in the SAP Printing Tool in order to show the physical location of the printer. You will connect virtually to BADGEPRINT.", "source": "Printing Services", "id": 215}, {"topic": "2. User Menu", "section": "2.2 Registration to the HP AC database for Badge Printing", "paragraphs": ["It is necessary to register every new badge once to the HP AC database. This registration enables all HP AC Badge Printing enabled printers worldwide to print documents stored in the printer Cloud. You need an active standard SAP access card (SIPORT - Appendix 1) or chip and an HP printer with an activated card reader. (You can identify an active card reader with a Led control light on it.)", "If you change your SAP Access Badge, you need to re-register it (follow the steps below).", "The registration of a badge doesn’t need any PUK.", "Registration Steps:", "Hold the printing badge to the card reader – only your single badge, no other card or mobile nearby", "Press Ok", "Enter your credentials (your Username = UserID = C-, D- or I-user, not the mail address and your computer login password) and press ok.", "Now you should see your name on the top of the display of the printer.", "If the registration failed, please use the IT Support Portal and request the reset of the registration of the card. Please enter in the field the description \"Reset a card / badge for printing\". We don't need any number of the badge, but the username and the UserID that will be shown at the display or the error message.", "Please don’t register any temporary card for Badge Printing"], "content": "It is necessary to register every new badge once to the HP AC database. This registration enables all HP AC Badge Printing enabled printers worldwide to print documents stored in the printer Cloud. You need an active standard SAP access card (SIPORT - Appendix 1) or chip and an HP printer with an activated card reader. (You can identify an active card reader with a Led control light on it.) If you change your SAP Access Badge, you need to re-register it (follow the steps below). The registration of a badge doesn’t need any PUK. Registration Steps: Hold the printing badge to the card reader – only your single badge, no other card or mobile nearby Press Ok Enter your credentials (your Username = UserID = C-, D- or I-user, not the mail address and your computer login password) and press ok. Now you should see your name on the top of the display of the printer. If the registration failed, please use the IT Support Portal and request the reset of the registration of the card. Please enter in the field the description \"Reset a card / badge for printing\". We don't need any number of the badge, but the username and the UserID that will be shown at the display or the error message. Please don’t register any temporary card for Badge Printing", "source": "Printing Services", "id": 216}, {"topic": "3. Printing with HP AC Badge Printing", "section": "3.1 Prerequisites", "paragraphs": ["Installed virtual print queue for BadgePrint, _BWS or _COS", "Successful registration of an access card or chip – one-time registration is good until your badge change worldwide", "Printouts to printers with the suffix _BWS or _COS will not be printed automatically but will be stored in the printer cloud. When you want to retrieve your printout, go to the next printer with a card reader, hold your access card to the card reader or enter you credentials (your Username = UserID = C-, D- or I-user, not the mail address and your computer login password) to print your documents."], "content": "Installed virtual print queue for BadgePrint, _BWS or _COS Successful registration of an access card or chip – one-time registration is good until your badge change worldwide Printouts to printers with the suffix _BWS or _COS will not be printed automatically but will be stored in the printer cloud. When you want to retrieve your printout, go to the next printer with a card reader, hold your access card to the card reader or enter you credentials (your Username = UserID = C-, D- or I-user, not the mail address and your computer login password) to print your documents.", "source": "Printing Services", "id": 217}, {"topic": "3. Printing with HP AC Badge Printing", "section": "3.2 Handling", "paragraphs": ["When the device is ready, hold your access card to card reader until you hear a beep. If you keep the card pressed against the reader for too long, your log in will fail. After a successful login, your name will be displayed in the first line of the screen.", "If the printer status is in Sleep/Standby Mode then your card will first activate the scanner before the printer becomes available for printing.", "HP AC Secure Pull Print opens a list of print jobs from the user who logged on. Now you can select the print job you would like to print or remove from the print queue.", "By default, print jobs are deleted from the Printer Cloud after printing. Print jobs not picked up are automatically deleted after 24 hours.", "If you hold the card against the reader again, the user will be sign out and no user ID will be displayed on the screen.", "If not take any action, you will be logged out automatically around 25 seconds", "3.3 Badge Printing from SAP Corporate ERP system (e.g. ISP)", "a. Set badge printer to default", "Enter \"Printer\" in the search field next to the Start Icon on your computer and select \"Printer & scanners\".", "Find a connected Badge Printer queue what you want to use and check the settings with \"Manage\".", "If not already done - \"Set as default\"", "PEM3_BWS is just an example! There are many more Badge Printer queues available around the globe like PWDF_BWS, PNSQ_COS, PPV0_BWS, PBLL_COS or PSIN_COS…etc.", "b. Add the default printer \"LOCL\" in your SAP system (ISP)", "In your SAP system add the default output device.", "Open the menu \"More\" - \"System\" - \"User Profile\" - \"User Data\" then switch to \"Defaults\".", "c. Print from SAP system using \"LOCL\" = Default printer", "In your SAP system at the right top corner hit the Printer symbol and a new window will open and show your output device LOCL.", "Click the check mark and your printer selection window will popup."], "content": "When the device is ready, hold your access card to card reader until you hear a beep. If you keep the card pressed against the reader for too long, your log in will fail. After a successful login, your name will be displayed in the first line of the screen. If the printer status is in Sleep/Standby Mode then your card will first activate the scanner before the printer becomes available for printing. HP AC Secure Pull Print opens a list of print jobs from the user who logged on. Now you can select the print job you would like to print or remove from the print queue. By default, print jobs are deleted from the Printer Cloud after printing. Print jobs not picked up are automatically deleted after 24 hours. If you hold the card against the reader again, the user will be sign out and no user ID will be displayed on the screen. If not take any action, you will be logged out automatically around 25 seconds 3.3 Badge Printing from SAP Corporate ERP system (e.g. ISP) a. Set badge printer to default Enter \"Printer\" in the search field next to the Start Icon on your computer and select \"Printer & scanners\". Find a connected Badge Printer queue what you want to use and check the settings with \"Manage\". If not already done - \"Set as default\" PEM3_BWS is just an example! There are many more Badge Printer queues available around the globe like PWDF_BWS, PNSQ_COS, PPV0_BWS, PBLL_COS or PSIN_COS…etc. b. Add the default printer \"LOCL\" in your SAP system (ISP) In your SAP system add the default output device. Open the menu \"More\" - \"System\" - \"User Profile\" - \"User Data\" then switch to \"Defaults\". c. Print from SAP system using \"LOCL\" = Default printer In your SAP system at the right top corner hit the Printer symbol and a new window will open and show your output device LOCL. Click the check mark and your printer selection window will popup.", "source": "Printing Services", "id": 218}, {"topic": "4. Scan to Email", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["How to Scan to Email?", "Scan Selection: Hold your badge to the card reader (if available). Select Scan to Email on the printer menu. Note: The email size is limited to 32 MB.", "Adjust: Your name will automatically populate under the To section when you successfully scan your badge, else enter your desired recipient user ID using the keyboard below the display.", "Option: Select Options to change default settings if needed (e.g. Color/Black, dpi Resolution,).", "Scanning: To begin the scan procedure, press the Send button.", "Reset: Press the button in the left upper corner to close the session. (after 10 sec the device resets automatically)", "Important notes:", "This function is only available for internal SAP addresses - not for external addresses.", "Tip: Send the document to your own User-ID, check it and forward it via Outlook.", "For details, you may refer to “Badge Printing”."], "content": "How to Scan to Email? Scan Selection: Hold your badge to the card reader (if available). Select Scan to Email on the printer menu. Note: The email size is limited to 32 MB. Adjust: Your name will automatically populate under the To section when you successfully scan your badge, else enter your desired recipient user ID using the keyboard below the display. Option: Select Options to change default settings if needed (e.g. Color/Black, dpi Resolution,). Scanning: To begin the scan procedure, press the Send button. Reset: Press the button in the left upper corner to close the session. (after 10 sec the device resets automatically) Important notes: This function is only available for internal SAP addresses - not for external addresses. Tip: Send the document to your own User-ID, check it and forward it via Outlook. For details, you may refer to “Badge Printing”.", "source": "Printing Services", "id": 219}, {"topic": "5. How do you find a special printer", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Link to the SAP Printing tool", "Go to SAP Printing Tool. If you only see a blank page, please refresh / reload the page once again, e. g. with <F5>.", "Find the nearest printer with a card reader on the floor of your building, where you can pick up your printouts.", "To find the nearest printer with a card reader on your floor of your building, where you can pick up your printouts, use the left navigation section. Not to be confused with “Connect to printer”. Then please see Connect to printer. You must navigate in the left navigation section from up to down: Region > Country > Location > Building > Floor > section", "1. Example: You are in EMEA > DE > RATINGEN > DUE04 > 3rd floor > section B", "2. Example: You are in EMEA > IT > ROME > ROM02 > 2nd floor", "Find a special printer, e.g. a DIN A3 format enabled printer or a plotter.", "Below the search field, there is a search function with various filter options for special printer types.", "You could select one or more Filter Options below the search field:", "and you could enter only or additional a City / Office Location (e. g. Eschborn) or a building code (e. g. FRA01) in the search field when you search a printer in a location.", "The example below shows the search for A3 printers in the location Eschborn. These are the printers, where you could pick up printouts in format DIN A3. However, we cannot guarantee that A3 paper lies in the appropriate printers. If the tray for A3 paper is empty you must ask the colleagues from Facility or IT onsite.", "A larger format is not available in our standard office. Please be aware: When there is a _BADGE printer queue without a button \"Connect to Printer\", you must print to your virtual Printer Queue, for example PEM3_BWS, PEM4_COS, PWDF_BWS or PWDF_COS, ... Then you can pick up your printouts on the corresponding A3 printers that you found during your search.", "Icons in the SAP Printing tool", "The small icons next to the printer icon show the type of the printer:", "This printer can print color. Is this icon not there, then it prints only black, no colors, also when you have sent your print job to a virtual color BADGEPRINT queue (_COS).", "This printer can print format DIN A4 and A3, however we cannot guarantee that also A3 paper lies in the appropriate printer."], "content": "Link to the SAP Printing tool Go to SAP Printing Tool. If you only see a blank page, please refresh / reload the page once again, e. g. with <F5>. Find the nearest printer with a card reader on the floor of your building, where you can pick up your printouts. To find the nearest printer with a card reader on your floor of your building, where you can pick up your printouts, use the left navigation section. Not to be confused with “Connect to printer”. Then please see Connect to printer. You must navigate in the left navigation section from up to down: Region > Country > Location > Building > Floor > section 1. Example: You are in EMEA > DE > RATINGEN > DUE04 > 3rd floor > section B 2. Example: You are in EMEA > IT > ROME > ROM02 > 2nd floor Find a special printer, e.g. a DIN A3 format enabled printer or a plotter. Below the search field, there is a search function with various filter options for special printer types. You could select one or more Filter Options below the search field: and you could enter only or additional a City / Office Location (e. g. Eschborn) or a building code (e. g. FRA01) in the search field when you search a printer in a location. The example below shows the search for A3 printers in the location Eschborn. These are the printers, where you could pick up printouts in format DIN A3. However, we cannot guarantee that A3 paper lies in the appropriate printers. If the tray for A3 paper is empty you must ask the colleagues from Facility or IT onsite. A larger format is not available in our standard office. Please be aware: When there is a _BADGE printer queue without a button \"Connect to Printer\", you must print to your virtual Printer Queue, for example PEM3_BWS, PEM4_COS, PWDF_BWS or PWDF_COS, ... Then you can pick up your printouts on the corresponding A3 printers that you found during your search. Icons in the SAP Printing tool The small icons next to the printer icon show the type of the printer: This printer can print color. Is this icon not there, then it prints only black, no colors, also when you have sent your print job to a virtual color BADGEPRINT queue (_COS). This printer can print format DIN A4 and A3, however we cannot guarantee that also A3 paper lies in the appropriate printer.", "source": "Printing Services", "id": 220}, {"topic": "6. How to Perform Cloud Mobile Printing", "section": "6.1 What is Cloud Printing?", "paragraphs": ["Cloud Printing has an additional feature that allows you to print emails, attachments, pictures and other contents from your mobile device.", "With any SAP certified mobile device, as long as you can reach the Internet and send emails from your SAP email account, you will be able to print from your mobile device.", "Step 1 - Send the Print Job", "Note: It is very important to use the MobilePrint addresses from your own region to avoid performance issues.", "With your SAP Email account, forward or create an email and send this to the following MobilePrint address:", "AMER", "If you are located in the AMER region, send to: am@print.corp.sap or amer@print.corp.sap", "APJ", "If you are located in the APJ region, send to: ap@print.corp.sap or apj@print.corp.sap", "EMEA", "If you are located in the EMEA region, send to: em@print.corp.sap or emea@print.corp.sap", "Germany (DE)", "If you are located in Germany (DE), send to: de@print.corp.sap", "You can attach files like PDF, Word, Excel, PowerPoint, photos, etc. Every email attachment sent to this email address will be converted into PDF format. Forwarded emails with attachments will be listed as two or more separate print jobs.", "Step 2 - Pick up Print Job", "Your print job can be printed on each Badge printer based in an SAP office around the globe.", "If you print only via MobilePrint* or only via normal BadgePrint*, you will see your jobs listed directly in the printer display as shown below:", "Sign in with your badge or manual logon:", "This is what you will see using one method (either BadgePrint or MobilePrint), you may select the file and print accordingly:", "However, if you send print jobs using both methods (BadgePrint and MobilePrint) around the same time, the print jobs will be stored in different folders: BadgePrint in VPSX and MobilePrint in AM, AP, EM or DE.", "If you have a question regarding the folder name, please check KB article IKB0013530.", "Choose to open the folder which contains the print jobs you would like to print and select print accordingly:", "* BadgePrint = naming for standard print via server based printer queue (normal printing via SAP-issued laptop/desktop)", "* MobilePrint = naming for printing from a mobile device via email also known as Cloud Printing"], "content": "Cloud Printing has an additional feature that allows you to print emails, attachments, pictures and other contents from your mobile device. With any SAP certified mobile device, as long as you can reach the Internet and send emails from your SAP email account, you will be able to print from your mobile device. Step 1 - Send the Print Job Note: It is very important to use the MobilePrint addresses from your own region to avoid performance issues. With your SAP Email account, forward or create an email and send this to the following MobilePrint address: AMER If you are located in the AMER region, send to: am@print.corp.sap or amer@print.corp.sap APJ If you are located in the APJ region, send to: ap@print.corp.sap or apj@print.corp.sap EMEA If you are located in the EMEA region, send to: em@print.corp.sap or emea@print.corp.sap Germany (DE) If you are located in Germany (DE), send to: de@print.corp.sap You can attach files like PDF, Word, Excel, PowerPoint, photos, etc. Every email attachment sent to this email address will be converted into PDF format. Forwarded emails with attachments will be listed as two or more separate print jobs. Step 2 - Pick up Print Job Your print job can be printed on each Badge printer based in an SAP office around the globe. If you print only via MobilePrint* or only via normal BadgePrint*, you will see your jobs listed directly in the printer display as shown below: Sign in with your badge or manual logon: This is what you will see using one method (either BadgePrint or MobilePrint), you may select the file and print accordingly: However, if you send print jobs using both methods (BadgePrint and MobilePrint) around the same time, the print jobs will be stored in different folders: BadgePrint in VPSX and MobilePrint in AM, AP, EM or DE. If you have a question regarding the folder name, please check KB article IKB0013530. Choose to open the folder which contains the print jobs you would like to print and select print accordingly: * BadgePrint = naming for standard print via server based printer queue (normal printing via SAP-issued laptop/desktop) * MobilePrint = naming for printing from a mobile device via email also known as Cloud Printing", "source": "Printing Services", "id": 221}, {"topic": "6. How to Perform Cloud Mobile Printing", "section": "6.2 Support", "paragraphs": ["If you are experiencing issues, please try the following options:", "Frequently asked questions (IKB0013530)", "Send us feedback via the respective region mailbox: AMER, APJ and EMEA/DE"], "content": "If you are experiencing issues, please try the following options: Frequently asked questions (IKB0013530) Send us feedback via the respective region mailbox: AMER, APJ and EMEA/DE", "source": "Printing Services", "id": 222}, {"topic": "7. Troubleshooting for Printer", "section": "7.1 Printing - Reset Print Spooler", "paragraphs": ["Overview", "Some printing and communications issues may be caused by a problem with the Print Spooler. Re-starting or clearing the Print Spooler may resolve these issues. The print spooler controls print options within the Windows environment. A problem with the print spooler can affect printer driver performance and print queue responsiveness.", "Please be aware:", "This only applies to printer connections connected locally to the computer, e. g. in the home office, but not for printer connections via print servers that were installed using the SAP Printing tool, as is usual at SAP.", "Stop and Start the Print Spooler", "1. Type services.msc in the Windows Start Search box.", "2. Open the Services desktop app", "3. Locate and right-click on Print Spooler, and then click Stop from the drop-down menu.", "4. Right-click Print Spooler again, and then click Start from the drop down menu.", "Refer IKB0011219", "Method 2: Delete Files from the Spool Folder", "If you have jobs stuck in the print queue that will not delete, you might have to manually delete them.", "1. Stop the Print spooler service as shown in method 2.", "2. Navigate to: C:\\Windows\\System32\\spool\\PRINTERS", "3. Delete all the files located in this folder", "4. Start the spooler service again as shown in method 2"], "content": "Overview Some printing and communications issues may be caused by a problem with the Print Spooler. Re-starting or clearing the Print Spooler may resolve these issues. The print spooler controls print options within the Windows environment. A problem with the print spooler can affect printer driver performance and print queue responsiveness. Please be aware: This only applies to printer connections connected locally to the computer, e. g. in the home office, but not for printer connections via print servers that were installed using the SAP Printing tool, as is usual at SAP. Stop and Start the Print Spooler 1. Type services.msc in the Windows Start Search box. 2. Open the Services desktop app 3. Locate and right-click on Print Spooler, and then click Stop from the drop-down menu. 4. Right-click Print Spooler again, and then click Start from the drop down menu. Refer IKB0011219 Method 2: Delete Files from the Spool Folder If you have jobs stuck in the print queue that will not delete, you might have to manually delete them. 1. Stop the Print spooler service as shown in method 2. 2. Navigate to: C:\\Windows\\System32\\spool\\PRINTERS 3. Delete all the files located in this folder 4. Start the spooler service again as shown in method 2", "source": "Printing Services", "id": 223}, {"topic": "8. Printer FAQ", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Q1. The link to the SAPprinting UI5 App", "SAP Printing UI5 If you only see a blank page, please refresh / reload the page once again.", "Q2. Can't find the \"Connect to Printer\" button", "To connect a Badge Printing queue, please use the left navigation section to select your printer connection: (Region > Country > Location > BADGEPRINT).", "Please note the important first red lines on the home page of SAP Printing UI5.", "Q3. Unable to download and install printer", "You need a connection to VPN or corporate network.", "Q4. The Browser blocks the installation", "In the Download window select the three dots next to the message and there select “Keep”. Click on “Show more” and select “Keep anyway”.", "Click “Open file”", "Or click at the “CMD” file in the Downloads folder.", "If you get \"Window protect your PC\" click More Info and then Run Anyway", "and the printer queue will be installed.", "Q5: The installation of a printer queue doesn't work on a MacBook?", "If you have seen this message:", "The reason could be the missing “Add Printer” App, which you find in Self Service.", "Q6: You only see a blank page when you want to start the SAP Printing tool?", "Please refresh / reload the page once again.", "Q7: If you unable to printer on windows machine, what are the first things should check?", "Check Printer Driver installed or check network connection or Printer status", "Q8: How to check printer status (IP address) from Backend?", "Open Browser ->https://{PrinterMachineName} you will be able access this printer info", "Example: https://CN96", "Q8: Why is SAP IT implementing Badge Printing?", "In the past, you had to print to a specific printer and only at this printer you could collect your printouts. With the Badge Printing solution, you can print to an “anonymous” printer with a virtual printer queue. Then collect your printouts from any printer with an activated card reader worldwide.", "You can collect your printouts with your own badge or also without a badge only with your credentials (UserID - not the Email address! and your computer login password) every time on every printer with an activated card reader.", "Q9: What are the advantages for Badge Printing?", "In addition to the enhanced security of your printouts, the key benefits for all SAP employees are:", "No uncollected, unnecessary printouts in the printer room", "Print jobs that have not been printed within a certain time period are automatically deleted", "Follow Me Printing: Printing to a specific printer is now history. Instead, you will be able to store your print jobs on an internal SAP Printer Cloud. Then print them out on any MFP printer in the public printer rooms at any location worldwide.", "More info please view IKB0011778", "Q10: SAP Cloud Mobile Printing how to customize print settings...", "Customizing print settings is not possible with this Mobile Printing solution.", "All parameters like simplex, the number of prints or the paper source cannot be changed!", "This new feature is designed for easy and fast printing from mobile devices. In case you want to modify or change any print settings, kindly print from SAP issued Windows or MAC computer.", "Q11: How to Reset Print Spooler", "Please view 3 methods via IKB0011219"], "content": "Q1. The link to the SAPprinting UI5 App SAP Printing UI5 If you only see a blank page, please refresh / reload the page once again. Q2. Can't find the \"Connect to Printer\" button To connect a Badge Printing queue, please use the left navigation section to select your printer connection: (Region > Country > Location > BADGEPRINT). Please note the important first red lines on the home page of SAP Printing UI5. Q3. Unable to download and install printer You need a connection to VPN or corporate network. Q4. The Browser blocks the installation In the Download window select the three dots next to the message and there select “Keep”. Click on “Show more” and select “Keep anyway”. Click “Open file” Or click at the “CMD” file in the Downloads folder. If you get \"Window protect your PC\" click More Info and then Run Anyway and the printer queue will be installed. Q5: The installation of a printer queue doesn't work on a MacBook? If you have seen this message: The reason could be the missing “Add Printer” App, which you find in Self Service. Q6: You only see a blank page when you want to start the SAP Printing tool? Please refresh / reload the page once again. Q7: If you unable to printer on windows machine, what are the first things should check? Check Printer Driver installed or check network connection or Printer status Q8: How to check printer status (IP address) from Backend? Open Browser ->https://{PrinterMachineName} you will be able access this printer info Example: https://CN96 Q8: Why is SAP IT implementing Badge Printing? In the past, you had to print to a specific printer and only at this printer you could collect your printouts. With the Badge Printing solution, you can print to an “anonymous” printer with a virtual printer queue. Then collect your printouts from any printer with an activated card reader worldwide. You can collect your printouts with your own badge or also without a badge only with your credentials (UserID - not the Email address! and your computer login password) every time on every printer with an activated card reader. Q9: What are the advantages for Badge Printing? In addition to the enhanced security of your printouts, the key benefits for all SAP employees are: No uncollected, unnecessary printouts in the printer room Print jobs that have not been printed within a certain time period are automatically deleted Follow Me Printing: Printing to a specific printer is now history. Instead, you will be able to store your print jobs on an internal SAP Printer Cloud. Then print them out on any MFP printer in the public printer rooms at any location worldwide. More info please view IKB0011778 Q10: SAP Cloud Mobile Printing how to customize print settings... Customizing print settings is not possible with this Mobile Printing solution. All parameters like simplex, the number of prints or the paper source cannot be changed! This new feature is designed for easy and fast printing from mobile devices. In case you want to modify or change any print settings, kindly print from SAP issued Windows or MAC computer. Q11: How to Reset Print Spooler Please view 3 methods via IKB0011219", "source": "Printing Services", "id": 224}, {"topic": "", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["ONE Support", "Internal- SAP Only", "Version control", "If you find any content in this document is out of date, feel free to contact the Authors for feedback!", "Thanks for your cooperation in advance!", "Area: SAP Mobile Devices"], "content": "ONE Support Internal- SAP Only Version control If you find any content in this document is out of date, feel free to contact the Authors for feedback! Thanks for your cooperation in advance! Area: SAP Mobile Devices", "source": "SAP Mobile devices", "id": 225}, {"topic": "1.Set up Apple Mobile Devices", "section": "1.1 iOS & iPad OS", "paragraphs": ["Each year, Apple releases major Operating System (OS) updates for iPhone, iPad and other popular devices. In early Sep, 2025, Apple released the official list of supported devices for iOS 26 (iPhone) and iPadOS 26 (iPad). Devices that do not support current OS versions are not compliant. Non-compliant devices will have their access to SAP data restricted.", "More information", "What’s New in iOS 26", "Below is the complete list of supported devices for iOS 26 and iPadOS 26:", "For iPhone:", "And for iPad:", "With this update, iPadOS 26 introduces an all-new design call Liquid Glass, even more customization options, and powerful updates for staying connected by bringing the Phone app to the iPad. Additionally, iPadOS 26 enhances file management with Preview and other improvements to the Files app.", "More information", "What’s New in iPadOS 26", "Not sure which model you have?", "Identify your iPhone model", "Identify your iPad model", "If you have a corporately owned device, but you cannot upgrade to a newer device or you have an approved device in the BYOD program that does not support iPadOS 26, please discuss your options with your manager.", "The device will continue to be compliant until it is unable to receive OS updates later this year.", "1.2 iPhone and iPad - Keep your iOS updated", "To update your device, open Settings on your device and tap General, then Software Update. Follow the on-screen instructions to install the latest update.", "Did you lose your SAP services?", "How to Sync Information to your device after update", "Follow these steps to regain access to SAP services:", "After the OS upgrade, launch the Apple@SAP app.", "Tap and hold on the word “Sync” for 3 to 5 seconds, release and tap OK when the synchronization box prompts.", "Wait 30-40 minutes, then launch the native mail app on the device. This will restore access to your emails.", "Be sure to keep your OS updated to avoid issues in future.", "Once SAP IT certifies the latest iOS/iPadOS version, that version will become the minimum approved OS version after 60 days.", "If you have not updated to at least the minimum version of iOS/iPadOS listed in the Compliance Timer before that version becomes the minimum approved, your Apple mobile device will not be compliant and at risk.", "Non-compliant devices will have access removed which will include, but not limited to, access to SAP Email, SAP contacts, and SAP Calendar on the non-compliant device(s)."], "content": "Each year, Apple releases major Operating System (OS) updates for iPhone, iPad and other popular devices. In early Sep, 2025, Apple released the official list of supported devices for iOS 26 (iPhone) and iPadOS 26 (iPad). Devices that do not support current OS versions are not compliant. Non-compliant devices will have their access to SAP data restricted. More information What’s New in iOS 26 Below is the complete list of supported devices for iOS 26 and iPadOS 26: For iPhone: And for iPad: With this update, iPadOS 26 introduces an all-new design call Liquid Glass, even more customization options, and powerful updates for staying connected by bringing the Phone app to the iPad. Additionally, iPadOS 26 enhances file management with Preview and other improvements to the Files app. More information What’s New in iPadOS 26 Not sure which model you have? Identify your iPhone model Identify your iPad model If you have a corporately owned device, but you cannot upgrade to a newer device or you have an approved device in the BYOD program that does not support iPadOS 26, please discuss your options with your manager. The device will continue to be compliant until it is unable to receive OS updates later this year. 1.2 iPhone and iPad - Keep your iOS updated To update your device, open Settings on your device and tap General, then Software Update. Follow the on-screen instructions to install the latest update. Did you lose your SAP services? How to Sync Information to your device after update Follow these steps to regain access to SAP services: After the OS upgrade, launch the Apple@SAP app. Tap and hold on the word “Sync” for 3 to 5 seconds, release and tap OK when the synchronization box prompts. Wait 30-40 minutes, then launch the native mail app on the device. This will restore access to your emails. Be sure to keep your OS updated to avoid issues in future. Once SAP IT certifies the latest iOS/iPadOS version, that version will become the minimum approved OS version after 60 days. If you have not updated to at least the minimum version of iOS/iPadOS listed in the Compliance Timer before that version becomes the minimum approved, your Apple mobile device will not be compliant and at risk. Non-compliant devices will have access removed which will include, but not limited to, access to SAP Email, SAP contacts, and SAP Calendar on the non-compliant device(s).", "source": "SAP Mobile devices", "id": 226}, {"topic": "1.Set up Apple Mobile Devices", "section": "1.3 Set up iOS Devices (ADE)", "paragraphs": ["ADE (Automated Devices Enrollment) - program from Apple which allows SAP to purchase and assign Apple device directly to SAP, based on the device's serial number. When you first set up an ADE device it automatically knows to start enrolment under SAP's management system. This allows you to simply power on the device, directly out of the box, and sign in. Everything else happens automatically for you for setup, installation, and enrollment.", "Prerequisites", "Before continuing with the process, be sure that you have:", "A stable WiFi connection or cellular data", "Configured Multifacton-factor Authentication", "Your previously enrolled device (if applicable) so that you can use Multifactor Authentication (MFA) to enrol your new device", "In the event you do not have an existing device with MFA configured, you will need a Temporary Access Pass (TAP) to enrol your device. Contact IT Support to get a Temporary Access Pass to be used during the enrolment procedure.", "How to set up your iOS device", "Follow the instructions KB0777915"], "content": "ADE (Automated Devices Enrollment) - program from Apple which allows SAP to purchase and assign Apple device directly to SAP, based on the device's serial number. When you first set up an ADE device it automatically knows to start enrolment under SAP's management system. This allows you to simply power on the device, directly out of the box, and sign in. Everything else happens automatically for you for setup, installation, and enrollment. Prerequisites Before continuing with the process, be sure that you have: A stable WiFi connection or cellular data Configured Multifacton-factor Authentication Your previously enrolled device (if applicable) so that you can use Multifactor Authentication (MFA) to enrol your new device In the event you do not have an existing device with MFA configured, you will need a Temporary Access Pass (TAP) to enrol your device. Contact IT Support to get a Temporary Access Pass to be used during the enrolment procedure. How to set up your iOS device Follow the instructions KB0777915", "source": "SAP Mobile devices", "id": 227}, {"topic": "1.Set up Apple Mobile Devices", "section": "1.4 Setting up iOS devices (non-ADE)", "paragraphs": ["This guide tells users how to set up their Corporate iPhone or iPad and manually enroll it in Jamf for access to SAP email, calendar, and apps.", "IMPORTANT: If you are setting up your privately-owned (BYOD) iPhone or iPad, please do not use this guide, as privately owned devices are managed differently than SAP owned devices. Instead, use the guide for enrolling BYOD devices in JAMF.", "Prerequisites", "Before continuing with the process, be sure that you have:", "An SAP issued iPhone or iPad", "Configured Multifacton-factor Authentication", "Your previously enrolled device (if applicable) so that you can use Multifactor Authentication (MFA) to enroll your new device", "In the event you do not have an existing device with MFA configured, you will need a Temporary Access Pass (TAP) to enroll your device. Contact IT Support to get a Temporary Access Pass to be used during the enrollment procedure", "How to set up your new iPhone or iPad following", "Set Up Your Corporate iPhone or iPad Manually (Non-ADE) - iOS & iPadOS"], "content": "This guide tells users how to set up their Corporate iPhone or iPad and manually enroll it in Jamf for access to SAP email, calendar, and apps. IMPORTANT: If you are setting up your privately-owned (BYOD) iPhone or iPad, please do not use this guide, as privately owned devices are managed differently than SAP owned devices. Instead, use the guide for enrolling BYOD devices in JAMF. Prerequisites Before continuing with the process, be sure that you have: An SAP issued iPhone or iPad Configured Multifacton-factor Authentication Your previously enrolled device (if applicable) so that you can use Multifactor Authentication (MFA) to enroll your new device In the event you do not have an existing device with MFA configured, you will need a Temporary Access Pass (TAP) to enroll your device. Contact IT Support to get a Temporary Access Pass to be used during the enrollment procedure How to set up your new iPhone or iPad following Set Up Your Corporate iPhone or iPad Manually (Non-ADE) - iOS & iPadOS", "source": "SAP Mobile devices", "id": 228}, {"topic": "1.Set up Apple Mobile Devices", "section": "1.5 Set up your personal iPhone or iPad (BYOD) – iOS & iPadOS", "paragraphs": ["Get access to SAP services by using your privately owned mobile device", "Since July 2024, we're excited to offer the convenience of using your personal device at SAP! This option is available at selected locations, allowing you to seamlessly download and use SAP and Office apps on your phone. Experience flexibility and efficiency of working from your own device. Give it a try today.", "BYOD Participation Conditions", "BYOD is allowed in all countries except Israel.", "Read and understand the Terms of Use (TOU) for using your private mobile device for SAP work/business purposes.", "In the AMER region, SAP employees, contractors, and designated third parties are prohibited from using personally owned devices, including those in our Bring Your Own Device (BYOD) Program, when performing tasks related to U.S. federal contracts and subcontracts.", "Global Protect or F5 (for VPN access) apps are not available for use on BYOD devices.", "Prerequisites", "Filled out and submitted the BYOD Consent Form", "An approved personal iPhone or iPad under BYOD", "Configured Multifactor Authentication", "Your previously enrolled device (if applicable) so that you can use Multifactor Authentication (MFA) to enroll your new device", "In the event you do not have an existing device with MFA configured, you will need a Temporary Access Pass (TAP) to enroll your device. Contact IT Support to get a Temporary Access Pass to be used during the enrollment procedure", "The latest approved OS version supported by SAP IT", "A working connection to SAP-Guest Wi-Fi, a personal Wi-Fi network, or your mobile device's data connection (SAP-Corporate Wi-Fi should not be used during the setup and enrollment)", "Apple's Stolen Device Protection is not enabled (can be enabled after the enrollment is successful).", "How to enroll your personal iPhone or iPad in Jamf (BYOD)", "Follow the instructions BYOD enrollment guide SAP iPhone & iPad Setup Guide: Company & Personal Devices", "For more information, you may refer to iOS - iPad & iPhone"], "content": "Get access to SAP services by using your privately owned mobile device Since July 2024, we're excited to offer the convenience of using your personal device at SAP! This option is available at selected locations, allowing you to seamlessly download and use SAP and Office apps on your phone. Experience flexibility and efficiency of working from your own device. Give it a try today. BYOD Participation Conditions BYOD is allowed in all countries except Israel. Read and understand the Terms of Use (TOU) for using your private mobile device for SAP work/business purposes. In the AMER region, SAP employees, contractors, and designated third parties are prohibited from using personally owned devices, including those in our Bring Your Own Device (BYOD) Program, when performing tasks related to U.S. federal contracts and subcontracts. Global Protect or F5 (for VPN access) apps are not available for use on BYOD devices. Prerequisites Filled out and submitted the BYOD Consent Form An approved personal iPhone or iPad under BYOD Configured Multifactor Authentication Your previously enrolled device (if applicable) so that you can use Multifactor Authentication (MFA) to enroll your new device In the event you do not have an existing device with MFA configured, you will need a Temporary Access Pass (TAP) to enroll your device. Contact IT Support to get a Temporary Access Pass to be used during the enrollment procedure The latest approved OS version supported by SAP IT A working connection to SAP-Guest Wi-Fi, a personal Wi-Fi network, or your mobile device's data connection (SAP-Corporate Wi-Fi should not be used during the setup and enrollment) Apple's Stolen Device Protection is not enabled (can be enabled after the enrollment is successful). How to enroll your personal iPhone or iPad in Jamf (BYOD) Follow the instructions BYOD enrollment guide SAP iPhone & iPad Setup Guide: Company & Personal Devices For more information, you may refer to iOS - iPad & iPhone", "source": "SAP Mobile devices", "id": 229}, {"topic": "2.Setup Android Devices", "section": "2.1 Set up Android (Corporate owned device)", "paragraphs": ["Introduction", "After a successful enrollment, your device will have access to basic SAP services and can be managed by the SAP Helpdesk remotely. The enrollment process should take approximately 10-15 minutes. It may vary based on the speed of your internet connection.", "Prepare your device", "Use only a compliant Samsung or Google device which runs on Android 15 or higher", "Install available Security patches - check it every month", "Unpack and charge device", "Own a Google account if you like to install private apps", "Backup any private data from your device if you already used it", "Change Multi Factor Authentication", "In general, you must use a Multi Factor Authentication (MFA) method to access internal services. To enroll and register your Android device MFA is also needed.", "Therefore, be prepared and set up your MFA method before you proceed.", "Open the MFA guide and explore which authentication options are available for you", "Change the MFA method by using this link: https://aka.ms/mfasetup", "Select either your Office phone (Teams) or an alternative phone as the default sign-in method for verification", "(Optional) Select Phone only if you still own your old corporate enrolled device - Your SIM card must be inserted", "Note", "To enroll a company device, you need a second device for verification: Either your laptop or a mobile device", "If you use the SAP Authenticator app, please deactivate the use of this app before your proceed", "Reset your device to Factory Settings *", "* This step is not needed for new devices - proceed with the QR code enrollment step!", "Perform a backup", "Reset the device following the description for your Samsung or Google device on the next pages", "If you follow the instructions and perform a factory reset, all data on your device will be deleted", "To perform a backup of your device you might use the Samsung Smart Switch app or the Google One app. Check our Backup & Restore Guide for Android for more details. After a successful enrollment you can restore the backup to your device", "Samsung Galaxy", "Open your phone's Settings app", "Go to General Management > Reset > Factory data reset", "Tap Reset and choose Delete all", "Google Pixel", "Open your phone's Settings app", "Tap System > Reset options", "Tap Erase all data (factory reset) > Reset phone. If asked, enter your PIN, pattern, or password", "To erase all data from your phone's internal storage, tap Erase everything", "When your phone has finished erasing, pick the option to restart", "How to enroll your Corporate owned Android device", "Follow the instructions Android Enrollment (Corporate owned device)", "More information you can check Android Devices - IT CSD One-Pager"], "content": "Introduction After a successful enrollment, your device will have access to basic SAP services and can be managed by the SAP Helpdesk remotely. The enrollment process should take approximately 10-15 minutes. It may vary based on the speed of your internet connection. Prepare your device Use only a compliant Samsung or Google device which runs on Android 15 or higher Install available Security patches - check it every month Unpack and charge device Own a Google account if you like to install private apps Backup any private data from your device if you already used it Change Multi Factor Authentication In general, you must use a Multi Factor Authentication (MFA) method to access internal services. To enroll and register your Android device MFA is also needed. Therefore, be prepared and set up your MFA method before you proceed. Open the MFA guide and explore which authentication options are available for you Change the MFA method by using this link: https://aka.ms/mfasetup Select either your Office phone (Teams) or an alternative phone as the default sign-in method for verification (Optional) Select Phone only if you still own your old corporate enrolled device - Your SIM card must be inserted Note To enroll a company device, you need a second device for verification: Either your laptop or a mobile device If you use the SAP Authenticator app, please deactivate the use of this app before your proceed Reset your device to Factory Settings * * This step is not needed for new devices - proceed with the QR code enrollment step! Perform a backup Reset the device following the description for your Samsung or Google device on the next pages If you follow the instructions and perform a factory reset, all data on your device will be deleted To perform a backup of your device you might use the Samsung Smart Switch app or the Google One app. Check our Backup & Restore Guide for Android for more details. After a successful enrollment you can restore the backup to your device Samsung Galaxy Open your phone's Settings app Go to General Management > Reset > Factory data reset Tap Reset and choose Delete all Google Pixel Open your phone's Settings app Tap System > Reset options Tap Erase all data (factory reset) > Reset phone. If asked, enter your PIN, pattern, or password To erase all data from your phone's internal storage, tap Erase everything When your phone has finished erasing, pick the option to restart How to enroll your Corporate owned Android device Follow the instructions Android Enrollment (Corporate owned device) More information you can check Android Devices - IT CSD One-Pager", "source": "SAP Mobile devices", "id": 230}, {"topic": "2.Setup Android Devices", "section": "2.2 Android BYOD Enrolment for Privately Owned Devices", "paragraphs": ["Please note that BYOD (Bring Your Own Device) is not approved for every county at SAP.", "Before you proceed make sure your country is in the list of approved countries.", "New countries are being added to list regularly. Check BYOD@SAP site for the latest list of countries where BYOD is allowed.", "* SAP employees, contractors, and designated third parties in the AMER region are prohibited from using personally owned devices, including those in our Bring Your Own Device (BYOD) Program, when performing tasks related to U.S. federal contracts and subcontracts.", "** Android devices are not allowed in China as Google Play Store is not available.", "Prepare your device", "Run minimum Android 15 or higher on your device", "Use an approved device. [Samsung or Google only]", "Connect your device to the Internet", "Own a Google account [Needed for personal apps]", "Set an 8-digit PIN or Password [No direct following numbers, triples or more!]", "Change Multi Factor Authentication (MFA) [Mandatory before enrollment]", "Request the BYOD use", "Open the BYOD Consent form (SharePoint) to start your enrollment request.", "Fill in the details, review the Terms of Use, and submit the Consent Form.", "After submitting the consent form, please follow the step-by-step instructions in the Android BYOD enrollment guide.", "Change Multi Factor Authentication (MFA)", "To be able to enrol & register your personal Android at SAP, you must use the Multi Factor Authentication. You need to prepare the MFA sign-in method before starting the enrolment:", "Open the MFA guide and explore which authentication options are available for you", "Change the MFA method by using this link: https://aka.ms/mfasetup", "We recommend using one of these strong authentication methods as the default MFA method:", "Windows Hello for Business", "Passwordless sign-in (previously phone sign-in)", "FIDO2 security key", "We recommend using one of these options as the default MFA method:", "Phone call", "Phone Text", "Office phone call", "Therefore, you need to:", "Add your preferred option (if not already done) and", "Change the default sign-in method by choosing your preferred option", "How to enrol your private owned Android device following guidance", "Android BYOD Enrollment for Privately Owned Devices"], "content": "Please note that BYOD (Bring Your Own Device) is not approved for every county at SAP. Before you proceed make sure your country is in the list of approved countries. New countries are being added to list regularly. Check BYOD@SAP site for the latest list of countries where BYOD is allowed. * SAP employees, contractors, and designated third parties in the AMER region are prohibited from using personally owned devices, including those in our Bring Your Own Device (BYOD) Program, when performing tasks related to U.S. federal contracts and subcontracts. ** Android devices are not allowed in China as Google Play Store is not available. Prepare your device Run minimum Android 15 or higher on your device Use an approved device. [Samsung or Google only] Connect your device to the Internet Own a Google account [Needed for personal apps] Set an 8-digit PIN or Password [No direct following numbers, triples or more!] Change Multi Factor Authentication (MFA) [Mandatory before enrollment] Request the BYOD use Open the BYOD Consent form (SharePoint) to start your enrollment request. Fill in the details, review the Terms of Use, and submit the Consent Form. After submitting the consent form, please follow the step-by-step instructions in the Android BYOD enrollment guide. Change Multi Factor Authentication (MFA) To be able to enrol & register your personal Android at SAP, you must use the Multi Factor Authentication. You need to prepare the MFA sign-in method before starting the enrolment: Open the MFA guide and explore which authentication options are available for you Change the MFA method by using this link: https://aka.ms/mfasetup We recommend using one of these strong authentication methods as the default MFA method: Windows Hello for Business Passwordless sign-in (previously phone sign-in) FIDO2 security key We recommend using one of these options as the default MFA method: Phone call Phone Text Office phone call Therefore, you need to: Add your preferred option (if not already done) and Change the default sign-in method by choosing your preferred option How to enrol your private owned Android device following guidance Android BYOD Enrollment for Privately Owned Devices", "source": "SAP Mobile devices", "id": 231}, {"topic": "2.Setup Android Devices", "section": "2.3 How can I check whether my device is properly enrolled?", "paragraphs": ["If you followed one of the enrollment guides, you would find the app \"Company Portal\" within the list of the work profile apps.", "Swipe up to see the installed apps and select the work profile", "Open the “Company Portal \" app on your Android device", "Check if you find your device in the list of devices", "The device highlighted with a bold font-style is your current device", "If you don't see any device entry, visit the IT Support portal under https://itsupport.sap.com to get in touch with a support colleague", "If you see one or more device entries, please open the entire(s) and check the status of the enrolled device(s)", "If you see an exclamation mark within a red circle! - check the entry and follow the instructions."], "content": "If you followed one of the enrollment guides, you would find the app \"Company Portal\" within the list of the work profile apps. Swipe up to see the installed apps and select the work profile Open the “Company Portal \" app on your Android device Check if you find your device in the list of devices The device highlighted with a bold font-style is your current device If you don't see any device entry, visit the IT Support portal under https://itsupport.sap.com to get in touch with a support colleague If you see one or more device entries, please open the entire(s) and check the status of the enrolled device(s) If you see an exclamation mark within a red circle! - check the entry and follow the instructions.", "source": "SAP Mobile devices", "id": 232}, {"topic": "2.Setup Android Devices", "section": "2.4 Removing MDM from Privately Owned Android Mobile Devices", "paragraphs": ["Why remove MDM?", "If you no longer want access to your SAP email, apps, and data, you may want to remove device management from your private Android device. Removing MDM automatically removes all associated SAP installed apps and configurations from your Android device.", "All private apps and data will remain. They won't be touched or affected by this removal process.", "How to remove the work profile from Microsoft Intune?", "Open the Intune Company Portal App", "Tap on the Menu (3 lines)", "Tap on \"Remove Company Portal\"", "Accept the removal by tapping on \"OK\"", "Work Profile will be removed.", "All corporate data and apps will be removed. Personal data and apps will remain untouched.", "More information you can check Removing MDM from Privately Owned Android Mobile Devices"], "content": "Why remove MDM? If you no longer want access to your SAP email, apps, and data, you may want to remove device management from your private Android device. Removing MDM automatically removes all associated SAP installed apps and configurations from your Android device. All private apps and data will remain. They won't be touched or affected by this removal process. How to remove the work profile from Microsoft Intune? Open the Intune Company Portal App Tap on the Menu (3 lines) Tap on \"Remove Company Portal\" Accept the removal by tapping on \"OK\" Work Profile will be removed. All corporate data and apps will be removed. Personal data and apps will remain untouched. More information you can check Removing MDM from Privately Owned Android Mobile Devices", "source": "SAP Mobile devices", "id": 233}, {"topic": "3. Install SAP Apps", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Self Service is SAP IT's internal App Store. It is installed by default on enrolled corporate devices.", "Self Service has several categories: Compliance, Be Productive, Get Connected, Manager, Me@SAP, Microsoft, Sales, SAP Products, 'Try, Play, learn', and 'Betas and Demos', in which you can quickly find useful apps according to their functions.", "In Featured, you will find apps that we recommend for you.", "You can also easily search for apps you need. Simply tap the Install button next to the app to install it.", "On the iPhone, Menu options are found at the bottom of the screen. Home, Folders/Categories, Search, and Notifications. For the iPad (not shown), the Menu options are found at top left of screen.", "How do I delete an app?", "Delete apps just like you'd normally do on iPhones/iPad:", "Lightly touch and hold the app.", "Tap 'Remove App'.", "Tap 'Delete App'.", "Tap Delete.", "More information: Self Service - iOS & iPadOS"], "content": "Self Service is SAP IT's internal App Store. It is installed by default on enrolled corporate devices. Self Service has several categories: Compliance, Be Productive, Get Connected, Manager, Me@SAP, Microsoft, Sales, SAP Products, 'Try, Play, learn', and 'Betas and Demos', in which you can quickly find useful apps according to their functions. In Featured, you will find apps that we recommend for you. You can also easily search for apps you need. Simply tap the Install button next to the app to install it. On the iPhone, Menu options are found at the bottom of the screen. Home, Folders/Categories, Search, and Notifications. For the iPad (not shown), the Menu options are found at top left of screen. How do I delete an app? Delete apps just like you'd normally do on iPhones/iPad: Lightly touch and hold the app. Tap 'Remove App'. Tap 'Delete App'. Tap Delete. More information: Self Service - iOS & iPadOS", "source": "SAP Mobile devices", "id": 234}, {"topic": "4. Backup methods for iPhone/iPad", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["A backup allows you to copy and save the information from your iPhone/ iPad. If you replace your device, you can use a backup to transfer your information to a new device."], "content": "A backup allows you to copy and save the information from your iPhone/ iPad. If you replace your device, you can use a backup to transfer your information to a new device.", "source": "SAP Mobile devices", "id": 235}, {"topic": "4. Backup methods for iPhone/iPad", "section": "4.1 Decide which method is best for you", "paragraphs": ["In case you ever need an alternative backup, you can back up your device using iCloud and also using your computer. Learn how to back up your device or restore your device from a backup."], "content": "In case you ever need an alternative backup, you can back up your device using iCloud and also using your computer. Learn how to back up your device or restore your device from a backup.", "source": "SAP Mobile devices", "id": 236}, {"topic": "4. Backup methods for iPhone/iPad", "section": "4.2 iCloud backups", "paragraphs": ["With a Wi-Fi network connection, you can back up your device using iCloud. You don't need to plug your device into a computer to back up with iCloud.", "iCloud backups include all the information and settings stored on your device that don't already sync to iCloud. iCloud backups don't include:", "Data that you already store and sync in iCloud, like Contacts, Calendars, and Notes", "Photos, if you turn on iCloud Photos", "iMessages, text (SMS) and multimedia (MMS) messages, if you sync messages with iCloud", "Data stored in other cloud services, like Gmail and Exchange mail", "Apple Mail data", "Apple Pay information and settings", "Face ID or Touch ID settings", "iCloud Music Library and App Store content", "Offline maps", "Learn more about what iCloud backs up"], "content": "With a Wi-Fi network connection, you can back up your device using iCloud. You don't need to plug your device into a computer to back up with iCloud. iCloud backups include all the information and settings stored on your device that don't already sync to iCloud. iCloud backups don't include: Data that you already store and sync in iCloud, like Contacts, Calendars, and Notes Photos, if you turn on iCloud Photos iMessages, text (SMS) and multimedia (MMS) messages, if you sync messages with iCloud Data stored in other cloud services, like Gmail and Exchange mail Apple Mail data Apple Pay information and settings Face ID or Touch ID settings iCloud Music Library and App Store content Offline maps Learn more about what iCloud backs up", "source": "SAP Mobile devices", "id": 237}, {"topic": "4. Backup methods for iPhone/iPad", "section": "4.3 Backups from your computer", "paragraphs": ["A computer backup of your device, which is not the same as a sync, includes almost all of your device's data and settings. A backup from a computer doesn't include:", "Content from the iTunes and App Stores, or PDFs downloaded directly to Apple Books", "Content synced from your Mac or PC, like imported MP3s or CDs, videos, books, and photos", "Data already synced and stored in iCloud, like iCloud Photos, iMessages, text (SMS) and multimedia (MMS) messages", "Face ID or Touch ID settings", "Apple Pay information and settings", "Apple Mail data", "Activity, Health, and Keychain data (to back up this content, you'll need to create an encrypted backup)", "Offline maps", "Learn how to backup, find backups, and delete backups that you no longer need on your Mac or PC", "5. Restore your iPhone / iPad from a backup"], "content": "A computer backup of your device, which is not the same as a sync, includes almost all of your device's data and settings. A backup from a computer doesn't include: Content from the iTunes and App Stores, or PDFs downloaded directly to Apple Books Content synced from your Mac or PC, like imported MP3s or CDs, videos, books, and photos Data already synced and stored in iCloud, like iCloud Photos, iMessages, text (SMS) and multimedia (MMS) messages Face ID or Touch ID settings Apple Pay information and settings Apple Mail data Activity, Health, and Keychain data (to back up this content, you'll need to create an encrypted backup) Offline maps Learn how to backup, find backups, and delete backups that you no longer need on your Mac or PC 5. Restore your iPhone / iPad from a backup", "source": "SAP Mobile devices", "id": 238}, {"topic": "4. Backup methods for iPhone/iPad", "section": "5.1 Restore your device from an iCloud backup", "paragraphs": ["Turn on your device. You should see a Hello Screen. If you already set up your device, you need to erase all of its content before you can use these steps to restore from your backup.", "Follow the onscreen setup steps until you reach the Transfer Your Apps & Data screen, then tap From iCloud Backup.", "Sign in to iCloud with your Apple ID.", "Choose a backup. Look at the date and size of each and pick the most relevant. After you choose a backup, the transfer starts. If a message says that a newer version of software is required, follow the onscreen steps to update. Learn what to do if you don't see onscreen steps to help you update your device.", "When asked, sign in with your Apple ID to restore your apps and purchases. If you've purchased iTunes or App Store content using multiple Apple IDs, you'll be asked to sign in to each. If you can't remember your password, you can tap Skip this Step and sign in later. You won't be able to use the apps until you sign in with your Apple ID.", "Stay connected to Wi-Fi and wait for a progress bar to appear and complete. Depending on the size of the backup and the network speed, the progress bar might need a few minutes to an hour to complete. If you disconnect from Wi-Fi too soon, the progress will pause until you reconnect.", "Finish setting up your device. Content like your apps, photos, music, and other information will continue to restore in the background for the next several hours or days, depending on the amount of information on your device. Try to connect often to Wi-Fi and power to let the process complete."], "content": "Turn on your device. You should see a Hello Screen. If you already set up your device, you need to erase all of its content before you can use these steps to restore from your backup. Follow the onscreen setup steps until you reach the Transfer Your Apps & Data screen, then tap From iCloud Backup. Sign in to iCloud with your Apple ID. Choose a backup. Look at the date and size of each and pick the most relevant. After you choose a backup, the transfer starts. If a message says that a newer version of software is required, follow the onscreen steps to update. Learn what to do if you don't see onscreen steps to help you update your device. When asked, sign in with your Apple ID to restore your apps and purchases. If you've purchased iTunes or App Store content using multiple Apple IDs, you'll be asked to sign in to each. If you can't remember your password, you can tap Skip this Step and sign in later. You won't be able to use the apps until you sign in with your Apple ID. Stay connected to Wi-Fi and wait for a progress bar to appear and complete. Depending on the size of the backup and the network speed, the progress bar might need a few minutes to an hour to complete. If you disconnect from Wi-Fi too soon, the progress will pause until you reconnect. Finish setting up your device. Content like your apps, photos, music, and other information will continue to restore in the background for the next several hours or days, depending on the amount of information on your device. Try to connect often to Wi-Fi and power to let the process complete.", "source": "SAP Mobile devices", "id": 239}, {"topic": "4. Backup methods for iPhone/iPad", "section": "5.2 Restore your device from a backup on your computer", "paragraphs": ["Open the Finder or the Apple Devices app on Windows. Open iTunes on Windows without the Apple Devices app or macOS Mojave or earlier. Find out which macOS your Mac is using.", "Connect your device to your computer with a USB cable. If a message asks for your device passcode or to Trust This Computer, follow the onscreen steps. Get help if you forgot your passcode.", "Select your iPhone / iPad when it appears in the Finder window, the Apple Devices app sidebar, or the iTunes window. Learn what to do if your device doesn't appear.", "Select Restore Backup. Learn what to do if a message says that your device's software is too old.", "Look at the date of each backup and pick the most relevant.", "Click Restore and wait for the restore to finish. If asked, enter the password for your encrypted backup.", "Keep your device connected after it restarts and wait for it to sync with your computer. You can disconnect after the sync finishes.", "6. Mobile Single Sign-On (SSO)", "Overview", "When you receive your iPhone or iPad from SAP IT and complete enrollment and setup your Single Sign-On Certificate (SSO) is automatically installed for you. The SSO certificate is stored in your iPhone and iPad securely (via Keychain). Your SSO certificate is valid for 3 months, after which the app will automatically notify you to renew it.", "Verifying your SSO is installed and valid", "To check your SSO status and installation, open the Apple@SAP app. Your certificate status is displayed.", "How to update my certificate", "Open the Apple@SAP app on your device.", "Tap the Renew button in the upper right corner of the screen.", "After the warning is displayed, accept, and select Renew. Your certificate will automatically renew.", "7. Wi-Fi iOS", "Wi-Fi", "View your WiFi status at the top of your screen."], "content": "Open the Finder or the Apple Devices app on Windows. Open iTunes on Windows without the Apple Devices app or macOS Mojave or earlier. Find out which macOS your Mac is using. Connect your device to your computer with a USB cable. If a message asks for your device passcode or to Trust This Computer, follow the onscreen steps. Get help if you forgot your passcode. Select your iPhone / iPad when it appears in the Finder window, the Apple Devices app sidebar, or the iTunes window. Learn what to do if your device doesn't appear. Select Restore Backup. Learn what to do if a message says that your device's software is too old. Look at the date of each backup and pick the most relevant. Click Restore and wait for the restore to finish. If asked, enter the password for your encrypted backup. Keep your device connected after it restarts and wait for it to sync with your computer. You can disconnect after the sync finishes. 6. Mobile Single Sign-On (SSO) Overview When you receive your iPhone or iPad from SAP IT and complete enrollment and setup your Single Sign-On Certificate (SSO) is automatically installed for you. The SSO certificate is stored in your iPhone and iPad securely (via Keychain). Your SSO certificate is valid for 3 months, after which the app will automatically notify you to renew it. Verifying your SSO is installed and valid To check your SSO status and installation, open the Apple@SAP app. Your certificate status is displayed. How to update my certificate Open the Apple@SAP app on your device. Tap the Renew button in the upper right corner of the screen. After the warning is displayed, accept, and select Renew. Your certificate will automatically renew. 7. Wi-Fi iOS Wi-Fi View your WiFi status at the top of your screen.", "source": "SAP Mobile devices", "id": 240}, {"topic": "4. Backup methods for iPhone/iPad", "section": "7.1 Connect to SAP Wifi when in the Office", "paragraphs": ["When you are in an SAP Office, please ensure you have Wifi enabled and are connected to the SAP Corporate Wifi", "From the enrollment / setup of your Corporate Device the necessary certification and configuration will be in place to enable you to seamlessly connect to \"SAP\" Wifi", "To Connect please follow the instructions", "Apple: Settings - Wifi - Select \"SAP\" from the list of available network", "Android: Settings - Wi-Fi or Wireless & Networks - Turn on Wi-Fi - Select \"SAP\" from the list of available networks"], "content": "When you are in an SAP Office, please ensure you have Wifi enabled and are connected to the SAP Corporate Wifi From the enrollment / setup of your Corporate Device the necessary certification and configuration will be in place to enable you to seamlessly connect to \"SAP\" Wifi To Connect please follow the instructions Apple: Settings - Wifi - Select \"SAP\" from the list of available network Android: Settings - Wi-Fi or Wireless & Networks - Turn on Wi-Fi - Select \"SAP\" from the list of available networks", "source": "SAP Mobile devices", "id": 241}, {"topic": "8. iOS/iPadOS Device - Azure Registration", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Overview", "The policy registers your device with SAP's Azure Active Directory and links it with our mobile device management system (Jamf). This is required as part of our ongoing compliance and device health efforts. If your iPhone or iPad device is deemed compliant (i.e. latest OS version is installed and up to date) a compliance flag is sent from Jamf to Azure Active Directory. This ensures you'll keep your seamless access to your apps and Microsoft 365 services.", "How do I use the policy and register my iPhone & iPad devices?", "Registering your devices directly from the MS Authenticator app does not complete the process. Your device needs to be registered thru the Self Service app to send the correct Compliance data to Azure AD. Launch the Self Service app on your device. You'll see a Compliance category if you click the three vertical dots icon in the upper left part of the screen. Inside this category, you'll see an item titled Register with Microsoft. Simply click on the Register button to start the registration process and follow the steps below:", "Step 1: Self services", "Step 2: Scroll down to Compliance", "After tapping the item in Self Service it will automatically open the Microsoft Authenticator app that is already preinstalled on your managed iPhone & iPad. Hit the Register button to continue.", "If you have not configured Authenticator, you will be asked to sign in with your complete xxx.xxx@sap.com email.", "The next few screens will move by quickly and use your existing SSO certificate to authenticate.", "Step 1", "Step 2", "Next, you will see a screen that says Help us keep your device secure. At this point, you'll actually be registering your device with SAP's Azure Active Directory. Click Register.", "Afterward, you'll be redirected back to the Self Service app and registration is complete!", "Can I check that my device is properly registered?", "You can verify that the registration was completed by checking your device status: • Launch the MS Authenticator app • Tap on the hamburger icon, in the top left corner, next to \"Authenticator\" • Tap on Settings > Device Registration", "Please follow KB0779309 iOS/iPadOS Device Compliance - Azure Registration"], "content": "Overview The policy registers your device with SAP's Azure Active Directory and links it with our mobile device management system (Jamf). This is required as part of our ongoing compliance and device health efforts. If your iPhone or iPad device is deemed compliant (i.e. latest OS version is installed and up to date) a compliance flag is sent from Jamf to Azure Active Directory. This ensures you'll keep your seamless access to your apps and Microsoft 365 services. How do I use the policy and register my iPhone & iPad devices? Registering your devices directly from the MS Authenticator app does not complete the process. Your device needs to be registered thru the Self Service app to send the correct Compliance data to Azure AD. Launch the Self Service app on your device. You'll see a Compliance category if you click the three vertical dots icon in the upper left part of the screen. Inside this category, you'll see an item titled Register with Microsoft. Simply click on the Register button to start the registration process and follow the steps below: Step 1: Self services Step 2: Scroll down to Compliance After tapping the item in Self Service it will automatically open the Microsoft Authenticator app that is already preinstalled on your managed iPhone & iPad. Hit the Register button to continue. If you have not configured Authenticator, you will be asked to sign in with your complete xxx.xxx@sap.com email. The next few screens will move by quickly and use your existing SSO certificate to authenticate. Step 1 Step 2 Next, you will see a screen that says Help us keep your device secure. At this point, you'll actually be registering your device with SAP's Azure Active Directory. Click Register. Afterward, you'll be redirected back to the Self Service app and registration is complete! Can I check that my device is properly registered? You can verify that the registration was completed by checking your device status: • Launch the MS Authenticator app • Tap on the hamburger icon, in the top left corner, next to \"Authenticator\" • Tap on Settings > Device Registration Please follow KB0779309 iOS/iPadOS Device Compliance - Azure Registration", "source": "SAP Mobile devices", "id": 242}, {"topic": "9. What is a compliant device?", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["All devices used at SAP must meet the SAP IT Security Policies and Standards for requirements, including enrollment in SAP IT MDM.", "For iPhone and iPad devices, this means that the device is:", "1. Able to run the latest version of iOS or iPadOS (as released by Apple)", "2. The iPhone or iPad is updated to the latest version of iOS or iPadOS", "3. It is registered in Azure AD for Conditional Access", "4. Have other mandatory apps and management settings enforced (per SAP IT Security Policies and Standards)", "Devices which are unable to run the required iOS or iPadOS version must be replaced.", "Security updates and patches for Mobile Devices must be regularly installed as mandated by the SAP Vulnerability Advisory Services (VAS) timelines.", "In the event that a major OS version is released and known security vulnerabilities were not patched to the previous OS version, the Mobile Devices must be updated to the newest version.", "All OS versions in use must be known to be secure and supported by SAP IT. Mobile Device models that do not support the current OS version must not be used."], "content": "All devices used at SAP must meet the SAP IT Security Policies and Standards for requirements, including enrollment in SAP IT MDM. For iPhone and iPad devices, this means that the device is: 1. Able to run the latest version of iOS or iPadOS (as released by Apple) 2. The iPhone or iPad is updated to the latest version of iOS or iPadOS 3. It is registered in Azure AD for Conditional Access 4. Have other mandatory apps and management settings enforced (per SAP IT Security Policies and Standards) Devices which are unable to run the required iOS or iPadOS version must be replaced. Security updates and patches for Mobile Devices must be regularly installed as mandated by the SAP Vulnerability Advisory Services (VAS) timelines. In the event that a major OS version is released and known security vulnerabilities were not patched to the previous OS version, the Mobile Devices must be updated to the newest version. All OS versions in use must be known to be secure and supported by SAP IT. Mobile Device models that do not support the current OS version must not be used.", "source": "SAP Mobile devices", "id": 243}, {"topic": "9. What is a compliant device?", "section": "9.1 How can I see if my iPhone or iPad is compliant?", "paragraphs": ["SAP IT has made it very simple to check your device's compliance! Simply open the Apple@SAP app on your device, and you can see your compliance.", "If you see a message Unsupported iOS Version / Non-Compliant, it means your iPhone or iPad needs to be updated.", "Please read iPhone and iPad - Keep your iOS updated", "CSD Teams can check Global Employees’ Mobile Microsoft registers from Microsoft Azure website", "Open Microsoft Azure page https://portal.azure.com/", "Put user’s SAP mail address", "Select Devices and check Mobile register status", "If iOS device compliant status is Yes with a green tick, which means Microsoft 365 Apps access is fine on that device. If the status is red exclamation mark, which means iOS device registration failed. Check the Mobile devices compliance following compliance check using Apple@SAP. After the iOS device compliance issue is fixed, register the device from Self Service again."], "content": "SAP IT has made it very simple to check your device's compliance! Simply open the Apple@SAP app on your device, and you can see your compliance. If you see a message Unsupported iOS Version / Non-Compliant, it means your iPhone or iPad needs to be updated. Please read iPhone and iPad - Keep your iOS updated CSD Teams can check Global Employees’ Mobile Microsoft registers from Microsoft Azure website Open Microsoft Azure page https://portal.azure.com/ Put user’s SAP mail address Select Devices and check Mobile register status If iOS device compliant status is Yes with a green tick, which means Microsoft 365 Apps access is fine on that device. If the status is red exclamation mark, which means iOS device registration failed. Check the Mobile devices compliance following compliance check using Apple@SAP. After the iOS device compliance issue is fixed, register the device from Self Service again.", "source": "SAP Mobile devices", "id": 244}, {"topic": "9. What is a compliant device?", "section": "9.2 How to delete a Mobile device from Azure Active Directory admin center", "paragraphs": ["In case we need to delete a device from Azure Portal must go to Manage Azure Active Directory find the user by the sap email address, go to devices and click on the relevant device.", "Then, copy the Device ID or the Object ID, and use it to purge it from https://intunetoolbox.cfapps.eu10.hana.ondemand.com/AADdevice"], "content": "In case we need to delete a device from Azure Portal must go to Manage Azure Active Directory find the user by the sap email address, go to devices and click on the relevant device. Then, copy the Device ID or the Object ID, and use it to purge it from https://intunetoolbox.cfapps.eu10.hana.ondemand.com/AADdevice", "source": "SAP Mobile devices", "id": 245}, {"topic": "9. What is a compliant device?", "section": "9.3 Android Device Security Compliance", "paragraphs": ["The security of Android devices is a combination of OS version and Security Patch level. Security updates are released by Google monthly, device manufactures, and carriers make these updates available to their devices. Two latest major OS releases are supported and security update (patch) is not allowed to be older than 180 days.", "The security is a combination of OS version and Security Patch level", "Security updates are released by Google monthly. Device manufactures, and carriers make these updates available", "Introduce compliance rules on the installed OS version AND used security patch version", "Use only a compliant device (Google or Samsung)", "Details", "Two latest major OS releases are supported and security update (patch) is not allowed to be older than 180 days.", "Currently, devices with patches more than 6 months old are set as non-compliant and access to SAP resources (email, O365, etc..) blocked.", "Current", "Android versions 15 and 16 are now compliant and must enroll to MS Intune.", "Users of devices with patches older than 6 months will get a warning email and will be eventually set as non-compliant."], "content": "The security of Android devices is a combination of OS version and Security Patch level. Security updates are released by Google monthly, device manufactures, and carriers make these updates available to their devices. Two latest major OS releases are supported and security update (patch) is not allowed to be older than 180 days. The security is a combination of OS version and Security Patch level Security updates are released by Google monthly. Device manufactures, and carriers make these updates available Introduce compliance rules on the installed OS version AND used security patch version Use only a compliant device (Google or Samsung) Details Two latest major OS releases are supported and security update (patch) is not allowed to be older than 180 days. Currently, devices with patches more than 6 months old are set as non-compliant and access to SAP resources (email, O365, etc..) blocked. Current Android versions 15 and 16 are now compliant and must enroll to MS Intune. Users of devices with patches older than 6 months will get a warning email and will be eventually set as non-compliant.", "source": "SAP Mobile devices", "id": 246}, {"topic": "9. What is a compliant device?", "section": "9.4 What it means to enroll your device at SAP", "paragraphs": ["Overview", "Mobile Device Management (MDM for short) is a means of distributing data and settings to iPhone, iPad and Mac devices. Apple has allowed corporations to use Mobile device management (MDM) as a type of security software used by an IT department to monitor, manage and secure employees' mobile devices that are deployed across multiple mobile service providers and across multiple mobile operating systems being used in the organization. If MDM is removed from Mobile devices, Mails will be removed from the Mobile phone as well.", "From the home screen on your iPhone or iPad:", "Tap Settings", "Select General", "Scroll down and select Profiles & Device Management", "Click on Config Payload", "Select Remove Management", "Enter your device passcode (the code that you previously set to unlock the device) and press Done.", "Select Remove from the pop-up to complete the removal.", "9.4.1 Removing MDM – iOS", "In some cases, such as returning a device to SAP IT or troubleshooting, you may want to remove device management from your iPhone or iPad. Removing MDM also automatically removes all associated installed apps and configurations from your iPhone or iPad.", "How do I remove MDM management from my iPhone or iPad?", "From the home screen on your iPhone or iPad:", "Tap Settings", "Select General", "Scroll down and select VPN & Device Management", "Select MDM Profile", "Scroll down and select Remove Management", "Enter your device passcode (the code that you previously set to unlock the device) and press Done", "Select Remove from the pop-up to complete the removal", "Important: SAP Corporate email, calendar, task list, and SAP apps will be temporarily removed until the device is re-enrolled.", "The following WILL NOT be impacted:", "Private e-mail accounts", "Private calendars not associated with SAP calendar", "Local Pictures", "Safari Bookmarks", "Private Apps", "Wi-Fi Settings", "Microsoft Authenticator", "9.4.2 How to remove MDM from Privately Owned Android Mobile Devices", "How to remove the work profile from Microsoft Intune", "Step-by-step", "Open the Intune Company Portal App", "Tap on the Menu (3 lines)", "Tap on \"Remove Company Portal\"", "Accept the removal by tapping on \"OK\"", "Work Profile will be removed. All corporate data and apps will be removed. Personal data and apps will remain untouched.", "More information you can check Mobile Info Session BYOD @SAP."], "content": "Overview Mobile Device Management (MDM for short) is a means of distributing data and settings to iPhone, iPad and Mac devices. Apple has allowed corporations to use Mobile device management (MDM) as a type of security software used by an IT department to monitor, manage and secure employees' mobile devices that are deployed across multiple mobile service providers and across multiple mobile operating systems being used in the organization. If MDM is removed from Mobile devices, Mails will be removed from the Mobile phone as well. From the home screen on your iPhone or iPad: Tap Settings Select General Scroll down and select Profiles & Device Management Click on Config Payload Select Remove Management Enter your device passcode (the code that you previously set to unlock the device) and press Done. Select Remove from the pop-up to complete the removal. 9.4.1 Removing MDM – iOS In some cases, such as returning a device to SAP IT or troubleshooting, you may want to remove device management from your iPhone or iPad. Removing MDM also automatically removes all associated installed apps and configurations from your iPhone or iPad. How do I remove MDM management from my iPhone or iPad? From the home screen on your iPhone or iPad: Tap Settings Select General Scroll down and select VPN & Device Management Select MDM Profile Scroll down and select Remove Management Enter your device passcode (the code that you previously set to unlock the device) and press Done Select Remove from the pop-up to complete the removal Important: SAP Corporate email, calendar, task list, and SAP apps will be temporarily removed until the device is re-enrolled. The following WILL NOT be impacted: Private e-mail accounts Private calendars not associated with SAP calendar Local Pictures Safari Bookmarks Private Apps Wi-Fi Settings Microsoft Authenticator 9.4.2 How to remove MDM from Privately Owned Android Mobile Devices How to remove the work profile from Microsoft Intune Step-by-step Open the Intune Company Portal App Tap on the Menu (3 lines) Tap on \"Remove Company Portal\" Accept the removal by tapping on \"OK\" Work Profile will be removed. All corporate data and apps will be removed. Personal data and apps will remain untouched. More information you can check Mobile Info Session BYOD @SAP.", "source": "SAP Mobile devices", "id": 247}, {"topic": "Overview", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Users are unable to sign in to their device as they have forgotten their sign in PIN/passcode", "IMPORTANT: Before performing the steps listed you will need to verify that the user has the device in their possession. We should not be clearing passcodes without verifying first to ensure SAP data remains secure.", "Verification methods not allowed: SMS, Call back, Soft token", "-Head to the JAMF Mobile Portal at this link: Advanced Mobile Device Search** (jamfcloud.com) If you do not have admin access you may need to request it, reach out to someone who does or open a support ticket to further assist you.", "-Search for the device by Serial Number in the box shown below. If you do not know the serial number, you can find it by looking up the equipment number in ISP. The serial number is also listed there.", "-In the event that these steps do not resolve the user's issue, they will need to reach out to Apple Support for assistance. Please arrange for the user to receive a temporary replacement device in the meantime.", "-Once the iPhone is discovered and shown in the list below click on it to open its JAMF Profile.", "-Click on the Management Tab. There are two buttons you will need to push as shown below: Clear Passcode and Send Blank Push. After this is done, the user will be able to enter their device and set a new passcode.", "You can check KB User Has Forgotten Their Sign-In PIN on iOS Device"], "content": "Users are unable to sign in to their device as they have forgotten their sign in PIN/passcode IMPORTANT: Before performing the steps listed you will need to verify that the user has the device in their possession. We should not be clearing passcodes without verifying first to ensure SAP data remains secure. Verification methods not allowed: SMS, Call back, Soft token -Head to the JAMF Mobile Portal at this link: Advanced Mobile Device Search** (jamfcloud.com) If you do not have admin access you may need to request it, reach out to someone who does or open a support ticket to further assist you. -Search for the device by Serial Number in the box shown below. If you do not know the serial number, you can find it by looking up the equipment number in ISP. The serial number is also listed there. -In the event that these steps do not resolve the user's issue, they will need to reach out to Apple Support for assistance. Please arrange for the user to receive a temporary replacement device in the meantime. -Once the iPhone is discovered and shown in the list below click on it to open its JAMF Profile. -Click on the Management Tab. There are two buttons you will need to push as shown below: Clear Passcode and Send Blank Push. After this is done, the user will be able to enter their device and set a new passcode. You can check KB User Has Forgotten Their Sign-In PIN on iOS Device", "source": "SAP Mobile devices", "id": 248}, {"topic": "11. Apple ID managed", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Overview", "The Apple ID you currently use on your Apple device is yours and it is a private Apple ID. It is not owned by SAP even if you connected it to SAP email address. This private Apple ID enables the installation of App Store apps and the use of Apple services like Apple Pay and FaceTime e.g. for private purposes only. You will need to change your Apple ID to a non-SAP address, otherwise you will lose the functions offered by the Apple ID on your device.", "Apple is introducing a new feature for enterprise customers, called Managed Apple ID. It will help to enable a further separation of private and business data and their use on Apple devices at SAP.", "Managed Apple IDs use SAP email addresses and will help SAP prepare for future projects such as Bring Your Own Device, Passkey, and Mac Single Sign On extension. To prepare for these future projects, SAP needs to claim the sap.com domain for corporate use and create Managed Apple IDs using SAP email addresses only. Please help by changing the email address of your private Apple ID.", "When Apple devices were introduced at SAP in 2012, they were not enterprise ready when we adopted them. However they are ready now, and SAP needs to claim ownership of company email addresses for Managed Apple IDs.", "In early December 2023, the process to enable Managed Apple IDs started with Apple, email address conflicts will be identified, and those users who are using an SAP email address for their private Apple ID will be notified.", "Any change to these private Apple IDs must be completed by February 5th of 2024.", "After this date, your Apple ID can no longer be accessed using your SAP e-mail address but only by a temporary e-mail address. The procedure for an update remains the same, including the password. You can find more information about this change to a temporary e-mail address on our Work Zone page: Managed Apple ID (int.sap).", "However, Apple users can still change the email address associated with their Apple ID at any time.", "What is an Apple ID?", "Typically, a user owns an Apple ID to manage personal data, even on a corporate device. It is therefore often called personal Apple ID.", "An Apple ID is not required on the device. It can be used with SAP apps and the administrative settings only - if enrolled with JAMF.", "An Apple ID is an account that gives access to Apple services like the App Store, iCloud, iMessage, FaceTime, and Apple Music. The email address associated with this account is called Apple ID.", "Today, all Apple IDs in use (personal or business) at SAP are Personal Apple IDs. SAP will be configuring Managed Apple IDs for all “@sap.com” email addresses for future projects.", "What is a Managed Apple ID?", "A Managed Apple ID is owned and managed by your organization — including password resets and role-based administration.", "It also provides access to iCloud for collaboration with iWork and backup on iPhone and iPad devices.", "To log into those devices, the Managed Apple ID and a password with two-factor authentication (Microsoft Azure) are needed.", "Step-by-step instructions", "Affected users will receive an email by Apple Inc. - \"Update Apple ID” - early December 2023.", "If you are not using your SAP email address as your Apple ID, no action is required.", "If you are using an SAP email address as your Apple ID, please follow these steps:", "Sign out of the Apple ID on all connected devices.", "Go to https://appleid.apple.com/ and login with your SAP email address.", "Update your Apple ID by replacing the SAP email address with your private, non-SAP email address.", "Confirm the “new” email address with a verification code that Apple sends to your non-SAP email address.", "Logout from the Apple website to complete the change. Your Apple ID should now be associated with your private, non-SAP email address.", "Sign back in to the Apple ID on all connected devices.", "More information you can check iOS/MacOS - Why we need managed Apple IDs"], "content": "Overview The Apple ID you currently use on your Apple device is yours and it is a private Apple ID. It is not owned by SAP even if you connected it to SAP email address. This private Apple ID enables the installation of App Store apps and the use of Apple services like Apple Pay and FaceTime e.g. for private purposes only. You will need to change your Apple ID to a non-SAP address, otherwise you will lose the functions offered by the Apple ID on your device. Apple is introducing a new feature for enterprise customers, called Managed Apple ID. It will help to enable a further separation of private and business data and their use on Apple devices at SAP. Managed Apple IDs use SAP email addresses and will help SAP prepare for future projects such as Bring Your Own Device, Passkey, and Mac Single Sign On extension. To prepare for these future projects, SAP needs to claim the sap.com domain for corporate use and create Managed Apple IDs using SAP email addresses only. Please help by changing the email address of your private Apple ID. When Apple devices were introduced at SAP in 2012, they were not enterprise ready when we adopted them. However they are ready now, and SAP needs to claim ownership of company email addresses for Managed Apple IDs. In early December 2023, the process to enable Managed Apple IDs started with Apple, email address conflicts will be identified, and those users who are using an SAP email address for their private Apple ID will be notified. Any change to these private Apple IDs must be completed by February 5th of 2024. After this date, your Apple ID can no longer be accessed using your SAP e-mail address but only by a temporary e-mail address. The procedure for an update remains the same, including the password. You can find more information about this change to a temporary e-mail address on our Work Zone page: Managed Apple ID (int.sap). However, Apple users can still change the email address associated with their Apple ID at any time. What is an Apple ID? Typically, a user owns an Apple ID to manage personal data, even on a corporate device. It is therefore often called personal Apple ID. An Apple ID is not required on the device. It can be used with SAP apps and the administrative settings only - if enrolled with JAMF. An Apple ID is an account that gives access to Apple services like the App Store, iCloud, iMessage, FaceTime, and Apple Music. The email address associated with this account is called Apple ID. Today, all Apple IDs in use (personal or business) at SAP are Personal Apple IDs. SAP will be configuring Managed Apple IDs for all “@sap.com” email addresses for future projects. What is a Managed Apple ID? A Managed Apple ID is owned and managed by your organization — including password resets and role-based administration. It also provides access to iCloud for collaboration with iWork and backup on iPhone and iPad devices. To log into those devices, the Managed Apple ID and a password with two-factor authentication (Microsoft Azure) are needed. Step-by-step instructions Affected users will receive an email by Apple Inc. - \"Update Apple ID” - early December 2023. If you are not using your SAP email address as your Apple ID, no action is required. If you are using an SAP email address as your Apple ID, please follow these steps: Sign out of the Apple ID on all connected devices. Go to https://appleid.apple.com/ and login with your SAP email address. Update your Apple ID by replacing the SAP email address with your private, non-SAP email address. Confirm the “new” email address with a verification code that Apple sends to your non-SAP email address. Logout from the Apple website to complete the change. Your Apple ID should now be associated with your private, non-SAP email address. Sign back in to the Apple ID on all connected devices. More information you can check iOS/MacOS - Why we need managed Apple IDs", "source": "SAP Mobile devices", "id": 249}, {"topic": "12. Frequently used Mobile Apps", "section": "12.1 Soft Tokens (Mobile App)", "paragraphs": ["How do I activate my RSA token to a new iPhone or iPad?", "Prerequisites:", "SoftToken has already been ordered", "RSA SecurID app is already installed on new device", "Email is configured on your new device", "On your new device:", "Open the RSA SecurID app", "From the Welcome screen, press the contact card icon near the bottom", "Press Email Binding ID", "Enter your own SAP email address in the To: field and press Send", "From a browser while on SAP-Corporate or VPN:", "Open your browser and go to: https://secureidadm.wdf.sap.corp/deploy.htm", "Copy the Binding ID from the mail as Device ID / Device PIN", "Select iPhone from the drop-down menu and click Send", "Take note of your activation password (highlighted in red) from the SoftToken Deployment screen.", "On your new device:", "Open the email from firewall.admin@sap.com", "Tap on the link found at the bottom of the email", "On the Token Import screen, enter the activation password from the SoftToken Deployment screen and press return", "Press OK complete the process", "More information you can check RSA token - All about SecurID SoftTokens (Mobile App)", "12.2 Mail iOS & iPadOS", "How do I configure my mail account?", "Mail is included in iOS and iPadOS as the default mail application.", "It is configured for you automatically when you enroll your iPhone or iPad for management.", "Manual configurations of your mail account to your SAP mail account are not supported as they will conflict with the automatic configuration on your device as part of your enrollment into management.", "How do I add a personal email account?", "You can add additional email accounts to your iPhone or iPad by using the Add Accounts wizard on your device.", "If you use an email provider like iCloud, Google, or Yahoo, Mail can automatically set up your email account with just your email address and password. Here's how:", "Go to Settings → Mail → Accounts, then tap Add Account.", "Tap your email provider.", "Enter your email address and password.", "Tap Next and wait for Mail to verify your account.", "Choose information from your email account, like Contacts or Calendars, that you want to see on your device.", "Tap Save.", "If you don't see your email provider, tap Other to add your account manually.", "iOS Managed Mail Account Update", "Before the update, it’s crucial to take note of any customized sync settings you have configured. This ensures you can reproduce these settings after your device has been updated.", "Steps:", "Go to Settings: Open the Settings app on your device.", "Open your SAP Account: Navigate to Apps > Mail > Mail Accounts section.", "Select the SAP Account: Tap on your existing SAP Exchange account to view its settings.", "Review Sync Settings: Take note of your sync settings including Mail Days to Sync, Contacts, Calendars, Reminders, Notes", "Authentication Prompt", "Once the new Exchange profile is applied to the device, you will be prompted to re-authenticate. This is a security measure designed to ensure that the device correctly syncs with the company’s Exchange server.", "Note: Before proceeding, please make sure you have a strong and reliable WiFi connection!", "Steps:", "1. Notification: You will receive a notification that the Exchange profile has been updated. Tap “Edit Settings.”", "2. Authentication Prompt: The Mail Account settings will be opened. Then you will be prompted for your microsoftonline.com credentials to sign in. Tap “Continue.”", "3. Enter Credentials if necessary: If prompted, enter your SAP email address, password, and Microsoft Authenticator prompts to complete the login process.", "Re-configuring Sync Settings", "After entering your authentication details, you may need to check and adjust your sync settings. The update might reset any custom settings you previously configured.", "Steps:", "Go to Settings: Open the Settings app on your device.", "Open your SAP Account: Navigate to Apps > Mail > Mail Accounts section.", "Select the SAP Account: Tap on your existing SAP Exchange account to view its settings.", "Reconfigure Custom Settings:", "Mail Days to Sync: Set the sync duration (e.g., 1 week, 1 month).", "Contacts, Calendars, Reminders, and Notes: Make sure each of these sync options is configured as per your preference.", "12.3 Cisco Security Connector – iOS & iPadOS", "Secure Connector is an app provided for DNS security on your iPhone and iPad. It provides encrypted DNS service to Umbrella which protects your DNS resolutions for external resources. The Umbrella service is configured to protect your iPhone and iPad against security related issues such as phishing attacks and other potentially harmful attacks.", "There is no visual indication on your iPhone or iPad when the Secure Connector is active. You can open the app and view the status at any time.", "There is virtually no performance impact on your device when using Secure Connector. As the framework is natively provided in iOS and iPadOS from Apple, everything is handled automatically for you. In most cases, your Internet may improve for speed due to the improved DNS resolutions provided by Umbrella as Umbrella has a large global DataCenter coverage, 100% uptime as well as some of the fastest DNS resolution speeds available.", "If Secure Connector is unable to successfully start or communicate with the service, it will simply fail open and there is no impact on your iPhone or iPad.", "Currently, we do not use Endpoint Visibility (Clarity) and it is normal that this is shown as inactive.", "Note: After installation, open Cisco Security Connector and grant network access. If network access is not allowed, cellular data appears in the status bar but it will not work while Wi-Fi is off, as Secure Connector requires cellular data.", "Alternatively, go to Settings → Cisco Security and make sure \"WLAN & Cellular\" is allowed.", "Collecting Logs", "The Cisco Security Connector Diagnostics logs provides some useful troubleshooting information about a particular mobile device.", "Open the CSC app on the device.", "Go to \"About\" and click on Report a Problem.", "This sends a diagnostic email to the administrator email.", "If you are submitting an IT Direct ticket, please attach the diagnostic report from this email to your ticket.", "You may be asked to collect additional logs using a full system diagnostic. In this event, simply follow the steps outlined here. The captured file will be large, so you will need to securely share that file (use OneDrive) with support.", "Security Connector Installation / Uninstall / Reinstall", "For supervised (ADE or Automatic Device Enrollment) devices, Secure Connector is automatically installed, and no interaction is required from you.", "For BYOD or managed devices (enrolled manually with Device Enrollment), a one-time prompt will be shown during enrollment to approve installation of Secure Connector.", "The Security Connector can be installed, uninstalled, or reinstalled using Self Service. If you uninstall the Security Connector, the Profile will remain on your iPhone or iPad as it contains the configuration to the SAP Org ID when you reinstall the Roaming Client. The Security Connector will automatically re-install on your device if you remove it.", "More information", "Introducing Security Connector for iPhone and iPad", "MH1017 - Cisco Security Connector - iOS & iPadOS"], "content": "How do I activate my RSA token to a new iPhone or iPad? Prerequisites: SoftToken has already been ordered RSA SecurID app is already installed on new device Email is configured on your new device On your new device: Open the RSA SecurID app From the Welcome screen, press the contact card icon near the bottom Press Email Binding ID Enter your own SAP email address in the To: field and press Send From a browser while on SAP-Corporate or VPN: Open your browser and go to: https://secureidadm.wdf.sap.corp/deploy.htm Copy the Binding ID from the mail as Device ID / Device PIN Select iPhone from the drop-down menu and click Send Take note of your activation password (highlighted in red) from the SoftToken Deployment screen. On your new device: Open the email from firewall.admin@sap.com Tap on the link found at the bottom of the email On the Token Import screen, enter the activation password from the SoftToken Deployment screen and press return Press OK complete the process More information you can check RSA token - All about SecurID SoftTokens (Mobile App) 12.2 Mail iOS & iPadOS How do I configure my mail account? Mail is included in iOS and iPadOS as the default mail application. It is configured for you automatically when you enroll your iPhone or iPad for management. Manual configurations of your mail account to your SAP mail account are not supported as they will conflict with the automatic configuration on your device as part of your enrollment into management. How do I add a personal email account? You can add additional email accounts to your iPhone or iPad by using the Add Accounts wizard on your device. If you use an email provider like iCloud, Google, or Yahoo, Mail can automatically set up your email account with just your email address and password. Here's how: Go to Settings → Mail → Accounts, then tap Add Account. Tap your email provider. Enter your email address and password. Tap Next and wait for Mail to verify your account. Choose information from your email account, like Contacts or Calendars, that you want to see on your device. Tap Save. If you don't see your email provider, tap Other to add your account manually. iOS Managed Mail Account Update Before the update, it’s crucial to take note of any customized sync settings you have configured. This ensures you can reproduce these settings after your device has been updated. Steps: Go to Settings: Open the Settings app on your device. Open your SAP Account: Navigate to Apps > Mail > Mail Accounts section. Select the SAP Account: Tap on your existing SAP Exchange account to view its settings. Review Sync Settings: Take note of your sync settings including Mail Days to Sync, Contacts, Calendars, Reminders, Notes Authentication Prompt Once the new Exchange profile is applied to the device, you will be prompted to re-authenticate. This is a security measure designed to ensure that the device correctly syncs with the company’s Exchange server. Note: Before proceeding, please make sure you have a strong and reliable WiFi connection! Steps: 1. Notification: You will receive a notification that the Exchange profile has been updated. Tap “Edit Settings.” 2. Authentication Prompt: The Mail Account settings will be opened. Then you will be prompted for your microsoftonline.com credentials to sign in. Tap “Continue.” 3. Enter Credentials if necessary: If prompted, enter your SAP email address, password, and Microsoft Authenticator prompts to complete the login process. Re-configuring Sync Settings After entering your authentication details, you may need to check and adjust your sync settings. The update might reset any custom settings you previously configured. Steps: Go to Settings: Open the Settings app on your device. Open your SAP Account: Navigate to Apps > Mail > Mail Accounts section. Select the SAP Account: Tap on your existing SAP Exchange account to view its settings. Reconfigure Custom Settings: Mail Days to Sync: Set the sync duration (e.g., 1 week, 1 month). Contacts, Calendars, Reminders, and Notes: Make sure each of these sync options is configured as per your preference. 12.3 Cisco Security Connector – iOS & iPadOS Secure Connector is an app provided for DNS security on your iPhone and iPad. It provides encrypted DNS service to Umbrella which protects your DNS resolutions for external resources. The Umbrella service is configured to protect your iPhone and iPad against security related issues such as phishing attacks and other potentially harmful attacks. There is no visual indication on your iPhone or iPad when the Secure Connector is active. You can open the app and view the status at any time. There is virtually no performance impact on your device when using Secure Connector. As the framework is natively provided in iOS and iPadOS from Apple, everything is handled automatically for you. In most cases, your Internet may improve for speed due to the improved DNS resolutions provided by Umbrella as Umbrella has a large global DataCenter coverage, 100% uptime as well as some of the fastest DNS resolution speeds available. If Secure Connector is unable to successfully start or communicate with the service, it will simply fail open and there is no impact on your iPhone or iPad. Currently, we do not use Endpoint Visibility (Clarity) and it is normal that this is shown as inactive. Note: After installation, open Cisco Security Connector and grant network access. If network access is not allowed, cellular data appears in the status bar but it will not work while Wi-Fi is off, as Secure Connector requires cellular data. Alternatively, go to Settings → Cisco Security and make sure \"WLAN & Cellular\" is allowed. Collecting Logs The Cisco Security Connector Diagnostics logs provides some useful troubleshooting information about a particular mobile device. Open the CSC app on the device. Go to \"About\" and click on Report a Problem. This sends a diagnostic email to the administrator email. If you are submitting an IT Direct ticket, please attach the diagnostic report from this email to your ticket. You may be asked to collect additional logs using a full system diagnostic. In this event, simply follow the steps outlined here. The captured file will be large, so you will need to securely share that file (use OneDrive) with support. Security Connector Installation / Uninstall / Reinstall For supervised (ADE or Automatic Device Enrollment) devices, Secure Connector is automatically installed, and no interaction is required from you. For BYOD or managed devices (enrolled manually with Device Enrollment), a one-time prompt will be shown during enrollment to approve installation of Secure Connector. The Security Connector can be installed, uninstalled, or reinstalled using Self Service. If you uninstall the Security Connector, the Profile will remain on your iPhone or iPad as it contains the configuration to the SAP Org ID when you reinstall the Roaming Client. The Security Connector will automatically re-install on your device if you remove it. More information Introducing Security Connector for iPhone and iPad MH1017 - Cisco Security Connector - iOS & iPadOS", "source": "SAP Mobile devices", "id": 250}, {"topic": "12. Frequently used Mobile Apps", "section": "12.4 iPhone and iPad F5 access", "paragraphs": ["F5 Access enables you to access the SAP Corporate Network via Virtual Private Network (VPN) connection.", "It can be downloaded from Self Service.", "Additional note:", "F5 Access and Global Protect will not be available in Self Service for new BYOD Devices. (ADUE enrollments don’t allow full device managed VPN)", "It can be downloaded from Self Service.", "On your iPhone or iPad, download F5 Access from Self Service.", "Open F5 Access.", "Tap Agree in Terms and Conditions.", "Tap Allow to allow notifications.", "In the Configuration field, choose the server you would like to connect to.", "Return to the Connection page.", "Next to Connection, tap the slider to turn it on.", "You will be automatically authenticated and redirected to the Connection page.", "Your Status will be shown as Connected. A duration of connection will be displayed next to it.", "If you no longer need access to the SAP Corporate Network, simply tab the slider in the Connection field to disconnect.", "Important: Before connecting F5 Access, Allow notification for F5 Access App from IOS settings", "More information you can check F5 Access - iOS & iPadOS."], "content": "F5 Access enables you to access the SAP Corporate Network via Virtual Private Network (VPN) connection. It can be downloaded from Self Service. Additional note: F5 Access and Global Protect will not be available in Self Service for new BYOD Devices. (ADUE enrollments don’t allow full device managed VPN) It can be downloaded from Self Service. On your iPhone or iPad, download F5 Access from Self Service. Open F5 Access. Tap Agree in Terms and Conditions. Tap Allow to allow notifications. In the Configuration field, choose the server you would like to connect to. Return to the Connection page. Next to Connection, tap the slider to turn it on. You will be automatically authenticated and redirected to the Connection page. Your Status will be shown as Connected. A duration of connection will be displayed next to it. If you no longer need access to the SAP Corporate Network, simply tab the slider in the Connection field to disconnect. Important: Before connecting F5 Access, Allow notification for F5 Access App from IOS settings More information you can check F5 Access - iOS & iPadOS.", "source": "SAP Mobile devices", "id": 251}, {"topic": "12. Frequently used Mobile Apps", "section": "12.5 SSA (GlobalProtect) for Apple iOS", "paragraphs": ["Overview", "SAP Seamless Access (GlobalProtect) is the next-generation VPN solution that is designed for the cloud and provides you with seamless, secure, and high-performance connectivity at SAP.", "With ​​​​more than 30,000 active users on macOS and more than 86,000 active users on Windows and Android Mobile, we are now making SAP Seamless Access (GlobalProtect) available to all SAP Apple iOS mobile devices globally (except China).", "We hope you will enjoy the new boost in performance and usability as much as we do. Please ensure to disable your F5 VPN Client as soon as GlobalProtect is installed to avoid any limitations.", "Go Live of SAP Seamless Access (GlobalProtect) for Apple iOS starts in CW33/2023.", "The app is available on your Apple iOS mobile device.", "You can follow these instructions to get it set up and start using GlobalProtect.", "MH1033 - GlobalProtect VPN for iOS/iPadOS (int.sap)", "Open the Self Service app, scroll to GlobalProtect, and tap \"Install\":", "Once installed, launch GlobalProtect, tap \"Allow\" to allow notifications:", "Tap \"Connect\". Safari will launch, perform authentication with Azure AD, then prompt you to re-open GlobalProtect. Go ahead and tap \"Open\":", "Once GlobalProtect is re-opened, it should show \"Connected\":"], "content": "Overview SAP Seamless Access (GlobalProtect) is the next-generation VPN solution that is designed for the cloud and provides you with seamless, secure, and high-performance connectivity at SAP. With ​​​​more than 30,000 active users on macOS and more than 86,000 active users on Windows and Android Mobile, we are now making SAP Seamless Access (GlobalProtect) available to all SAP Apple iOS mobile devices globally (except China). We hope you will enjoy the new boost in performance and usability as much as we do. Please ensure to disable your F5 VPN Client as soon as GlobalProtect is installed to avoid any limitations. Go Live of SAP Seamless Access (GlobalProtect) for Apple iOS starts in CW33/2023. The app is available on your Apple iOS mobile device. You can follow these instructions to get it set up and start using GlobalProtect. MH1033 - GlobalProtect VPN for iOS/iPadOS (int.sap) Open the Self Service app, scroll to GlobalProtect, and tap \"Install\": Once installed, launch GlobalProtect, tap \"Allow\" to allow notifications: Tap \"Connect\". Safari will launch, perform authentication with Azure AD, then prompt you to re-open GlobalProtect. Go ahead and tap \"Open\": Once GlobalProtect is re-opened, it should show \"Connected\":", "source": "SAP Mobile devices", "id": 252}, {"topic": "12. Frequently used Mobile Apps", "section": "12.6 SSA (GlobalProtect) for Android - Go Live", "paragraphs": ["Overview", "SAP's Seamless Access (GlobalProtect) is the next generation solution for seamless, secure, high-performance, \"designed for cloud\" connectivity at SAP.", "With more than 85,000 active users already on Windows, we are making SAP Seamless Access (GlobalProtect) available now to all SAP Android mobile devices globally (except China).", "We hope you will enjoy the new boost in performance and usability as much as we do. Please disable your F5 VPN Client as soon as GlobalProtect is installed to avoid any limitations.", "Go Live of SAP Seamless Access (GlobalProtect) for Android starts on Monday, July 25.", "On Monday, July 25, 2022, GlobalProtect will be available in the managed PlayStore for Microsoft Intune managed Android 12 devices.", "Note: This service app will only be available for mobile Android devices.", "Where can I get more information?", "More information on Seamless Access (GlobalProtect) on the Android@SAP community page.", "12.7 Microsoft Teams – iOS/Android", "Microsoft Teams is your hub for teamwork in Microsoft 365. All your team conversations, files, meetings, and apps live together in a single shared workspace, and you can take it with you on your favorite mobile device. Whether you’re sprinting towards a deadline or sharing your next big idea, Teams can help you achieve more.", "For more information on what Teams offers and how it can benefit you, please visit the Teams - IT for You page.", "Installation", "The Teams mobile app can be installed on your SAP-managed mobile device through the Self Service (iOS) or Google Play in Work profile (Android):", "Camera/microphone permissions on iOS", "If Teams cannot access the camera of your iPhone, open the settings and navigate to Apps -> Teams and make sure that Microphone and Camera are enabled:"], "content": "Overview SAP's Seamless Access (GlobalProtect) is the next generation solution for seamless, secure, high-performance, \"designed for cloud\" connectivity at SAP. With more than 85,000 active users already on Windows, we are making SAP Seamless Access (GlobalProtect) available now to all SAP Android mobile devices globally (except China). We hope you will enjoy the new boost in performance and usability as much as we do. Please disable your F5 VPN Client as soon as GlobalProtect is installed to avoid any limitations. Go Live of SAP Seamless Access (GlobalProtect) for Android starts on Monday, July 25. On Monday, July 25, 2022, GlobalProtect will be available in the managed PlayStore for Microsoft Intune managed Android 12 devices. Note: This service app will only be available for mobile Android devices. Where can I get more information? More information on Seamless Access (GlobalProtect) on the Android@SAP community page. 12.7 Microsoft Teams – iOS/Android Microsoft Teams is your hub for teamwork in Microsoft 365. All your team conversations, files, meetings, and apps live together in a single shared workspace, and you can take it with you on your favorite mobile device. Whether you’re sprinting towards a deadline or sharing your next big idea, Teams can help you achieve more. For more information on what Teams offers and how it can benefit you, please visit the Teams - IT for You page. Installation The Teams mobile app can be installed on your SAP-managed mobile device through the Self Service (iOS) or Google Play in Work profile (Android): Camera/microphone permissions on iOS If Teams cannot access the camera of your iPhone, open the settings and navigate to Apps -> Teams and make sure that Microphone and Camera are enabled:", "source": "SAP Mobile devices", "id": 253}, {"topic": "13. How to Perform Cloud Mobile Printing", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Overview", "In this article, you will learn how you can print directly from any SAP certified mobile device, such as smartphone, tablet or lightweight laptop computer.", "What is Cloud Printing?", "Cloud Printing has an additional feature that allows you to print emails, attachments, pictures and other contents from your mobile device.", "With any SAP certified mobile device, as long as you can reach the Internet and send emails from your SAP email account, you will be able to print from your mobile device.", "Step 1 - Send the Print Job", "Note: It is very important to use the MobilePrint addresses from your own region to avoid performance issues.", "With your SAP Email account, forward or create an email and send this to the following MobilePrint address:", "AMER", "If you are located in the AMER region, send to: am@print.corp.sap or amer@print.corp.sap", "APJ", "If you are located in the APJ region, send to: ap@print.corp.sap or apj@print.corp.sap", "EMEA", "If you are located in the EMEA region, send to: em@print@corp.sap or emea@print.corp.sap", "Germany (DE)", "If you are located in Germany (DE), send to: de@print.corp.sap", "You can attach files like PDF, Word, Excel, PowerPoint, photos, etc. Every email attachment sent to this email address will be converted into PDF format. Forwarded emails with attachments will be listed as two or more separate print jobs.", "Step 2 - Pick up Print Job", "Your print job can be printed on each Badge printer based in an SAP office around the globe.", "If you print only via MobilePrint* or only via normal BadgePrint*, you will see your jobs listed directly in the printer display as shown below:", "Sign in with your badge or manual logon:", "This is what you will see using one method (either BadgePrint or MobilePrint), you may select the file and print accordingly:", "However, if you send print jobs using both methods (BadgePrint and MobilePrint) around the same time, the print jobs will be stored in different folders: BadgePrint in VPSX and MobilePrint in AM, AP, EM or DE.", "If you have a question regarding the folder name see here (question 1).", "Choose to open the folder which contains the print jobs you would like to print and select print accordingly:", "* BadgePrint = naming for standard print via server-based printer queue (normal printing via SAP-issued laptop/desktop)", "* MobilePrint = naming for printing from a mobile device via email also known as Cloud Printing", "You can get more Cloud Mobile Printing with IKB0013529 Printing - How to Perform Cloud Mobile Printing"], "content": "Overview In this article, you will learn how you can print directly from any SAP certified mobile device, such as smartphone, tablet or lightweight laptop computer. What is Cloud Printing? Cloud Printing has an additional feature that allows you to print emails, attachments, pictures and other contents from your mobile device. With any SAP certified mobile device, as long as you can reach the Internet and send emails from your SAP email account, you will be able to print from your mobile device. Step 1 - Send the Print Job Note: It is very important to use the MobilePrint addresses from your own region to avoid performance issues. With your SAP Email account, forward or create an email and send this to the following MobilePrint address: AMER If you are located in the AMER region, send to: am@print.corp.sap or amer@print.corp.sap APJ If you are located in the APJ region, send to: ap@print.corp.sap or apj@print.corp.sap EMEA If you are located in the EMEA region, send to: em@print@corp.sap or emea@print.corp.sap Germany (DE) If you are located in Germany (DE), send to: de@print.corp.sap You can attach files like PDF, Word, Excel, PowerPoint, photos, etc. Every email attachment sent to this email address will be converted into PDF format. Forwarded emails with attachments will be listed as two or more separate print jobs. Step 2 - Pick up Print Job Your print job can be printed on each Badge printer based in an SAP office around the globe. If you print only via MobilePrint* or only via normal BadgePrint*, you will see your jobs listed directly in the printer display as shown below: Sign in with your badge or manual logon: This is what you will see using one method (either BadgePrint or MobilePrint), you may select the file and print accordingly: However, if you send print jobs using both methods (BadgePrint and MobilePrint) around the same time, the print jobs will be stored in different folders: BadgePrint in VPSX and MobilePrint in AM, AP, EM or DE. If you have a question regarding the folder name see here (question 1). Choose to open the folder which contains the print jobs you would like to print and select print accordingly: * BadgePrint = naming for standard print via server-based printer queue (normal printing via SAP-issued laptop/desktop) * MobilePrint = naming for printing from a mobile device via email also known as Cloud Printing You can get more Cloud Mobile Printing with IKB0013529 Printing - How to Perform Cloud Mobile Printing", "source": "SAP Mobile devices", "id": 254}, {"topic": "14. Mobile Device return process", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["For mobile devices (smartphone, tablet) please follow the steps described below before their return.", "Apple Mobile Devices", "For Apple equipment, ensure that you disable \"Find My\" before proceeding with the steps below.", "Apple Mobile (iOS)", "Open Settings and tap your name at the top for Apple ID settings.", "Tap Find My, then Find My iPhone/iPad, and toggle this setting off.", "If Find My is greyed out, you first have to disable Stolen Device Protection (Settings, Face ID & Passcode, Stolen Device Protection, toggle off this setting. Maybe you have to wait at least one hour, based on your security delay setting above, before you can really disable it again)", "Enter your Apple ID password, then tap Turn Off.", "Return to Apple ID settings and sign out of your iCloud Account at the bottom to ensure data is cleared.", "Android Mobile Devices", "For Android equipment, ensure that you disable \"Find My Device\" before proceeding with any further steps.", "Google Pixel", "Open Settings and tap Security.", "Tap Find My Device and toggle Find My Device off.", "Return to Settings and tap Passwords & Accounts.", "Select your Google Account, then tap Remove account to ensure data is cleared.", "Samsung", "Open Settings and tap Biometrics and Security.", "Tap Find My Mobile and toggle Find My Mobile off.", "Return to Settings and tap Accounts and Backup, followed by Manage accounts.", "Select your Google Account, then tap Remove account to ensure data is cleared.", "Returning Mobile phone number", "If you are also returning your SAP mobile phone number with the device, please make sure to change it for personal accounts or websites (Microsoft account, Google account, Banking, …) before returning your equipment, especially if used for multi-factor authentications!", "More device return information, you may refer to KB How to return Equipment"], "content": "For mobile devices (smartphone, tablet) please follow the steps described below before their return. Apple Mobile Devices For Apple equipment, ensure that you disable \"Find My\" before proceeding with the steps below. Apple Mobile (iOS) Open Settings and tap your name at the top for Apple ID settings. Tap Find My, then Find My iPhone/iPad, and toggle this setting off. If Find My is greyed out, you first have to disable Stolen Device Protection (Settings, Face ID & Passcode, Stolen Device Protection, toggle off this setting. Maybe you have to wait at least one hour, based on your security delay setting above, before you can really disable it again) Enter your Apple ID password, then tap Turn Off. Return to Apple ID settings and sign out of your iCloud Account at the bottom to ensure data is cleared. Android Mobile Devices For Android equipment, ensure that you disable \"Find My Device\" before proceeding with any further steps. Google Pixel Open Settings and tap Security. Tap Find My Device and toggle Find My Device off. Return to Settings and tap Passwords & Accounts. Select your Google Account, then tap Remove account to ensure data is cleared. Samsung Open Settings and tap Biometrics and Security. Tap Find My Mobile and toggle Find My Mobile off. Return to Settings and tap Accounts and Backup, followed by Manage accounts. Select your Google Account, then tap Remove account to ensure data is cleared. Returning Mobile phone number If you are also returning your SAP mobile phone number with the device, please make sure to change it for personal accounts or websites (Microsoft account, Google account, Banking, …) before returning your equipment, especially if used for multi-factor authentications! More device return information, you may refer to KB How to return Equipment", "source": "SAP Mobile devices", "id": 255}, {"topic": "15. Mobile Lost / Stolen device", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["How to find your mobile device", "iPhone:", "SAP IT can remotely enable Lost Mode on a supervised device. Lost Mode is a locked state of the device but does not remotely wipe it or its data.", "You can also enable Lost Mode using Find My Phone yourself if you have enabled Find My on your device and signed into your personal iCloud account.", "See Find My iPhone: Lock and track your device using Lost Mode for more information.", "Android:", "Please check: Be ready to find a lost Android device - Android Help (google.com)", "If you are sure your device is stolen, please follow these steps below.", "Create Lost/Stolen incident report", "When an SAP device is lost or stolen, e.g., mobile devices, Tablet devices, laptop devices, desktop devices, monitors, please follow the steps below.", "1. SAP Security Incident Report:", "If Stolen/Lost:", "Please additionally get a Police Report from your local Police Office if possible", "To report a Lost /Stolen device, go to the My IT Equipment app, select “My Device(s),” and select “Lost or Stolen.” Proceed to fill in the required information.", "An additional IT Ticket will be automatically created to notify our team to lock/block your device.", "2. If you need to request replacement SIM card for your mobile/tablet/notebook please use the Mobile - SIM Card Form", "3. Order your replacement device in Ariba Guided Buying.", "SAP IT will retire the Public “IT Equipment Rent Tool”. If you need a device, please consider the following options:", "For emergency cases or short-term rent (max. 10 working days), the IT Link Centers can offer you a loaner device.", "You can find all locations and addresses of an IT Link Centers near you on Schedule Support - itsupport.sap.com and allow the Browser to detect your Location.", "Do you need a notebook for a longer period of time? Please book yourself a reuse device in our IT Equipment Reuse Tool. (Germany Only)", "You can find more information on Hardware – Lost / Stolen device"], "content": "How to find your mobile device iPhone: SAP IT can remotely enable Lost Mode on a supervised device. Lost Mode is a locked state of the device but does not remotely wipe it or its data. You can also enable Lost Mode using Find My Phone yourself if you have enabled Find My on your device and signed into your personal iCloud account. See Find My iPhone: Lock and track your device using Lost Mode for more information. Android: Please check: Be ready to find a lost Android device - Android Help (google.com) If you are sure your device is stolen, please follow these steps below. Create Lost/Stolen incident report When an SAP device is lost or stolen, e.g., mobile devices, Tablet devices, laptop devices, desktop devices, monitors, please follow the steps below. 1. SAP Security Incident Report: If Stolen/Lost: Please additionally get a Police Report from your local Police Office if possible To report a Lost /Stolen device, go to the My IT Equipment app, select “My Device(s),” and select “Lost or Stolen.” Proceed to fill in the required information. An additional IT Ticket will be automatically created to notify our team to lock/block your device. 2. If you need to request replacement SIM card for your mobile/tablet/notebook please use the Mobile - SIM Card Form 3. Order your replacement device in Ariba Guided Buying. SAP IT will retire the Public “IT Equipment Rent Tool”. If you need a device, please consider the following options: For emergency cases or short-term rent (max. 10 working days), the IT Link Centers can offer you a loaner device. You can find all locations and addresses of an IT Link Centers near you on Schedule Support - itsupport.sap.com and allow the Browser to detect your Location. Do you need a notebook for a longer period of time? Please book yourself a reuse device in our IT Equipment Reuse Tool. (Germany Only) You can find more information on Hardware – Lost / Stolen device", "source": "SAP Mobile devices", "id": 256}, {"topic": "16. FAQ", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Q1: What is Conditional Access? A: Conditional Access is the tool used by Microsoft Entra ID to bring signals together, to make decisions, and enforce organizational policies.", "Q2: Can I register using only the Authenticator app? A: No. Always use Self Service > Compliance > Register for proper SAP compliance!", "Q3: Why do I see \"Register with Microsoft\" in Self Service after registering? A: This is a known issue and will be fixed. You don’t need to register again.", "Q4: What is managed on my device? A: See Understanding what is tracked for details on managed data and device privacy.", "Q5: What if a user travel between different regions?", "A: If a user will travel between different regions -it is NOT necessary to change the normally used MobilePrintemail address. Each regional MobilePrint email address will work together with all_BADGE printers around the world.", "Q6: How is this affecting private devices that are not managed?", "A. Clients will not be able to access Microsoft 365 apps after Conditional Access is turned on. All devices needing to access SAP data will need to be enrolled in each respective platform’s client management system."], "content": "Q1: What is Conditional Access? A: Conditional Access is the tool used by Microsoft Entra ID to bring signals together, to make decisions, and enforce organizational policies. Q2: Can I register using only the Authenticator app? A: No. Always use Self Service > Compliance > Register for proper SAP compliance! Q3: Why do I see \"Register with Microsoft\" in Self Service after registering? A: This is a known issue and will be fixed. You don’t need to register again. Q4: What is managed on my device? A: See Understanding what is tracked for details on managed data and device privacy. Q5: What if a user travel between different regions? A: If a user will travel between different regions -it is NOT necessary to change the normally used MobilePrintemail address. Each regional MobilePrint email address will work together with all_BADGE printers around the world. Q6: How is this affecting private devices that are not managed? A. Clients will not be able to access Microsoft 365 apps after Conditional Access is turned on. All devices needing to access SAP data will need to be enrolled in each respective platform’s client management system.", "source": "SAP Mobile devices", "id": 257}, {"topic": "", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["KB0952609", "ONE Support", "Internal- SAP Only", "Version control", "If you find any content in this document is out of date, feel free to contact the Authors for feedback!", "Thanks for your cooperation in advance!", "Area: Secure Services"], "content": "KB0952609 ONE Support Internal- SAP Only Version control If you find any content in this document is out of date, feel free to contact the Authors for feedback! Thanks for your cooperation in advance! Area: Secure Services", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 258}, {"topic": "1. Microsoft Defender for Endpoint in Windows", "section": "1.1 Overview", "paragraphs": ["Microsoft Defender for Endpoint (MDE) helps protect your work device from viruses, unsafe files, and suspicious activities. It works quietly in the background, keeping your device safe without needing any action from you. With MDE enabled, you can work confidently knowing that your system is continuously monitored and protected.", "Check if Defender is Active", "Navigate to the Security Dashboard in the System Tray.", "Look for the Microsoft Defender icon and verify that it is active and running smoothly.", "Check for conflicting Anti-Virus", "Ensure no ENS components or other third-party antivirus software is installed and active.", "Go to Settings and select Privacy & Security", "Navigate to Windows Security and click on Virus & threat protection> Manage providers.", "You should only see Microsoft Defender is turned on as primary Antivirus.", "If Trellix is still listed as the antivirus product:", "Check whether \"Trellix Endpoint Security Platform\" is still installed in Settings under Apps and Installed apps. If so, the computer has not yet been moved over to use Microsoft Defender and nothing needs to be done.", "Otherwise, reboot the computer to fix this problem.", "Check Defender services", "Ensure the Defender services are running using Start and \"services\".", "If any are not running, restart your computer. A simple restart can often resolve temporary glitches.", "Endpoint Security - Microsoft Defender For Windows KB0952200"], "content": "Microsoft Defender for Endpoint (MDE) helps protect your work device from viruses, unsafe files, and suspicious activities. It works quietly in the background, keeping your device safe without needing any action from you. With MDE enabled, you can work confidently knowing that your system is continuously monitored and protected. Check if Defender is Active Navigate to the Security Dashboard in the System Tray. Look for the Microsoft Defender icon and verify that it is active and running smoothly. Check for conflicting Anti-Virus Ensure no ENS components or other third-party antivirus software is installed and active. Go to Settings and select Privacy & Security Navigate to Windows Security and click on Virus & threat protection> Manage providers. You should only see Microsoft Defender is turned on as primary Antivirus. If Trellix is still listed as the antivirus product: Check whether \"Trellix Endpoint Security Platform\" is still installed in Settings under Apps and Installed apps. If so, the computer has not yet been moved over to use Microsoft Defender and nothing needs to be done. Otherwise, reboot the computer to fix this problem. Check Defender services Ensure the Defender services are running using Start and \"services\". If any are not running, restart your computer. A simple restart can often resolve temporary glitches. Endpoint Security - Microsoft Defender For Windows KB0952200", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 259}, {"topic": "1. Microsoft Defender for Endpoint in Windows", "section": "1.2 Microsoft Defender - Virus & threat protection settings", "paragraphs": ["Real–Time Protection", "Changes in Real-Time Protection are not possible due to MS Defender’s Tamper Protection enabled feature.", "It’s an important feature for detecting and blocking threats instantaneously. Thus, it should always be enabled.", "Ensure to check for conflicting software and uninstall them as the existence of any third-party antivirus instead of Defender can prevent effective threat detection and protection.", "Cloud–Delivered Protection", "This feature will be enabled by default as it provides faster and more accurate threat detection.", "Ensure your device has a stable internet connection for the feature to be effective on your device.", "To verify network communication with the Microsoft Defender Antivirus cloud service, use the command, “MpCmdRun.exe –ValidateMapsConnection”", "Review your privacy settings to ensure they don’t block cloud-delivered protection features.", "Tamper Protection", "MS Defender’s Tamper Protection will be enabled by default as this would help to prevent others from modifying or making unauthorized changes to the important security features.", "Raise an incident ticket to the IES CS Advanced - Secure Services (Client Protection) team if tamper protection needs to be disabled for troubleshooting. (include justification)", "Exclusions", "This feature is fully managed by IES CS Advanced - Secure Services (Client Protection) team. Thus, users may not be able to make any changes to it.", "Raise an incident ticket to the IES CS Advanced - Secure Services (Client Protection) team, if exclusions are required. (include justification)"], "content": "Real–Time Protection Changes in Real-Time Protection are not possible due to MS Defender’s Tamper Protection enabled feature. It’s an important feature for detecting and blocking threats instantaneously. Thus, it should always be enabled. Ensure to check for conflicting software and uninstall them as the existence of any third-party antivirus instead of Defender can prevent effective threat detection and protection. Cloud–Delivered Protection This feature will be enabled by default as it provides faster and more accurate threat detection. Ensure your device has a stable internet connection for the feature to be effective on your device. To verify network communication with the Microsoft Defender Antivirus cloud service, use the command, “MpCmdRun.exe –ValidateMapsConnection” Review your privacy settings to ensure they don’t block cloud-delivered protection features. Tamper Protection MS Defender’s Tamper Protection will be enabled by default as this would help to prevent others from modifying or making unauthorized changes to the important security features. Raise an incident ticket to the IES CS Advanced - Secure Services (Client Protection) team if tamper protection needs to be disabled for troubleshooting. (include justification) Exclusions This feature is fully managed by IES CS Advanced - Secure Services (Client Protection) team. Thus, users may not be able to make any changes to it. Raise an incident ticket to the IES CS Advanced - Secure Services (Client Protection) team, if exclusions are required. (include justification)", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 260}, {"topic": "1. Microsoft Defender for Endpoint in Windows", "section": "1.3 Microsoft Defender Scan options", "paragraphs": ["On your Windows device, open the Windows Security app, and then Scan options.", "Quick Scan", "A quick scan looks at all the locations where there could be malware registered to start with the system, such as registry keys and known Windows startup folders. Quick scans also run on mounted removable devices, such as USB drives.", "Full scan", "A full scan begins with a quick scan and then scans all mounted fixed disks and removable/network drives (if the full scan is configured to do so). A full scan can take a few hours or days to complete, depending on the amount and type of data that needs to be scanned.", "Custom Scan", "A custom scan runs on files and folders that you specify. For example, you can choose to scan a USB drive or a specific folder on your device's local drive.", "Microsoft Defender Antivirus (Offline scan)", "Microsoft Defender Offline is an anti-malware scanning tool that lets you boot and run a scan from a trusted environment. The scan runs from outside the normal Windows kernel so it can target malware that attempts to bypass the Windows shell, such as viruses and rootkits that infect or overwrite the master boot record (MBR).", "Microsoft Defender Offline Scan KB0952609", "Scan results", "Seeing the Microsoft Defender Offline scan results in Windows 11:", "Select Start, and then select Settings > Update & Security > Windows Security > Virus & threat protection.", "On the Virus & threat protection screen, under Current threats, select Scan options, and then select Protection history.", "Appendix: Detected threat", "When a threat is first detected, it is shown under Current threats.", "No action is required; the threat will be quarantined automatically.", "Please do not select “Allow on Device”. (This option is for advanced users who are certain that this is a false detection. If unsure, please proceed to raise a ticket.)", "Appendix: Protection history", "After a short period of time, threats are shown under Protection history.", "No further action is required.", "Please do not select “Restore”. (This option is for advanced users who are certain that this is a false detection. If unsure, please proceed to raise a ticket.)", "Raising a ticket", "Raise an incident ticket to the IES CS Advanced - Secure Services (Client Protection) team to submit the files that are deemed to be suspicious or false positive to Microsoft team.", "Microsoft Defender Virus or Malware Detected KB0952588"], "content": "On your Windows device, open the Windows Security app, and then Scan options. Quick Scan A quick scan looks at all the locations where there could be malware registered to start with the system, such as registry keys and known Windows startup folders. Quick scans also run on mounted removable devices, such as USB drives. Full scan A full scan begins with a quick scan and then scans all mounted fixed disks and removable/network drives (if the full scan is configured to do so). A full scan can take a few hours or days to complete, depending on the amount and type of data that needs to be scanned. Custom Scan A custom scan runs on files and folders that you specify. For example, you can choose to scan a USB drive or a specific folder on your device's local drive. Microsoft Defender Antivirus (Offline scan) Microsoft Defender Offline is an anti-malware scanning tool that lets you boot and run a scan from a trusted environment. The scan runs from outside the normal Windows kernel so it can target malware that attempts to bypass the Windows shell, such as viruses and rootkits that infect or overwrite the master boot record (MBR). Microsoft Defender Offline Scan KB0952609 Scan results Seeing the Microsoft Defender Offline scan results in Windows 11: Select Start, and then select Settings > Update & Security > Windows Security > Virus & threat protection. On the Virus & threat protection screen, under Current threats, select Scan options, and then select Protection history. Appendix: Detected threat When a threat is first detected, it is shown under Current threats. No action is required; the threat will be quarantined automatically. Please do not select “Allow on Device”. (This option is for advanced users who are certain that this is a false detection. If unsure, please proceed to raise a ticket.) Appendix: Protection history After a short period of time, threats are shown under Protection history. No further action is required. Please do not select “Restore”. (This option is for advanced users who are certain that this is a false detection. If unsure, please proceed to raise a ticket.) Raising a ticket Raise an incident ticket to the IES CS Advanced - Secure Services (Client Protection) team to submit the files that are deemed to be suspicious or false positive to Microsoft team. Microsoft Defender Virus or Malware Detected KB0952588", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 261}, {"topic": "1. Microsoft Defender for Endpoint in Windows", "section": "1.4 Defender for cloud apps – Application blocked", "paragraphs": ["Overview", "This article has information on how Microsoft Defender for Cloud Apps is blocking the access to applications that are prohibited to be used on SAP devices.", "Microsoft Defender for Cloud apps is a security solution that helps protect your organization's data by monitoring and controlling access to cloud applications. When an app is blocked by CASB, users may encounter various notifications and restrictions. This manual provides an overview of the user experience during such events.", "Ratings are done by the Software Asset Management – SaaS Management/ Governance at SAP team. For more information have a look at KB1244265", "Browsers Covered in this document", "Windows Edge Browser", "Windows Chrome Browser (same experience for any chromium browser)", "MacOS Chrome Browser", "MacOS Safari Browser", "Reasons for Blocking", "The notification usually includes the reason for the block, such as:", "Security Risks: The app may pose a security threat.", "Compliance Issues: The app may not comply with organizational policies.", "Steps to Resolve", "Request Access: Prohibited Software is software that is rated as prohibited in the Software Catalog (Ariba). It must not be used (via a SaaS portal or via an Installation) on SAP client and server devices. Usage of such software must be stopped immediately.", "Alternative Solutions: For most applications that are blocked, a separate KB article exists", "Notification of Blocked App KB1005168"], "content": "Overview This article has information on how Microsoft Defender for Cloud Apps is blocking the access to applications that are prohibited to be used on SAP devices. Microsoft Defender for Cloud apps is a security solution that helps protect your organization's data by monitoring and controlling access to cloud applications. When an app is blocked by CASB, users may encounter various notifications and restrictions. This manual provides an overview of the user experience during such events. Ratings are done by the Software Asset Management – SaaS Management/ Governance at SAP team. For more information have a look at KB1244265 Browsers Covered in this document Windows Edge Browser Windows Chrome Browser (same experience for any chromium browser) MacOS Chrome Browser MacOS Safari Browser Reasons for Blocking The notification usually includes the reason for the block, such as: Security Risks: The app may pose a security threat. Compliance Issues: The app may not comply with organizational policies. Steps to Resolve Request Access: Prohibited Software is software that is rated as prohibited in the Software Catalog (Ariba). It must not be used (via a SaaS portal or via an Installation) on SAP client and server devices. Usage of such software must be stopped immediately. Alternative Solutions: For most applications that are blocked, a separate KB article exists Notification of Blocked App KB1005168", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 262}, {"topic": "1. Microsoft Defender for Endpoint in Windows", "section": "1.5 MS Defender Update definitions", "paragraphs": ["Ensure to check updated Definitions and install the latest threat definitions.", "Open the Defender icon", "Navigate to Virus & threat protection", "Select Virus threat protection updates", "Click Check for updates", "Check and verify the latest installed Windows update via Windows Update, then select Update History", "You can also run signature updates via cmd with using MpCmdRun.exe -SignatureUpdate", "Refer to the link on the latest Security Signature update: Latest security intelligence updates for Microsoft Defender Antivirus and other Microsoft antimalware - Microsoft Security Intelligence", "Endpoint Security – Microsoft Defender – Common Issues KB0952841", "Generic IT Ticket : ITSM Service Catalog - itsupport.sap.com", "Service Offering: IES-CS-Security - EndPoint Security"], "content": "Ensure to check updated Definitions and install the latest threat definitions. Open the Defender icon Navigate to Virus & threat protection Select Virus threat protection updates Click Check for updates Check and verify the latest installed Windows update via Windows Update, then select Update History You can also run signature updates via cmd with using MpCmdRun.exe -SignatureUpdate Refer to the link on the latest Security Signature update: Latest security intelligence updates for Microsoft Defender Antivirus and other Microsoft antimalware - Microsoft Security Intelligence Endpoint Security – Microsoft Defender – Common Issues KB0952841 Generic IT Ticket : ITSM Service Catalog - itsupport.sap.com Service Offering: IES-CS-Security - EndPoint Security", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 263}, {"topic": "1. Microsoft Defender for Endpoint in Windows", "section": "1.6 Microsoft Defender for MacOS", "paragraphs": ["To verify Microsoft Defender has installed correctly and is up to date you can open the status menu and check these three areas with Timestamp and hostname:", "All green check marks", "No Action Needed", "Protection definitions are up to date", "If definitions are not up to date, click check for updates", "Troubleshooting Non-compliance and Microsoft Defender for MacOS KB0626540"], "content": "To verify Microsoft Defender has installed correctly and is up to date you can open the status menu and check these three areas with Timestamp and hostname: All green check marks No Action Needed Protection definitions are up to date If definitions are not up to date, click check for updates Troubleshooting Non-compliance and Microsoft Defender for MacOS KB0626540", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 264}, {"topic": "1. Microsoft Defender for Endpoint in Windows", "section": "1.7 Excluding developer applications from Microsoft Windows Defender On-Access Scan", "paragraphs": ["Computers are too slow due to scanning files and folder being compiled by code or its blocking services from network access.", "Create an IT Ticket with Hostname/Business Reason", "Title SAPDevelop folder exclusion request Service Software", "Service Offering IES-CS-Security - EndPoint Security", "Assignment group IES CS Advanced - Secure Services (Client Protection)", "Once the created ticket is completed, user would be advised to take action as below.", "Create a SAPDevelop folder in the directory in your Mac/WindowsOS/Linux", "Mac-> /Users/*/SAPDevelop/* (case sensitive)", "Windows-> C:\\SAPDevelop (case sensitive)", "Linux-> /home/*/SAPDevelop/* or */SAPDevelop/ (case sensitive)", "For more information, refer to User needs to exclude developer applications from Microsoft Windows Defender On-Access Scan KB0647809"], "content": "Computers are too slow due to scanning files and folder being compiled by code or its blocking services from network access. Create an IT Ticket with Hostname/Business Reason Title SAPDevelop folder exclusion request Service Software Service Offering IES-CS-Security - EndPoint Security Assignment group IES CS Advanced - Secure Services (Client Protection) Once the created ticket is completed, user would be advised to take action as below. Create a SAPDevelop folder in the directory in your Mac/WindowsOS/Linux Mac-> /Users/*/SAPDevelop/* (case sensitive) Windows-> C:\\SAPDevelop (case sensitive) Linux-> /home/*/SAPDevelop/* or */SAPDevelop/ (case sensitive) For more information, refer to User needs to exclude developer applications from Microsoft Windows Defender On-Access Scan KB0647809", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 265}, {"topic": "2. Linux - Windows Subsystem for Linux (WSL) - improve our daily workflow", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["The WSL is a built-in feature that enables developers to run a native Linux shell interface in Windows without using a virtual machine.", "The first release of WSL provides a Linux-compatible kernel interface, which can then run a GNU user space on top of it, such as that of any Linux distribution.", "The major advantage of WSL is that users get a Linux environment for their development or tests requirements directly from their personal windows OS.", "The compatible kernel allows users to run bash shell on top of Windows10 and use command language, with native GNU/Linux command-line tools (ssh, wget, curl, git, find, grep, sed, awk, etc.), programming-language interpreters (Ruby, Python, etc.), and even graphical applications (like X11).", "WSL2 (Has been released as part of Windows 18917 build) was announced as the next generation of this feature. WSL2 provides a real Linux kernel within Windows OS.", "The WSL2 is a lightweight VM (like container with real Linux kernel inside) based on a subset of Hyper-V features. This attribute imparts WSL2 better performance, speed and provides us better-isolated environment.", "This enables us to install software that wouldn’t run under the previous WSL, like the Docker engine.", "In WSL2, the Linux file system is using an ext4-formatted inside a virtual disk, so it provides Linux native filesystem performance on the Linux side.", "The GUI will be available from Windows 10 build 21364 and Windows 11.", "The main difference between WSL and WSL2 is the backend architecture. While WSL is built to transform the Linux shell system calls into NT kernel system calls (via WSL driver), WSL2 is a real Linux kernel, which means it handles the calls as any Linux OS.", "Unlike WSL, WSL2 gets a virtual NIC and a different IP address, just like a regular VM.", "In SAP this situation causes the blockage of communication from the client-side.", "For more information, refer to Linux - Windows Subsystem for Linux (WSL) - improve our daily workflow KB0013525"], "content": "The WSL is a built-in feature that enables developers to run a native Linux shell interface in Windows without using a virtual machine. The first release of WSL provides a Linux-compatible kernel interface, which can then run a GNU user space on top of it, such as that of any Linux distribution. The major advantage of WSL is that users get a Linux environment for their development or tests requirements directly from their personal windows OS. The compatible kernel allows users to run bash shell on top of Windows10 and use command language, with native GNU/Linux command-line tools (ssh, wget, curl, git, find, grep, sed, awk, etc.), programming-language interpreters (Ruby, Python, etc.), and even graphical applications (like X11). WSL2 (Has been released as part of Windows 18917 build) was announced as the next generation of this feature. WSL2 provides a real Linux kernel within Windows OS. The WSL2 is a lightweight VM (like container with real Linux kernel inside) based on a subset of Hyper-V features. This attribute imparts WSL2 better performance, speed and provides us better-isolated environment. This enables us to install software that wouldn’t run under the previous WSL, like the Docker engine. In WSL2, the Linux file system is using an ext4-formatted inside a virtual disk, so it provides Linux native filesystem performance on the Linux side. The GUI will be available from Windows 10 build 21364 and Windows 11. The main difference between WSL and WSL2 is the backend architecture. While WSL is built to transform the Linux shell system calls into NT kernel system calls (via WSL driver), WSL2 is a real Linux kernel, which means it handles the calls as any Linux OS. Unlike WSL, WSL2 gets a virtual NIC and a different IP address, just like a regular VM. In SAP this situation causes the blockage of communication from the client-side. For more information, refer to Linux - Windows Subsystem for Linux (WSL) - improve our daily workflow KB0013525", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 266}, {"topic": "3.Data Loss Prevention (DLP)", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Data Loss Prevention (DLP) is a content-based solution that provides protection against intentional or accidental disclosure of business sensitive data DLP's unique and proven architecture makes it possible to implement a data-centric security framework from which SAP can:", "Discover and classify sensitive data by context and content to gain visibility into how it is used by employees, contractors, partners, and outsourcers.", "Utilize actionable decision support to assess the risk associated with the sharing of sensitive data, enabling managers to make informed business decisions and create effective data security policies.", "Implement automated policy-driven information protection, driving accountability down to the user resulting in voluntary compliance and increased risk awareness behavior.", "Alert, block, and record high-risk behavior ultimately prevent costly and damaging data loss incidents.", "DLP safeguards sensitive business information by deploying policies consisting of definitions, classifications, rule sets, and endpoint client configurations. It then monitors and blocks users' outbound actions containing business sensitive information over protected channels as defined in the DLP policies. Alternately, it can encrypt sensitive content before allowing the action to proceed. Finally, the DLP software creates reports for review and control of the process and can store sensitive content as evidence", "Endpoint DLP works primarily with the data-in-use vector. It uses advanced text patterns, predefined dictionaries, defined keywords, and file properties to identify sensitive content during an outbound action and perform steps like allowing the transaction, encrypt the content, ask for a justification or block the transmission. It incorporates device management and can work with third-party software for additional layers of control. It oversees transactions at the \"point of use”, Endpoint DLP is capable of protecting data simultaneously across applications, devices, and channels of communication from a single management console to anywhere in the world.", "DLP monitors and prevents data loss in \"hard to detect\" hi-risk user actions such as:", "Burn, Cut/Paste or Copy to media devices including USB sticks and CD/DVD", "Clipboard operations", "Screen Capture", "Print", "Email and attachments", "Upload to a network share or a cloud storage", "Web browser actions", "Use of unauthorized applications", "Service offering: IES-CS-Security-Data Loss Prevention", "Assignment group: IES CS Advanced-Secure Services (Client Protection)", "For more information, refer to Data Loss Prevention (DLP) KB0013469"], "content": "Data Loss Prevention (DLP) is a content-based solution that provides protection against intentional or accidental disclosure of business sensitive data DLP's unique and proven architecture makes it possible to implement a data-centric security framework from which SAP can: Discover and classify sensitive data by context and content to gain visibility into how it is used by employees, contractors, partners, and outsourcers. Utilize actionable decision support to assess the risk associated with the sharing of sensitive data, enabling managers to make informed business decisions and create effective data security policies. Implement automated policy-driven information protection, driving accountability down to the user resulting in voluntary compliance and increased risk awareness behavior. Alert, block, and record high-risk behavior ultimately prevent costly and damaging data loss incidents. DLP safeguards sensitive business information by deploying policies consisting of definitions, classifications, rule sets, and endpoint client configurations. It then monitors and blocks users' outbound actions containing business sensitive information over protected channels as defined in the DLP policies. Alternately, it can encrypt sensitive content before allowing the action to proceed. Finally, the DLP software creates reports for review and control of the process and can store sensitive content as evidence Endpoint DLP works primarily with the data-in-use vector. It uses advanced text patterns, predefined dictionaries, defined keywords, and file properties to identify sensitive content during an outbound action and perform steps like allowing the transaction, encrypt the content, ask for a justification or block the transmission. It incorporates device management and can work with third-party software for additional layers of control. It oversees transactions at the \"point of use”, Endpoint DLP is capable of protecting data simultaneously across applications, devices, and channels of communication from a single management console to anywhere in the world. DLP monitors and prevents data loss in \"hard to detect\" hi-risk user actions such as: Burn, Cut/Paste or Copy to media devices including USB sticks and CD/DVD Clipboard operations Screen Capture Print Email and attachments Upload to a network share or a cloud storage Web browser actions Use of unauthorized applications Service offering: IES-CS-Security-Data Loss Prevention Assignment group: IES CS Advanced-Secure Services (Client Protection) For more information, refer to Data Loss Prevention (DLP) KB0013469", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 267}, {"topic": "4. CyberArk Endpoint Privileged Account Management (EPAM)", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["As a D, I or C user, we all have local administrator privilege on our Windows endpoints which allows us to carry out daily functions. For example: End-users can install / run software and change system settings without involving IT support. However, such privileges come with a cybersecurity risk because gaining access to administrative privileges can be weaponized by a malicious threat actor. The EPAM solution will help SAP with it's security in the endpoint by applying the cybersecurity concept of least privilege (which is explained below) without impacting user’s daily tasks or IT help desk productivity.", "CyberArk Endpoint Privilege Manager is SAP’s solution to enforce privilege security on endpoints to effectively reduce the attack surface and mitigate the risk of serious data breach. In addition, it ensures that SAP meets endpoint compliance and audit requirements."], "content": "As a D, I or C user, we all have local administrator privilege on our Windows endpoints which allows us to carry out daily functions. For example: End-users can install / run software and change system settings without involving IT support. However, such privileges come with a cybersecurity risk because gaining access to administrative privileges can be weaponized by a malicious threat actor. The EPAM solution will help SAP with it's security in the endpoint by applying the cybersecurity concept of least privilege (which is explained below) without impacting user’s daily tasks or IT help desk productivity. CyberArk Endpoint Privilege Manager is SAP’s solution to enforce privilege security on endpoints to effectively reduce the attack surface and mitigate the risk of serious data breach. In addition, it ensures that SAP meets endpoint compliance and audit requirements.", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 268}, {"topic": "4. CyberArk Endpoint Privileged Account Management (EPAM)", "section": "4.1 How does CyberArk Endpoint Privilege Manager work?", "paragraphs": ["CyberArk Endpoint Privilege Manager works by supporting users in performing administrative actions at the endpoint, reducing the risk of information being stolen or encrypted and held for ransom. A combination of privilege security, credential protection, and application control, (all described below) reduces the risk of malware infection. Unknown applications run in a restricted mode to contain threats and behavioral analysis blocks credential theft attempts. These critical protection technologies are deployed as a single agent to strengthen SAP’s existing endpoint security."], "content": "CyberArk Endpoint Privilege Manager works by supporting users in performing administrative actions at the endpoint, reducing the risk of information being stolen or encrypted and held for ransom. A combination of privilege security, credential protection, and application control, (all described below) reduces the risk of malware infection. Unknown applications run in a restricted mode to contain threats and behavioral analysis blocks credential theft attempts. These critical protection technologies are deployed as a single agent to strengthen SAP’s existing endpoint security.", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 269}, {"topic": "4. CyberArk Endpoint Privileged Account Management (EPAM)", "section": "4.2 Check EPAM Agent version", "paragraphs": ["To be sure you have the latest agent version or to see if your agent has all the updated policies, right click on the CyberArk icon in the task tray, select About CyberArk EPM Agent:", "This menu will show the version that is installed on your machine (orange highlight) and the last time policies were updated on your machine (yellow highlight).", "To update settings, you can request the most recent changes to be applied from the console. Right click on the CyberArk icon in the task tray and click Request Settings. Then select “Yes” to the pop-up asking if you are sure. The most recent CyberArk settings will then be running on your machine.", "For more information, refer to Endpoint Privileged Account Management (EPAM) - no necessary permissions or poor performance"], "content": "To be sure you have the latest agent version or to see if your agent has all the updated policies, right click on the CyberArk icon in the task tray, select About CyberArk EPM Agent: This menu will show the version that is installed on your machine (orange highlight) and the last time policies were updated on your machine (yellow highlight). To update settings, you can request the most recent changes to be applied from the console. Right click on the CyberArk icon in the task tray and click Request Settings. Then select “Yes” to the pop-up asking if you are sure. The most recent CyberArk settings will then be running on your machine. For more information, refer to Endpoint Privileged Account Management (EPAM) - no necessary permissions or poor performance", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 270}, {"topic": "4. CyberArk Endpoint Privileged Account Management (EPAM)", "section": "4.3 Proper Administrative Rights Configuration", "paragraphs": ["All Windows endpoints should have privileges managed by CyberArk Endpoint Privilege Manager Agent. If an end user does not have the expected administrative rights, check the following configurations to ensure that the app and the groups are configured properly.", "Local Group Configuration", "End users should be in the Power Users group and not in the Administrators group.", "To check: Computer Management > Local Users and Groups > Groups > Administrators - users C/D/I account should not be listed Computer Management > Local Users and Groups > Groups > Power Users - users C/D/I account should be listed", "If users’ groups are not properly configured, please send ticket to EPAM team: Service Offering: IES-CS-Security - Endpoint Privileged Account Management (EPAM) Assignment Group: IES CS Experts - Secure Services", "CyberArk EPM Agent", "The CyberArk Endpoint Privilege Manager Agent application should be shown in all places (Sometimes it shows up when searching for Endpoint, sometimes CyberArk):", "A) Control Panel > Programs and Features B) Settings > Apps > Installed apps C) Task bar - the blue CyberArk C icon (pictured below) should appear in the system tray, choose the up arrow next to the OneDrive icon D) Company Portal - the newest version of CyberArk should be listed as installed. You can compare your current CyberArk version by clicking on the C icon in your task bar > About CyberArk EPM Agent", "The UAC pop-up that appears when a user performs an administrative task (like open CMD as admin) should be a CyberArk pop-up (should have the C icon in the top corner) as pictured below", "If any of the following are not true, please send a ticket to EPAM team: Service Offering: IES-CS-Security - Endpoint Privileged Account Management (EPAM) Assignment Group: IES CS Experts - Secure Services"], "content": "All Windows endpoints should have privileges managed by CyberArk Endpoint Privilege Manager Agent. If an end user does not have the expected administrative rights, check the following configurations to ensure that the app and the groups are configured properly. Local Group Configuration End users should be in the Power Users group and not in the Administrators group. To check: Computer Management > Local Users and Groups > Groups > Administrators - users C/D/I account should not be listed Computer Management > Local Users and Groups > Groups > Power Users - users C/D/I account should be listed If users’ groups are not properly configured, please send ticket to EPAM team: Service Offering: IES-CS-Security - Endpoint Privileged Account Management (EPAM) Assignment Group: IES CS Experts - Secure Services CyberArk EPM Agent The CyberArk Endpoint Privilege Manager Agent application should be shown in all places (Sometimes it shows up when searching for Endpoint, sometimes CyberArk): A) Control Panel > Programs and Features B) Settings > Apps > Installed apps C) Task bar - the blue CyberArk C icon (pictured below) should appear in the system tray, choose the up arrow next to the OneDrive icon D) Company Portal - the newest version of CyberArk should be listed as installed. You can compare your current CyberArk version by clicking on the C icon in your task bar > About CyberArk EPM Agent The UAC pop-up that appears when a user performs an administrative task (like open CMD as admin) should be a CyberArk pop-up (should have the C icon in the top corner) as pictured below If any of the following are not true, please send a ticket to EPAM team: Service Offering: IES-CS-Security - Endpoint Privileged Account Management (EPAM) Assignment Group: IES CS Experts - Secure Services", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 271}, {"topic": "4. CyberArk Endpoint Privileged Account Management (EPAM)", "section": "4.4 Endpoint Privileged Account Management (EPAM) - No remote desktop access", "paragraphs": ["Reason: User account is not defined in the Remote Desktop Users group (EPAM restricts local administrator privileges)", "If you lose remote desktop access to a machine, and cannot physically access the machine, please submit a Support Ticket. Click “Create Ticket” at the top of this page, enter “EPAM - Remote Desktop Access” in the Description and select “Software” for the Issue Category. This includes if the machine is a VDI and the owner cannot access the machine via RDC.", "If you lose remote desktop access to a machine, and can physically access the machine, follow the instructions below:", "If the Remote Desktop Setting is turned Off and the switch is greyed out like so:", "Open Settings", "Scroll to the bottom and choose About", "Choose Advanced System Settings", "Choose the Remote tab. Check \"Allow Remote Assistance connections to this computer\" and click Apply.", "If the problem is that the user does not have the correct group policies:", "Run CMD as an administrator (click OK on the CyberArk UAC prompt that appears) and run the relevant command:", "For Azure AD Joined Machines:", "net localgroup \"Remote Desktop Users\" /add AzureAD\\xxxxxxxxx@sap.com", "(replace xxxxxxxxx with your SAP email address)", "For OnPrem AD Joined Machines:", "net localgroup \"Remote Desktop Users\" /add Global\\xxxxxxx", "(replace xxxxxxx with your user ID - C/D/I number)", "If this doesn’t work, check your machine’s default policies:", "1. Open the machine’s Local Security Policy (click OK on the CyberArk UAC prompt that appears)", "2. Go to Local Policies > User Rights Assignment", "3. Ensure that Access this computer from the network and Allow log on through Remote Desktop Services have both Administrators and Remote Desktop Users in the Security Settings", "4. If both Administrators and Remote Desktop Users are not in the specified groups, you will need to add them.", "Double click the policy", "Click Add User or Group (if this option is greyed out, try launching Local Security Policy with “Run as administrator”)", "Click Object Types", "Select box “Groups”, then OK", "e. Select Advanced", "f. Select Find Now", "g. Scroll to find \"Remote Desktop Users”, highlight, and select OK", "h. Click OK", "i. Click Apply and OK", "If the machine is a shared VDI and the issue is not related to permission or privilege (i.e. Network Layer Authentication), the owner of the VDI should add the user to the \"Direct Access Users\" group by doing the following:", "Run CMD as an administrator (click OK on the CyberArk UAC prompt that appears) and run the commands:", "net localgroup \"Remote Desktop Users\" /add \"GLOBAL\\xxxxxxxxx\"", "net localgroup \"Direct Access Users\" /add \"GLOBAL\\xxxxxxxxx\"", "For more information, refer to IKB0012923"], "content": "Reason: User account is not defined in the Remote Desktop Users group (EPAM restricts local administrator privileges) If you lose remote desktop access to a machine, and cannot physically access the machine, please submit a Support Ticket. Click “Create Ticket” at the top of this page, enter “EPAM - Remote Desktop Access” in the Description and select “Software” for the Issue Category. This includes if the machine is a VDI and the owner cannot access the machine via RDC. If you lose remote desktop access to a machine, and can physically access the machine, follow the instructions below: If the Remote Desktop Setting is turned Off and the switch is greyed out like so: Open Settings Scroll to the bottom and choose About Choose Advanced System Settings Choose the Remote tab. Check \"Allow Remote Assistance connections to this computer\" and click Apply. If the problem is that the user does not have the correct group policies: Run CMD as an administrator (click OK on the CyberArk UAC prompt that appears) and run the relevant command: For Azure AD Joined Machines: net localgroup \"Remote Desktop Users\" /add AzureAD\\xxxxxxxxx@sap.com (replace xxxxxxxxx with your SAP email address) For OnPrem AD Joined Machines: net localgroup \"Remote Desktop Users\" /add Global\\xxxxxxx (replace xxxxxxx with your user ID - C/D/I number) If this doesn’t work, check your machine’s default policies: 1. Open the machine’s Local Security Policy (click OK on the CyberArk UAC prompt that appears) 2. Go to Local Policies > User Rights Assignment 3. Ensure that Access this computer from the network and Allow log on through Remote Desktop Services have both Administrators and Remote Desktop Users in the Security Settings 4. If both Administrators and Remote Desktop Users are not in the specified groups, you will need to add them. Double click the policy Click Add User or Group (if this option is greyed out, try launching Local Security Policy with “Run as administrator”) Click Object Types Select box “Groups”, then OK e. Select Advanced f. Select Find Now g. Scroll to find \"Remote Desktop Users”, highlight, and select OK h. Click OK i. Click Apply and OK If the machine is a shared VDI and the issue is not related to permission or privilege (i.e. Network Layer Authentication), the owner of the VDI should add the user to the \"Direct Access Users\" group by doing the following: Run CMD as an administrator (click OK on the CyberArk UAC prompt that appears) and run the commands: net localgroup \"Remote Desktop Users\" /add \"GLOBAL\\xxxxxxxxx\" net localgroup \"Direct Access Users\" /add \"GLOBAL\\xxxxxxxxx\" For more information, refer to IKB0012923", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 272}, {"topic": "5. RSA SecurID Tokens", "section": "5.1 Overview", "paragraphs": ["RSA is a method of Securing access to SAP from the internet. It can also be used to secure internal resources. All SAP employees can order a token to work from home. It Secures WTS connections and is also given to partners of SAP to access our systems.", "There are 2 forms of token – keyfob (Hard/Physical token) and soft-token (Mobile App)."], "content": "RSA is a method of Securing access to SAP from the internet. It can also be used to secure internal resources. All SAP employees can order a token to work from home. It Secures WTS connections and is also given to partners of SAP to access our systems. There are 2 forms of token – keyfob (Hard/Physical token) and soft-token (Mobile App).", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 273}, {"topic": "5. RSA SecurID Tokens", "section": "5.3 Firewall Access Groups", "paragraphs": ["SecurID authentication grants a user access through a firewall, either the DMZ-facing firewall for external connections or internal firewalls for access to restricted systems (e.g., HR). Here are the most common firewall permissions:", "Dial-in", "Most commonly used access group for standard office WTS (SAP Desktop).", "Only needed for C users.", "D and I users have this access assigned automatically when the token is activated (\"SDIuser\").", "Must also have the group \"PsapgateX\" (assigned automatically when activated).", "AHR-WTS", "For access to the HR system.", "Also requires the group \"AHRUser\" as well as AD permissions.", "For AD and SecurID permissions – SRASIAMAUTH_HR (ITSC Infra are unable to add this firewall group).", "ISP-Admin", "For access to BSS WTS/Service Center B. ITSD are unable to add this group.", "Risk_Management", "For access to the ORP WTS.", "Does not require additional AD permissions.", "WTS_AMS", "Normally, requests to add users to project AMS should go directly to SRASIAMAUTH_SUSY.", "If you receive any ticket requesting to add a user to project AMS, simply close the ticket advising the user to raise a ticket in this category.", "If the ticket comes back saying that the access is not working, please add the WTS_AMS firewall group to the user.", "All those tickets come from the AMS team, so no additional approval is needed.", "3RUserAG", "For access to 4R AG WTS (internal).", "Also requires AD permissions.", "3RUserA1S", "For access to 4R ByD Consultant WTS (internal).", "Also requires AD permissions.", "3RUserA1S_Dialin", "For access to select 4R systems (external).", "Permissions to individual 4R systems must still be added."], "content": "SecurID authentication grants a user access through a firewall, either the DMZ-facing firewall for external connections or internal firewalls for access to restricted systems (e.g., HR). Here are the most common firewall permissions: Dial-in Most commonly used access group for standard office WTS (SAP Desktop). Only needed for C users. D and I users have this access assigned automatically when the token is activated (\"SDIuser\"). Must also have the group \"PsapgateX\" (assigned automatically when activated). AHR-WTS For access to the HR system. Also requires the group \"AHRUser\" as well as AD permissions. For AD and SecurID permissions – SRASIAMAUTH_HR (ITSC Infra are unable to add this firewall group). ISP-Admin For access to BSS WTS/Service Center B. ITSD are unable to add this group. Risk_Management For access to the ORP WTS. Does not require additional AD permissions. WTS_AMS Normally, requests to add users to project AMS should go directly to SRASIAMAUTH_SUSY. If you receive any ticket requesting to add a user to project AMS, simply close the ticket advising the user to raise a ticket in this category. If the ticket comes back saying that the access is not working, please add the WTS_AMS firewall group to the user. All those tickets come from the AMS team, so no additional approval is needed. 3RUserAG For access to 4R AG WTS (internal). Also requires AD permissions. 3RUserA1S For access to 4R ByD Consultant WTS (internal). Also requires AD permissions. 3RUserA1S_Dialin For access to select 4R systems (external). Permissions to individual 4R systems must still be added.", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 274}, {"topic": "5. RSA SecurID Tokens", "section": "5.4 How to obtain/return a token", "paragraphs": ["All needed information can be found in IKB0012885 RSA token request/return or refer to RSA token FAQ"], "content": "All needed information can be found in IKB0012885 RSA token request/return or refer to RSA token FAQ", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 275}, {"topic": "5. RSA SecurID Tokens", "section": "5.5 How to activate a token / token deactivation", "paragraphs": ["Administration of SecurID tokens is performed via the Netsec site.", "Token Activation Process", "There are two parts to a token activation: 1) Registration and 2) Activation itself.", "1. Registration:", "Go to 'register users and SecurID token serial numbers'.", "Change the 'SecurID card' dropdown box to 'handed out', and the 'mail format to be sent' box to 'none'.", "Enter the user ID and token serial number, then click 'submit'.", "This registers the user ID to the token.", "2. Activation:", "Click 'go to activation page'.", "All registered users awaiting activation are listed here. Search for the user you are activating using ctrl+F.", "Note that the user name next to the ID may be different; do not worry about this as the columns in this table are sorted separately. Ensure you click on the USERID to continue.", "Activation Page Differences:", "D/I Users:", "D/I users automatically get full access to VPN and Office WTS via the firewall group \"SDIUser\", which is automatically assigned when a D/I user token is activated.", "At this stage, you will just have an 'activate now' button.", "C Users:", "C users must have their access groups defined, and also a 'SAP Responsible' employee nominated.", "Select the group(s) that the requestor has selected in their request, enter the responsible's ID, and hit 'activate now'. The token is now active and the user must set a PIN.", "RSA Token Deactivation:", "Any I/D user can request RSA token deactivation for any user (I/D/C).", "C users can request token deactivation for their own token only.", "On Netsec, select 'Delete an activated user (from the ACE server database)' to delete an active user, enter the User ID and serial number, and hit submit.", "No verification step is required for deactivation"], "content": "Administration of SecurID tokens is performed via the Netsec site. Token Activation Process There are two parts to a token activation: 1) Registration and 2) Activation itself. 1. Registration: Go to 'register users and SecurID token serial numbers'. Change the 'SecurID card' dropdown box to 'handed out', and the 'mail format to be sent' box to 'none'. Enter the user ID and token serial number, then click 'submit'. This registers the user ID to the token. 2. Activation: Click 'go to activation page'. All registered users awaiting activation are listed here. Search for the user you are activating using ctrl+F. Note that the user name next to the ID may be different; do not worry about this as the columns in this table are sorted separately. Ensure you click on the USERID to continue. Activation Page Differences: D/I Users: D/I users automatically get full access to VPN and Office WTS via the firewall group \"SDIUser\", which is automatically assigned when a D/I user token is activated. At this stage, you will just have an 'activate now' button. C Users: C users must have their access groups defined, and also a 'SAP Responsible' employee nominated. Select the group(s) that the requestor has selected in their request, enter the responsible's ID, and hit 'activate now'. The token is now active and the user must set a PIN. RSA Token Deactivation: Any I/D user can request RSA token deactivation for any user (I/D/C). C users can request token deactivation for their own token only. On Netsec, select 'Delete an activated user (from the ACE server database)' to delete an active user, enter the User ID and serial number, and hit submit. No verification step is required for deactivation", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 276}, {"topic": "5. RSA SecurID Tokens", "section": "5.6 Deploy a Softoken", "paragraphs": ["Soft tokens are not activated by SAP IT, but deployed by the users themselves. It is a self-service.", "First of all check with the user if the mobile device is a personal one, or provided by SAP (SAP equipment). If the mobile device is personal, inform the user that it is not allowed to deploy the soft token on non-SAP equipment unless it is an Android BYOD device enrolled in InTune.", "To deploy a soft token:", "Users must order the soft token HERE", "They will receive a confirmation email with links to deployment instructions.", "Deployment instructions can be found in IKB0013426 RSA token - All about SecurID SoftTokens (Mobile App)", "Note: The process for C users is different if they do not have an assigned token at the moment. Please check Firewall Access Groups."], "content": "Soft tokens are not activated by SAP IT, but deployed by the users themselves. It is a self-service. First of all check with the user if the mobile device is a personal one, or provided by SAP (SAP equipment). If the mobile device is personal, inform the user that it is not allowed to deploy the soft token on non-SAP equipment unless it is an Android BYOD device enrolled in InTune. To deploy a soft token: Users must order the soft token HERE They will receive a confirmation email with links to deployment instructions. Deployment instructions can be found in IKB0013426 RSA token - All about SecurID SoftTokens (Mobile App) Note: The process for C users is different if they do not have an assigned token at the moment. Please check Firewall Access Groups.", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 277}, {"topic": "5. RSA SecurID Tokens", "section": "5.7 Set a PIN", "paragraphs": ["Important Notice: Setting Your Token PIN", "Users must set a PIN to their tokens themselves, we cannot do this for them.", "If they are on the SAP network (i.e. in an SAP office, already connected via VPN or WTS, or using Global Protect), this can be done using any of the internal links below:", "https://netsec.wdf.sap.corp/sdi_selfservice/sdi_change_pin.cgi", "https://secureidadm.wdf.sap.corp/set_pin.html", "If the user is accessing externally (i.e. not on the SAP network):", "Go to https://access.sap.com -> EMEA -> Office Project WTS and VDI", "Enter user ID and password as normal", "For the passcode, just enter the code currently displayed on the token's screen without entering any PIN (or if a soft-token user, just hit \">\" in the app without entering any PIN to display the code)", "If there is no PIN already set for the user, the system will recognize this and prompt the user to set one", "The new PIN must be between 4 and 8 digits, and cannot start with \"0\"", "Once the PIN is set, login again as normal using the new PIN to generate a passcode"], "content": "Important Notice: Setting Your Token PIN Users must set a PIN to their tokens themselves, we cannot do this for them. If they are on the SAP network (i.e. in an SAP office, already connected via VPN or WTS, or using Global Protect), this can be done using any of the internal links below: https://netsec.wdf.sap.corp/sdi_selfservice/sdi_change_pin.cgi https://secureidadm.wdf.sap.corp/set_pin.html If the user is accessing externally (i.e. not on the SAP network): Go to https://access.sap.com -> EMEA -> Office Project WTS and VDI Enter user ID and password as normal For the passcode, just enter the code currently displayed on the token's screen without entering any PIN (or if a soft-token user, just hit \">\" in the app without entering any PIN to display the code) If there is no PIN already set for the user, the system will recognize this and prompt the user to set one The new PIN must be between 4 and 8 digits, and cannot start with \"0\" Once the PIN is set, login again as normal using the new PIN to generate a passcode", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 278}, {"topic": "5. RSA SecurID Tokens", "section": "5.8 Reset a PIN - Check a user's passcode", "paragraphs": ["To reset a PIN, follow these steps:", "1Go to the Netsec administration site: https://netsec.wdf.sap.corp/SecurID/.", "Select \"Clear/Remove PIN from user's SecurID card\".", "Enter the user ID and SecurID serial number. If you do not know the serial number, use the 'display SecurID user or card info' link first, enter the user ID, and retrieve the card details.", "The PIN will now be reset, and the user will need to create a new one before the card can be used.", "Check User's Passcode:", "To check a user's passcode, follow these steps:", "Go to the Netsec administration site: https://netsec.wdf.sap.corp/SecurID/.", "Select \"Check User's passcode\".", "Ask the user to generate a code and read it out to you.", "Fill in the user ID and the passcode field, then submit the form.", "A result will come back as either 'success' or 'fail'."], "content": "To reset a PIN, follow these steps: 1Go to the Netsec administration site: https://netsec.wdf.sap.corp/SecurID/. Select \"Clear/Remove PIN from user's SecurID card\". Enter the user ID and SecurID serial number. If you do not know the serial number, use the 'display SecurID user or card info' link first, enter the user ID, and retrieve the card details. The PIN will now be reset, and the user will need to create a new one before the card can be used. Check User's Passcode: To check a user's passcode, follow these steps: Go to the Netsec administration site: https://netsec.wdf.sap.corp/SecurID/. Select \"Check User's passcode\". Ask the user to generate a code and read it out to you. Fill in the user ID and the passcode field, then submit the form. A result will come back as either 'success' or 'fail'.", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 279}, {"topic": "5. RSA SecurID Tokens", "section": "5.9 Give emergency access", "paragraphs": ["Emergency Access:", "Emergency access can be granted to any user who requests it via phone or ticket. However, if there is no PIN set to the card, you MUST verify the user first.", "Granting Emergency Access:", "Emergency access (EA) can be given to users who do not have their token with them for any reason. We can supply two (2) codes that can only be used to log in once each and are valid for 24 hours.", "Using the Emergency Code:", "To use the code, the user must enter their PIN into the passcode field, followed by one of the codes. For example, if the user's PIN is 1234 and the emergency code is 987654, the passcode the user must use will be 1234987654.", "Returning to Normal Access:", "A user must contact us to use the card 'normally' again after emergency access has been set. It needs to be removed. Once EA has been removed, the user's PIN will remain set.", "Steps to Grant Emergency Access:", "From the Netsec administration site: https://netsec.wdf.sap.corp/SecurID/", "Select \"Give emergency access to a user\"", "Enter the reason for the request, user ID, and card serial number (if you do not know the serial, go to \"display securid user or card info\" from the main Netsec menu)"], "content": "Emergency Access: Emergency access can be granted to any user who requests it via phone or ticket. However, if there is no PIN set to the card, you MUST verify the user first. Granting Emergency Access: Emergency access (EA) can be given to users who do not have their token with them for any reason. We can supply two (2) codes that can only be used to log in once each and are valid for 24 hours. Using the Emergency Code: To use the code, the user must enter their PIN into the passcode field, followed by one of the codes. For example, if the user's PIN is 1234 and the emergency code is 987654, the passcode the user must use will be 1234987654. Returning to Normal Access: A user must contact us to use the card 'normally' again after emergency access has been set. It needs to be removed. Once EA has been removed, the user's PIN will remain set. Steps to Grant Emergency Access: From the Netsec administration site: https://netsec.wdf.sap.corp/SecurID/ Select \"Give emergency access to a user\" Enter the reason for the request, user ID, and card serial number (if you do not know the serial, go to \"display securid user or card info\" from the main Netsec menu)", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 280}, {"topic": "5. RSA SecurID Tokens", "section": "5.10 Processing tickets from the SecurID bot", "paragraphs": ["When a request is made for a card activation through the activation form, this is submitted to an application to activate the card. If the activation is successful, an incident ticket will be created by the application informing the user that the card is activated, and how to set a PIN. If the activation fails, an incident ticket is created with the failure reason and must be processed manually by IT CSD.", "Occasionally an activation fails:", "If the token is already activated to another user", "If the requestor does not have authorization to activate the token (this is the most common failure reason)", "If the permissions groups selected are invalid or not selected at all", "Token S/N invalid", "Token expired", "If the token is already activated to another user", "The auto-activation will fail if the token is already assigned. Check the current assignment of the token. If the ‘last logon’ is more than 1 month ago, if it was never used, or if the user it is assigned to is disabled, go ahead and re-assign it. If it is less than 1 month ago, reply to the user and ask if the serial number is correct. If the user confirms the serial number is correct, proceed with activating the RSA token. If the user indicates the serial number is incorrect, ask them to provide the correct serial number and then proceed with activation.", "If the requestor does not have authorization to activate the token", "This happens when:", "C user tries to request a new activation:", "Check if they are an office assistant, a member of Local IT, or on the exceptions list.", "If so, activate the card.", "If not, reply to the user asking them to have the activation form submitted by a D/I user (doesn't need to be their CC manager): https://ifp.bss.net.sap/ITFORM/ZITFORM.HTM?formname=SA-SECUR_EXTERNALS", "D/I user tries to activate a card on behalf of another D/I user:", "Check if they are the user's manager, an office assistant, a member of Local IT, or on the exceptions list.", "If so, activate the card.", "If not, reply to the user asking them to get the user themselves, or their cost center manager, to complete the SecurID Token Activation (new / replaced) form.", "Token S/N invalid", "Check this by trying to activate the token - if the number is invalid, an error will return \"unknown token serial number\". Reply to the user asking them to check the S/N and re-submit the activation form.", "Token expired", "Check this by trying to activate the card – if it has expired, an error will return \"cannot activate expired token\". Double-check with the user to check the expiration date on the back side of the token and ask them to resubmit the form with a valid token's S/N.", "You will find more SecurID token with IKB0012890", "You will find more RSA Token FAQ with IKB0012886 and IKB0012888"], "content": "When a request is made for a card activation through the activation form, this is submitted to an application to activate the card. If the activation is successful, an incident ticket will be created by the application informing the user that the card is activated, and how to set a PIN. If the activation fails, an incident ticket is created with the failure reason and must be processed manually by IT CSD. Occasionally an activation fails: If the token is already activated to another user If the requestor does not have authorization to activate the token (this is the most common failure reason) If the permissions groups selected are invalid or not selected at all Token S/N invalid Token expired If the token is already activated to another user The auto-activation will fail if the token is already assigned. Check the current assignment of the token. If the ‘last logon’ is more than 1 month ago, if it was never used, or if the user it is assigned to is disabled, go ahead and re-assign it. If it is less than 1 month ago, reply to the user and ask if the serial number is correct. If the user confirms the serial number is correct, proceed with activating the RSA token. If the user indicates the serial number is incorrect, ask them to provide the correct serial number and then proceed with activation. If the requestor does not have authorization to activate the token This happens when: C user tries to request a new activation: Check if they are an office assistant, a member of Local IT, or on the exceptions list. If so, activate the card. If not, reply to the user asking them to have the activation form submitted by a D/I user (doesn't need to be their CC manager): https://ifp.bss.net.sap/ITFORM/ZITFORM.HTM?formname=SA-SECUR_EXTERNALS D/I user tries to activate a card on behalf of another D/I user: Check if they are the user's manager, an office assistant, a member of Local IT, or on the exceptions list. If so, activate the card. If not, reply to the user asking them to get the user themselves, or their cost center manager, to complete the SecurID Token Activation (new / replaced) form. Token S/N invalid Check this by trying to activate the token - if the number is invalid, an error will return \"unknown token serial number\". Reply to the user asking them to check the S/N and re-submit the activation form. Token expired Check this by trying to activate the card – if it has expired, an error will return \"cannot activate expired token\". Double-check with the user to check the expiration date on the back side of the token and ask them to resubmit the form with a valid token's S/N. You will find more SecurID token with IKB0012890 You will find more RSA Token FAQ with IKB0012886 and IKB0012888", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 281}, {"topic": "6. Windows 11 - Security patching with WUfB (Windows Update for Business)", "section": "6.1 Overview", "paragraphs": ["Windows Update for Business or WUfB is a service that manages all monthly updates (Quality updates, Security Updates, etc.), OS updates (Feature updates) and other Microsoft product updates. The updates are being pulled directly from Microsoft, SAP IT creates the configuration and decides when and how those updates should become visible and installed. WUfB interacts with the service Windows Update on your computer. You can open Windows Updates by just searching for the application or by navigating through the Windows settings there.", "The following update types are offered in Windows Update:", "Quality updates are OS security updates released on the 2nd Tuesday each month", "Feature Updates are OS upgrades such as Windows 11 upgrades", "Microsoft product updates such as Visual Studio, Microsoft Office that older than O365, Microsoft Malicious Software Removal Tools, definitions update, .NET updates", "Non-Microsoft Software updates such as Notepad++", "Windows Update is implemented on all Windows 11 clients:", "Autopilot provisioned devices", "VDIs", "WUfB does not cover:", "Windows Servers", "Linux devices", "Mac devices", "Mobile devices (Android, IOS)", "Windows Update is a standard Microsoft OS service, which is available on all Windows 11 devices to manage the update process. You will see the monthly updates; feature update and other Microsoft updates appear in your Windows Update Settings."], "content": "Windows Update for Business or WUfB is a service that manages all monthly updates (Quality updates, Security Updates, etc.), OS updates (Feature updates) and other Microsoft product updates. The updates are being pulled directly from Microsoft, SAP IT creates the configuration and decides when and how those updates should become visible and installed. WUfB interacts with the service Windows Update on your computer. You can open Windows Updates by just searching for the application or by navigating through the Windows settings there. The following update types are offered in Windows Update: Quality updates are OS security updates released on the 2nd Tuesday each month Feature Updates are OS upgrades such as Windows 11 upgrades Microsoft product updates such as Visual Studio, Microsoft Office that older than O365, Microsoft Malicious Software Removal Tools, definitions update, .NET updates Non-Microsoft Software updates such as Notepad++ Windows Update is implemented on all Windows 11 clients: Autopilot provisioned devices VDIs WUfB does not cover: Windows Servers Linux devices Mac devices Mobile devices (Android, IOS) Windows Update is a standard Microsoft OS service, which is available on all Windows 11 devices to manage the update process. You will see the monthly updates; feature update and other Microsoft updates appear in your Windows Update Settings.", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 282}, {"topic": "6. Windows 11 - Security patching with WUfB (Windows Update for Business)", "section": "6.2 How to check for updates manually in Windows Update", "paragraphs": ["You can manually check for Windows Updates by clicking on 'Check for updates'. By doing so, all patches that are ready for you will be verified and installed.", "Click on the Start menu at the bottom left corner of your screen.", "Click on the Settings icon (cog). Alternatively, you can open the Settings window by pressing the (Win + I) hotkeys.", "Scroll down the list and at the bottom of the Settings window, click on ‘Update & Security’. This is the window where you can manually check for Windows Updates and install them.", "Click on the <Check for updates> button"], "content": "You can manually check for Windows Updates by clicking on 'Check for updates'. By doing so, all patches that are ready for you will be verified and installed. Click on the Start menu at the bottom left corner of your screen. Click on the Settings icon (cog). Alternatively, you can open the Settings window by pressing the (Win + I) hotkeys. Scroll down the list and at the bottom of the Settings window, click on ‘Update & Security’. This is the window where you can manually check for Windows Updates and install them. Click on the <Check for updates> button", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 283}, {"topic": "6. Windows 11 - Security patching with WUfB (Windows Update for Business)", "section": "6.3 Schedules and Deadlines", "paragraphs": ["Installation start time: 7 days after the release of the updates by Microsoft, they will be downloaded to your computer and installed silently in the background.", "Deadline: There is no deadline for the installation itself as it happens in the background, only for the reboot. You will have again 7 days to perform the reboot yourself. If you haven’t rebooted your device within those seven days, the reboot count down will start (see below).", "Offline grace period: If you were offline for longer and the deadline for the reboot has passed, you will be granted another two days, so your device will not restart immediately upon your return. Once the installation has finished, the reboot will be in 2 days.", "Reboot notification: You’ll receive a toast notification 8 hours before the automated reboot starts.", "Reboot final approval: 60 minutes before the enforced reboot might happen, you will get a very prominent notification to remind you to close your work in time."], "content": "Installation start time: 7 days after the release of the updates by Microsoft, they will be downloaded to your computer and installed silently in the background. Deadline: There is no deadline for the installation itself as it happens in the background, only for the reboot. You will have again 7 days to perform the reboot yourself. If you haven’t rebooted your device within those seven days, the reboot count down will start (see below). Offline grace period: If you were offline for longer and the deadline for the reboot has passed, you will be granted another two days, so your device will not restart immediately upon your return. Once the installation has finished, the reboot will be in 2 days. Reboot notification: You’ll receive a toast notification 8 hours before the automated reboot starts. Reboot final approval: 60 minutes before the enforced reboot might happen, you will get a very prominent notification to remind you to close your work in time.", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 284}, {"topic": "6. Windows 11 - Security patching with WUfB (Windows Update for Business)", "section": "6.4 How to Fix Windows Update Issues", "paragraphs": ["1. Check Available Disk Space", "Ensure at least 20 GB of free disk space is available to download and install updates. Remove unnecessary files or move data to OneDrive to free up local storage.", "2. Run Windows Update Troubleshooter", "To launch the Windows Update Troubleshooter, follow these steps:", "Press Win + R", "Type the following command and press Enter: msdt.exe /id WindowsUpdateDiagnostic", "Click Advanced", "Ensure Apply repairs automatically is selected", "Click Next and allow the troubleshooter to run", "3. Restart After Troubleshooting", "Once the troubleshooter completes, restart your device to apply any fixes.", "4. Recheck Windows Update", "Go to Settings > Windows Update, then select Check for updates to verify whether any additional updates are pending.", "For more information, refer to Security patching with WUfB KB0013301 & Missing updates in WUfB KB0011671"], "content": "1. Check Available Disk Space Ensure at least 20 GB of free disk space is available to download and install updates. Remove unnecessary files or move data to OneDrive to free up local storage. 2. Run Windows Update Troubleshooter To launch the Windows Update Troubleshooter, follow these steps: Press Win + R Type the following command and press Enter: msdt.exe /id WindowsUpdateDiagnostic Click Advanced Ensure Apply repairs automatically is selected Click Next and allow the troubleshooter to run 3. Restart After Troubleshooting Once the troubleshooter completes, restart your device to apply any fixes. 4. Recheck Windows Update Go to Settings > Windows Update, then select Check for updates to verify whether any additional updates are pending. For more information, refer to Security patching with WUfB KB0013301 & Missing updates in WUfB KB0011671", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 285}, {"topic": "7. Sensitivity Labels and Sub-Labels", "section": "7.1 Sensitivity Labels", "paragraphs": ["Sensitivity Labels are based on the SAP Global Information Classification & Handling Standard​​​​​​​ with a few additional labels, which were added to meet the requirements of all SAP's Lines of Business"], "content": "Sensitivity Labels are based on the SAP Global Information Classification & Handling Standard​​​​​​​ with a few additional labels, which were added to meet the requirements of all SAP's Lines of Business", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 286}, {"topic": "7. Sensitivity Labels and Sub-Labels", "section": "7.2 Internal Sub-Labels", "paragraphs": ["A few notes on the \"Sensitivity\" labels and sub-labels", "When a \"Sensitivity\" label is selected for a document or email, under the covers, the label is stored in metadata so that applications can read the label without accessing the document itself.", "Non-Business was added so employees can separate their SAP business data from their private information if required. This label does nothing more than allow a non-business category, and data will not be processed any differently for this label.", "Internal has a few sub-labels, and the label \"Internal\" is not directly selectable. The Internal sub-labels were developed in collaboration with our LOB's who have specific requirements when sharing SAP business data.", "The table above shows the label names on the left, with the associated \"ToolTip\", Footer (if it exists), and any encryption that the label may cause (note the \"Internal | SAP Only\" label and Confidential (Encrypted) causes encryption). btw, a tooltip is the text that is shown when hovering over the label with your mouse on a Windows or Mac computer.", "Please note only document owner can remove/change the encrypted documents and email.", "Please read Security - Unified Labeling, Label and Protect KB0013574 about applying sensitivity levels to your Office files"], "content": "A few notes on the \"Sensitivity\" labels and sub-labels When a \"Sensitivity\" label is selected for a document or email, under the covers, the label is stored in metadata so that applications can read the label without accessing the document itself. Non-Business was added so employees can separate their SAP business data from their private information if required. This label does nothing more than allow a non-business category, and data will not be processed any differently for this label. Internal has a few sub-labels, and the label \"Internal\" is not directly selectable. The Internal sub-labels were developed in collaboration with our LOB's who have specific requirements when sharing SAP business data. The table above shows the label names on the left, with the associated \"ToolTip\", Footer (if it exists), and any encryption that the label may cause (note the \"Internal | SAP Only\" label and Confidential (Encrypted) causes encryption). btw, a tooltip is the text that is shown when hovering over the label with your mouse on a Windows or Mac computer. Please note only document owner can remove/change the encrypted documents and email. Please read Security - Unified Labeling, Label and Protect KB0013574 about applying sensitivity levels to your Office files", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 287}, {"topic": "7. Sensitivity Labels and Sub-Labels", "section": "7.3 Default/Mandatory Label", "paragraphs": ["Overview", "All new M365 documents will get a default Sensitivity Label at Save", "This means any time you open a new Word Document/Excel Spreadsheet/PowerPoint Presentation, it will be labeled “Internal | SAP Only (No Footer)” by default", "The default Sensitivity Label will not apply to all unopened files stored in OneDrive or SharePoint, as it’s only applied to existing content if an unlabeled file is opened for editing.", "You can change this label to a more fitting Sensitivity Label like “Non-Business” which is to be used for Personal Information, or “Public”, or “Confidential” when the document contains Sensitive SAP Business data", "“Internal | SAP Only (No Footer)” will be the default label for all new M365 data, and will replace the label “Internal |SAP Only (encrypted)”. The new default label will not encrypt M365 data", "The new default label is only for three M365 apps; Word, PPT, and Excel. Outlook emails will not get a default label", "Default labels will occur no matter how you access M365 content, whether it is Windows, macOS, iOS, Android, or web browser. The label options are available on all clients where M365 apps are accessible", "The previously existing “Internal | SAP Only (Encrypted)” label will be removed from view in SAP Employee’s Sensitivity Labels. All existing documents with this label will remain encrypted. If you want to update to the new label to decrypt the document, you can open the document and manually change the label if you have the appropriate permissions", "Mandatory label", "If you have the appropriate editing permissions on a document, you can select a different label, but you cannot unselect a label and save the document without a label", "A mandatory label will be required at Save for new data being created in Word, PPT, and Excel. Outlook emails will not have a mandatory label", "Please read KB0981106 Default/Mandatory Label", "Note: All old internal Lable will change to Internal Old, non business no change"], "content": "Overview All new M365 documents will get a default Sensitivity Label at Save This means any time you open a new Word Document/Excel Spreadsheet/PowerPoint Presentation, it will be labeled “Internal | SAP Only (No Footer)” by default The default Sensitivity Label will not apply to all unopened files stored in OneDrive or SharePoint, as it’s only applied to existing content if an unlabeled file is opened for editing. You can change this label to a more fitting Sensitivity Label like “Non-Business” which is to be used for Personal Information, or “Public”, or “Confidential” when the document contains Sensitive SAP Business data “Internal | SAP Only (No Footer)” will be the default label for all new M365 data, and will replace the label “Internal |SAP Only (encrypted)”. The new default label will not encrypt M365 data The new default label is only for three M365 apps; Word, PPT, and Excel. Outlook emails will not get a default label Default labels will occur no matter how you access M365 content, whether it is Windows, macOS, iOS, Android, or web browser. The label options are available on all clients where M365 apps are accessible The previously existing “Internal | SAP Only (Encrypted)” label will be removed from view in SAP Employee’s Sensitivity Labels. All existing documents with this label will remain encrypted. If you want to update to the new label to decrypt the document, you can open the document and manually change the label if you have the appropriate permissions Mandatory label If you have the appropriate editing permissions on a document, you can select a different label, but you cannot unselect a label and save the document without a label A mandatory label will be required at Save for new data being created in Word, PPT, and Excel. Outlook emails will not have a mandatory label Please read KB0981106 Default/Mandatory Label Note: All old internal Lable will change to Internal Old, non business no change", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 288}, {"topic": "7. Sensitivity Labels and Sub-Labels", "section": "7.4 Add a sensitivity label to SharePoint Site and document library", "paragraphs": ["Overview", "How to update New Sensitivity Labels for SharePoint Site", "Make sure you have Site Collection Administrator role, if not please follow this article to request one.", "Click Tool Menu, then Site Information.", "Select the desired sensitivity label and click Save.", "The new label will appear below the site name.", "How to configure a default sensitivity label for a SharePoint document library", "For an existing document library:", "In SharePoint, navigate to the document library > Settings > Library settings.", "From the Library settings flyout pane, select Default sensitivity labels, and then select a label from the drop-down box. For example:", "When SharePoint is enabled for sensitivity labels, you can configure a default label for document libraries. Then, any new files uploaded to that library, or existing files edited in the library will have that label applied if they don't already have a sensitivity label, or they have a sensitivity label but with lower priority.", "A default label offers a baseline level of protection and a form of automatic labeling without content inspection. To help you distinguish between this feature's default label with the default label in label policies:", "Default sensitivity label for a document library: Location-based labeling, applicable only for SharePoint. Overrides a lower-priority label unless manually applied.", "Default sensitivity label from a policy: Always applicable for all locations. Never overrides an existing label.", "When you use Office for the web to create or edit a file, the default sensitivity label for a document library can be applied without delays. However, labeling is not immediate if you upload a file or create it using Microsoft 365 Apps on Windows, macOS, iOS or Android, and then save to SharePoint:", "File upload: it can take a few minutes for the label to be applied.", "Microsoft 365 Apps: the label is applied after the app is closed.", "For more information, you may refer to Add a sensitivity label to SharePoint document library and New Sensitivity Labels for SharePoint document library and SharePoint Site"], "content": "Overview How to update New Sensitivity Labels for SharePoint Site Make sure you have Site Collection Administrator role, if not please follow this article to request one. Click Tool Menu, then Site Information. Select the desired sensitivity label and click Save. The new label will appear below the site name. How to configure a default sensitivity label for a SharePoint document library For an existing document library: In SharePoint, navigate to the document library > Settings > Library settings. From the Library settings flyout pane, select Default sensitivity labels, and then select a label from the drop-down box. For example: When SharePoint is enabled for sensitivity labels, you can configure a default label for document libraries. Then, any new files uploaded to that library, or existing files edited in the library will have that label applied if they don't already have a sensitivity label, or they have a sensitivity label but with lower priority. A default label offers a baseline level of protection and a form of automatic labeling without content inspection. To help you distinguish between this feature's default label with the default label in label policies: Default sensitivity label for a document library: Location-based labeling, applicable only for SharePoint. Overrides a lower-priority label unless manually applied. Default sensitivity label from a policy: Always applicable for all locations. Never overrides an existing label. When you use Office for the web to create or edit a file, the default sensitivity label for a document library can be applied without delays. However, labeling is not immediate if you upload a file or create it using Microsoft 365 Apps on Windows, macOS, iOS or Android, and then save to SharePoint: File upload: it can take a few minutes for the label to be applied. Microsoft 365 Apps: the label is applied after the app is closed. For more information, you may refer to Add a sensitivity label to SharePoint document library and New Sensitivity Labels for SharePoint document library and SharePoint Site", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 289}, {"topic": "8. Windows – TempAdmin Accounts IT Guide", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["!!IMPORTANT!!!:", "This process provides IT Support capabilities in a scenario where an end-user's managed Windows device lost its binding with EntraID (former Azure Active Directory) and the SAP user's account cannot be used for logon into the system any longer or when legitimate organization outsiede IT e.g. HR, Legal etc. request access to data on the disk. These are the only approved scenarios for this tool.", "This article describes the procedure of using TempAdmin.", "Assumption: there is a support ticket for this support case – you will need this ticket number at a later stage."], "content": "!!IMPORTANT!!!: This process provides IT Support capabilities in a scenario where an end-user's managed Windows device lost its binding with EntraID (former Azure Active Directory) and the SAP user's account cannot be used for logon into the system any longer or when legitimate organization outsiede IT e.g. HR, Legal etc. request access to data on the disk. These are the only approved scenarios for this tool. This article describes the procedure of using TempAdmin. Assumption: there is a support ticket for this support case – you will need this ticket number at a later stage.", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 290}, {"topic": "8. Windows – TempAdmin Accounts IT Guide", "section": "8.1 Obtain AzureAD group membership allowing you to send remote action", "paragraphs": ["Go to https://portal.azure.com", "Go to the Privileged Identity Management (PIM) and select ‘My roles’", "Go to Groups", "Request tempAdmin group ‘WLRBAC_Nexthink_TempAdmin’ membership activation", "Make sure you have the role assigned (you can check this in ‘Active assignments’)"], "content": "Go to https://portal.azure.com Go to the Privileged Identity Management (PIM) and select ‘My roles’ Go to Groups Request tempAdmin group ‘WLRBAC_Nexthink_TempAdmin’ membership activation Make sure you have the role assigned (you can check this in ‘Active assignments’)", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 291}, {"topic": "8. Windows – TempAdmin Accounts IT Guide", "section": "8.2 Send remote action to a specific computer", "paragraphs": ["Once you complete the role request in Azure Portal you need to sign out from NexThink console/Amplify and then sign in again.", "Select the account icon on top of the menu and then select ‘Sign out’", "Then select ‘Sign in with SSO’", "Once you re-login again in the NexThink you can send remote action to create tempAdmin user", "Look up the computer for which you may need the local admin user", "Go to remote actions and run TempAdmin action", "Provide ticket number that was a base for the action and click ‘Run’", "Note: please provide only valid ticket numbers – this action is strictly monitored against potential abuse!", "Once remote action is sent to a computer and executed locally the new TempAdmin local account is created:"], "content": "Once you complete the role request in Azure Portal you need to sign out from NexThink console/Amplify and then sign in again. Select the account icon on top of the menu and then select ‘Sign out’ Then select ‘Sign in with SSO’ Once you re-login again in the NexThink you can send remote action to create tempAdmin user Look up the computer for which you may need the local admin user Go to remote actions and run TempAdmin action Provide ticket number that was a base for the action and click ‘Run’ Note: please provide only valid ticket numbers – this action is strictly monitored against potential abuse! Once remote action is sent to a computer and executed locally the new TempAdmin local account is created:", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 292}, {"topic": "8. Windows – TempAdmin Accounts IT Guide", "section": "8.3 Obtain necessary password for created admin account", "paragraphs": ["The password for local TempAdmin user can be obtained using one of the methods below:", "an email sent to the owner of the device from ‘SAP EndUser Analytics’", "via a dedicated ‘Temp Admin Executions’ investigation available for an IT support technician who has TempAdmin remote action role enabled", "Logon locally with TempAdmin account and perform local actions", "Once you confirm the user was created on a target machine (mail about Temp Admin user creation has been received by enduser) you can log in locally onto a computer using ‘.\\TempAdmin’ as a user name and the appropriate password generated for this account.", "Now you can run necessary actions to join computer back to EntraID.", "For more information, you may refer to TempAdmin Accounts IT Guide"], "content": "The password for local TempAdmin user can be obtained using one of the methods below: an email sent to the owner of the device from ‘SAP EndUser Analytics’ via a dedicated ‘Temp Admin Executions’ investigation available for an IT support technician who has TempAdmin remote action role enabled Logon locally with TempAdmin account and perform local actions Once you confirm the user was created on a target machine (mail about Temp Admin user creation has been received by enduser) you can log in locally onto a computer using ‘.\\TempAdmin’ as a user name and the appropriate password generated for this account. Now you can run necessary actions to join computer back to EntraID. For more information, you may refer to TempAdmin Accounts IT Guide", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 293}, {"topic": "9. BitLocker ---------HardDisk Encryption", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Based on SAP Policies and Security implementation, it is mandatory for all SAP IT managed hard drives to be encrypted.", "SAP uses Microsoft BitLocker technology for Windows hard drive encryption, encrypting drives with security industry standard XTS - AES 256 bit encryption.", "Bitlocker uses the capabilities of TPM 1.2 hardware to provide a transparent user experience --> user powers up and logs into Windows as normal. The key used for encryption is sealed (encrypted) by the TPM chip and will only be released to the OS loader code if the early boot files appear to be unmodified. If boot files is modified, the Bitlocker Recovery Process will kicks in and logging to the machine will not be possible without going through the process."], "content": "Based on SAP Policies and Security implementation, it is mandatory for all SAP IT managed hard drives to be encrypted. SAP uses Microsoft BitLocker technology for Windows hard drive encryption, encrypting drives with security industry standard XTS - AES 256 bit encryption. Bitlocker uses the capabilities of TPM 1.2 hardware to provide a transparent user experience --> user powers up and logs into Windows as normal. The key used for encryption is sealed (encrypted) by the TPM chip and will only be released to the OS loader code if the early boot files appear to be unmodified. If boot files is modified, the Bitlocker Recovery Process will kicks in and logging to the machine will not be possible without going through the process.", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 294}, {"topic": "9. BitLocker ---------HardDisk Encryption", "section": "9.1 How to recover from BitLocker recovery process", "paragraphs": ["Request Intune Bitlocker Recovery Admin", "How to generate Intune Bitlocker Key in Azure Portal", "BitLocker Recovery Key Self-Service by SAP managed PC", "How to retrieve BitLocker recovery key with the registered phones", "Get BitLocker key by non-SAP managed device by WTS", "How to retrieve a BitLocker recovery key for an Intune device (For CSD Remote Support Only)", "If the service owners verify that there is no key available, then the PC needs to be reimaged.", "If you are not able to get the recovery key through your BitLocker Recovery Key Admin role, please forward the ticket to \"IES CS Experts - Secure Services\" or create an IT ticket. Or, Secure Services EndUser Experience Management", "Details to provide in the ticket:", "Full recovery key IDs, not just the first few digits", "Machine hostname", "Reasons why OS started into Bitlocker recovery (should be stated on BL recovery screen)", "Why employee wasn't able to access self-service", "For more information, go to Bitlocker Hard Drive Encryption - IT CS One-Pager"], "content": "Request Intune Bitlocker Recovery Admin How to generate Intune Bitlocker Key in Azure Portal BitLocker Recovery Key Self-Service by SAP managed PC How to retrieve BitLocker recovery key with the registered phones Get BitLocker key by non-SAP managed device by WTS How to retrieve a BitLocker recovery key for an Intune device (For CSD Remote Support Only) If the service owners verify that there is no key available, then the PC needs to be reimaged. If you are not able to get the recovery key through your BitLocker Recovery Key Admin role, please forward the ticket to \"IES CS Experts - Secure Services\" or create an IT ticket. Or, Secure Services EndUser Experience Management Details to provide in the ticket: Full recovery key IDs, not just the first few digits Machine hostname Reasons why OS started into Bitlocker recovery (should be stated on BL recovery screen) Why employee wasn't able to access self-service For more information, go to Bitlocker Hard Drive Encryption - IT CS One-Pager", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 295}, {"topic": "9. BitLocker ---------HardDisk Encryption", "section": "9.2 Vulnerability management – BitLocker Encryption for VMs", "paragraphs": ["All SAP managed Windows devices must use a Trusted Platform Module (TPM) as an encryption protector and your Virtual Machine does not support vTPM technology. Unfortunately, you may be running a legacy device which cannot be switched to UEFI, which is required for vTPM and to properly encrypt your VM. If you need a virtual device which connects to SAP network resources, you must use a VM based on UEFI.", "Ensuring vTPM is Enabled", "Accessing the VM in the VM manager, encrypting the VM, and enabling vTPM, for example in VMWare:", "Enter a strong password and click Encrypt", "Note: Make a note of this password, otherwise the VM cannot be decrypted again Depending on the size of the virtual machine, the encryption process could take some time", "Checking the Hardware tab for the presence of a vTPM", "Ensure it's set to UEFI firmware with Secure Boot enabled:", "(Care needed - changing BIOS to UEFI may make it unbootable!)", "If it's not taken CSP policy and be encrypted Checking through manage-bde Open CM as admin and run: manage-bde -status c:", "If encryption is on but encrypted with different Method or Protectors, run: Manage-bde c: -off After decryption occurs, re-encryption to SAP company policy should occur automatically", "If it still does not work, please open a ticket", "For more information, you may refer to KB0013386", "You can get more information on TPM Related issues - troublshooting"], "content": "All SAP managed Windows devices must use a Trusted Platform Module (TPM) as an encryption protector and your Virtual Machine does not support vTPM technology. Unfortunately, you may be running a legacy device which cannot be switched to UEFI, which is required for vTPM and to properly encrypt your VM. If you need a virtual device which connects to SAP network resources, you must use a VM based on UEFI. Ensuring vTPM is Enabled Accessing the VM in the VM manager, encrypting the VM, and enabling vTPM, for example in VMWare: Enter a strong password and click Encrypt Note: Make a note of this password, otherwise the VM cannot be decrypted again Depending on the size of the virtual machine, the encryption process could take some time Checking the Hardware tab for the presence of a vTPM Ensure it's set to UEFI firmware with Secure Boot enabled: (Care needed - changing BIOS to UEFI may make it unbootable!) If it's not taken CSP policy and be encrypted Checking through manage-bde Open CM as admin and run: manage-bde -status c: If encryption is on but encrypted with different Method or Protectors, run: Manage-bde c: -off After decryption occurs, re-encryption to SAP company policy should occur automatically If it still does not work, please open a ticket For more information, you may refer to KB0013386 You can get more information on TPM Related issues - troublshooting", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 296}, {"topic": "10.Modern Authentication", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Modern Authentication (IT for You) introduces a completely redesigned cloud native authentication framework, safeguarding SAP against increasingly sophisticated threats and ensuring security for SAP.", "This reduces password entries as much as possible and ensures that strengthened security requirements are met, protecting SAP in an increasingly complex and challenging environment, and gets SAP ready for next-generation authentication methods such as passkeys.", "Modern Authentication leverages a new streamlined risk-based conditional access framework on Entra ID (former Azure AD) that balances convenience with the need for a strengthened security architecture, while also laying the foundation for next-generation authentication technologies such as passkeys.", "Modern authentication is not replacing multi-factor authentication (MFA) but focuses on the following strong authentication methods:", "Phone sign-in (part of the Microsoft Authenticator app)", "Windows Hello for Business (PIN or biometrics)", "FIDO2 security keys (only to be used if no other strong authentication method is available for you / can only be set up after migration, or after joining the Early Adopter program)", "Passkey in Microsoft Authenticator app (primarily for use on private devices avoiding the device registration)", "These strong authentication methods are integrating all sign-in steps in one go for convenience, while ensuring a high security level. The need of entering passwords to sign in is significantly reduced. In daily operations, entering passwords is only required for local login, e.g., on macOS or mobile devices.", "You can set up and configure all (strong and regular) MFA methods on the Microsoft Security info page (short link https://url.sap/getmfa). For an overview of (regular) multi-factor authentication (MFA), see Multi-factor Authentication.", "You can get more Morden authentication from KB Entra ID - Modern Authentication - Getting Started", "Overview of Strong Authentication Methods", "11.1 Passwordless sign-in (phone sign-in)", "Passwordless sign-in (phone sign-in) uses the Microsoft Authenticator app, built-in mobile device security, and biometrics for an integrated authentication.", "Recommended for all users with corporate or private mobile phone, including mobile phones provided by other companies.If you have a mobile phone and a tablet, it is recommended to set up passwordless sign-in on both devices.", "How to use to authenticate", "When requested to authenticate, enter or select your e-mail address, enter the two displayed digits in the Microsoft Authenticator app, and confirm with Face ID, Touch ID, or similar.", "When using for the first time, you may need to click \"Other ways to sign in\", and select \"Approve a request on my Microsoft Authenticator app\" first.", "How to set up in a nutshell", "On your corporate or private phone, open the Microsoft Authenticator app. Then, click on 'Setup passwordless sign-in requests' and follow the steps.", "If you don’t have set up the Microsoft Authenticator app, install the app, and add it as a sign-in method in your SAP MFA setup page (read more).", "Note: It is allowed to use a private or \"other company's\" phone, it just needs to be registered as part of the setup process.", "Read more - Android / iOS", "You can get more Morden authentication from KB Entra ID - MFA - How to set up passwordless sign-in (phone sign-in) on iOS or KB Entra ID - MFA - How to set up passwordless sign-in (phone sign-in) on Android", "11.2 Windows Hello for Business", "Windows Hello for Business uses a PIN or optional biometrics for an integrated authentication.", "Recommended for all Windows users. If you have a corporate phone, make sure to set up passwordless sign-in as well!", "How to use to authenticate", "When prompted, authenticate by using built-in biometrics (optional) or a device-bound PIN code.", "Make sure to always use Hello for Business to log in to your Windows PC (either PIN oder Biometrics) - if you use the domain password to log in to your Windows PC, this is not considered strong authentication, and you may receive additional authentication requests", "When using for the first time, you may need to click \"Other ways to sign in\", and select \"Face, fingerprint, PIN or security key\" first.", "How to set up in a nutshell", "On your corporate Windows device, go to Settings > Accounts > Sign-in Options.", "Set a PIN by scrolling down to PIN and clicking on the 'Add' button.", "Optionally, and if available on your device, enable biometrics, under 'Ways to sign in', e.g. fingerprint or face recognition.", "Read more on how to set up Hello for Business in Windows.", "11.3 FIDO2 security key", "A FIDO2 security key is a small external device that allows you to store multiple accounts and secure account access with a PIN code or biometrics. Note: Use certified devices only!", "Only needed if none of the options above can be used, or for special requirements.", "How to use to authenticate", "When prompted, plug in the FIDO2 security key in the USB port or, for NFC connection, hold it against the upper part of the mobile device.", "Confirm by entering the PIN code and tap the device, or use the built-in fingerprint reader.", "When using for the first time, you may need to click \"Other ways to sign in\", and select \"Face, fingerprint, PIN or security key\" first.", "How to set up in a nutshell", "Order a certified FIDO2 security key in Ariba Guided Buying (SAP internal only). Then, add it as a sign-in method through the SAP MFA setup page ('Security key'). Select USB or NFC depending on the device type and follow the steps to set a PIN code or fingerprint.", "Read more on how to add a FIDO2 security key as an authentication method.", "11.4 Passkey in Microsoft Authenticator app", "Recommended primarily for users’ private mobile phone, or mobile phones provided by other companies.", "Passkey in Microsoft Authenticator app is less convenient than passwordless sign-in, but does not require device registration, which might be preferred by some users.", "How to use to authenticate", "When requested to authenticate with the passkey, select \"iPhone, iPad, or Android device\", then open the Microsoft Authenticator app on your mobile device, tap the QR code scan button in the lower right corner, scan the displayed QR code, and confirm with Face ID, Touch ID, or similar.", "When using for the first time, you may need to click \"Other ways to sign in\", and select \"Face, fingerprint, PIN or security key\" first.", "How to set up in a nutshell", "On your corporate or private phone, open the Microsoft Authenticator app. Then, click on 'Create a passkey' and follow the steps.", "If you don’t have set up the Microsoft Authenticator app, install the app, and add it as a sign-in method in your SAP MFA setup page (read more).", "Note: It is allowed to use a private or \"other company's\" phone to store the Passkey.", "Read more on how to set up Passkeys with Microsoft Authenticator app"], "content": "Modern Authentication (IT for You) introduces a completely redesigned cloud native authentication framework, safeguarding SAP against increasingly sophisticated threats and ensuring security for SAP. This reduces password entries as much as possible and ensures that strengthened security requirements are met, protecting SAP in an increasingly complex and challenging environment, and gets SAP ready for next-generation authentication methods such as passkeys. Modern Authentication leverages a new streamlined risk-based conditional access framework on Entra ID (former Azure AD) that balances convenience with the need for a strengthened security architecture, while also laying the foundation for next-generation authentication technologies such as passkeys. Modern authentication is not replacing multi-factor authentication (MFA) but focuses on the following strong authentication methods: Phone sign-in (part of the Microsoft Authenticator app) Windows Hello for Business (PIN or biometrics) FIDO2 security keys (only to be used if no other strong authentication method is available for you / can only be set up after migration, or after joining the Early Adopter program) Passkey in Microsoft Authenticator app (primarily for use on private devices avoiding the device registration) These strong authentication methods are integrating all sign-in steps in one go for convenience, while ensuring a high security level. The need of entering passwords to sign in is significantly reduced. In daily operations, entering passwords is only required for local login, e.g., on macOS or mobile devices. You can set up and configure all (strong and regular) MFA methods on the Microsoft Security info page (short link https://url.sap/getmfa). For an overview of (regular) multi-factor authentication (MFA), see Multi-factor Authentication. You can get more Morden authentication from KB Entra ID - Modern Authentication - Getting Started Overview of Strong Authentication Methods 11.1 Passwordless sign-in (phone sign-in) Passwordless sign-in (phone sign-in) uses the Microsoft Authenticator app, built-in mobile device security, and biometrics for an integrated authentication. Recommended for all users with corporate or private mobile phone, including mobile phones provided by other companies.If you have a mobile phone and a tablet, it is recommended to set up passwordless sign-in on both devices. How to use to authenticate When requested to authenticate, enter or select your e-mail address, enter the two displayed digits in the Microsoft Authenticator app, and confirm with Face ID, Touch ID, or similar. When using for the first time, you may need to click \"Other ways to sign in\", and select \"Approve a request on my Microsoft Authenticator app\" first. How to set up in a nutshell On your corporate or private phone, open the Microsoft Authenticator app. Then, click on 'Setup passwordless sign-in requests' and follow the steps. If you don’t have set up the Microsoft Authenticator app, install the app, and add it as a sign-in method in your SAP MFA setup page (read more). Note: It is allowed to use a private or \"other company's\" phone, it just needs to be registered as part of the setup process. Read more - Android / iOS You can get more Morden authentication from KB Entra ID - MFA - How to set up passwordless sign-in (phone sign-in) on iOS or KB Entra ID - MFA - How to set up passwordless sign-in (phone sign-in) on Android 11.2 Windows Hello for Business Windows Hello for Business uses a PIN or optional biometrics for an integrated authentication. Recommended for all Windows users. If you have a corporate phone, make sure to set up passwordless sign-in as well! How to use to authenticate When prompted, authenticate by using built-in biometrics (optional) or a device-bound PIN code. Make sure to always use Hello for Business to log in to your Windows PC (either PIN oder Biometrics) - if you use the domain password to log in to your Windows PC, this is not considered strong authentication, and you may receive additional authentication requests When using for the first time, you may need to click \"Other ways to sign in\", and select \"Face, fingerprint, PIN or security key\" first. How to set up in a nutshell On your corporate Windows device, go to Settings > Accounts > Sign-in Options. Set a PIN by scrolling down to PIN and clicking on the 'Add' button. Optionally, and if available on your device, enable biometrics, under 'Ways to sign in', e.g. fingerprint or face recognition. Read more on how to set up Hello for Business in Windows. 11.3 FIDO2 security key A FIDO2 security key is a small external device that allows you to store multiple accounts and secure account access with a PIN code or biometrics. Note: Use certified devices only! Only needed if none of the options above can be used, or for special requirements. How to use to authenticate When prompted, plug in the FIDO2 security key in the USB port or, for NFC connection, hold it against the upper part of the mobile device. Confirm by entering the PIN code and tap the device, or use the built-in fingerprint reader. When using for the first time, you may need to click \"Other ways to sign in\", and select \"Face, fingerprint, PIN or security key\" first. How to set up in a nutshell Order a certified FIDO2 security key in Ariba Guided Buying (SAP internal only). Then, add it as a sign-in method through the SAP MFA setup page ('Security key'). Select USB or NFC depending on the device type and follow the steps to set a PIN code or fingerprint. Read more on how to add a FIDO2 security key as an authentication method. 11.4 Passkey in Microsoft Authenticator app Recommended primarily for users’ private mobile phone, or mobile phones provided by other companies. Passkey in Microsoft Authenticator app is less convenient than passwordless sign-in, but does not require device registration, which might be preferred by some users. How to use to authenticate When requested to authenticate with the passkey, select \"iPhone, iPad, or Android device\", then open the Microsoft Authenticator app on your mobile device, tap the QR code scan button in the lower right corner, scan the displayed QR code, and confirm with Face ID, Touch ID, or similar. When using for the first time, you may need to click \"Other ways to sign in\", and select \"Face, fingerprint, PIN or security key\" first. How to set up in a nutshell On your corporate or private phone, open the Microsoft Authenticator app. Then, click on 'Create a passkey' and follow the steps. If you don’t have set up the Microsoft Authenticator app, install the app, and add it as a sign-in method in your SAP MFA setup page (read more). Note: It is allowed to use a private or \"other company's\" phone to store the Passkey. Read more on how to set up Passkeys with Microsoft Authenticator app", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 297}, {"topic": "11. FAQ", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Q1: What does the CyberArk Agent do?", "Users are not administrators on their own endpoints, but the CyberArk Endpoint Privileged Account Management agent will allow them to perform administrative tasks. For example, install software or change system settings.", "Q2: Will I still be able to perform my daily tasks?", "Users will be able to run applications that require administrative privileges. All they need to do is select “OK” on the new User Account Control prompt as seen below.", "Some applications and scripts that require administrative privileges will have to be launched with the user right-clicking on the application and choosing Run As Administrator", "Users will be able to install new software in the same way as before as well, except explicitly blocked applications.", "If for some reason an application will not run or install as expected due to insufficient privileges, users can open an incident ticket to be granted temporary administrative rights or a policy elevation for the application.", "Q3: What is in scope of the EPAM service?", "Windows Endpoints including VDIs", "Q4: Will MAC and Linux endpoints be included?", "SAP Mac endpoints already have an application that manages administrative privileges on endpoints and are being further investigated to supplement management with CyberArk. Linux endpoints are currently being investigated.", "Q5: What data is collected from my machine?", "The following information is the only NPI (non-public information)/PII (personally identifiable information) that CyberArk's Endpoint Privilege Manager SaaS collects for the purpose of providing services to its customers:", "Computer Data", "Computer name, MAC address, IP addresses of the endpoint. For endpoints connected to SaaS, usernames and the groups they are in, and the username of the currently logged in user.", "Application Data", "Programs or applications installed on endpoints and details about their behavior (including access to files, registry, network requests and processes).", "Q6: How long will collected data be stored?", "Data Retention", "Computer data is retained for 30 days if a computer has not connected to the console.", "Application data is retained for 30 days.", "Data Deletion Procedure (Right to be forgotten)", "Automatically 100 days after the CyberArk Endpoint Privilege Manager SaaS customer expiration/termination (or non-renewal) date.", "CyberArk's Endpoint Privilege Manager SaaS backups with customer data will be overridden after a period of 21 days from the deletion date.", "Q7: Will CyberArk share your personal data with third parties?", "CyberArk won’t provide any third parties with your personal data without first obtaining your consent.", "Q8: Will EPAM Solution let Employees to install any software in end users' systems. Yes, you can still install software. If any installation is not working, you can raise a ticket and a backend expert will support you on this", "Q9: Is Bitlocker encryption enabled for Windows VM?", "Yes, new VMs have Bitlocker enabled", "Q10: How to exclude developer applications from Microsoft Windows Defender On-Access Scan?", "Create an IT Ticket with Hostname/Business Reason", "Title SAPDevelop folder exclusion request Service Software", "Service Offering IES-CS-Security - EndPoint Security", "Assignment group IES CS Advanced - Secure Services (Client Protection)", "Once the created ticket is completed, user would be advised to take action as below.", "Create a SAPDevelop folder in the directory in your Mac/WindowsOS/Linux", "Mac-> /Users/*/SAPDevelop/* (case sensitive)", "Windows-> C:\\SAPDevelop (case sensitive)", "Linux-> /home/*/SAPDevelop/* or */SAPDevelop/ (case sensitive)", "Q11: What information is required for escalating BitLocker key tickets?", "services offerings – IES-CS-Security – Encryption RMS AIP", "Correct Recovery key", "Hostname / Serial number of the machine", "Employee ID"], "content": "Q1: What does the CyberArk Agent do? Users are not administrators on their own endpoints, but the CyberArk Endpoint Privileged Account Management agent will allow them to perform administrative tasks. For example, install software or change system settings. Q2: Will I still be able to perform my daily tasks? Users will be able to run applications that require administrative privileges. All they need to do is select “OK” on the new User Account Control prompt as seen below. Some applications and scripts that require administrative privileges will have to be launched with the user right-clicking on the application and choosing Run As Administrator Users will be able to install new software in the same way as before as well, except explicitly blocked applications. If for some reason an application will not run or install as expected due to insufficient privileges, users can open an incident ticket to be granted temporary administrative rights or a policy elevation for the application. Q3: What is in scope of the EPAM service? Windows Endpoints including VDIs Q4: Will MAC and Linux endpoints be included? SAP Mac endpoints already have an application that manages administrative privileges on endpoints and are being further investigated to supplement management with CyberArk. Linux endpoints are currently being investigated. Q5: What data is collected from my machine? The following information is the only NPI (non-public information)/PII (personally identifiable information) that CyberArk's Endpoint Privilege Manager SaaS collects for the purpose of providing services to its customers: Computer Data Computer name, MAC address, IP addresses of the endpoint. For endpoints connected to SaaS, usernames and the groups they are in, and the username of the currently logged in user. Application Data Programs or applications installed on endpoints and details about their behavior (including access to files, registry, network requests and processes). Q6: How long will collected data be stored? Data Retention Computer data is retained for 30 days if a computer has not connected to the console. Application data is retained for 30 days. Data Deletion Procedure (Right to be forgotten) Automatically 100 days after the CyberArk Endpoint Privilege Manager SaaS customer expiration/termination (or non-renewal) date. CyberArk's Endpoint Privilege Manager SaaS backups with customer data will be overridden after a period of 21 days from the deletion date. Q7: Will CyberArk share your personal data with third parties? CyberArk won’t provide any third parties with your personal data without first obtaining your consent. Q8: Will EPAM Solution let Employees to install any software in end users' systems. Yes, you can still install software. If any installation is not working, you can raise a ticket and a backend expert will support you on this Q9: Is Bitlocker encryption enabled for Windows VM? Yes, new VMs have Bitlocker enabled Q10: How to exclude developer applications from Microsoft Windows Defender On-Access Scan? Create an IT Ticket with Hostname/Business Reason Title SAPDevelop folder exclusion request Service Software Service Offering IES-CS-Security - EndPoint Security Assignment group IES CS Advanced - Secure Services (Client Protection) Once the created ticket is completed, user would be advised to take action as below. Create a SAPDevelop folder in the directory in your Mac/WindowsOS/Linux Mac-> /Users/*/SAPDevelop/* (case sensitive) Windows-> C:\\SAPDevelop (case sensitive) Linux-> /home/*/SAPDevelop/* or */SAPDevelop/ (case sensitive) Q11: What information is required for escalating BitLocker key tickets? services offerings – IES-CS-Security – Encryption RMS AIP Correct Recovery key Hostname / Serial number of the machine Employee ID", "source": "Secure Services", "id": 298}, {"topic": "", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["ONE Support", "Internal- SAP Only", "Version control", "If you find any content in this document is out of date, feel free to contact the Authors for feedback!", "Thanks for your cooperation in advance!", "Area: Unified Communications"], "content": "ONE Support Internal- SAP Only Version control If you find any content in this document is out of date, feel free to contact the Authors for feedback! Thanks for your cooperation in advance! Area: Unified Communications", "source": "Unified Communications", "id": 299}, {"topic": "1. Microsoft Teams - Unified Communication Cockpit", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Overview", "For new starters at SAP: use the UC Cockpit to request a telephone number if you require it for your role.", "The Unified Communication Cockpit (UC Cockpit) Self-Service Portal is your central tool to manage your Unified Communications service. It offers various options to customize your Microsoft Teams workspace and integrates nicely into the SAP Launchpad.", "The UC Cockpit is located on the SAP Launchpad. Click the Home Navigation option in the upper left corner of the screen. Click on “Search” button, the type in “UC” in search field, choose UC Cockpit – Self Service.", "Please refer to Microsoft Teams - Unified Communication Cockpit"], "content": "Overview For new starters at SAP: use the UC Cockpit to request a telephone number if you require it for your role. The Unified Communication Cockpit (UC Cockpit) Self-Service Portal is your central tool to manage your Unified Communications service. It offers various options to customize your Microsoft Teams workspace and integrates nicely into the SAP Launchpad. The UC Cockpit is located on the SAP Launchpad. Click the Home Navigation option in the upper left corner of the screen. Click on “Search” button, the type in “UC” in search field, choose UC Cockpit – Self Service. Please refer to Microsoft Teams - Unified Communication Cockpit", "source": "Unified Communications", "id": 300}, {"topic": "2. Microsoft Teams - Unified Communication Cockpit - Account settings", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["The UC Cockpit now contains all settings and scenarios you need to manage your telephone number allocated to your Teams client. Your assigned phone number is displayed in the header information. If you do not have a number provisioned, please refer to the phone number activation request.", "For the full feature set of the UC Cockpit please have a look at the overview article.", "Caller ID", "When set to “ON” your extension is displayed to external callees. If set to \"OFF\", the reception's number will be signaled.", "Music On Hold", "When set to “ON” callers will hear music when placed on hold or parked.", "Busy on Busy", "When set to “ON” all additional incoming calls to your number will receive a busy signal tone if you are already in a call", "My Preferred Conference Dial-In Number", "My Preferred Conference Dial-In Number allows you to change the dial-in phone number shown in your Teams meeting invite. You may select the country of the dial in number you would like to show in the meeting invite", "Voicemail Transcription", "Voicemail Transcription provides you with a transcription service for received voicemails. Please make sure to add the information to your voicemail greetings message as indicated in the confirmation mail. You may refer to Teams Voicemail KBA for more information", "Webinar feature activation", "Webinar feature activation allows you to enable your account to have the capability to organize a webinar via your Teams client. You may refer to Teams Webinar KBA for more information", "Please refer to Microsoft Teams - Unified Communication Cockpit – Account settings"], "content": "The UC Cockpit now contains all settings and scenarios you need to manage your telephone number allocated to your Teams client. Your assigned phone number is displayed in the header information. If you do not have a number provisioned, please refer to the phone number activation request. For the full feature set of the UC Cockpit please have a look at the overview article. Caller ID When set to “ON” your extension is displayed to external callees. If set to \"OFF\", the reception's number will be signaled. Music On Hold When set to “ON” callers will hear music when placed on hold or parked. Busy on Busy When set to “ON” all additional incoming calls to your number will receive a busy signal tone if you are already in a call My Preferred Conference Dial-In Number My Preferred Conference Dial-In Number allows you to change the dial-in phone number shown in your Teams meeting invite. You may select the country of the dial in number you would like to show in the meeting invite Voicemail Transcription Voicemail Transcription provides you with a transcription service for received voicemails. Please make sure to add the information to your voicemail greetings message as indicated in the confirmation mail. You may refer to Teams Voicemail KBA for more information Webinar feature activation Webinar feature activation allows you to enable your account to have the capability to organize a webinar via your Teams client. You may refer to Teams Webinar KBA for more information Please refer to Microsoft Teams - Unified Communication Cockpit – Account settings", "source": "Unified Communications", "id": 301}, {"topic": "3. Microsoft Teams - Unified Communication Cockpit – Teams Telephony Phone Number Activation/Deactivation Service Request", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["In this section, you will learn how to request phone number activation for Teams Telephony using the UC Cockpit and deactivate the phone number if you no longer require making any calls with external world. The cost associated with the assignment of a phone number refers to active usage of telephony, i.e. for outgoing calls.", "Notes: For new users (C, D, I), by default you are not assigned with a Teams Telephony phone number. Please use this feature to request one. For C-users there is additional approval workflow which requires an approval by the service owner and your cost center manager.", "Please refer to Knowledge Article about Unified Communication Cockpit – Teams Telephony Phone Number Activation/Deactivation Service Request"], "content": "In this section, you will learn how to request phone number activation for Teams Telephony using the UC Cockpit and deactivate the phone number if you no longer require making any calls with external world. The cost associated with the assignment of a phone number refers to active usage of telephony, i.e. for outgoing calls. Notes: For new users (C, D, I), by default you are not assigned with a Teams Telephony phone number. Please use this feature to request one. For C-users there is additional approval workflow which requires an approval by the service owner and your cost center manager. Please refer to Knowledge Article about Unified Communication Cockpit – Teams Telephony Phone Number Activation/Deactivation Service Request", "source": "Unified Communications", "id": 302}, {"topic": "4. Microsoft Teams - Unified Communication Cockpit –Teams Telephony Phone Number Relocation Request", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["In this section, we will guide you on how to request a new Teams Telephony Phone Number if you relocate to another office permanently or you would like to have another location Teams Telephony Phone Number due to business justification. For example, contact center agent in Philippines needs a US Teams Telephony Phone Number.", "Please refer to Knowledge Article about Unified Communication Cockpit –Teams Telephony Phone Number Relocation Request"], "content": "In this section, we will guide you on how to request a new Teams Telephony Phone Number if you relocate to another office permanently or you would like to have another location Teams Telephony Phone Number due to business justification. For example, contact center agent in Philippines needs a US Teams Telephony Phone Number. Please refer to Knowledge Article about Unified Communication Cockpit –Teams Telephony Phone Number Relocation Request", "source": "Unified Communications", "id": 303}, {"topic": "5. Microsoft Teams - Unified Communication Cockpit – Teams Personal Hard Phone Activation Service Request", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["If you are using your own Teams credential to sign into a hard phone, you are required to register your ID and phone’s serial number in the Microsoft backend system to get permission for the access.", "Please refer to Knowledge Article about Unified Communication Cockpit – Teams Personal Hard Phone Activation Service Request"], "content": "If you are using your own Teams credential to sign into a hard phone, you are required to register your ID and phone’s serial number in the Microsoft backend system to get permission for the access. Please refer to Knowledge Article about Unified Communication Cockpit – Teams Personal Hard Phone Activation Service Request", "source": "Unified Communications", "id": 304}, {"topic": "6. Microsoft Teams - Unified Communication Cockpit – Temporary Teams Telephony Phone Number Request", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["In this section, we are showing you how to request a Temporary Teams Telephony Phone Number, in case you are on a short business trip to another SAP office and need a local number. After your trip, you can return the Temporary Teams Telephony Phone Number and system will automatically re-assign your original Teams Telephony Phone Number.", "Notes: The Temporary Teams Telephony Phone Number is valid for one (1) year and the system will automatically re-assign your original phone number. If you need a longer time, please use “Relocation” request.", "Please refer to Knowledge Article about Unified Communication Cockpit – Temporary Teams Telephony Phone Number Request", "Please refer to Knowledge Articles about more Unified Communication", "Call Quality Statistic Dashboard", "Teams Common Area Phone (CAP) Lifecycle Management", "Teams Analog Port Service Lifecycle Management"], "content": "In this section, we are showing you how to request a Temporary Teams Telephony Phone Number, in case you are on a short business trip to another SAP office and need a local number. After your trip, you can return the Temporary Teams Telephony Phone Number and system will automatically re-assign your original Teams Telephony Phone Number. Notes: The Temporary Teams Telephony Phone Number is valid for one (1) year and the system will automatically re-assign your original phone number. If you need a longer time, please use “Relocation” request. Please refer to Knowledge Article about Unified Communication Cockpit – Temporary Teams Telephony Phone Number Request Please refer to Knowledge Articles about more Unified Communication Call Quality Statistic Dashboard Teams Common Area Phone (CAP) Lifecycle Management Teams Analog Port Service Lifecycle Management", "source": "Unified Communications", "id": 305}, {"topic": "", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["ONE Support", "Internal- SAP Only", "Version control", "If you find any content in this document is out of date, feel free to contact the Authors for feedback!", "Thanks for your cooperation in advance!"], "content": "ONE Support Internal- SAP Only Version control If you find any content in this document is out of date, feel free to contact the Authors for feedback! Thanks for your cooperation in advance!", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 306}, {"topic": "What is WTS", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Windows Terminal Server - WTS provides hosted shared desktops and applications, enabling a flexible and secured way for SAP employees to access the company network and standard applications.", "There are two main groups of WTS in use at SAP, Office and Project WTS."], "content": "Windows Terminal Server - WTS provides hosted shared desktops and applications, enabling a flexible and secured way for SAP employees to access the company network and standard applications. There are two main groups of WTS in use at SAP, Office and Project WTS.", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 307}, {"topic": "What is WTS", "section": "1.1 Office WTS", "paragraphs": ["Commonly known as SAP Desktop, it contains a common set of standard Corporate software such as, Office, SAPGUI, IE, Outlook, etc. that are available for all users to easily access from anywhere at any time from many types of devices.", "How to access", "Please navigate to our Access Portal https://access.sap.com, choose Region, here you have to log in either with the classic or with the MFA option to the [Office / Project WTS and VDI]. If you are outside of the corporate network, the classic login requires your UserID, password and passcode. Passcode is generated by the RSA token or app, you can find out more about it on this Page. The MFA authentication requires, that you are enrolled for MFA authentication. More details can be found on this Page."], "content": "Commonly known as SAP Desktop, it contains a common set of standard Corporate software such as, Office, SAPGUI, IE, Outlook, etc. that are available for all users to easily access from anywhere at any time from many types of devices. How to access Please navigate to our Access Portal https://access.sap.com, choose Region, here you have to log in either with the classic or with the MFA option to the [Office / Project WTS and VDI]. If you are outside of the corporate network, the classic login requires your UserID, password and passcode. Passcode is generated by the RSA token or app, you can find out more about it on this Page. The MFA authentication requires, that you are enrolled for MFA authentication. More details can be found on this Page.", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 308}, {"topic": "What is WTS", "section": "1.2 Project WTS", "paragraphs": ["Often referred to as Project Server, it provides a specific set of installed software to dedicated user groups whose requirements cannot be fulfilled by the standard Office WTS. For example, HR WTS, Jumphost.", "How to Order WTS Project Server?", "Please read through the document How to order a WTS Project Server for details of how to:", "place an order", "see server specs available", "assign billing info", "provide additional information for requested software", "How to Request Access?", "After ordering the WTS Project Server, the user authorization process will be triggered. An Active Directory (AD) user group will be created. This AD user group can be maintained by the WTS Project Server requester. It is also possible to have additional users authorized, to maintain this AD user group. Only members of this AD group can see and access the ordered WTS Project Server.", "How to Logon?", "Use the VDI/WTS Access Portal, choose the region where the WTS Project Server resides, and choose [Office and Project WTS].", "Required only for the first time: Search for the Project WTS name in the top right corner by clicking on the magnifying glass. If you see the Project WTS, please click on the \"star\" in the top right corner to add to your dashboard.", "After this simply clicking the icon will open the Project WTS. For more details on how to access, you can go to our User Guide Document Repository."], "content": "Often referred to as Project Server, it provides a specific set of installed software to dedicated user groups whose requirements cannot be fulfilled by the standard Office WTS. For example, HR WTS, Jumphost. How to Order WTS Project Server? Please read through the document How to order a WTS Project Server for details of how to: place an order see server specs available assign billing info provide additional information for requested software How to Request Access? After ordering the WTS Project Server, the user authorization process will be triggered. An Active Directory (AD) user group will be created. This AD user group can be maintained by the WTS Project Server requester. It is also possible to have additional users authorized, to maintain this AD user group. Only members of this AD group can see and access the ordered WTS Project Server. How to Logon? Use the VDI/WTS Access Portal, choose the region where the WTS Project Server resides, and choose [Office and Project WTS]. Required only for the first time: Search for the Project WTS name in the top right corner by clicking on the magnifying glass. If you see the Project WTS, please click on the \"star\" in the top right corner to add to your dashboard. After this simply clicking the icon will open the Project WTS. For more details on how to access, you can go to our User Guide Document Repository.", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 309}, {"topic": "What is VDI", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["VDI (Virtual Desktop Infrastructure) is a hosted virtual machine technology. The virtual machines are centrally hosted and can be accessed via a web portal from within SAP network, or from an external internet connection using RSA authentication. Once connected, the machine provides the same functions of a virtual machine hosted directly on your local PC. However, unlike a locally hosted machine, it does not use your local machine’s CPU or storage."], "content": "VDI (Virtual Desktop Infrastructure) is a hosted virtual machine technology. The virtual machines are centrally hosted and can be accessed via a web portal from within SAP network, or from an external internet connection using RSA authentication. Once connected, the machine provides the same functions of a virtual machine hosted directly on your local PC. However, unlike a locally hosted machine, it does not use your local machine’s CPU or storage.", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 310}, {"topic": "What is VDI", "section": "2.1 How to order a VDI", "paragraphs": ["Details you can click here"], "content": "Details you can click here", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 311}, {"topic": "What is VDI", "section": "2.2.1 Windows VDIs", "paragraphs": ["Requirements", "Citrix Workspace version 2203 CU1 or higher.", "The current Citrix Workspace application can be downloaded from our \"Downloads\" section for MacOS and Windows based devices.", "Logon to the VDI environment via the web Access Portal", "Regardless of whether you are outside or inside SAP network, you can log on to the VDI environment via WTS/VDI Access Portal", "Just choose the Region (EMEA for VDIs located in the EMEA datacenter and AMER for VDIs in the Americas datacenter). Now choose \"Office / Project WTS and VDI\" landscape. You can also select the Azure MFA option for the Microsoft Authenticator login, if you have access to this solution.", "For internal access, the SSO authentication will sign you in to the portal. If you are accessing from external device, network, you will be prompted for SAP login credentials with multi factor authentication (RSA passcode for example)."], "content": "Requirements Citrix Workspace version 2203 CU1 or higher. The current Citrix Workspace application can be downloaded from our \"Downloads\" section for MacOS and Windows based devices. Logon to the VDI environment via the web Access Portal Regardless of whether you are outside or inside SAP network, you can log on to the VDI environment via WTS/VDI Access Portal Just choose the Region (EMEA for VDIs located in the EMEA datacenter and AMER for VDIs in the Americas datacenter). Now choose \"Office / Project WTS and VDI\" landscape. You can also select the Azure MFA option for the Microsoft Authenticator login, if you have access to this solution. For internal access, the SSO authentication will sign you in to the portal. If you are accessing from external device, network, you will be prompted for SAP login credentials with multi factor authentication (RSA passcode for example).", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 312}, {"topic": "What is VDI", "section": "2.2.2 Linux VDIs", "paragraphs": ["From May 2018 on, any new Linux VDI deployment can be accessed in the same way, as you connect to a Windows VDI: The Linux VDI will be available in the Office/Project and VDI landscape menu in the Access Portal (access.sap.com).", "The Linux VDIs have a different naming convention, the hostname starts with \"WDFL41\" and \"PHLL41\".", "Important steps for all Linux VDI user:", "Check if your SAP-ID has been unix-enabled (or Linux-enabled) by launching the Unix AD Attribute web page.", "If your ID is not yet enabled, you can enable your user account via self-service on the portal mentioned above. The activation process can take 10-30 minutes.", "You can then log in your Linux VDI with your SAP-ID credential (User name in format of \"global\\SAP-ID\")."], "content": "From May 2018 on, any new Linux VDI deployment can be accessed in the same way, as you connect to a Windows VDI: The Linux VDI will be available in the Office/Project and VDI landscape menu in the Access Portal (access.sap.com). The Linux VDIs have a different naming convention, the hostname starts with \"WDFL41\" and \"PHLL41\". Important steps for all Linux VDI user: Check if your SAP-ID has been unix-enabled (or Linux-enabled) by launching the Unix AD Attribute web page. If your ID is not yet enabled, you can enable your user account via self-service on the portal mentioned above. The activation process can take 10-30 minutes. You can then log in your Linux VDI with your SAP-ID credential (User name in format of \"global\\SAP-ID\").", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 313}, {"topic": "What is VDI", "section": "2.2.3 VDI Snapshots", "paragraphs": ["VDI Support snapshot function for mirror system."], "content": "VDI Support snapshot function for mirror system.", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 314}, {"topic": "Requirements for WTS/VDI", "section": "3.1 Software Requirements", "paragraphs": ["For the best experience, make sure that the suggested Citrix Workspace app is installed on the local client. See “Downloads” section at https://access.sap.com either accessible from the “hamburger” menu or directly in the top right corner"], "content": "For the best experience, make sure that the suggested Citrix Workspace app is installed on the local client. See “Downloads” section at https://access.sap.com either accessible from the “hamburger” menu or directly in the top right corner", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 315}, {"topic": "Requirements for WTS/VDI", "section": "Network Requirement", "paragraphs": ["On the local device, if it is a non-SAP device, please turn off any kind of VPN service, as they might conflict with the SAP WTS/VDI service. A reliable Internet connection is required. Check the network quality using the SAP tool on https://access.sap.com", "Performance check as We recommend, that the network quality fulfills the following:", "• Latency is below 280 ms.", "• Bandwidth is greater than 2 Mbt."], "content": "On the local device, if it is a non-SAP device, please turn off any kind of VPN service, as they might conflict with the SAP WTS/VDI service. A reliable Internet connection is required. Check the network quality using the SAP tool on https://access.sap.com Performance check as We recommend, that the network quality fulfills the following: • Latency is below 280 ms. • Bandwidth is greater than 2 Mbt.", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 316}, {"topic": "Requirements for WTS/VDI", "section": "3.3 Audio Requirements", "paragraphs": ["To ensure the best MS Teams experience, users need either a Microsoft Certified Headset or SAP Certified Headset Keep the headset’s firmware up to date by using the tool provided by your headset manufacturer:", "Plantronics headset", "Jabra", "EPOS (formerly known as Sennheiser)", "Logitech", "Please make sure to close a local installed MS Teams instance before connecting to WTS/VDI"], "content": "To ensure the best MS Teams experience, users need either a Microsoft Certified Headset or SAP Certified Headset Keep the headset’s firmware up to date by using the tool provided by your headset manufacturer: Plantronics headset Jabra EPOS (formerly known as Sennheiser) Logitech Please make sure to close a local installed MS Teams instance before connecting to WTS/VDI", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 317}, {"topic": "Requirements for WTS/VDI", "section": "3.4 windows system requirement.", "paragraphs": ["Microsoft Windows 10 VDIs will be blocked from access starting at the end of October. To ensure continued access and security compliance, all users must migrate to a Windows 11 VDI before this deadline.", "If you don't take action your VDI will be blocked by end of October 2025 and you won't be able to access it any longer."], "content": "Microsoft Windows 10 VDIs will be blocked from access starting at the end of October. To ensure continued access and security compliance, all users must migrate to a Windows 11 VDI before this deadline. If you don't take action your VDI will be blocked by end of October 2025 and you won't be able to access it any longer.", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 318}, {"topic": "Citrix Workspace app/Receiver", "section": "4.1 What is Citrix Workspace app/Receiver", "paragraphs": ["Citrix Workspace app/Receiver allows you to connect to SAP WTS (Windows Terminal Services) and VDI virtual desktops provided by the Client Virtualization Team.", "The virtual desktops can be accessed via our new VDI / WTS Access Portal (https://access.sap.com) using a web browser on a Windows, Macintosh or mobile device that has the Citrix Workspace app/Receiver installed.", "Citrix client supports text copy and paste between WTS and local PC."], "content": "Citrix Workspace app/Receiver allows you to connect to SAP WTS (Windows Terminal Services) and VDI virtual desktops provided by the Client Virtualization Team. The virtual desktops can be accessed via our new VDI / WTS Access Portal (https://access.sap.com) using a web browser on a Windows, Macintosh or mobile device that has the Citrix Workspace app/Receiver installed. Citrix client supports text copy and paste between WTS and local PC.", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 319}, {"topic": "Citrix Workspace app/Receiver", "section": "4.2 Installation", "paragraphs": ["The latest supported version of Citrix Workspace app/Receiver is available in company portal", "Install/upgrade Citrix Workspace app/Receiver for Windows", "For SAP-Imaged Windows computers:", "Please launch company portal, on the Application search for Citrix", "Once the installation complete, you need to reboot the computer"], "content": "The latest supported version of Citrix Workspace app/Receiver is available in company portal Install/upgrade Citrix Workspace app/Receiver for Windows For SAP-Imaged Windows computers: Please launch company portal, on the Application search for Citrix Once the installation complete, you need to reboot the computer", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 320}, {"topic": "Difference between WTS &VDI", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Windows Terminal Server (WTS) - preconfigured, shared, multiuser environment and it’s a Desktop based on Server Operating System. Virtual Desktop Infrastructure (VDI) - dedicated user environment, users have administrative rights to install additional software and it’s a Desktop based Client Operating System.", "The key difference between WTS and VDI to end user is that user has local administrative right in the VDI VM and hence can install software applications on the VDI, whereas users on WTS does not have privilege to install software.", "MS Office Optimized WTS Profile", "To further improve usability and performance we are implementing a new profile solution for selected WTS environments. This change takes advantage of Microsoft FSLogix technology and provides more storage space for individual user data while working with WTS. Previously on WTS, important applications such as Microsoft Teams, Outlook and OneDrive all needed to run with a focus on conserving profile space, but now they can run at full capacity, just as they do on local computers. FSLogix brings improvements in usability and performance. The following documentation is meant to explain these changes and point out some important details."], "content": "Windows Terminal Server (WTS) - preconfigured, shared, multiuser environment and it’s a Desktop based on Server Operating System. Virtual Desktop Infrastructure (VDI) - dedicated user environment, users have administrative rights to install additional software and it’s a Desktop based Client Operating System. The key difference between WTS and VDI to end user is that user has local administrative right in the VDI VM and hence can install software applications on the VDI, whereas users on WTS does not have privilege to install software. MS Office Optimized WTS Profile To further improve usability and performance we are implementing a new profile solution for selected WTS environments. This change takes advantage of Microsoft FSLogix technology and provides more storage space for individual user data while working with WTS. Previously on WTS, important applications such as Microsoft Teams, Outlook and OneDrive all needed to run with a focus on conserving profile space, but now they can run at full capacity, just as they do on local computers. FSLogix brings improvements in usability and performance. The following documentation is meant to explain these changes and point out some important details.", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 321}, {"topic": "Difference between WTS &VDI", "section": "6.1 Starting with a fresh profile", "paragraphs": ["Your WTS profile contains all the personal operating system and application settings you configured as well as configuration files, caches and possibly documents. Migrating your current user-specific settings to the new solution is not supported by the manufacturer. During testing, several complications with migrations were encountered. For this reason, you will begin with a new user profile. With a new user profile, some application and system specific settings (e.g., view settings in File Explorer, Outlook signature settings) which were saved in your previous profile, will be reverted to default settings. If you customized these settings in the past, you may need to reconfigure them.", "Please see Chapter 3 for instructions on how to transfer common settings to your new profile. Your personal documents on the Desktop or in the Documents folder, as well as files hosted in the cloud (e.g., OneDrive, e-mails) will be kept."], "content": "Your WTS profile contains all the personal operating system and application settings you configured as well as configuration files, caches and possibly documents. Migrating your current user-specific settings to the new solution is not supported by the manufacturer. During testing, several complications with migrations were encountered. For this reason, you will begin with a new user profile. With a new user profile, some application and system specific settings (e.g., view settings in File Explorer, Outlook signature settings) which were saved in your previous profile, will be reverted to default settings. If you customized these settings in the past, you may need to reconfigure them. Please see Chapter 3 for instructions on how to transfer common settings to your new profile. Your personal documents on the Desktop or in the Documents folder, as well as files hosted in the cloud (e.g., OneDrive, e-mails) will be kept.", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 322}, {"topic": "Difference between WTS &VDI", "section": "6.2.1 Microsoft Teams", "paragraphs": ["After starting the application, Microsoft Teams saves temporary data to your profile. Previously this data was deleted while logging off from WTS and had to be downloaded again each time you logged on and started the application. With FSLogix, this data will be downloaded and kept in your profile, thereby speeding up subsequent uses of the application and significantly improving stability. Regarding audio and video file transfers, the same principles apply as previously. Please refer to the \"SAP WTS and VDI quick start guide\" for more details."], "content": "After starting the application, Microsoft Teams saves temporary data to your profile. Previously this data was deleted while logging off from WTS and had to be downloaded again each time you logged on and started the application. With FSLogix, this data will be downloaded and kept in your profile, thereby speeding up subsequent uses of the application and significantly improving stability. Regarding audio and video file transfers, the same principles apply as previously. Please refer to the \"SAP WTS and VDI quick start guide\" for more details.", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 323}, {"topic": "Difference between WTS &VDI", "section": "6.2.2 Microsoft Outlook", "paragraphs": ["Outlook typically downloads your data to your computer to provide faster access and better performance. Previously this was not supported on WTS due to storage space limitations, which resulted in the lack of a few social functions, and all searches were performed via the Internet. With the new profile solution, a portion of your Outlook profile will be downloaded to your WTS profile, enabling full functionality and faster access. However, automatic download is limited to items from the past month. Older items can be accessed as well, but they will be downloaded on demand. Searching still shows all results, even if they are older."], "content": "Outlook typically downloads your data to your computer to provide faster access and better performance. Previously this was not supported on WTS due to storage space limitations, which resulted in the lack of a few social functions, and all searches were performed via the Internet. With the new profile solution, a portion of your Outlook profile will be downloaded to your WTS profile, enabling full functionality and faster access. However, automatic download is limited to items from the past month. Older items can be accessed as well, but they will be downloaded on demand. Searching still shows all results, even if they are older.", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 324}, {"topic": "Difference between WTS &VDI", "section": "6.2.3 Microsoft OneDrive", "paragraphs": ["Previously it was not possible to use the native OneDrive client on WTS due to storage limitations. Instead, we provided the OneDrive mapper script to remotely connect to your OneDrive in the cloud. With the new profile solution, the native OneDrive client will be used, providing full functionality as seen on local computers. As with Outlook (see above), not all files will be downloaded immediately because this will take too much space, even with the new profile solution. Instead, the files that you commonly use will be downloaded on demand and remain downloaded for 14 days. After this time period, the files will be deleted locally, but can be downloaded again the next time they are needed.", "You can also right-click important files and select Always keep on this device to keep them available locally. The status of these files is displayed in Explorer with an icon. (solid green circle with a white tick mark)", "Always keeping files on the device should only be used when necessary, as you will not be able to download additional files from your OneDrive when your profile space runs low (see Chapter 4 below)."], "content": "Previously it was not possible to use the native OneDrive client on WTS due to storage limitations. Instead, we provided the OneDrive mapper script to remotely connect to your OneDrive in the cloud. With the new profile solution, the native OneDrive client will be used, providing full functionality as seen on local computers. As with Outlook (see above), not all files will be downloaded immediately because this will take too much space, even with the new profile solution. Instead, the files that you commonly use will be downloaded on demand and remain downloaded for 14 days. After this time period, the files will be deleted locally, but can be downloaded again the next time they are needed. You can also right-click important files and select Always keep on this device to keep them available locally. The status of these files is displayed in Explorer with an icon. (solid green circle with a white tick mark) Always keeping files on the device should only be used when necessary, as you will not be able to download additional files from your OneDrive when your profile space runs low (see Chapter 4 below).", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 325}, {"topic": "Difference between WTS &VDI", "section": "6.2.4 Microsoft OneNote", "paragraphs": ["As with MS Teams, your OneNote content will also be downloaded and made available for future use by the application, thereby speeding up OneNote performance significantly. Keep in mind, the size limitation for your Office files explained in the Chapter 4."], "content": "As with MS Teams, your OneNote content will also be downloaded and made available for future use by the application, thereby speeding up OneNote performance significantly. Keep in mind, the size limitation for your Office files explained in the Chapter 4.", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 326}, {"topic": "Difference between WTS &VDI", "section": "6.3 Backing up your settings to transfer them to your fresh profile", "paragraphs": ["Although most user specific settings will be reapplied as needed, without any help and with little effort, we wanted to point out some specific settings you may choose to back-up from your old profile and import to your fresh profile with the new profile solution."], "content": "Although most user specific settings will be reapplied as needed, without any help and with little effort, we wanted to point out some specific settings you may choose to back-up from your old profile and import to your fresh profile with the new profile solution.", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 327}, {"topic": "Difference between WTS &VDI", "section": "6.3.1 Microsoft Outlook", "paragraphs": ["If you use the classic signatures in Outlook, go to File > Options > Mail > Signatures... and copy your existing signatures to a Word document saved on your OneDrive, for example. In your fresh profile, copy and paste the signatures from the Word document back into Outlook.", "With recent changes to Outlook by Microsoft, your other configuration data may already be saved in the cloud as well. In that case, you should see your familiar settings in your new profile without further actions."], "content": "If you use the classic signatures in Outlook, go to File > Options > Mail > Signatures... and copy your existing signatures to a Word document saved on your OneDrive, for example. In your fresh profile, copy and paste the signatures from the Word document back into Outlook. With recent changes to Outlook by Microsoft, your other configuration data may already be saved in the cloud as well. In that case, you should see your familiar settings in your new profile without further actions.", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 328}, {"topic": "Difference between WTS &VDI", "section": "6.3.2 SAP GUI", "paragraphs": ["You can find a separate document on backing-up and restoring SAP GUI settings by following this link."], "content": "You can find a separate document on backing-up and restoring SAP GUI settings by following this link.", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 329}, {"topic": "Difference between WTS &VDI", "section": "6.3.3 Browser bookmarks / favorites", "paragraphs": ["In your browser, press Ctrl+Shift+O (the letter 'o' not the number zero), click the three dots at the top and select Export favorites or Export bookmarks. Save this file to your OneDrive, then later when you're missing the bookmarks in your new profile, you can import the previously saved file in the same way. You can skip this step if you already set up cloud syncing for your Bookmarks and Favorites, alternately you can set up cloud syncing now, instead of exporting the data."], "content": "In your browser, press Ctrl+Shift+O (the letter 'o' not the number zero), click the three dots at the top and select Export favorites or Export bookmarks. Save this file to your OneDrive, then later when you're missing the bookmarks in your new profile, you can import the previously saved file in the same way. You can skip this step if you already set up cloud syncing for your Bookmarks and Favorites, alternately you can set up cloud syncing now, instead of exporting the data.", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 330}, {"topic": "Difference between WTS &VDI", "section": "6.3.4 Accessing your old profile", "paragraphs": ["In the unexpected case that you're missing something important in your fresh profile, we will temporarily provide a shortcut to your old profile on the desktop within the WTS session."], "content": "In the unexpected case that you're missing something important in your fresh profile, we will temporarily provide a shortcut to your old profile on the desktop within the WTS session.", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 331}, {"topic": "Difference between WTS &VDI", "section": "6.4 Limitations of the new profile solution", "paragraphs": ["There are three size restrictions in place for the new profile solution:", "Office has been given a separate 10 GB of space, which is available for the caching of the MS Office products (i.e., Outlook, OneDrive, Teams, SharePoint, OneNote)", "To prevent your Outlook data from taking up all the space of in the Office container there is a separate size limitation of 7 GB for Outlook data file (OST) in place (this should not have any impact, considering only data of the last month is downloaded)", "What was previously known as TSHome still has 1 GB for the Desktop, Documents, Music, Pictures and Videos", "Your roaming profile, which contains the rest of your settings (like application data, operating system personalization), has grown to 2 GB.", "If your Outlook data from the last month is more than 7 GB, you will stop seeing new emails in Outlook. Use Outlook Web (https://outlook.office.com/mail/) as a temporary workaround to clean up your mailbox.", "This solution, despite its limitations, offers considerably more storage space than was previously available. If you reach less than 10% of your space remaining, a warning message will be displayed when logging on to the WTS. See the following chapters with guidance on how to solve this issue. It is recommended to use OneDrive as your preferred saving location instead of the folders on the TSHome (Desktop, Documents, Music, Pictures and Videos). OneDrive provides a thousandfold increase to your personal storage space. Please note, that not all landscapes are using this profile solution (e.g., JumpHosts, Project servers), in these landscapes you will still use the standard profile solution. Changes you make in your new MS optimized profile in one landscape or region will not be reflected in other landscapes and regions, and vice versa. To prevent unused profiles from taking up expensive storage space, old profiles will be automatically deleted if not used for 90 days. After 90 days users will receive a new profile as described previously."], "content": "There are three size restrictions in place for the new profile solution: Office has been given a separate 10 GB of space, which is available for the caching of the MS Office products (i.e., Outlook, OneDrive, Teams, SharePoint, OneNote) To prevent your Outlook data from taking up all the space of in the Office container there is a separate size limitation of 7 GB for Outlook data file (OST) in place (this should not have any impact, considering only data of the last month is downloaded) What was previously known as TSHome still has 1 GB for the Desktop, Documents, Music, Pictures and Videos Your roaming profile, which contains the rest of your settings (like application data, operating system personalization), has grown to 2 GB. If your Outlook data from the last month is more than 7 GB, you will stop seeing new emails in Outlook. Use Outlook Web (https://outlook.office.com/mail/) as a temporary workaround to clean up your mailbox. This solution, despite its limitations, offers considerably more storage space than was previously available. If you reach less than 10% of your space remaining, a warning message will be displayed when logging on to the WTS. See the following chapters with guidance on how to solve this issue. It is recommended to use OneDrive as your preferred saving location instead of the folders on the TSHome (Desktop, Documents, Music, Pictures and Videos). OneDrive provides a thousandfold increase to your personal storage space. Please note, that not all landscapes are using this profile solution (e.g., JumpHosts, Project servers), in these landscapes you will still use the standard profile solution. Changes you make in your new MS optimized profile in one landscape or region will not be reflected in other landscapes and regions, and vice versa. To prevent unused profiles from taking up expensive storage space, old profiles will be automatically deleted if not used for 90 days. After 90 days users will receive a new profile as described previously.", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 332}, {"topic": "Difference between WTS &VDI", "section": "6.5.1 Cleaning up unused MS Office data from your profile", "paragraphs": ["See suggestions below in case you get this warning message when logging on.", "In your OneDrive, look for large files that have been downloaded (check the status icon as explained in chapter 2.3), right click them and select the option Free up space. The files will be removed from your WTS profile but will remain in the OneDrive cloud for you to download again as needed.", "For Teams, double click the desktop shortcut Delete Teams Cache in your session to clean up your cache. It may contain older content that you don't access frequently anymore. If needed, it will be downloaded again automatically.", "In Outlook, as mentioned above only the content of the last month is downloaded. You can go to File > Tools > Mailbox Cleanup to find large files. However, only files deleted from within the last month will help free up space in your profile (older items are stored in the cloud already). Please note that in this case the deletion is permanent, so only delete items you're sure you don't need.", "To reduce the size used by Outlook, your data file can be compacted. This is not performed immediately by Outlook, it may help to do this manually if your Office container is running low on space and you deleted some files.", "To perform this action, please navigate:", "Outlook > File > Account Settings > Account Settings...", "Select your data file on the Data Files tab and click Settings", "On the Advanced tab click Outlook Data Files Settings... and then click Compact Now", "If you're using a shared mailbox (team mailbox or from your colleagues), this mailbox may be the reason you're reaching the OST file size limit. We recommend that you connect to a shared mailbox as described: Open Outlook, click File > Account Settings > Account Settings... > Select your own email address and click Change... > More Settings > Advanced > Add > enter the mailbox information and confirm all dialogs", "You can also use Outlook in your web browser as an alternative to the Outlook application or to free up space in your mailbox. In case none of these options work for you we recommend requesting a VDI. On your personal VDI more space is available, but it will generate a cost to your cost center."], "content": "See suggestions below in case you get this warning message when logging on. In your OneDrive, look for large files that have been downloaded (check the status icon as explained in chapter 2.3), right click them and select the option Free up space. The files will be removed from your WTS profile but will remain in the OneDrive cloud for you to download again as needed. For Teams, double click the desktop shortcut Delete Teams Cache in your session to clean up your cache. It may contain older content that you don't access frequently anymore. If needed, it will be downloaded again automatically. In Outlook, as mentioned above only the content of the last month is downloaded. You can go to File > Tools > Mailbox Cleanup to find large files. However, only files deleted from within the last month will help free up space in your profile (older items are stored in the cloud already). Please note that in this case the deletion is permanent, so only delete items you're sure you don't need. To reduce the size used by Outlook, your data file can be compacted. This is not performed immediately by Outlook, it may help to do this manually if your Office container is running low on space and you deleted some files. To perform this action, please navigate: Outlook > File > Account Settings > Account Settings... Select your data file on the Data Files tab and click Settings On the Advanced tab click Outlook Data Files Settings... and then click Compact Now If you're using a shared mailbox (team mailbox or from your colleagues), this mailbox may be the reason you're reaching the OST file size limit. We recommend that you connect to a shared mailbox as described: Open Outlook, click File > Account Settings > Account Settings... > Select your own email address and click Change... > More Settings > Advanced > Add > enter the mailbox information and confirm all dialogs You can also use Outlook in your web browser as an alternative to the Outlook application or to free up space in your mailbox. In case none of these options work for you we recommend requesting a VDI. On your personal VDI more space is available, but it will generate a cost to your cost center.", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 333}, {"topic": "Difference between WTS &VDI", "section": "6.5.2 Cleaning up the rest of your profile", "paragraphs": ["See suggestions below in case you get this warning message when logging on.", "Open File Explorer and enter %appdata% in the address bar.", "Right click folders that you suspect might use a lot of space (applications you use) and choose Properties to see their size. Do not consider folders for Outlook, OneDrive, Teams, SharePoint and OneNote, as those are stored in the MS Office part of your profile and thus not relevant to the warning message you received. If you find a folder taking up a lot of space, please investigate the folder and delete any data which looks like temporary files, cache files, etc.. If you are unsure of what is safe to delete, please create an IT support ticket"], "content": "See suggestions below in case you get this warning message when logging on. Open File Explorer and enter %appdata% in the address bar. Right click folders that you suspect might use a lot of space (applications you use) and choose Properties to see their size. Do not consider folders for Outlook, OneDrive, Teams, SharePoint and OneNote, as those are stored in the MS Office part of your profile and thus not relevant to the warning message you received. If you find a folder taking up a lot of space, please investigate the folder and delete any data which looks like temporary files, cache files, etc.. If you are unsure of what is safe to delete, please create an IT support ticket", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 334}, {"topic": "Difference between WTS &VDI", "section": "6.5.3 Cleaning up special folders of your profile (TSHome)", "paragraphs": ["If you cannot save any more data to the folders Desktop, Documents, Music, Pictures and Videos do the following.", "Open File Explorer and enter \\\\TSHomeServer\\TShome$\\UserID where you replace UserID with your C/D/I username.", "Look through the folders mentioned at the beginning of this chapter. Delete files you don't need any more or move them to a different location (your OneDrive for example)."], "content": "If you cannot save any more data to the folders Desktop, Documents, Music, Pictures and Videos do the following. Open File Explorer and enter \\\\TSHomeServer\\TShome$\\UserID where you replace UserID with your C/D/I username. Look through the folders mentioned at the beginning of this chapter. Delete files you don't need any more or move them to a different location (your OneDrive for example).", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 335}, {"topic": "7 Known limitations", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["In this page the limitations of the virtual sessions will be described for WTS and VDI", "Most of the limitations listed here were requested by SAP Global Security to safeguard SAPs data, brand, intellectual property, and in general enhance the security of the environment."], "content": "In this page the limitations of the virtual sessions will be described for WTS and VDI Most of the limitations listed here were requested by SAP Global Security to safeguard SAPs data, brand, intellectual property, and in general enhance the security of the environment.", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 336}, {"topic": "7 Known limitations", "section": "7.1 Performance", "paragraphs": ["The WTS and VDI sessions are both virtual environments, they are flexible, stable and in general offer a good performance. However, please keep in mind, that there are scenarios, where WTS and VDI cannot offer the same feature set or performance as a same sized physical device.", "To optimize a session and the performance, there are steps you can take as a preparation. Please check out the Quick Start Guide, where the critical optimization steps are listed and briefly explained. For an in depth explanation, please visit our Onboarding page, where you can view a training video or navigate to other knowledge articles."], "content": "The WTS and VDI sessions are both virtual environments, they are flexible, stable and in general offer a good performance. However, please keep in mind, that there are scenarios, where WTS and VDI cannot offer the same feature set or performance as a same sized physical device. To optimize a session and the performance, there are steps you can take as a preparation. Please check out the Quick Start Guide, where the critical optimization steps are listed and briefly explained. For an in depth explanation, please visit our Onboarding page, where you can view a training video or navigate to other knowledge articles.", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 337}, {"topic": "7 Known limitations", "section": "7.2 Copy & Paste", "paragraphs": ["Copy and paste operations are very limited due to security requirements. From the local machine you can copy and paste into the WTS or VDI session, for example some text, but the other way around, does not work. You can't copy and paste anything from your session to your local device . This is a security enhancement we had to implement.​​​​​​​ This limitation depends on the specific WTS or VDI session."], "content": "Copy and paste operations are very limited due to security requirements. From the local machine you can copy and paste into the WTS or VDI session, for example some text, but the other way around, does not work. You can't copy and paste anything from your session to your local device . This is a security enhancement we had to implement.​​​​​​​ This limitation depends on the specific WTS or VDI session.", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 338}, {"topic": "7 Known limitations", "section": "7.3 Microsoft Teams functionality", "paragraphs": ["Microsoft Teams is available both in VDI and WTS sessions, however there is limited functionality. For example, background effects such as blur or pictures cannot be inserted. This is a technical limitation coming from the vendor, Microsoft. Up-to-date limitations can be checked on the dedicated Microsoft article.​​​​​"], "content": "Microsoft Teams is available both in VDI and WTS sessions, however there is limited functionality. For example, background effects such as blur or pictures cannot be inserted. This is a technical limitation coming from the vendor, Microsoft. Up-to-date limitations can be checked on the dedicated Microsoft article.​​​​​", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 339}, {"topic": "7 Known limitations", "section": "7.4 Mapping local drives", "paragraphs": ["To prevent data theft or data leaks, mapping of the local client's drives (C:\\ or DVD) is prohibited in the sessions. This was also a security requirement, which had to be applied. ​​​​​​​This limitation depends on the specific WTS or VDI session."], "content": "To prevent data theft or data leaks, mapping of the local client's drives (C:\\ or DVD) is prohibited in the sessions. This was also a security requirement, which had to be applied. ​​​​​​​This limitation depends on the specific WTS or VDI session.", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 340}, {"topic": "7 Known limitations", "section": "7.5 Lock Screen", "paragraphs": ["Lock screens were enabled on the virtual sessions with a timeout of 15 minutes. This was necessary to meet the SAP Security Policies standards and to be aligned with client devices (Laptop/Workstation) configuration."], "content": "Lock screens were enabled on the virtual sessions with a timeout of 15 minutes. This was necessary to meet the SAP Security Policies standards and to be aligned with client devices (Laptop/Workstation) configuration.", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 341}, {"topic": "7 Known limitations", "section": "7.6.1 WTS sessions", "paragraphs": ["The SAP Desktop and all other WTS sessions are centrally managed virtual sessions. The available applications and software are installed and configured centrally based on the requirements defined by the server owners. For this reason, there are software missing from WTS sessions and can not be installed by the end user.", "If a program is needed in a specific WTS session, please clarify the request and business justification with the server owner, who then can decide to deploy the software or not."], "content": "The SAP Desktop and all other WTS sessions are centrally managed virtual sessions. The available applications and software are installed and configured centrally based on the requirements defined by the server owners. For this reason, there are software missing from WTS sessions and can not be installed by the end user. If a program is needed in a specific WTS session, please clarify the request and business justification with the server owner, who then can decide to deploy the software or not.", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 342}, {"topic": "7 Known limitations", "section": "7.6.2 VDI sessions", "paragraphs": ["All VDI devices are considered client devices, therefor if an application is missing, the end user can install it.", "As a first step, please always check Company Portal! It may be that the software you need is already available in Company Portal and you can install it with one click.", "If a program you need is not available in Company Portal, please consult the SRI database to determine if the required application is safe to install, or if SAP recommends an alternative. The SRI database can be found on this link: https://sri.bss.net.sap/"], "content": "All VDI devices are considered client devices, therefor if an application is missing, the end user can install it. As a first step, please always check Company Portal! It may be that the software you need is already available in Company Portal and you can install it with one click. If a program you need is not available in Company Portal, please consult the SRI database to determine if the required application is safe to install, or if SAP recommends an alternative. The SRI database can be found on this link: https://sri.bss.net.sap/", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 343}, {"topic": "8. ESC Desktop", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["On December 8th, 2025 we are releasing the new ECS Desktop in the Global domain which allows logon directly via Internet using Azure MFA authentication. For details and help, see ECS Desktop Authentication via Azure MFA on SAP Global Domain.", "An active SecureID Card is required for the internal logon to the ECS Desktop.", "Before requesting access, check whether you already have a relevant profile assigned as follows:", "Open the CAM Tool", "CAM (Production) (ondemand.com)", "Navigate to \"My Access\". In case you do not see this, you do not seem to have access yet.", "Filter for the Access Level Name \"CAM_HEC_WTS_MCD_DESKTOP\"", "If you don't have the desired access yet, request the following profile.", "Navigate to Requester → Request Profile", "Use \"Search by Keywords\" with name \"ECS HEC Administrative Desktop WTS\".", "Then click Next, select an approver, and enter a reason."], "content": "On December 8th, 2025 we are releasing the new ECS Desktop in the Global domain which allows logon directly via Internet using Azure MFA authentication. For details and help, see ECS Desktop Authentication via Azure MFA on SAP Global Domain. An active SecureID Card is required for the internal logon to the ECS Desktop. Before requesting access, check whether you already have a relevant profile assigned as follows: Open the CAM Tool CAM (Production) (ondemand.com) Navigate to \"My Access\". In case you do not see this, you do not seem to have access yet. Filter for the Access Level Name \"CAM_HEC_WTS_MCD_DESKTOP\" If you don't have the desired access yet, request the following profile. Navigate to Requester → Request Profile Use \"Search by Keywords\" with name \"ECS HEC Administrative Desktop WTS\". Then click Next, select an approver, and enter a reason.", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 344}, {"topic": "8. ESC Desktop", "section": "8.1 How to Log in", "paragraphs": ["ECS Desktop is accessible only from internal Office Network.", "If someone connects from a remote location, it is advisable to connect directly to office network through VPN or \" Office WTS \" first and then from there connect to ECS WTS. There is a performance tool available on this page to check whether the latency and speed from remote to SAP is sufficient.", "If you are working at the TCS location, you can connect to ECS Desktop directly.", "There is no need to log in to any of the Offshore WTS first or to SAP Desktop first and then hop to the ECS Desktop! This could cause issues in performance and the stability of your session.", "Your can access the ECS Desktop by using the following links: https://access.sap.com https://citrix-access.global.corp.sap/AccessPortal", "Select the region you want to connect to and then \"SAP ECS Access\".", "It requires 2-Factor authentication to log in.", "1) SAPHEC Password → Password for SAPHEC Domain (ECS Active directory password = Password)", "If you have to reset your SAPHEC Password, please use the TIC self-service TIC - Portal (net.sap) (Tools → Self Services → Execute Self Service → (USER tab) Reset Active Directory Password).", "2) Passcode → Secure ID Token (SAP RSA PIN + SAP SecureID 6 digit Rotating password = Passcode) (Note: In case you use a SecureID Soft Token, you must not provide the PIN before the RSA Passcode! Only the 8 digits from the RSA Passcode)", "If the access portal is not available, there is a possibility to log in directly to the particular regional ECS Desktop by the following links.", "EMEA: https://hec.citrix-access.global.corp.sap/logon/LogonPoint/index.html", "AMER: https://hec.citrix-access.phl.global.corp.sap/logon/LogonPoint/index.html", "APJ: https://hec.citrix-access.sin.global.corp.sap/logon/LogonPoint/index.html"], "content": "ECS Desktop is accessible only from internal Office Network. If someone connects from a remote location, it is advisable to connect directly to office network through VPN or \" Office WTS \" first and then from there connect to ECS WTS. There is a performance tool available on this page to check whether the latency and speed from remote to SAP is sufficient. If you are working at the TCS location, you can connect to ECS Desktop directly. There is no need to log in to any of the Offshore WTS first or to SAP Desktop first and then hop to the ECS Desktop! This could cause issues in performance and the stability of your session. Your can access the ECS Desktop by using the following links: https://access.sap.com https://citrix-access.global.corp.sap/AccessPortal Select the region you want to connect to and then \"SAP ECS Access\". It requires 2-Factor authentication to log in. 1) SAPHEC Password → Password for SAPHEC Domain (ECS Active directory password = Password) If you have to reset your SAPHEC Password, please use the TIC self-service TIC - Portal (net.sap) (Tools → Self Services → Execute Self Service → (USER tab) Reset Active Directory Password). 2) Passcode → Secure ID Token (SAP RSA PIN + SAP SecureID 6 digit Rotating password = Passcode) (Note: In case you use a SecureID Soft Token, you must not provide the PIN before the RSA Passcode! Only the 8 digits from the RSA Passcode) If the access portal is not available, there is a possibility to log in directly to the particular regional ECS Desktop by the following links. EMEA: https://hec.citrix-access.global.corp.sap/logon/LogonPoint/index.html AMER: https://hec.citrix-access.phl.global.corp.sap/logon/LogonPoint/index.html APJ: https://hec.citrix-access.sin.global.corp.sap/logon/LogonPoint/index.html", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 345}, {"topic": "9. FAQ", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Q1: How can I change my SAP domain password in my WTS or VDI virtual desktop?", "On the virtual desktop, at the top click on the small black box to access the Session Menu", "Now please click on the \"Ctrl+Alt+Del\" button to send this command to the virtual PC.", "Here select the \"Change a Password\" option and you will be prompted for your current password and for a new one", ".", "Q2: What is the difference between WTS and VDI", "The key difference between WTS and VDI to end user is that user has local administrative right in the VDI VM and hence can install software applications on the VDI.", "Users on WTS do not have privileges to install software.", "Software Centre is not available in WTS.", "For more comparison between WTS and VDI, you may go to WTS / VDI Comparison Chart.", "Q3: How can I change my Citrix session resolution?", "Open Citrix -> choose preference->display -> choose solution.", "Q4: How to use WTS/VDI on Linux", "login to the machine, open Terminal and run following command:", "curl -s -x '' https://github.wdf.sap.corp/raw/LDT/lapos/master/files/default/linuxinfra/ldt_addon.sh | sudo bash", "When script finished successfully - \"Citrix Receiver\" shortcut will be added to the desktop. Start Citrix Receiver, it should open login dialog, provide valid username and password. When logged in - you should see all your Citrix shortcuts.", "https://itsupportportal.services.sap/itsupport?id=kb_article_view&sysparm_article=IKB0011789", "Q5: How to use WTS/VDI on IOS devices", "Install workspace with self service", "Use access.sap.com and download access info. Open with workspace.", "Q6: How does printing work on WTS?", "You have to install a Printer Queue inside the WTS Session.", "Use any browser and go to the SAP Printing Tool.", "If you only see a blank page, please refresh / reload the page.", "Search the printer queue PWTS_BWS and / or PWTS_COS with \"WTS\" in the Search field or what you want to install.", "Go to the Drop-Down Menu next to the button “Connect to printer” and select “Download install script”", "Q7: How to access my OneDrive for Business data from WTS / VDI?", "OneDrive for Virtual Desktops system tray icon", "Simply right click the blue OneDrive for Virtual Desktops cloud icon on the system tray (near bottom right of the desktop screen). The following menu will pop up:", "Tooltip showing message", "Click the second item on the menu, view online, and you are on the way to your OneDrive for Business cloud on the web.", "OneDrive Web shortcut icon on the Desktop", "There is also a shortcut icon on your WTS / VDI desktop, named OneDrive Web, for you to launch directly your OneDrive cloud via the web browser.", "Using Open in... feature to launch your MS Office documents manually.", "Q8. Profile Reset", "Escalate ticket to Service Desktop Virtualization (WTS/VDI)", "Service offering IES-CS-WTS - Office / Project", "Assignment group IES CS Advanced - Client Virtualization (WTS, VDI)", "2nd level will process profile reset.", "Q9: How can I change my Citrix session resolution?", "After logon, you get a collection of published applications. At the top of the Published Application box, you have a set of small icons. Click on the settings icon and you'll get the settings menu. Here you can select which resolution you want to use (changes only apply to new sessions, not to existing sessions).", "Q10: Can I use the Azure Multi-Factor Authentication Authenticator App on a non-SAP device?", "Yes, the Microsoft Authenticator app can be used on private devices as well, to get started, please visit this page for more details.", "Q11: How to Request a VDI", "Requesting a VDI is simply a case of going to the DesktopCloud and choosing the specification of VDI you require.", "See the \"How to order a VDI\" page for more details.", "Q12: Does VDI support multi-monitor?", "Yes, we support multi-monitor.", "After you have launched VDI session, point your mouse at the Citrix Deskview toolbar at the top, and click [Window] to turn your VDI session from Full Screen to Windowed one.", "Then drag your VDI Window along the way to your second monitor, and place that VDI window across the 2 monitors, i.e. half of the VDI window on laptop screen & half on monitor. Now maximise (full screen) the VDI window and it will expand across the 2 monitors.", "Q13: How to change the VM parameter like CPU or RAM", "Open the DesktopCloud app, select the VDI, shut it down and when it shows \"Stopped\" click on \"Configuration\"", "Click on \"Edit\" and pick the new size from the list.", "Save your changes and start the VDI", "Q14: Does VDI support BYOD (Bring Your Own Device)?", "In general, it is possible to use VDI with any device (private or Corporate) if the Citrix Receiver is properly installed.", "Support is of course limited for private devices, as it is not possible to support and troubleshoot all types of Citrix Client installations.", "Q15: What are the monthly costs per VDI desktop?", "Please check the VDI costs explained page for details about cost calculation.", "Q16: Is there any backup for the data in my VDI VM?", "Backup is not available for VDI. Therefore, you will be responsible for backing up important data by yourself, for example, to your OneDrive for Business. For more details, please visit this SharePoint site.", "Q17: What if I need more disk / storage space in my VDI?", "Each VDI has a default Disk space (C:\\drive). The capacity of this C:\\ drive can be changed, but it is recommended to order an additional data disk (D:\\ drive with different sizes) can be requested via the Desktop Cloud, either at the time when you make your new VDI, or later on by using the \"Configure\" function. Note: There is an additional cost for getting an additional data disk.", "To request for an additional data disk for an existing VDI VM, just go to Desktop Cloud, click \"Configure\" under your VM,", "You will be brought to the Configuration dialog page as below. Just choose one of the available disk size options.", "Now please click on \"Save\" to apply the changes. The additional data disk will show up in your VDI shortly, a reboot might be required.", "If you need more space on your VDI's data disk C:\\ or D:\\ drive, please raise a ticket to the support.", "In the ticket please state, the VDI's name (WDFV4100XXXXD), which drive you would like to extend and to what size. Please support this request with a valid business reason.", "Q18: Can I share my VDI with my colleagues?", "Technically it is possible, but it is not recommended. A VDI is your personal Virtual machine (VM). Only the owner of the VDI, are able to access the VM through the optimized Citrix Receiver the colleagues can only access via Microsoft Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP) connection (RDP needs to be enabled in your VM and SAP UserIDs have to added to the local admins group and remote desktop users group), meaning that they can only access your VDI from within SAP network. Also note that only one user can access the VM at the same time.", "With all these stated reasons, we don’t recommend you to share VDI with others.", "You can transfer the ownership of the VDI based on this guide: How to transfer a VDI to another user (sharepoint.com)", "Q19: How can I delete my VDI completely?", "Please navigate to the DesktopCloud application and select the VDI you wish to delete and shut it down, when it shows \"Stopped\" status, click on the \"Destroy\" button.", "Q19: ow does printing work on WTS?", "During your logon all your local installed printers are mapped automatically to the session. You can also map the pool printers to the WTS session from the Printing@SAP page Due to the design, printing could take a while. Do not cancel your Citrix ICA connection while printing, otherwise printing will be cancelled too.", "Q20: Profile Reset", "To reset your profile, please request a profile reset by issuing an IT Ticket. In the ticket, please state the problem issue that you are encountering that leads to the need of profile reset, and also the region where the reset is needed. The support team will help to determine if this is really a profile issue or possibly caused by another problem.", "Warning: Profile Reset will clear all your settings includes shortcuts and IE favourites. So before requesting for profile reset, please back up your files and settings if you still need them.", "Note: Profile Reset is the last resort. Please seethe \"Understanding your WTS Profile\" FAQ below for alternative troubleshooting and resolution methods.", "Q21: How to configure the automatic shutdown", "Open the DesktopCloud app.", "Select the virtual machine.", "In the detail pane, select Configuration - Auto Shutdown.", "Click the Edit button.", "Set ‘Enabled’ to ‘ON’", "Pick a time and the time zone when you want the VM being stopped.", "If you want a notification being sent to your e-mail address 30 minutes prior to the shutdown event, set ‘Send notifications before auto-shutdown’ to YES and enter your e-mail address. The notification will contain 2 links to postpone the automatic shutdown with 1 or 2 hours and a third to skip the shutdown for this one schedule.", "Save your changes.", "Reference:", "https://sap.sharepoint.com/sites/ITforYou/wts-vdi/SitePages/Home.aspx", "https://sap.sharepoint.com/sites/ITforYou/wts-vdi/SitePages/WTS%20and%20VDI%20FAQ.aspx", "Q22: How to deactivate screensaver in WTS?", "Screensaver is active in WTS. Screensaver has been mandatory activated for all WTS users, because this is necessary to meet the SAP Security Policies standards and to be aligned with client devices (Laptop / Workstation) configuration. Timeout value is 15 Minutes.", "Q23: VDI, WTS Standard Desktop - Outlook Cannot be started in WTS", "You will need to generate a new Outlook profile with the following steps:", "1) Click Start, Control Panel, Mail (32-bit) 2) Click Show Profiles 3) Click Add, type \"WTS\" (or any unique name) as the Profile Name 4) Change the drop down for \"Always use this profile\" to the newly created profile 5) Click OK, and then launch Outlook from the desktop shortcut"], "content": "Q1: How can I change my SAP domain password in my WTS or VDI virtual desktop? On the virtual desktop, at the top click on the small black box to access the Session Menu Now please click on the \"Ctrl+Alt+Del\" button to send this command to the virtual PC. Here select the \"Change a Password\" option and you will be prompted for your current password and for a new one . Q2: What is the difference between WTS and VDI The key difference between WTS and VDI to end user is that user has local administrative right in the VDI VM and hence can install software applications on the VDI. Users on WTS do not have privileges to install software. Software Centre is not available in WTS. For more comparison between WTS and VDI, you may go to WTS / VDI Comparison Chart. Q3: How can I change my Citrix session resolution? Open Citrix -> choose preference->display -> choose solution. Q4: How to use WTS/VDI on Linux login to the machine, open Terminal and run following command: curl -s -x '' https://github.wdf.sap.corp/raw/LDT/lapos/master/files/default/linuxinfra/ldt_addon.sh | sudo bash When script finished successfully - \"Citrix Receiver\" shortcut will be added to the desktop. Start Citrix Receiver, it should open login dialog, provide valid username and password. When logged in - you should see all your Citrix shortcuts. https://itsupportportal.services.sap/itsupport?id=kb_article_view&sysparm_article=IKB0011789 Q5: How to use WTS/VDI on IOS devices Install workspace with self service Use access.sap.com and download access info. Open with workspace. Q6: How does printing work on WTS? You have to install a Printer Queue inside the WTS Session. Use any browser and go to the SAP Printing Tool. If you only see a blank page, please refresh / reload the page. Search the printer queue PWTS_BWS and / or PWTS_COS with \"WTS\" in the Search field or what you want to install. Go to the Drop-Down Menu next to the button “Connect to printer” and select “Download install script” Q7: How to access my OneDrive for Business data from WTS / VDI? OneDrive for Virtual Desktops system tray icon Simply right click the blue OneDrive for Virtual Desktops cloud icon on the system tray (near bottom right of the desktop screen). The following menu will pop up: Tooltip showing message Click the second item on the menu, view online, and you are on the way to your OneDrive for Business cloud on the web. OneDrive Web shortcut icon on the Desktop There is also a shortcut icon on your WTS / VDI desktop, named OneDrive Web, for you to launch directly your OneDrive cloud via the web browser. Using Open in... feature to launch your MS Office documents manually. Q8. Profile Reset Escalate ticket to Service Desktop Virtualization (WTS/VDI) Service offering IES-CS-WTS - Office / Project Assignment group IES CS Advanced - Client Virtualization (WTS, VDI) 2nd level will process profile reset. Q9: How can I change my Citrix session resolution? After logon, you get a collection of published applications. At the top of the Published Application box, you have a set of small icons. Click on the settings icon and you'll get the settings menu. Here you can select which resolution you want to use (changes only apply to new sessions, not to existing sessions). Q10: Can I use the Azure Multi-Factor Authentication Authenticator App on a non-SAP device? Yes, the Microsoft Authenticator app can be used on private devices as well, to get started, please visit this page for more details. Q11: How to Request a VDI Requesting a VDI is simply a case of going to the DesktopCloud and choosing the specification of VDI you require. See the \"How to order a VDI\" page for more details. Q12: Does VDI support multi-monitor? Yes, we support multi-monitor. After you have launched VDI session, point your mouse at the Citrix Deskview toolbar at the top, and click [Window] to turn your VDI session from Full Screen to Windowed one. Then drag your VDI Window along the way to your second monitor, and place that VDI window across the 2 monitors, i.e. half of the VDI window on laptop screen & half on monitor. Now maximise (full screen) the VDI window and it will expand across the 2 monitors. Q13: How to change the VM parameter like CPU or RAM Open the DesktopCloud app, select the VDI, shut it down and when it shows \"Stopped\" click on \"Configuration\" Click on \"Edit\" and pick the new size from the list. Save your changes and start the VDI Q14: Does VDI support BYOD (Bring Your Own Device)? In general, it is possible to use VDI with any device (private or Corporate) if the Citrix Receiver is properly installed. Support is of course limited for private devices, as it is not possible to support and troubleshoot all types of Citrix Client installations. Q15: What are the monthly costs per VDI desktop? Please check the VDI costs explained page for details about cost calculation. Q16: Is there any backup for the data in my VDI VM? Backup is not available for VDI. Therefore, you will be responsible for backing up important data by yourself, for example, to your OneDrive for Business. For more details, please visit this SharePoint site. Q17: What if I need more disk / storage space in my VDI? Each VDI has a default Disk space (C:\\drive). The capacity of this C:\\ drive can be changed, but it is recommended to order an additional data disk (D:\\ drive with different sizes) can be requested via the Desktop Cloud, either at the time when you make your new VDI, or later on by using the \"Configure\" function. Note: There is an additional cost for getting an additional data disk. To request for an additional data disk for an existing VDI VM, just go to Desktop Cloud, click \"Configure\" under your VM, You will be brought to the Configuration dialog page as below. Just choose one of the available disk size options. Now please click on \"Save\" to apply the changes. The additional data disk will show up in your VDI shortly, a reboot might be required. If you need more space on your VDI's data disk C:\\ or D:\\ drive, please raise a ticket to the support. In the ticket please state, the VDI's name (WDFV4100XXXXD), which drive you would like to extend and to what size. Please support this request with a valid business reason. Q18: Can I share my VDI with my colleagues? Technically it is possible, but it is not recommended. A VDI is your personal Virtual machine (VM). Only the owner of the VDI, are able to access the VM through the optimized Citrix Receiver the colleagues can only access via Microsoft Remote Desktop Protocol (RDP) connection (RDP needs to be enabled in your VM and SAP UserIDs have to added to the local admins group and remote desktop users group), meaning that they can only access your VDI from within SAP network. Also note that only one user can access the VM at the same time. With all these stated reasons, we don’t recommend you to share VDI with others. You can transfer the ownership of the VDI based on this guide: How to transfer a VDI to another user (sharepoint.com) Q19: How can I delete my VDI completely? Please navigate to the DesktopCloud application and select the VDI you wish to delete and shut it down, when it shows \"Stopped\" status, click on the \"Destroy\" button. Q19: ow does printing work on WTS? During your logon all your local installed printers are mapped automatically to the session. You can also map the pool printers to the WTS session from the Printing@SAP page Due to the design, printing could take a while. Do not cancel your Citrix ICA connection while printing, otherwise printing will be cancelled too. Q20: Profile Reset To reset your profile, please request a profile reset by issuing an IT Ticket. In the ticket, please state the problem issue that you are encountering that leads to the need of profile reset, and also the region where the reset is needed. The support team will help to determine if this is really a profile issue or possibly caused by another problem. Warning: Profile Reset will clear all your settings includes shortcuts and IE favourites. So before requesting for profile reset, please back up your files and settings if you still need them. Note: Profile Reset is the last resort. Please seethe \"Understanding your WTS Profile\" FAQ below for alternative troubleshooting and resolution methods. Q21: How to configure the automatic shutdown Open the DesktopCloud app. Select the virtual machine. In the detail pane, select Configuration - Auto Shutdown. Click the Edit button. Set ‘Enabled’ to ‘ON’ Pick a time and the time zone when you want the VM being stopped. If you want a notification being sent to your e-mail address 30 minutes prior to the shutdown event, set ‘Send notifications before auto-shutdown’ to YES and enter your e-mail address. The notification will contain 2 links to postpone the automatic shutdown with 1 or 2 hours and a third to skip the shutdown for this one schedule. Save your changes. Reference: https://sap.sharepoint.com/sites/ITforYou/wts-vdi/SitePages/Home.aspx https://sap.sharepoint.com/sites/ITforYou/wts-vdi/SitePages/WTS%20and%20VDI%20FAQ.aspx Q22: How to deactivate screensaver in WTS? Screensaver is active in WTS. Screensaver has been mandatory activated for all WTS users, because this is necessary to meet the SAP Security Policies standards and to be aligned with client devices (Laptop / Workstation) configuration. Timeout value is 15 Minutes. Q23: VDI, WTS Standard Desktop - Outlook Cannot be started in WTS You will need to generate a new Outlook profile with the following steps: 1) Click Start, Control Panel, Mail (32-bit) 2) Click Show Profiles 3) Click Add, type \"WTS\" (or any unique name) as the Profile Name 4) Change the drop down for \"Always use this profile\" to the newly created profile 5) Click OK, and then launch Outlook from the desktop shortcut", "source": "WTS VDI", "id": 346}, {"topic": "", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["ONE Support", "INTERNAL- SAP ONLY", "Version control", "If you find any content in this document is out of date, feel free to contact the Authors for feedback!", "Thanks for your cooperation in advance!", "Area：Workplace Delivery"], "content": "ONE Support INTERNAL- SAP ONLY Version control If you find any content in this document is out of date, feel free to contact the Authors for feedback! Thanks for your cooperation in advance! Area：Workplace Delivery", "source": "Workplace Delivery", "id": 347}, {"topic": "About Windows", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Windows version", "Windows 11", "Windows Device Name", "In SAP, the correct naming convention is usually W-xxxxxxx.", "W is an acronym for windows to indicate, that this is a windows machine. There are a few exceptions, like S- for a shared machine. DS- for a Digital Signage Intune System.", "xxxxxxx is the serial number from your device which is the information that is available when you are provisioning your device, maybe from home.", "It is linked to our Asset Management and other services, such as Service Now. Only with a correct computer name all the assignments can be done properly which is a pre-requisite for a lot of things to work, like Software Center.", "Windows update", "The gradual rollout has started, and the new Operating System should be visible in \"Windows Update\" since Calendar week 47, 2022 ​​​​​​​", "How can I upgrade to Windows 11?", "Refer to the KB article for the steps to upgrade to Windows 11.​​​​​​​​​​​​​​", "Remark! Please note – only devices enrolled into the SAP SE cloud tenant (Azure AD joined and Intune managed) are in scope for Windows 11 upgrade at SAP.", "Devices running older, so called “bare metal” images, although their hardware might be supported for Windows 11, are out of scope. For such devices ask IT Support for reinstallation of the operating system directly to Windows 11. How to recognize you are running \"bare metal\" image? Go to Start -> Settings -> System -> About If the device name starts with 3-letter location code (e.g. WDF, PHL, PAR etc.) then you are running the bare metal image.", "Devices, where hardware requirements are not met, must be replaced for Windows 11.", "List of computer models eligible for Windows 11 update", "LENOVO / DELL / HP / Microsoft"], "content": "Windows version Windows 11 Windows Device Name In SAP, the correct naming convention is usually W-xxxxxxx. W is an acronym for windows to indicate, that this is a windows machine. There are a few exceptions, like S- for a shared machine. DS- for a Digital Signage Intune System. xxxxxxx is the serial number from your device which is the information that is available when you are provisioning your device, maybe from home. It is linked to our Asset Management and other services, such as Service Now. Only with a correct computer name all the assignments can be done properly which is a pre-requisite for a lot of things to work, like Software Center. Windows update The gradual rollout has started, and the new Operating System should be visible in \"Windows Update\" since Calendar week 47, 2022 ​​​​​​​ How can I upgrade to Windows 11? Refer to the KB article for the steps to upgrade to Windows 11.​​​​​​​​​​​​​​ Remark! Please note – only devices enrolled into the SAP SE cloud tenant (Azure AD joined and Intune managed) are in scope for Windows 11 upgrade at SAP. Devices running older, so called “bare metal” images, although their hardware might be supported for Windows 11, are out of scope. For such devices ask IT Support for reinstallation of the operating system directly to Windows 11. How to recognize you are running \"bare metal\" image? Go to Start -> Settings -> System -> About If the device name starts with 3-letter location code (e.g. WDF, PHL, PAR etc.) then you are running the bare metal image. Devices, where hardware requirements are not met, must be replaced for Windows 11. List of computer models eligible for Windows 11 update LENOVO / DELL / HP / Microsoft", "source": "Workplace Delivery", "id": 348}, {"topic": "How to set up your new Windows computer", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Follow the instructions below to set up and customize your new Windows device. Plan for approximately 1 hour to complete. Later, you can install additional software with only a few clicks. If you are using a desktop connected to the LAN, contact IT Support for the Fore x`scout exclusion.", "Set up your new computer", "Power on your device. Choose your region and keyboard layout and select language. For now, skip additional languages and keyboard layouts – add them after set up completion.", "Connect to SAP-Guest or your home Wi-Fi, check “Connect automatically”."], "content": "Follow the instructions below to set up and customize your new Windows device. Plan for approximately 1 hour to complete. Later, you can install additional software with only a few clicks. If you are using a desktop connected to the LAN, contact IT Support for the Fore x`scout exclusion. Set up your new computer Power on your device. Choose your region and keyboard layout and select language. For now, skip additional languages and keyboard layouts – add them after set up completion. Connect to SAP-Guest or your home Wi-Fi, check “Connect automatically”.", "source": "Workplace Delivery", "id": 349}, {"topic": "How to set up your new Windows computer", "section": "2.2 Prepare your current laptop (If it is for PC replacement)", "paragraphs": ["Enable Desktop & Document folder.", "Syncing to OneDrive, Sync your OneDrive client to OneDrive so it is up to date.", "Make note of any sharepoint files, folder, or sites your synced to windows.", "Make note of any group shares you have synced to Windows. Group share guidelines can be accessed here.", "Backup your Outlook signatures and Outlook Export Rules.", "Upload any local PST file to your 100 GB mailbox if necessary.", "Backup your bookmarks in Chrome and Edge.", "If you choose Password depot, see details here.", "All purchased software needs to be reinstalled."], "content": "Enable Desktop & Document folder. Syncing to OneDrive, Sync your OneDrive client to OneDrive so it is up to date. Make note of any sharepoint files, folder, or sites your synced to windows. Make note of any group shares you have synced to Windows. Group share guidelines can be accessed here. Backup your Outlook signatures and Outlook Export Rules. Upload any local PST file to your 100 GB mailbox if necessary. Backup your bookmarks in Chrome and Edge. If you choose Password depot, see details here. All purchased software needs to be reinstalled.", "source": "Workplace Delivery", "id": 350}, {"topic": "How to set up your new Windows computer", "section": "2.3 New PC Migration", "paragraphs": ["Let Software Install. You can start working with web applications while Microsoft365 and other important software installed.", "A progress indicator will pop up several times. You will also see installation notification from SAP Software Distribution or Microsoft Intune software Distribution:", "When completed you will see the following message.", "Your device is now set up for the SAP environment and ready to use.", "You will be able to check system is compliant within Company portal.", "After approximately 2-4 hours, additional software packages become available.", "Select your preferred applications and follow the installations instructions.", "You can also skip to defer installing of additional applications.", "Installation progress is shown, are start might be required to complete.", "Now you are all set to use these applications.", "Additional software is available in Company portal."], "content": "Let Software Install. You can start working with web applications while Microsoft365 and other important software installed. A progress indicator will pop up several times. You will also see installation notification from SAP Software Distribution or Microsoft Intune software Distribution: When completed you will see the following message. Your device is now set up for the SAP environment and ready to use. You will be able to check system is compliant within Company portal. After approximately 2-4 hours, additional software packages become available. Select your preferred applications and follow the installations instructions. You can also skip to defer installing of additional applications. Installation progress is shown, are start might be required to complete. Now you are all set to use these applications. Additional software is available in Company portal.", "source": "Workplace Delivery", "id": 351}, {"topic": "How to set up your new Windows computer", "section": "2.4 Network:", "paragraphs": ["After your device enrollment is done, you can access to sap network with below 2 options:"], "content": "After your device enrollment is done, you can access to sap network with below 2 options:", "source": "Workplace Delivery", "id": 352}, {"topic": "How to set up your new Windows computer", "section": "2.4.1 In SAP office", "paragraphs": ["Connect to SAP Corporate network from office", "Select SAP and Connect", "Or Connect to SAP-Guest (Internet access)"], "content": "Connect to SAP Corporate network from office Select SAP and Connect Or Connect to SAP-Guest (Internet access)", "source": "Workplace Delivery", "id": 353}, {"topic": "How to set up your new Windows computer", "section": "2.4.2 Not in SAP office", "paragraphs": ["Connect to VPN with F5 BIG-IP Edge client or Global Protect.", "For details, refer to IES Knowledge Base - F5 VPN Best Practice"], "content": "Connect to VPN with F5 BIG-IP Edge client or Global Protect. For details, refer to IES Knowledge Base - F5 VPN Best Practice", "source": "Workplace Delivery", "id": 354}, {"topic": "Company Portal", "section": "3.1 Company portal:", "paragraphs": ["Company Portal is the cloud equivalent to Software Center. Company Portal is managed by Microsoft Intune – it offers applications and scripts that SAP-IT made available for you, just like Software Center. It offers all available, mandatory, and optional applications, Microsoft security updates and options for installation."], "content": "Company Portal is the cloud equivalent to Software Center. Company Portal is managed by Microsoft Intune – it offers applications and scripts that SAP-IT made available for you, just like Software Center. It offers all available, mandatory, and optional applications, Microsoft security updates and options for installation.", "source": "Workplace Delivery", "id": 355}, {"topic": "Company Portal", "section": "3.1.1 Settings and Sync", "paragraphs": ["You can click Settings in order to perform a manual Sync / to personalize your app color/to collect performance and usage data/to find out the currently using Intune company portal version.", "The Sync device action initiates an immediate synchronization with Intune. It will check in to Intune, passes the current compliance status and will receive all pending actions or policies that have been assigned to the machine, like configuration updates or newly deployed applications."], "content": "You can click Settings in order to perform a manual Sync / to personalize your app color/to collect performance and usage data/to find out the currently using Intune company portal version. The Sync device action initiates an immediate synchronization with Intune. It will check in to Intune, passes the current compliance status and will receive all pending actions or policies that have been assigned to the machine, like configuration updates or newly deployed applications.", "source": "Workplace Delivery", "id": 356}, {"topic": "Company Portal", "section": "3.1.2 Devices", "paragraphs": ["To view the compliance status of your devices from Company Portal, you can select the Devices page to see device status. You can also sync your device to Intune here.", "Device status can be:", "‘Can access company resources’ = Compliant", "‘Checking access’ = Currently syncing the status to Intune", "‘Can't access company resources’ = not compliant", "3.1.3 application install", "The default page that appears when you open the Company Portal displays ‘Featured Apps’, recently published applications and a list of your devices.", "Apps", "From the menu, select ‘Apps’ tab to view all available applications.", "The available applications you can see depends on:", "the Operating System and version installed.", "applications/software existing on your device (e.g.: Add-ins for specific applications)", "App Categories", "App Categories show in detail all featured apps as well as other categories like Business, Computer Management etc.", "Downloads & Updates", "This tab provides summary of all the installed apps in your device as well as provide information on Available updates and replacements."], "content": "To view the compliance status of your devices from Company Portal, you can select the Devices page to see device status. You can also sync your device to Intune here. Device status can be: ‘Can access company resources’ = Compliant ‘Checking access’ = Currently syncing the status to Intune ‘Can't access company resources’ = not compliant 3.1.3 application install The default page that appears when you open the Company Portal displays ‘Featured Apps’, recently published applications and a list of your devices. Apps From the menu, select ‘Apps’ tab to view all available applications. The available applications you can see depends on: the Operating System and version installed. applications/software existing on your device (e.g.: Add-ins for specific applications) App Categories App Categories show in detail all featured apps as well as other categories like Business, Computer Management etc. Downloads & Updates This tab provides summary of all the installed apps in your device as well as provide information on Available updates and replacements.", "source": "Workplace Delivery", "id": 357}, {"topic": "Company Portal", "section": "3.2 What is Device Health?", "paragraphs": ["Using Device Health SAP IT implemented a security standard ensuring all SAP workstations are configured appropriately to", "Safeguard data.", "Reinforce protection against malware or ransomware attacks.", "Assist in minimizing system crashes.", "Facilitate the end user’s experience and productivity.", "Think of Device Health as a regular inspection of your computer to be sure it is always safe for you to log on and use. In a nutshell, Device Health consists of the following components:", "A set of rules (checks) are in place to ensure your device’s safety.", "You can see the compliance status and issues with those checks in Company Portal", "If your computer fails any check, you’ll receive a toast notification.", "You have a grace period of 24 hours to fix the issue before Conditional Access, blocks your device.", "Execute our ‘Fix-It’ application to automatically remediate the compliance issue.", "After the problem got fixed use our ‘Evaluate' application to re-check the compliant status.", "Access blocked – what now?", "Already before your device is blocked you will receive a pop-up message stating the issue. The problem must be fixed within 24 hours before Conditional Access blocks access to most of your resources, like all Microsoft applications (Office, Teams, …)", "The pop-up message provides you with a button called <Fix-it> ‘to remediate the problem. If you click on the link here, you’ll receive more information on your compliance issue and troubleshooting steps. If the popup notification disappears, don’t worry; it will reappear in 30 seconds.", "Additionally, the same solution is offered in Company Portal to be executed manually through the Fix-It application.", "How can I check my machine's compliance status?", "Open Company Portal using Windows search.", "On the Home screen you can see the compliance status.", "In the Device section the compliance problem will be indicated (if there is any), and the link offered to obtain more information.", "Open Company Portal – section Devices.", "Click on your active device to get details.", "On devices with a compliance issue, get instructions from the link ‘How to resolve this’.", "This will include running the Fix-it application you can find in the section “Apps” in Company Portal", "Run the Re-Evaluation application from Company Portal.", "Click on check access.", "If the device is blocked, after the grace period of 24 hours, you will see \"Can access company resources, but action required\".", "Re-evaluate Device Health", "What if the Fix-It application didn't work?", "If the issue couldn’t be resolved by the Fix-It application, you will receive another toast notification giving you the option to raise an IT ticket to get help from SAP IT to solve the issue.", "Note! For some problems, an automated fix might not be available as it will require user interaction or will cause a service disruption. In that case, the notification offers to create a ticket right away.", "Device compliance checks", "Once you know which of the below check has failed, for additional information on how to fix issues and advanced troubleshooting, click the link for your topic below:", "Disk Encryption", "Umbrella Services", "Secure Boot", "Cumulative Update Installation", "Windows OS build", "SAM Compliance", "Microsoft Defender", "How can I leave quarantine and access the internal SAP network again?", "First, you have to follow all steps given the Device Health knowledge article from the popup notification.", "Once your computer status is compliant again, and the status has synced, your computer can join the internal network again.", "Alas, ForeScout Once will not re-evaluate your status and find out that the computer is compliant again by itself. To get out of quarantine, you need to trigger a new check from ForeScout, which is done whenever there's a change in your network, like a new IP address.", "Hence you need to re-authenticate your device in the network. You can do this by switching networks (from LAN to WiFi or vice versa), reboot, restarting the ForeScout agent or turning WiFi on and off. This will trigger ForeScout to verify whether your computer is eligible to access the network again and (re-)check your Intune compliance status.", "Managing IT Equipment during long-term absences", "Managing IT Equipment during long-term absences", "Learn more", "FAQ on Compliance questions Find here the most common questions on Device Health, Conditional Access, and access problems.", "Conditional Access on Windows Devices Find here the most basic information on Conditional Access."], "content": "Using Device Health SAP IT implemented a security standard ensuring all SAP workstations are configured appropriately to Safeguard data. Reinforce protection against malware or ransomware attacks. Assist in minimizing system crashes. Facilitate the end user’s experience and productivity. Think of Device Health as a regular inspection of your computer to be sure it is always safe for you to log on and use. In a nutshell, Device Health consists of the following components: A set of rules (checks) are in place to ensure your device’s safety. You can see the compliance status and issues with those checks in Company Portal If your computer fails any check, you’ll receive a toast notification. You have a grace period of 24 hours to fix the issue before Conditional Access, blocks your device. Execute our ‘Fix-It’ application to automatically remediate the compliance issue. After the problem got fixed use our ‘Evaluate' application to re-check the compliant status. Access blocked – what now? Already before your device is blocked you will receive a pop-up message stating the issue. The problem must be fixed within 24 hours before Conditional Access blocks access to most of your resources, like all Microsoft applications (Office, Teams, …) The pop-up message provides you with a button called <Fix-it> ‘to remediate the problem. If you click on the link here, you’ll receive more information on your compliance issue and troubleshooting steps. If the popup notification disappears, don’t worry; it will reappear in 30 seconds. Additionally, the same solution is offered in Company Portal to be executed manually through the Fix-It application. How can I check my machine's compliance status? Open Company Portal using Windows search. On the Home screen you can see the compliance status. In the Device section the compliance problem will be indicated (if there is any), and the link offered to obtain more information. Open Company Portal – section Devices. Click on your active device to get details. On devices with a compliance issue, get instructions from the link ‘How to resolve this’. This will include running the Fix-it application you can find in the section “Apps” in Company Portal Run the Re-Evaluation application from Company Portal. Click on check access. If the device is blocked, after the grace period of 24 hours, you will see \"Can access company resources, but action required\". Re-evaluate Device Health What if the Fix-It application didn't work? If the issue couldn’t be resolved by the Fix-It application, you will receive another toast notification giving you the option to raise an IT ticket to get help from SAP IT to solve the issue. Note! For some problems, an automated fix might not be available as it will require user interaction or will cause a service disruption. In that case, the notification offers to create a ticket right away. Device compliance checks Once you know which of the below check has failed, for additional information on how to fix issues and advanced troubleshooting, click the link for your topic below: Disk Encryption Umbrella Services Secure Boot Cumulative Update Installation Windows OS build SAM Compliance Microsoft Defender How can I leave quarantine and access the internal SAP network again? First, you have to follow all steps given the Device Health knowledge article from the popup notification. Once your computer status is compliant again, and the status has synced, your computer can join the internal network again. Alas, ForeScout Once will not re-evaluate your status and find out that the computer is compliant again by itself. To get out of quarantine, you need to trigger a new check from ForeScout, which is done whenever there's a change in your network, like a new IP address. Hence you need to re-authenticate your device in the network. You can do this by switching networks (from LAN to WiFi or vice versa), reboot, restarting the ForeScout agent or turning WiFi on and off. This will trigger ForeScout to verify whether your computer is eligible to access the network again and (re-)check your Intune compliance status. Managing IT Equipment during long-term absences Managing IT Equipment during long-term absences Learn more FAQ on Compliance questions Find here the most common questions on Device Health, Conditional Access, and access problems. Conditional Access on Windows Devices Find here the most basic information on Conditional Access.", "source": "Workplace Delivery", "id": 358}, {"topic": "FAQ", "section": "", "paragraphs": ["Q1 : If user needs to backup the data in old PC, what would be your suggestions?", "Q2: Windows - PowerShell pop-up occurring every few seconds, How to close it .", "1. Press Windows Key + S and type: \"Task Scheduler\" and open it", "2. In the Task Scheduler window, Click \"Task Schedular Library\"", "3. Find the task \"Credmanager\" in the list > Right-click and select \"Disable\"", "4. Wait until the PowerShell window closes and check if the issue occurs again", "Click on Task Scheduler > Run", "Q3: What is the required bandwidth to enroll a Windows device?", "8 Mb/s", "Q4: How to Setup Multi Factor Authentication (MFA) for Office 365", "1. Go to https://aka.ms/mysecurityinfo", "2. Sign in using your SAP email address and password", "3. Select \"Security\" info on the left > Click + Add Method", "4. Setup Authenticator App", "5. Start by getting the app", "6. On your Mobile - Open the Microsoft Authenticator App", "7. On your Mobile - Click Add Account > Select Work or school account", "8. On the Microsoft Authenticator webpage - Click Next > You should now see a QR Code, use Authenticator app to scan it.", "For more info, please refer to “Azure AD – MFA\"", "Q5：How can end users install an additional licensed software on a Shared Intune device?", "IT Support agents can help to install additional licensed software on a Shared Intune device using an RACCOUNT.", "Q6: What is Templafy?", "Templafy is SAP's new cloud-based template and document management system which allows you to easily generate corporate new Microsoft PowerPoint presentations and e-mail signatures that are up to date with SAP visual brand identity, corporate data and legal information. Read more about it. IKB0012751", "Q7: How to disable touch screen", "it can be turned off from device manager.", "Q8：What are the supported VPN solutions in SAP for windows?", "GlobalProtect & F5 BIG-IP Edge Client"], "content": "Q1 : If user needs to backup the data in old PC, what would be your suggestions? Q2: Windows - PowerShell pop-up occurring every few seconds, How to close it . 1. Press Windows Key + S and type: \"Task Scheduler\" and open it 2. In the Task Scheduler window, Click \"Task Schedular Library\" 3. Find the task \"Credmanager\" in the list > Right-click and select \"Disable\" 4. Wait until the PowerShell window closes and check if the issue occurs again Click on Task Scheduler > Run Q3: What is the required bandwidth to enroll a Windows device? 8 Mb/s Q4: How to Setup Multi Factor Authentication (MFA) for Office 365 1. Go to https://aka.ms/mysecurityinfo 2. Sign in using your SAP email address and password 3. Select \"Security\" info on the left > Click + Add Method 4. Setup Authenticator App 5. Start by getting the app 6. On your Mobile - Open the Microsoft Authenticator App 7. On your Mobile - Click Add Account > Select Work or school account 8. On the Microsoft Authenticator webpage - Click Next > You should now see a QR Code, use Authenticator app to scan it. For more info, please refer to “Azure AD – MFA\" Q5：How can end users install an additional licensed software on a Shared Intune device? IT Support agents can help to install additional licensed software on a Shared Intune device using an RACCOUNT. Q6: What is Templafy? Templafy is SAP's new cloud-based template and document management system which allows you to easily generate corporate new Microsoft PowerPoint presentations and e-mail signatures that are up to date with SAP visual brand identity, corporate data and legal information. Read more about it. IKB0012751 Q7: How to disable touch screen it can be turned off from device manager. Q8：What are the supported VPN solutions in SAP for windows? GlobalProtect & F5 BIG-IP Edge Client", "source": "Workplace Delivery", "id": 359}];